{"abstract":"Denne bog giver et overblik over Indlandsisen og landskabets opståen og udvikling omkring Kangerlussuaq (tidligere Søndre Strømfjord) i Vestgrønland. For landskabet omkring 30 km veje fra Kangerlussuaq til Indlandsisen, illustrerer glimrende hvordan alle typer af landskaber i Grønland og – overraskende – i Danmark, er opstået under og siden istiden. I Kangerlussuaqområdet er processerne blot aktive i dag, og kan dermed umiddelbart ses. Der er beskrevet lokaliteter som ses fra områdets køreveje, og bogen er tænkt som en slags ”vejsideguide”. Bogen er en illustreret og letforståelig indføring i den dynamik som har skabt landskaberne. Målgruppen er besøgende i Vestgrønland og ved Indlandsisen, som har interesse for at forstå hvordan isen, smeltevandet og landskabet er opstået og hvordan de spiller sammen.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, N. Tvis","Kristiansen, Søren Munch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824767"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"indlandsisen kvartærgeologi og landskab omkring kangerlussuaq vestgrønland","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/aul.588","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-824767","ids":["au-2fc56c7e-75e6-44d3-8b22-8cb5e5dee1af"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-470645C06808C4A527E13EEF9D6775E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/436274544/Knudsen_Kristiansen_Kangerlussuaq_2025.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/aul.588","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N. Tvis","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"9a2f0627-7856-4ac4-b42d-f3357daa9557","name":"Knudsen, N. Tvis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren M.","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","name_org":"Kristiansen, Søren M.","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/aul.588","eisbn":["9788775075836"],"place":"Aarhus","publisher":"AU Library Scholarly Publishing Services","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2fc56c7e-75e6-44d3-8b22-8cb5e5dee1af"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Indlandsisen, kvartærgeologi og landskab omkring Kangerlussuaq, Vestgrønland","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-824767","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The somatic JAK2V617F sequence variation, a key driver of myeloproliferative neoplasms, has been associated with increased risk of aortic aneurysms. This study aimed to explore associations between the JAK2V617F variant allele frequency (VAF) and ascending, descending, and abdominal aortic aneurysms. METHODS: In the DANCAVAS I and II trials (Danish Cardiovascular Screening), 15 000 individuals underwent cardiovascular risk assessments including blood samples and noncontrast ECG-gated computed tomography scans. In this cross-sectional substudy, individuals with screening-detected aortic aneurysms (≥45 mm ascending, ≥35 mm descending, or ≥30 mm abdominal), random aneurysm-free male controls, and all women (only included during the DANCAVAS I pilot study) were tested for the JAK2V617F sequence variation. RESULTS: A total of 8056 individuals (90.9% men, mean age 68±4 years) were tested for the JAK2V617F sequence variation, which presented an overall prevalence of 7.1%. Ascending, descending, and abdominal aneurysm prevalences were 6.6%, 2.9%, and 6.8%, respectively. In JAK2V617F-negative participants (n=7486), JAK2V617F-positive participants with VAF <1% (n=491), and JAK2V617F-positive participants with VAF ≥1% (n=79), ascending aortic aneurysms were observed in 6.4%, 9.0%, and 16.5%, respectively (P<0.001). No significant differences were observed across sequence variation groups for descending and abdominal aneurysms. Among JAK2V617F-positive individuals, the median VAF was higher in those with ascending aneurysm (9.5%; interquartile range, 3.0–40.0) than in controls (4.4%; interquartile range, 1.8–20.0; P=0.021). Ascending aortic diameter correlated modestly with VAF (Spearman ρ=0.10; P=0.026). No significant correlations were observed for descending or abdominal diameters. For ascending aneurysms, JAK2V617F VAF <1% and ≥1% presented adjusted odds ratios of 1.4 (95% CI, 1.01–2.0; P=0.045) and 2.7 (95% CI, 1.5–5.1; P=0.002), respectively, compared with JAK2V617F-negative controls. For each doubling in VAF, the risk for ascending aneurysm increased by 11% (Padjusted=0.013). The JAK2V617F sequence variation was not significantly associated with descending or abdominal aneurysms after adjusting for covariates and using these VAF thresholds. CONCLUSIONS: In a study population of primarily men 60 to 74 years of age, the somatic JAK2V617F sequence variation was strongly and independently associated with ascending aortic aneurysms, presenting a positive correlation between aneurysm size and JAK2V617F VAF. No convincing associations were observed for descending or abdominal aneurysms. Screening patients with larger ascending aortic aneurysms for the JAK2V617F sequence variation, and vice versa, screening JAK2V617Fpositve individuals presenting higher VAFs for ascending aneurysms, may be clinically appropriate.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Obel, Lasse M.","Skovbo, Joachim S.","Diederichsen, Axel C.P.","Thomassen, Mads","Kjær, Lasse","Larsen, Morten Kranker","Knudsen, Trine A.","Skov, Vibe","Kruse, Torben A.","Burton, Mark","Dembic, Maja","Wienecke, Troels","Sabater-Lleal, Maria","Gerke, Oke","Bruun, Niels Eske","Ellervik, Christina","Brabrand, Mette","Steffensen, Flemming H.","Frost, Lars","Lambrechtsen, Jess","Busk, Martin","Urbonaviciene, Grazina","Egstrup, Kenneth","Karon, Marek","Feddersen, Søren","Rasmussen, Lars M.","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Lindholt, Jes S."],"cuid":["S02-086.84-822954"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Obel, Lasse M."],"country":["Spain","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston Children's Hospital","Harvard Medical School","Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Sant Pau Biomedical Research Institute","Spanish Network on Rare Diseases (CIBERER)"],"keyword":["Aorta Thoracic","Aortic aneurysm","Clonal hematopoiesis","Mass Screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aortic aneurysm risk and the somatic i jak000000000002 sup v000000000617f sup i mutation insights from a multicenter population based cardiovascular screening study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105007507930","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.84-822954","identifier":[{"id":"105007507930","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40464064","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5777108b-e0ee-4955-a35c-b03aaa23b382","sdu-f0d74c79-e052-4ab6-8dfd-95003bc3c066"],"keyword":["aorta, thoracic","aortic aneurysm","clonal hematopoiesis","mass screening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16677807BA4B57E29D9741BFC00794B3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiac, thoracic, and Vascular surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of