"Jespersen, Astrid Pernille","orcid":"0000-0002-7583-1701","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"scheibyeknudsenmortenpau","last":"Scheibye-Knudsen","locid":"161fd11a-45bf-427a-8307-f111b06510bb","name":"Scheibye-Knudsen, Morten","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Marie","key":"beckannemariepau","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Anne Marie","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13973290"],"newspaper":"Dagens Medicin","status":"p","title":"Dagens Medicin"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f8972099-9a85-43cc-be68-4090011c55fe"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Vi har brug for en national strategi for forskning i skrøbelige, ældre patienter","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820491","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Cardiac troponin (cTn) levels exceeding the 99th percentile upper reference limit and a rise/fall pattern are key for diagnosing myocardial injury and infarction. Macrotroponins, formed by patient anti-cTn antibodies targeting cTn, can cause persistently elevated cTn levels without ongoing myocardial injury. The frequency and impact of macrotroponin interference on cTn 99th percentiles are unclear. This study compares sex-specific 99th percentiles for 2 cTn assays, before and after excluding macrotroponin-positive samples, focusing on the top 10% of cTn levels.Methods We examined 1058 plasma samples from healthy individuals previously used for Danish cTn 99th percentiles. Following International Federation of Clinical Chemistry and Laboratory Medicine educational recommendations, macrotroponin presence was assessed in the top 10% cTn samples using immunoglobulin G (IgG) depletion screening and a reference sucrose gradient, confirming macrotroponin when both methods concurred. Due to analytical dilution constraints, [the highest] 88 of 135 Siemens Atellica high-sensitivity cTnI (hs-cTnI) samples were analyzed with both methods. All 106 Roche hs-cTnT samples were negative using IgG depletion, and sucrose analysis was limited to the highest 70 samples.Results Macrotroponin was found in 76% (67/88) of Siemens samples but in none of the Roche samples (0/70). Excluding macrotroponin-affected samples lowered the Siemens 99th percentiles from 117 ng/L to 22 ng/L in men and from 37 ng/L to 9 ng/L in women. The 99th/50th percentile ratio for Siemens decreased from 12- to 29-fold to 3- to 7-fold, approaching the Roche ratios.Conclusions Macrotroponin significantly influenced the Siemens Atellica hs-cTnI 99th percentiles, suggesting important clinical implications that warrant further prospective studies. The 99th/50th percentile ratio may help evaluate macrotroponin interference in troponin assays.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Strandkjær, Nina","Hansen, Morten Bagge","Afzal, Shoaib","Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Knudsen, Sophie Sander","Kristensen, Jonas Henrik","Kronborg, Alexander Holst","Kamstrup, Pia R.","Kobylecki, Camilla Jannie","Hilsted, Linda Maria","Dahl, Morten","Overgaard, Martin","Banerjee, Aditi","Ladefoged, Søren Andreas","Bundgaard, Henning","Jaffe, Allan S.","Iversen, Kasper","Hammarsten, Ola"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-823036"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Strandkjær, Nina"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mayo Clinic","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Clearance","Interference"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of macrotroponin on the 000000000099th percentile threshold in 000000000002 high sensitivity cardiac troponin assays","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105012448553","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-823036","identifier":[{"id":"001504931500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"105012448553","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40492538","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c43496bb-73f7-4c02-9d21-4bb5255acd46","sdu-a3463c7a-53c8-45d7-91dc-22957c259e6d"],"keyword":["Clearance","Interference"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5EC8F72643812BE8B4F0E75BB980C96"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2