":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-Term Natural Hydroxyapatite and Synthetic Collagen Hydroxyapatite Enhance Bone Regeneration and Implant Fixation Similar to Allograft in a Sheep Model of Implant Integration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.91-785426","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Research focusing on health care in end-of-life among cancer patients with mental disorders is limited and presents inconsistent findings. Aim: To investigate disparities in health care in end-of-life among patients who died from lung cancer according to pre-existing mental disorders. Design: A Danish nationwide cohort study linking nationwide registries on health care in end-of-life including specialist palliative care (including hospice admissions), ‘drug reimbursement for terminal illness’, high-intensity-treatment during the last 30 days before death and death at hospital, analysed using Poisson regression, adjusted for sociodemographic and clinical factors. Setting/participants: All adult decedents who died of lung cancer in Denmark from 2011 through 2020, including individuals with mental diagnoses prior to their cancer diagnosis. Results: Among 36,323 patients dying from lung cancer, 12% had pre-existing mental disorders. Patients with mental disorders were less likely to receive specialist palliative care (adjusted risk ratio (RR) 0.90; 95% CI: 0.87; 0.94), hospice admissions (RR: 0.86; 95% CI: 0.80; 0.94), chemotherapy (RR: 0.66; 95% CI: 0.57; 0.76), radiotherapy (RR: 0.82; 95% CI: 0.74; 0.92), surgery (RR: 0.47; 95% CI: 0.22; 1.00), hospital admissions (RR: 0.96; 95% CI: 0.92; 0.99) and to die in a hospital (RR: 0.88; 95% CI: 0.85; 0.91), compared to patients without mental disorders. No disparities were observed in receiving drug reimbursement, admissions to intensive care units or emergency care. Conclusion: Pre-existing mental disorders were associated with a lower probability of specialist palliative care, but also some high-intensity-treatments in end-of-life. These patients may be deprived of optimal palliative care but also appeared less subjected to possible overtreatment in end-of-life compared to patients without mental disorders.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Videbech, Nina Marie","Valentin, Jan Brink","Knudsen, Søren Valgreen","Vestergaard, Anne Høy Seeman","Vestergaard, Mogens","Rasmussen, Torben Riis","Tipsmark, Line Stjernholm","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Neergaard, Mette Asbjørn","Simoni, Amalie Helme"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813290"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Simoni, Amalie Helme"],"keyword":["Health inequities","Mental Disorders","Neoplasms","Palliative care","Terminal Care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["The Danish Health Technology Council"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disparity in health care in end of life among patients with lung cancer and pre existing mental disorders a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790940053/Accepteret_manuskript_Videbech_et_al_2025_Disparity_in_health_care_in_end-of-life_among_patients_with_lung_cancer_and_pre-existing_mental_disorders.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-813290","identifier":[{"id":"40515566","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105008183581","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0d173f20-3fb8-4fe8-a414-9c0da6662962","au-2afbe9fe-7ef1-4672-8f66-b4fcddf9aaa6"],"keyword":["Neoplasms","health inequities","mental disorders","palliative care","terminal care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30842E967189EAE2B2D9850B95F9800B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790940053/Accepteret_manuskript_Videbech_et_al_2025_Disparity_in_health_care_in_end-of-life_among_patients_with_lung_cancer_and_pre-existing_mental_disorders.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - DCPT - Danish Center for Particle Therapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The Danish Health Technology Council"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina Marie","key":"videbechninamariepau","last":"Videbech","locid":"99f20a86-8ec4-46ef-8de7-3833efb7b428","name":"Videbech, Nina Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Brink","key":"valentinjanbrinkpau","last":"Valentin","locid":"4fbcfaf7-a4af-46c9-b3b4-f113b45baf05","name":"Valentin, Jan Brink","orcid":"0000-0002-8205-7179","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Valgreen","key":"knudsensørenvalgreenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"d59094b5-44a6-4398-9acf-f3f530e0504b","name":"Knudsen, Søren Valgreen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Høy Seeman","key":"vestergaardannepau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"ff72e4f7-bbaf-406d-806e-ca9381da2760","name":"Vestergaard, Anne","name_org":"Vestergaard, Anne Høy Seeman","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"vestergaardmogenspau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"6f9d0f7c-8587-4e27-9c4c-d0decead7e3f","name":"Vestergaard, Mogens","orcid":"0009-0001-2937-4167","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Riis","key":"rasmussentorbenriispau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"311942d4-5b0f-4c92-879f-8d32a246ebf6","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7030-9260","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Stjernholm","key":"tipsmarklinestjernholmpau","last":"Tipsmark","name":"Tipsmark, Line Stjernholm","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Paaske","key":"johnsensørenpaaskepau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"c3e8b374-a343-484a-a10d-e6550efbb8dc","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","orcid":"0000-0002-2787-0271","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Asbjørn","key":"neergaardmetteasbjørnpau","last":"Neergaard","locid":"6000615c-dc69-42c8-b127-bf560482486b","name":"Neergaard, Mette Asbjørn","orcid":"0000-0003-3309-5838","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie Helme","key":"simoniamaliehelmepau","last":"Simoni","locid":"59640d1e-83fa-4723-9bf8-5e8f24e78053","name":"Simoni, Amalie Helme","orcid":"0000-0002-3327-8418","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40515566"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/02692163251344133","issn":["02692163","1477030X"],"issn_org":["02692163"],"issue":"7","journal":"Palliative Medicine","pages":"803-813","paperid":"02692163251344133","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Palliative Medicine","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008183581"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0d173f20-3fb8-4fe8-a414-9c0da6662962","au-2afbe9fe-7ef1-4672-8f66-b4fcddf9aaa6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Disparity in health care in end-of-life among patients with lung cancer and pre-existing mental disorders : A nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-813290","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Brain serotonin 4 receptor (5-HT4R) levels are lower in untreated patients with major depressive disorder (MDD) and are linked to verbal memory. Here, we investigated the relationship between 5-HT4R levels, clinical outcomes, and cognitive function in patients with MDD who initiated selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor drug treatment. Methods: Ninety patients with moderate to severe depression underwent molecular brain imaging to measure 5-HT4R binding prior to antidepressant treatment with escitalopram. Pretreatment 5-HT4R binding was assessed for its ability to predict treatment outcome at weeks 4, 8, or 12. In 40 patients who were rescanned 8 weeks posttreatment, change in cerebral 5-HT4R binding was correlated with change in verbal memory and with change in depressive symptoms, as evaluated by the 6-item Hamilton Depression Rating Scale. Results: After 8 weeks of serotonergic intervention, neostriatal 5-HT4R binding was reduced by 9%. Global change in 5-HT4R binding from baseline was associated with verbal memory outcomes, but not with overall clinical depressive symptom outcomes. Pretreatment 5-HT4R binding did not predict clinical recovery status at week 8 and was not associated with change in the 6-item Hamilton Depression Rating Scale scores. Conclusions: In patients with moderate to severe MDD, treatment with selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors downregulated neostriatal 5-HT4R levels, which is consistent with the notion that the drugs increase cerebral extracellular serotonin. The less global brain 5-HT4R levels were downregulated after selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, the more verbal memory improved, highlighting the potential importance of 5-HT4R as a treatment target in MDD. The findings offer insights into mechanisms that underlie antidepressant effects and point to new directions for precision medicine treatments for MDD.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Dam, Vibeke H.","Köhler-Forsberg, Kristin","Ozenne, Brice","Larsen, Søren V.","Ip, Cheng Teng","Jorgensen, Anders","Stenbæk, Dea Siggaard","Madsen, Jacob","Svarer, Claus","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","Knudsen, Gitte Moos","Frokjaer, Vibe G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790121"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Macao"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Macau"],"keyword":["Antidepressant treatment","Cognition","Depression","Positron emission tomography PET","Serotonin 4 receptor","Verbal memory"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of antidepressant treatment on 000000000005 ht sub 000000000004 sub receptor binding and associations with clinical outcomes and verbal memory in major depressive disorder","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-790121","identifier":[{"id":"85207716388","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39181386","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-367f7c36-a838-44eb-a626-9f4f641954cd"],"keyword":["Antidepressant treatment","Cognition","Depression","Positron emission tomography (PET)","Serotonin 4 receptor","Verbal memory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2056C95648D597DD7D615EE2FAAEECB0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"mo","key":"university of macau","loc":["Macao","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Macau","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Vibeke H.","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"b1207668-d50d-49fa-9556-cfc4ca38c91e","name":"Dam, Vibeke H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Kristin","key":"köhlerforsbergpau","last":"Köhler-Forsberg","locid":"f707478e-675b-4d0f-a0ff-fdff5e3ffec8","name":"Köhler-Forsberg, Kristin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Brice","key":"ozennepau","last":"Ozenne","locid":"52e17fb0-a702-4384-bb59-a3a09619877c","name":"Ozenne, Brice","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Søren V.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15f7f99a-0254-46d1-a47d-c8d6628f04b1","name":"Larsen, Søren V.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"Cheng Teng","key":"ippau","last":"Ip","locid":"6ad86471-9e4f-4bb6-8af2-1317d90b1271","name":"Ip, Cheng Teng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"46015f76-041c-4177-aa3a-8bcfd13eda19","name":"Jorgensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-6012-6965","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Dea S.","key":"stenbækpau","last":"Stenbæk","locid":"cbc45555-3350-4362-8b59-29f8ca64d575","name":"Stenbæk, Dea Siggaard","name_org":"Stenbæk, Dea S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Jacob","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Claus","key":"svarerpau","last":"Svarer","name":"Svarer, Claus","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Martin B.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"dfc70acd-d15d-44f9-891e-6a7646d1727d","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","name_org":"Jørgensen, Martin B.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Gitte M.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f02aee9e-69cf-491a-9765-ff062f734db8","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Moos","name_org":"Knudsen, Gitte M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1508-6866","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Vibe G.","key":"frokjaerpau","last":"Frokjaer","locid":"ab1287b2-e920-4656-b4bc-1b7d3dffd2dc","name":"Frokjaer, Vibe G.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39181386"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biopsych.2024.08.009","issn":["00063223","18732402"],"issn_org":["00063223"],"issue":"3","journal":"Biological Psychiatry","pages":"261-268","status":"p","title":"Biological Psychiatry","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207716388"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-367f7c36-a838-44eb-a626-9f4f641954cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of Antidepressant Treatment on 5-HT<sub>4</sub> Receptor Binding and Associations With Clinical Outcomes and Verbal Memory in Major Depressive Disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-790121","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"People with HIV (PWH) have a high risk of coronary artery disease (CAD). Cytomegalovirus (CMV) co-infection is very common in PWH, but little is known about its association with CAD. We aimed to investigate if CMV IgG serostatus and concentrations are associated with CAD in PWH. From the Copenhagen Comorbidity in HIV Infection (COCOMO) Study we included PWH with coronary CT angiography (CCTA) and quantitative CMV IgG concentration measurements. We measured the stenosis grades and plaque volumes in the coronary vessels. Using multivariable regressions adjusted for traditional CAD risk factors, we investigated if CMV IgG serostatus and concentrations were associated with any atherosclerosis, obstructive CAD, or plaque volumes. We included 620 PWH of whom 586 had positive CMV serostatus, which was not associated with any atherosclerosis, obstructive CAD, or plaque volumes. A doubling of CMV IgG concentrations was associated with any atherosclerosis (OR 1.21 [95% CI: 1.06–1.39]), obstructive CAD (OR 1.31 [95% CI: 1.07–1.59]), and higher total plaque volume (1.56 [95% CI: 1.21–2.01] fold increase), but the association did not remain significant after adjustment for traditional CAD risk factors. This indicates that CMV IgG serostatus and concentrations are not independently associated with prevalent CAD in PWH.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Suarez-Zdunek, Moises Alberto","Knudsen, Andreas Dehlbæk","Fuchs, Andreas","Kirkby, Nikolai Søren","Benfield, Thomas","Gerstoft, Jan","Trøseid, Marius","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Køber, Lars","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800386"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo University Hospital","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Coronary artery disease","Cytomegalovirus","HIV"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cytomegalovirus antibodies and coronary artery disease in people with hiv a cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v17020231","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-800386","identifier":[{"id":"40006986","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85219001045","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11860406","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ba324f63-f474-4432-b8f4-b1c5b371b0a7"],"keyword":["HIV","coronary artery disease","cytomegalovirus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-09E513FCFD06C5F9E97717D11DA626E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v17020231","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/431514835/viruses_17_00231.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, 