{"abstract":"Purpose: Netupitant 300 mg/palonosetron 0.5 mg (NEPA) would be ideal as antiemetic prophylaxis for patients receiving weekly cisplatin, as it would reduce concurrent medication intake compared to the 3-day aprepitant regimen. However, due to the longer half-life of netupitant (~ 88 h), weekly administration could potentially lead to accumulation and toxicity. This study aims to investigate the safety and antiemetic efficacy of weekly administration of NEPA plus dexamethasone (DEX) in patients treated for cervical cancer with radiotherapy and weekly cisplatin 40 mg/m2. Methods: This single-arm, open-label, phase II study evaluated patients with cervical cancer receiving NEPA and DEX before weekly cisplatin and concomitant radiotherapy for up to 5 weeks. Safety was assessed during weekly adverse event (AE) assessments. Efficacy was evaluated using Patient Diaries reporting daily nausea, vomiting, and use of rescue medication during the study period. Results: Between October 8, 2018, and January 2, 2024, 73 patients were recruited from two Danish departments of oncology; 37 completed all five weekly cycles. The majority of AEs were of mild or moderate intensity, with fatigue being the most frequently observed (95% of patients). Seven (10%) patients encountered ≥ 1 grade 3 treatment-related AEs (TRAEs). No grade 4 TRAEs or deaths were observed. In terms of efficacy, no vomiting and no nausea days 1–35 were 86% and 18%, respectively. Mean time to first emetic episode was 9 days. Conclusion: Weekly NEPA administration was safe, well-tolerated, and highly effective during concomitant radiotherapy and weekly cisplatin. Trial registration: This trial is registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT03668639-2018–09-10).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Detlefsen, Sofie S.","Andersen, Ditte S.","Ør Knudsen, Anja","Nøttrup, Trine J.","Möller, Sören","Nyvang, Gitte Bettina","Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","Herrstedt, Jørn","Ruhlmann, Christina H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821711"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ruhlmann, Christina H."],"keyword":["Nausea","Nepa","Palonosetron","Vomiting"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety and antiemetic efficacy of weekly administration of netupitant palonosetron plus dexamethasone during 000000000005 weeks of concomitant chemo radiotherapy the danger emesis study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-025-09573-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-821711","identifier":[{"id":"105006837508","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40437122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12119652","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-d19ecc78-5a27-49fb-8a03-49b2fe7aa937"],"keyword":["Concomitant chemoradiotherapy","NEPA","Nausea","Netupitant","Palonosetron","Vomiting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D838DC56B61502B104597EF2A6C1F474"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/291086979/s00520-025-09573-9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-025-09573-9","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie S.","key":"detlefsenpau","last":"Detlefsen","locid":"04189512-1a45-4e92-a76e-8c014ba268f4","name":"Detlefsen, Sofie S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte S.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ditte S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"093d1ee6-e574-4e28-92e3-833d7577be91","name":"Ør Knudsen, Anja","name_org