":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782311","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Madkundskab som valgfag er stadig et forholdvis nyt fag, og kun en enkelt årgang har gennemført afgangsprøven i faget. Mange lærere er derfor i fuld gang med at finde de gode rutiner og prøvepraksisser på området Vi har inviteret CFU Absalons konsulent i faget madkundskab, Marie Kjær Christiansen, i studiet til en samtale om faget og prøven. Det kommer både til at handle om fjer, fagsprog og (prøve)fiduser.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christiansen, Marie Kjær","Westergaard, Mette Bechmann","Pedersen, Maria Ulrik","Knudsen, Søren Bøgh","Hjuler, Kristian Neubert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782351"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"valgfaget i madkundskab m marie kjær christiansen 000000000032 praksis","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/32-valgfaget-i-madkundskab-m-marie-kj%C3%A6r-christiansen/id1553652931?i=1000640293364","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782351","ids":["pha-c2952e99-e6db-4410-946a-5f4a3c4f378a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-376EA7741A2EF70798134023DCC60CB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/32-valgfaget-i-madkundskab-m-marie-kj%C3%A6r-christiansen/id1553652931?i=1000640293364","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Center for Skole og Læring - Vordingborg"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Kjær","key":"christiansenoth","last":"Christiansen","locid":"145741a1-7033-4606-a259-cbedb47eba01","name":"Christiansen, Marie Kjær","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Bechmann","key":"westergaardoth","last":"Westergaard","locid":"bcad039f-582e-4bb9-8723-48ddfd3053d1","name":"Westergaard, Mette Bechmann","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Ulrik","key":"pedersenoth","last":"Pedersen","locid":"cabf4f02-911f-4b48-98c0-483024f4b46a","name":"Pedersen, Maria Ulrik","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Bøgh","key":"knudsenoth","last":"Knudsen","locid":"9db853d4-3f32-4055-9ca5-065fa96c5ed1","name":"Knudsen, Søren Bøgh","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Neubert","key":"hjuleroth","last":"Hjuler","locid":"f289fdc8-09e3-499a-8fd4-295fea8d7f21","name":"Hjuler, Kristian Neubert","orcid":"0009-0002-4213-2151","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Professionshøjskolen Absalon","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-c2952e99-e6db-4410-946a-5f4a3c4f378a"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Valgfaget i madkundskab m. Marie Kjær Christiansen : 32: Praksis","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782351","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we introduce the experimental prototype MoSS (Modular Smart Speaker). MoSS is a modular speech synthesis smart speaker system, and a feature-rich and capable platform that resembles and functions as an intelligent smart speaker, while featuring extended functions for advanced audio processing. MoSS is composed byanumberofsoftwareandhardwarecomponents, allowing people to customize, modify and modulate its synthetic voice in real-time. Through playfully combining the different tools and parameters, MoSS facilitates an investigation of human/machine interaction with voice controlled smart home objects, with a focus on the exploration of sound and voice synthesis. We present the process leading the creation of MoSS, how it works and the preliminary results from using the device to inspire novel vocal imaginaries in synthetic voice design.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lyngsø Knudsen, Søren","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S02-086.98-822873"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Smart Speakers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"moss unfolding playful imaginaries of synthetic voice design through a modular smart speaker","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665428","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.98-822873","identifier":[{"id":"85198906620","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69e87e34-8f72-4699-b684-22c0dcaa5a29","ku-95bd98f4-19df-496b-9dca-e0634e6476b4"],"keyword":["Exploratory Prototyping","Modular Synthesizers","Smart Speakers","Synthetic Voice Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AD14EE220BCF9D0CFD39227B75F7F781"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665428","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108403558/MoSSDIS2024Compantion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Arts and Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lyngsøknudsenpau","last":"Lyngsø Knudsen","name":"Lyngsø Knudsen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Lyngsø","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren Lyngsø","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","orcid":"0000-0001-6275-8966","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3665428","pages":"342-346","status":"p","title":"Companion Publication of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference (DIS '24 Companion)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198906620"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69e87e34-8f72-4699-b684-22c0dcaa5a29","ku-95bd98f4-19df-496b-9dca-e0634e6476b4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MoSS: Unfolding Playful Imaginaries of Synthetic Voice Design through a Modular Smart Speaker","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.98-822873","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cardiac troponins are the preferred biomarkers for the diagnosis of acute myocardial infarction. Although sex-specific 99th percentile thresholds of troponins are recommended in international guidelines, the clinical effect of their use is poorly investigated. The DANSPOT Study (The Danish Study of Sex- and Population-Specific 99th percentile upper reference limits of Troponin) aims to evaluate the clinical effect of a prospective implementation of population- and sex-specific diagnostic thresholds of troponins into clinical practice. METHODS: This study is a nationwide, multicenter, stepped-wedge cluster-randomized trial of the implementation of population- and sex-specific thresholds of troponins in 22 of 23 clinical centers in Denmark. We established sex-specific thresholds for 5 different troponin assays based on troponin levels in a healthy Danish reference population. Centers will sequentially cross over from current uniform manufacturer-derived thresholds to the new population- and sex-specific thresholds. The primary cohort is defined as patients with symptoms suggestive of acute coronary syndrome having at least 1 troponin measurement performed within 24 hours of arrival with a peak troponin value between the current uniform threshold and the new sex-specific female and male thresholds. The study will compare the occurrence of the primary outcome, defined as a composite of nonfatal myocardial infarction, unplanned revascularization, and all-cause mortality within 1 year, separately for men and women before and after the implementation of the new sex-specific thresholds. CONCLUSIONS: The DANSPOT Study is expected to show the clinical effects on diagnostics, treatment, and clinical outcomes in patients with myocardial infarction of implementing sex-specific diagnostic thresholds for troponin based on a national Danish reference population. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT05336435.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Strandkjær, Nina","Jørgensen, Nicoline","Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Kristensen, Jonas Henrik","Knudsen, Marie Sophie Sander","Kock, Thilde Olivia","Lange, Theis","Lindholm, Matias Greve","Bruun, Niels Eske","Holmvang, Lene","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Pedersen, Claus Kjær","Christensen, Martin Kirk","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Hilsted, Linda","Ladefoged, Søren","Nybo, Mads","Bor, Mustafa Vakur","Dahl, Morten","Hansen, Annebirthe Bo","Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","Bundgaard, Henning","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-741292"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Strandkjær, Nina"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Biomarkers","Biomarkers blood","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardial Infarction blood","Predictive Value of Tests","Prospective Studies","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Sex Factors","Troponin","Troponin blood"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danspot a multicenter stepped wedge cluster randomized trial of the reclassification of acute myocardial infarction rationale and study design","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.123.033493","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful to the participants included in our healthy reference population for their important contributions to the biobank. The study is funded in part by grants from Helsefonden (20-B-0431), Mauritzen La Fountaine Foundation, The Danish Heart Foundation (22-R156-A10257-22206), and the Independent Research Fund Denmark (2096-00157B). The study has also received support from Roche Diagnostics in terms of reagents for the Roche hs-TnT assay. The study is funded in part by grants from Helsefonden (20-B-0431), Mauritzen La Fountaine Foundation, The Danish Heart Foundation (22-R156-A10257-22206), and the Independent Research Fund Denmark (2096-00157B). The study has also received support from Roche Diagnostics in terms of reagents for the Roche hs-TnT assay."],"id":"S04-100.00-741292","identifier":[{"id":"38639348","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11179950","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85192428242","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1eec25e9-8023-402e-8a82-d7fd4cab558a","au-09f18dfd-93c4-49e1-894a-05f74171ef9d","ku-f2a93533-aaf6-4e7e-b6a7-5d5a6d751893","sdu-532ae107-f335-4609-9190-8cb9bc7207c8"],"keyword":["Biomarkers/blood","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Myocardial Infarction/blood","Predictive Value of Tests","Prospective Studies","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Troponin/blood","acute coronary syndrome","biomarkers","myocardial infarction","sex factors","troponin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-AC72D1A188B00110D5F2F2A45754FB59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/712435785/Strandkj_r_et_al._2024_._DANSPOT_A_Multicenter_Stepped-Wedge_Cluster-Randomized_Trial_of_the_Reclassification_of_Acute_Myocardial_Infarction_Rationale_and_Study_Design.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.123.033493","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findre