{"abstract":"Aim: Greenland is one of the places on Earth where the effects of climate change are most evident. The retreat of sea ice has made East Greenland more accessible for longer periods during the year. East Greenland fjords have been notoriously difficult to study due to their remoteness, dense sea ice conditions and lack of infrastructure. As a result, biological monitoring across latitudinal gradients is scarce in East Greenland and relies on sporadic research cruises and trawl data from commercial vessels. We here aim to investigate the transition in fish and marine mammal communities from South to Northeast Greenland using environmental DNA (eDNA). Location: South to Northeast Greenland. Methods: We investigated the transition in fish and marine mammal communities from South to Northeast Greenland using eDNA metabarcoding of seawater samples. We included both surface and mesopelagic samples, collected over approximately 2400 km waterway distance, by sampling from Cape Farewell to Ella Island in August 2021. Results: We demonstrate a clear transition in biological communities from south to northeast, with detected fish and mammal species matching known distributions. Samples from the southern areas were dominated by capelin (Mallotus villosus) and redfish (Sebastes), whereas northeastern samples were dominated by polar cod (Boreogadus saida), sculpins (Myoxocephalus) and ringed seal (Pusa hispida). We provide newly generated 12S rRNA barcodes from 87 fish species, bringing the public DNA database closer to full taxonomic coverage for Greenlandic fish species for this locus. Main Conclusions: Our results demonstrate that eDNA sampling can detect latitudinal shifts in marine biological communities of the Arctic region, which can supplement traditional fish surveys in understanding species distributions and community compositions of marine vertebrates. Importantly, sampling of eDNA can be a feasible approach for detecting northward range expansions in remote areas as climate change progresses.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jensen, Mads Reinholdt","Høgslund, Signe","Knudsen, Steen Wilhelm","Nielsen, Julius","Møller, Peter Rask","Rysgaard, Søren","Thomsen, Philip Francis"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018455"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Mads Reinholdt","Thomsen, Philip Francis"],"country":["Canada","Greenland","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Norwegian Institute for Water Research","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","University of Manitoba","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"keyword":["Biomonitoring","Climate change","Fish diversity","Fjord systems","Latitudinal gradient","Polar regions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["NIVA Denmark Water Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distinct latitudinal community patterns of arctic marine vertebrates along the east greenlandic coast detected by environmental dna","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ddi.13665","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018455","identifier":[{"id":"85144408575","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4f62e3e2-7d07-417e-b6bd-7c29f6a8c9e5","ku-0de1f72c-e21e-4bd9-a51e-9709a3923db1"],"keyword":["biomonitoring","climate change","fish diversity","fjord systems","latitudinal gradient","polar regions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8AA5A236DF2D4296F3FFA9628BFA20B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/335416639/Diversity_and_Distributions_2022_Jensen_Distinct_latitudinal_community_patterns_of_Arctic_marine_vertebrates_along.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ddi.13665","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Genetics, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["NIVA Denmark Water Research"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute for water research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute for Water Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"university of tromsø the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ca","key":"university of manitoba","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Manitoba","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Reinholdt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"edafc120-cec0-41cd-b556-c4726954065e","name":"Jensen, Mads Reinholdt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"høgslundpau","last":"Høgslund","locid":"a16b561b-3a9e-45a8-b2df-b298312e4ab1","name":"Høgslund, Signe","orcid":"0000-0001-5926-8464","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","first":"Steen Wilhelm","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"097de8b0-2ba2-4859-8188-156b11558f0a","name":"Knudsen, Steen Wilhelm","orcid":"0000-0003-0428-9940","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Julius","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Julius","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","first":"Peter Rask","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"4947afc1-cc18-4c51-8250-e5a783136c03","name":"Møller, Peter Rask","orcid":"0000-0002-0177-0977","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"rysgaardpau","last":"Rysgaard","locid":"781dd219-a3b6-45e7-82c8-917c7cb6112e","name":"Rysgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-1726-2958","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Philip Francis","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"42e3d0c2-8389-45cd-aa6f-82004d696ccb","name":"Thomsen, Philip Francis","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ddi.13665","issn":["13669516","14724642"],"issn_org":["13669516"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diversity and Distributions","pages":"316-334","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Diversity and Distributions","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144408575"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4f62e3e2-7d07-417e-b6bd-7c29f6a8c9e5","ku-0de1f72c-e21e-4bd9-a51e-9709a3923db1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Distinct latitudinal community patterns of Arctic marine vertebrates along the East Greenlandic coast detected by environmental DNA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-018455","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Chokeberries (Aronia spp.) are known to exhibit both direct and indirect antioxidant properties and have been associated with beneficial effects on human health, including cardiovascular risk factors (inflammation, serum lipids, sugars, blood pressure), oxidative stress, and semen quality. This prospective, double-blinded, randomized, crossover clinical trial was conducted to elucidate the effects of Aronia supplementation on these health targets in mildly hypercholesterolemic men. Methods: The standardized Aronia supplementation comprised three wild Aronia spp. (A. arbutifolia, A prunifolia and A. melanocarpa) and the Aronia hybrid × Sorbaronia mitschurinii (standardized to 150 mg anthocyanins daily). Participants (n = 109) were healthy men with respect to all outcome targets except for the total cholesterol level (5.0–7.0 mM). Participants were randomized to supplementation with either Aronia or placebo for 90 days, followed by a wash-out period and lastly the complementary supplementation. Effects on the health parameters were compared among both the whole group of men and in subgroups according to age, body mass index (BMI), lifestyle, dietary habits, and serum glutathione levels at baseline. The study is registered in ClinicalTrials.gov.: NCT03405753. Results: Glutathione levels were significantly improved after 90 days intake of Aronia supplementation compared to placebo in the subgroup of men with a low level of glutathione at baseline (p = 0.038) and a high coffee intake (p = 0.045). A significant decrease in levels of sperm DNA fragmentation and an increase in the percentage of motile sperm were observed in men aged >40 and in men with BMI > 25. Further, these parameters were significantly improved in the dietary subgroup defined by a high level of coffee intake. Total cholesterol and low-density lipoprotein-cholesterol levels decreased significantly in men <40 years after Aronia supplementation. No statistically significant effects were observed regarding blood pressure, markers of blood sugar regulation, hemoglobin A1c, superoxide dismutase, catalase, isoprostane levels, high sensitivity C reactive protein, or other semen parameters. Conclusions: This study demonstrated a significant increase in glutathione levels and improvement of cytoprotective targets following Aronia supplementation in specific subgroups of men >40 years of age and BMI > 25 but did not demonstrate a significant effect in the overall analysis. The observed concurrent increase in glutathione levels and improvement of cytoprotective targets following Aronia supplementation in subgroups of men, suggests that the endogenous phase II antioxidant glutathione is involved in the modulation of the observed cytoprotective effects. This study is a good foundation for further investigation of these cytoprotective effects in groups with oxidative stress in a dose–response study.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Sangild, Julie","Faldborg, Anne","Schousboe, Cecilie","Fedder, Maja D K","Christensen, Lars Porskjær","Lausdahl, Astrid K.","Arnspang, Eva C.","Gregersen, Søren","Jakobsen, Henrik Byrial","Knudsen, Ulla Breth","Fedder, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-704200"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Fedder, Jens"],"keyword":["Aronia supplementation","Cholesterol","Glutathione","Oxidative stress","crossover clinical trial","cytoprotective effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Byrial ApS, Blaesenborgvej 9, 4320 Lejre"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of chokeberries i aronia i spp on cytoprotective and cardiometabolic markers and semen quality in 000000000109 mildly hypercholesterolemic danish men a prospective double blinded randomized crossover trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm12010373","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-704200","identifier":[{"id":"36615174","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9821700","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85145896958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-828e43d7-23d6-443f-9650-7d8d9ebfb574","sdu-8e2c507c-c692-4fb2-a5eb-70c6dc1775c2"],"keyword":["Aronia supplementation","cholesterol","crossover clinical trial","cytoprotective effects","glutathione","oxidative stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9F0D1EB149C18F62E4F0078DF45E738B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm12010373","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/217212743/jcm_12_00373_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/422053344/jcm-12-00373-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Ortopædkirurgisk afdeling, Regionshospitalet Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"