{"abstract":"In this paper, we reflect on the educational challenges and research opportunities in running data visualization design activities in the context of large courses. With the increasing number and sizes of data visualization course, we need to better understand approaches to scaling our teaching efforts. We draw on experiences organizing and facilitating activities primarily based on one instance of a master’s course given to about 130 students. We provide a detailed account of the course with particular focus on the purpose, structure, and outcome of six two-hour design activities. Based on this, we reflect on three aspects of the course: First, how the course scale led us to thoroughly plan, evaluate, and revise communication between students, teaching assistants, and lecturers. Second, how we designed learning scaffolds through the design activities, and the reflections we received from students on this matter. Finally, we reflect on the diversity of the students that followed the course, the visualization exercises we used, the projects they worked on, and when to key in on simple boring problems and data sets. Thus, our paper contributes with discussions about balancing topical diversity, scaling courses to many students, and problem-based learning.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren","Bennetsen, Mathilde Bech","Høj, Terese Kimmie","Jensen, Camilla","Jørgensen, Rebecca Louise Nørskov","Loft, Christian Søe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718830"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data visualization","Design activities","Educational challenges","Large courses","Teaching scalability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reflections on designing and running visualization design and programming activities in courses with many students","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102551861/EduVis_2023b_Reflections_on_doing_visualisation_design_activities_in_large_courses_8_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718830","identifier":[{"id":"85182319350","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-17125be2-af86-4be9-b3d2-c0b243479d23"],"keyword":["Data visualization","Design activities","Educational challenges","Large courses","Teaching scalability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-94728C710F4F4060489166557DF2D05C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.08939","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102551861/EduVis_2023b_Reflections_on_doing_visualisation_design_activities_in_large_courses_8_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2575c800-642d-4984-9c56-41601cf07a26","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde Bech","key":"bennetsenpau","last":"Bennetsen","name":"Bennetsen, Mathilde Bech","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Terese Kimmie","key":"højpau","last":"Høj","name":"Høj, Terese Kimmie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Camilla","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rebecca Louise Nørskov","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Rebecca Louise Nørskov","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Søe","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","name":"Loft, Christian Søe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/eduvis60792.2023.00015","eisbn":["9798350330304"],"isbn":["9798350330311"],"pages":"55-64","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2023 IEEE VIS Workshop on Visualization Education, Literacy, and Activities (EduVis)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182319350"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-17125be2-af86-4be9-b3d2-c0b243479d23"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reflections on Designing and Running Visualization Design and Programming Activities in Courses with Many Students","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718830","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper is a call to action for research and discussion on data visualization education. As visualization evolves and spreads through our professional and personal lives, we need to understand how to support and empower a broad and diverse community of learners in visualization. Data Visualization is a diverse and dynamic discipline that combines knowledge from different fields, is tailored to suit diverse audiences and contexts, and frequently incorporates tacit knowledge. This complex nature leads to a series of interrelated challenges for data visualization education. Driven by a lack of consolidated knowledge, overview, and orientation for visualization education, the 21 authors of this paper—educators and researchers in data visualization—identify and describe 19 challenges informed by our collective practical experience. We organize these challenges around seven themes People, Goals & Assessment, Environment, Motivation, Methods, Materials , and Change . Across these themes, we formulate 43 research questions to address these challenges. As part of our call to action, we then conclude with 5 cross-cutting opportunities and respective action items: embrace DIVERSITY+INCLUSION, build COMMUNITIES, conduct RESEARCH, act AGILE, and relish RESPONSIBILITY. We aim to inspire researchers, educators and learners to drive visualization education forward and discuss why, how, who and where we educate, as we learn to use visualization to address challenges across many scales and many domains in a rapidly changing world: viseducationchallenges.github.io.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Bach, Benjamin","Keck, Mandy","Rajabiyazdi, Fateme","Losev, Tatiana","Meirelles, Isabel","Dykes, Jason","Laramee, Robert S.","AlKadi, Mashael","Stoiber, Christina","Huron, Samuel","Perin, Charles","Morais, Luiz","Aigner, Wolfgang","Kosminsky, Doris","Boucher, Magdalena","Knudsen, Søren","Manataki, Areti","Aerts, Jan","Hinrichs, Uta","Roberts, Jonathan C.","Carpendale, Sheelagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718866"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Brazil","Canada","France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bangor University","Carleton University","City, University of London","Federal University of Rio de Janeiro","Institut Polytechnique de Paris","KU Leuven","OCAD University","St. Pölten University of Applied Sciences","University of Applied Sciences Upper Austria","University of Edinburgh","University of Nottingham","University of St Andrews","University of Victoria","Vienna University of Technology"],"keyword":["Challenges","Data visualization","Education"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges and opportunities in data visualization education a call to action","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.07703","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718866","identifier":[{"id":"85175229487","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6923c60b-1cde-4d6b-8580-37965a9df780"],"keyword":["Challenges","Data Visualization","Education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-6D5A0B5C301B2E355B8E071C8E72B5F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07703","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102551946/2308.07703.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":