iversities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e40a7350-6685-44df-a843-3a4ba03e1e5c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Sjov, snyd og fejl : er det leg, når vi leger i undervisningen?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259534","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Bidraget undersøger et forskningsmæssigt underbelyst spørgsmål, nemlig hvordan leg og øvelse kan anskues som forskellige aktivitetsformer. I et forsøg på at kaste mere lys over, hvordan man kan anskue leg og øvelse som forskellige aktivitetsformer argumenterer for en ny måde at differentiere mellem leg og øvelse. Leg og øvelse adskiller sig i forhold til sociale normer: Hvor leg er kendetegnet ved, hvad jeg kalder ‘normudforskning’, er øvelse mere kendetegnet ved, hvad jeg kalder ‘normstræben’. Herudover adskiller leg og øvelse sig i forhold til opmærksomhed: Leg er kendetegnet ved såkaldt stimulusbetinget opmærksomhed, mens øvelse er kendetegnet ved såkaldt kontrolleret opmærksomhed. Jeg afrunder kapitlet ved at pege på øvelse som et vigtigt element i at få legende tilgange i pædagogiske kontekster til at lykkes, idet jeg ved hjælp af de ovenstående to differentieringer mellem leg og øvelse argumenterer for, at øvelse forøger vores evne til at lege.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Søren Hørning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-660566"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Leg","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Opmærksomhed","sociale normer","øvelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"øvelse forøger vores evne til at lege","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-660566","ids":["via-c8cf8f29-c759-487d-a14a-71b7384c6f92"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","leg","opmærksomhed","sociale normer","øvelse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-79B10B7A2F7B6BA06BFE1F33CBB53555"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Pædagogik og dannelse","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Research programme for body, physical education and movement"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Hørning","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"cf3bece2-5ccf-43a1-8383-5fc1ac86f8e4","name":"Hansen, Søren Hørning","orcid":"0000-0003-0845-8131","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne","key":"knudsenpedh","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Hanne","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Erik","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Jens Erik","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan","key":"bundgaardnielsenpedh","last":"Bundgaard Nielsen","name":"Bundgaard Nielsen, Johan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788750062752"],"pages":"249-262","place":"København","publisher":"Akademisk Forlag","status":"p","title":"Leg på spil i pædagogik og uddannelse"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-c8cf8f29-c759-487d-a14a-71b7384c6f92"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Øvelse forøger vores evne til at lege","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-660566","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Perennial grains have potential to contribute to ecological intensification of food production by enabling the direct harvest of human-edible crops without requiring annual cycles of disturbance and replanting. Studies of prototype perennial grains and other herbaceous perennials point to the ability of agroecosystems including these crops to protect water quality, enhance wildlife habitat, build soil quality, and sequester soil carbon. However, genetic improvement of perennial grain candidates has been hindered by limited investment due to uncertainty about whether the approach is viable. As efforts to develop perennial grain crops have expanded in past decades, critiques of the approach have arisen. With a recent report of perennial rice producing yields equivalent to those of annual rice over eight consecutive harvests, many theoretical concerns have been alleviated. Some valid questions remain over the timeline for new crop development, but we argue these may be mitigated by implementation of recent technological advances in crop breeding and genetics such as low-cost genotyping, genomic selection, and genome editing. With aggressive research investment in the development of new perennial grain crops, they can be developed and deployed to provide atmospheric greenhouse gas reductions.","author_count":29,"contributors":["DeHaan, Lee R.","Anderson, James A.","Bajgain, Prabin","Basche, Andrea","Cattani, Douglas J.","Crain, Jared","Crews, Timothy E.","David, Christophe","Duchene, Olivier","Gutknecht, Jessica","Hayes, Richard C.","Hu, Fengyi","Jungers, Jacob M.","Knudsen, Søren","Kong, Wenqian","Larson, Steve","Lundquist, Per Olof","Luo, Guangbin","Miller, Allison J.","Nabukalu, Pheonah","Newell, Matthew T.","Olsson, Lennart","Palmgren, Michael","Paterson, Andrew H.","Picasso, Valentin D.","Poland, Jesse A.","Sacks, Erik J.","Wang, Shuwen","Westerbergh, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684549"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_coun