":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Brazil is home to a multitude of venomous snakes, perhaps the most medically relevant of which belong to the Bothrops genus. Bothrops spp. are responsible for roughly 70% of all snakebites in Brazil, and envenomings caused by their bites can be treated with three types of antivenom: bothropic antivenom, bothro-lachetic antivenom, and bothro-crotalic antivenom. The choice to administer antivenom depends on the severity of the envenoming, while the choice of antivenom depends on availability and on how certain the treating physician is that the patient was bitten by a bothropic snake. The diagnosis of a bothropic envenoming can be made based on expert identification of a photo of the snake or based on a syndromic approach wherein the clinician examines the patient for characteristic manifestations of envenoming. This approach can be very effective but requires staff that has been trained in clinical snakebite management, which, unfortunately, far from all relevant staff has. Results: In this paper, we describe a prototype of the first lateral flow assay (LFA) capable of detecting venoms from Brazilian Bothrops spp. The monoclonal antibodies for the assay were generated using hybridoma technology and screened in sandwich enzyme-linked immunosorbent assays (ELISAs) to identify Bothrops spp. specific antibody sandwich pairs. The sandwich pairs were used to develop a prototype LFA that was able to detect venom from several different Bothrops spp. The LFA had a limit of detection (LoD) of 0.5 ng/mL in urine, when read with a commercial reader, and a visual LoD of approximately 25 ng/mL. Significance: The work presented here serves as a proof of concept of a genus-specific venom detection kit, which could support physicians in diagnosing Bothrops envenomings. Although further optimization and testing is needed before the LFA can find clinical use, such a device could aid in decentralising antivenoms in the Brazilian Amazon and help ensure optimal snakebite management for even more victims of this highly neglected disease.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Knudsen, Cecilie","Jürgensen, Jonas A.","D. Knudsen, Pelle","Oganesyan, Irina","Harrison, Julian A.","Dam, Søren Helweg","Haack, Aleksander M.","Friis, Rasmus Ulslev Wegener","Vitved, Lars","Belfakir, Selma B.","Ross, Georgina M.S.","Zenobi, Renato","Laustsen, Andreas H."],"cuid":["S02-097.99-672989"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Knudsen, Cecilie","Laustsen, Andreas H."],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich"],"keyword":["Animals","Antibodies Monoclonal therapeutic use","Bothrops","Diagnostics","Lateral flow assay","Neglected tropical diseases","Point of care","Prototype","Snakebite envenoming"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prototyping of a lateral flow assay based on monoclonal antibodies for detection of i bothrops i venoms","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aca.2023.341306","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.99-672989","identifier":[{"id":"85162087028","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37355315","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-dd638f27-e7e3-4576-99a3-94aff4c25dd1","sdu-ff008e14-ceef-42e7-a143-6b64a57297e4"],"keyword":["Animals","Antibodies, Monoclonal/therapeutic use","Antivenins/therapeutic use","Bothrops","Crotalid Venoms/therapeutic use","Diagnostics","Lateral flow assay","Neglected tropical diseases","Point-of-care","Prototype","Snake Bites/diagnosis","Snakebite envenoming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7207136D3CA3E7121E6DA7FDC18DF5A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/235803511/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/327091901/1_s2.0_S0003267023005275_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aca.2023.341306","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["VenomAid Diagnostics ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cancer and Inflammation Research Unit - InflammatInflammation Researchion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cecilie","key":"knudsenceciliepau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"cd8e6f62-a4b9-4ac4-98df-5e007d45419f","name":"Knudsen, Cecilie","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-3009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas A.","key":"jürgensenjonasapau","last":"Jürgensen","name":"Jürgensen, Jonas A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pelle","key":"dknudsenpellepau","last":"D. Knudsen","name":"D. Knudsen, Pelle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pelle D.","key":"knudsenpelledpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Pelle D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"oganesyanirinapau","last":"Oganesyan","name":"Oganesyan, Irina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian A.","key":"harrisonjulianapau","last":"Harrison","name":"Harrison, Julian A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren H.","key":"damsørenhelwegpau","last":"Dam","locid":"8b468e3a-efac-40c9-8361-ab95ed3bea2c","name":"Dam, Søren Helweg","name_org":"Dam, Søren H.","orcid":"0000-0003-0755-0016","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aleksander M.","key":"haackaleksandermpau","last":"Haack","locid":"8f12d95b-005d-43e6-b4d8-7232d4630162","name":"Haack, Aleksander M.","orcid":"0000-0002-1602-0175","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus U.W.","key":"friisrasmusulslevwegenerpau","last":"Friis","locid":"1984ac37-49cf-44c5-b2b6-5371de35339f","name":"Friis, Rasmus Ulslev Wegener","name_org":"Friis, Rasmus U.W.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"vitvedlarspau","last":"Vitved","locid":"7ef72ef8-ff6f-4372-adc1-ddb53eff5859","name":"Vitved, Lars","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Selma B.","key":"belfakirselmabpau","last":"Belfakir","locid":"058501e3-d53f-4645-aa93-77eeeffeaa5f","name":"Belfakir, Selma B.","orcid":"0000-0002-0085-4845","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgina M.S.","key":"rossgeorginamspau","last":"Ross","name":"Ross, Georgina M.S.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Renato","key":"zenobirenatopau","last":"Zenobi","name":"Zenobi, Renato","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"laustsenandreashpau","last":"H. Laustsen","locid":"0e4bb465-c620-461f-9970-29bad328cf8a","name":"Laustsen, Andreas H.","name_org":"H. Laustsen, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-6918-5574","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37355315"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.aca.2023.341306","issn":["00032670","18734324"],"issn_org":["00032670"],"journal":"Analytica Chimica Acta","paperid":"341306","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Analytica Chimica Acta","volume":"1272"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162087028"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","venomaid diagnostics aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-dd638f27-e7e3-4576-99a3-94aff4c25dd1","sdu-ff008e14-ceef-42e7-a143-6b64a57297e4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prototyping of a lateral flow assay based on monoclonal antibodies for detection of <i>Bothrops</i> venoms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.99-672989","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Green methanol production, based on intermittent renewable energy sources, requires a more flexible operation mode and close integration with other sections, such as, the electrical grid and electrolysis processes. In this study, methanol synthesis and distillation processes (MSD) for pilot-scale green methanol production (corresponding to 22236 tons/year) were investigated by dynamic modeling, focusing on energy analysis and dynamic characteristics during load change (LC) operations. The dynamic simulation results with a ramp rate of 50% load / h indicated energy efficiencies of 87.7% (at full-load) and 90.2% (at half-load) for the methanol synthesis process, 86.8% (full-load) and 82.4% (half-load) for the methanol distillation process, and 77.1% (full-load) and 75.4% (half-load) for the MSD process. Relatively small fluctuations were achieved with a ramp time of 1 h for the LC operations. Based on the constructed dynamic model, a surrogate modeling for the MSD process was conducted using the nonlinear autoregressive exogenous model (NARX) model, which exhibited good accuracy with the evaluated performance for the testing data of the root-mean-square error (RMSE) = 3.09 × 10-5, mean absolute error (MAE) = 2.30 × 10-4, and R2 = 1.0. The constructed NARX model can be further integrated with models for other sections of the power-to-methanol process.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Nielsen, Mads Pagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054451"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CO2 hydrogenation","Dynamic simulation","Methanol distillation","Methanol synthesis","Nonlinear autoregressive exogenous model","Power to methanol"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy analysis and surrogate modeling for the green methanol production under dynamic operating conditions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2021.121924","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054451","identifier":[{"id":"85114762053","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0f13d3f6-352d-49eb-a0dc-167ce2fa96f3"],"keyword":["CO2 hydrogenation","Dynamic simulation","Methanol distillation","Methanol synthesis","Nonlinear autoregressive exogenous model","Power-to-methanol"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-07D7D2E266C16849AC0430418DD8B5C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/459282897/Support_information.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2021.121924","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/444439566/Energy_analysis_and_surrogate_modeling_for_the_green_methanol_production.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electro Fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["REintegrate ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuel.2021.121924","issn":["00162361","18737153"],"issn_org":["00162361"],"journal":"Fuel","paperid":"121924","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel","volume":"307"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114762053"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","reintegrate aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0f13d3f6-352d-49eb-a0dc-167ce2fa96f3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Energy analysis and surrogate modeling for the green methanol production under dynamic operating conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054451","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A pseudo-homogeneous model for the methanol steam reforming process was developed based on reaction kinetics over a CuO/ZnO/Al2O3 catalyst and non-adiabatic heat and mass transfer performances in a co-current packed-bed reactor. A Thiele modulus method and an intraparticle distribution method were applied for predicting the effectiveness factors for main reactions and providing insights into the diffusion-reaction process in a cylindrical catalyst pellet. The results of both methods are validated and show good agreements with the experimental data, but the intraparticle distribution method provides better predictions. Results indicate that increases in catalyst size and bulk fluid temperature amplify the impact of intraparticle diffusion limitations, showing a decrease in effectiveness factors. To satisfy the requirements of a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell stack, the optimized operating conditions, which bring the methanol and CO concentrations to less than 1% vol in the reformate stream, are determined based on the simulation results.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhu, Jimin","Araya, Samuel Simon","Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107000"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Zhu, Jimin"],"keyword":["Effectiveness factor","Hydrogen production","Methanol steam reforming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of effectiveness factor on the modeling of methanol steam reforming over cuo zno al000000000002o000000000003 catalyst in a multi tubular reactor","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2021.12.223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107000","identifier":[{"id":"85122917271","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c4405785-c11a-49a4-94fe-1454e0fbb4bb"],"keyword":["Effectiveness factor","Hydrogen production","Intraparticle diffusion","Methanol steam reforming","Thiele modulus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-003B03DCD2FA046DB9ACFF43579DED00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/459199180/The_role_of_effectiveness_factor_on_the_modeling_of_methanol_steam_reforming_over_CuOZnOAl2O3_catalyst_in_a_multi_tubular_reactor.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2021.12.223","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fuel Cell Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jimin","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"646bbb27-0236-46fb-9e23-beb875af834f","name":"Zhu, Jimin","orcid":"0000-0001-7889-4233","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2021.12.223","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"14","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"8700-8715","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122917271"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","13. Climate Action","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c4405785-c11a-49a4-94fe-1454e0fbb4bb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The role of effectiveness factor on the modeling of methanol steam reforming over CuO/ZnO/Al2O3 catalyst in a multi-tubular reactor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107000","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A liquid chromatography–mass spectrometry method based on multiple reaction monitoring (MRM) was developed for the simultaneous quantification of markers representing two potentially competing pathways, the Maillard reaction and the dehydroalanine pathway. The two pathways involve the same residues in the proteins to some extent, namely, the essential amino acid lysine, as well as free-amino terminals available on proteins and polypeptides, competition between the two pathways in food systems may occur. The developed method comprises the following markers of the Maillard reaction: furosine, N-ε-(carboxyethyl)lysine (CEL) and N-ε-(carboxymethyl)lysine (CML), together with the dehydroalanine reaction pathway markers; lanthionine (LAN) and lysinoalanine (LAL), as well as lysine itself. The validated method was then used for the absolute quantification of heat-induced protein modifications in model systems of micellar casein and whey protein isolates (MCI and WPI, respectively) in the presence or absence of lactose. As expected, the Maillard reaction markers furosine, CEL and CML increased during the applied heat treatment in the presence of lactose, whereas the dehydroalanine markers, LAN and LAL increased with heating in both MCI and WPI, both in the presence and absence of lactose, although at lower levels in the presence of lactose, confirming the competing state of the two pathways.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","Knudsen, Lotte Juul","Bækgaard, Line Thunæs","Rauh, Valentin","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263100"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Advanced glycation end products","Glycation","Milk","Multiple reaction monitoring","Processing","Protein modification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of lactose on the maillard reaction and dehydroalanine mediated protein cross linking in casein and whey","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/foods11070897","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263100","identifier":[{"id":"35406984","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85127585050","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8997915","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-ea6312ae-d885-486e-95b5-2b33964a2cd6"],"keyword":["advanced glycation end products","glycation","milk","multiple reaction monitoring","processing","protein modification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A196AE75040939C7492378A253476DA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/foods11070897","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Drud-Heydary","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"030ede5c-2e12-40c1-9d0c-543f0c5ffadf","name":"Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Juul","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7ee04b01-4825-401c-93b0-64ffaa7e3452","name":"Knudsen, Lotte Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Thunæs","key":"bækgaardpau","last":"Bækgaard","locid":"882d0ac5-af18-405e-8ec0-09e5db71abc7","name":"Bækgaard, Line Thunæs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentin","key":"rauhpau","last":"Rauh","name":"Rauh, Valentin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35406984"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/foods11070897","issn":["23048158"],"issue":"7","journal":"Foods","paperid":"897","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Foods","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127585050"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ea6312ae-d885-486e-95b5-2b33964a2cd6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Influence of Lactose on the Maillard Reaction and Dehydroalanine-Mediated Protein Cross-Linking in Casein and Whey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263100","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In the past few years, large high-resolution displays (LHRDs) have attracted considerable attention from researchers, industries, and application areas that increasingly rely on data-driven decision-making. An up-to-date survey on the use of LHRDs for interactive data visualization seems warranted to summarize how new solutions meet the characteristics and requirements of LHRDs and take advantage of their unique benefits. In this survey, we start by defining LHRDs and outlining the consequence of LHRD environments on interactive visualizations in terms of more pixels, space, users, and devices. Then, we review related literature along the four axes of visualization, interaction, evaluation studies, and applications. With these four axes, our survey provides a unique perspective and covers a broad range of aspects being relevant when developing interactive visual data analysis solutions for LHRDs. We conclude this survey by reflecting on a number of opportunities for future research to help the community take up the still open challenges of interactive visualization on LHRDs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Belkacem, Ilyasse","Tominski, Christian","Médoc, Nicolas","Knudsen, Søren","Dachselt, Raimund","Ghoniem, Mohammad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381925"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Luxembourg"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luxembourg Institute of Science and Technology","TU Dresden","University of Rostock"],"keyword":["FOS Computer and information sciences","Human Computer Interaction cs HC","I 3 3","I 3 6"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive visualization on large high resolution displays a survey","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2212.04346","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381925","ids":["itu-2cc5c2ab-1a90-45b1-b54a-d4a7f9e25ec3"],"keyword":["FOS: Computer and information sciences","Human-Computer Interaction (cs.HC)","I.3.3","I.3.6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-69E91630897B517F33A76EC4448F9360"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2212.04346","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"lu","key":"luxembourg institute of science and technology","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Luxembourg Institute of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of rostock","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rostock","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"tu dresden","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Dresden","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ilyasse","key":"belkacempau","last":"Belkacem","name":"Belkacem, Ilyasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"tominskipau","last":"Tominski","name":"Tominski, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolas","key":"médocpau","last":"Médoc","name":"Médoc, Nicolas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2575c800-642d-4984-9c56-41601cf07a26","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Raimund","key":"dachseltpau","last":"Dachselt","name":"Dachselt, Raimund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"ghoniempau","last":"Ghoniem","name":"Ghoniem, Mohammad","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2212.04346","issn":["23318422"],"series":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2cc5c2ab-1a90-45b1-b54a-d4a7f9e25ec3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive Visualization on Large High-Resolution Displays: A Survey","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381925","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Walled-off necrosis (WON) is a serious complication to necrotizing acute pancreatitis with a high morbidity and mortality. The aim of this study was to investigate the long-term changes in pancreatic function, metabolic function and body composition in patients with WON. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Observational study including patients with WON who underwent endoscopic transmural drainage and necrosectomy. Patients were prospectively evaluated at baseline, 3-6 months after discharge, and 12 months after discharge. Patients were characterized with fecal elastase, blood samples, computer tomography, dual energy X-ray absorptiometry and Lundh's test. RESULTS: The study includes 17 patients (11 men) with WON. The etiologies were gallstones (53%) alcohol intake (35%) and 12% had an unknown etiology. The body mass index (BMI) dropped during baseline and 3 months after discharge (p = .03) and increased 12 months after discharge (p = .002). Twelve months after discharge, 29% had mild exocrine insufficiency, 7% moderate insufficiency and 50% severe insufficiency based on the Lundh's test. Fecal elastase was <100 μg/g in 35% and <200 μg/g in 59% 12 months after discharge. Only, 24% required pancreatic enzyme substitution. Endocrine insufficiency developed in 24%. These patients also had exocrine insufficiency. CONCLUSIONS: A considerable proportion of patients with WON experience both endocrine and exocrine pancreatic insufficiency suggesting that long-term follow-up is needed in order to ensure adequate treatment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nøjgaard, Camilla","Werge, Mikkel","Naver, Astrid Vinsand","Wilkens Knudsen, Anne","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Møller, Søren","Gluud, Lise Lotte","Novovic, Srdan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-439268"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term changes of pancreatic function in patients with complicated walled off necrosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-439268","identifier":[{"id":"85130260062","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35546222","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4cd4392e-5193-4795-98a8-53b56c95b5bd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48C5ADB71D55AD6B7A05829D6889B088"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Gastroenterology and Hepatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla","key":"nøjgaardpau","last":"Nøjgaard","name":"Nøjgaard, Camilla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Mikkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Astrid","key":"naverpau","last":"Naver","locid":"2e28ce9b-3d17-44a6-a542-3dea04d2cd80","name":"Naver, Astrid Vinsand","name_org":"Naver, Astrid","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"wilkensknudsenpau","last":"Wilkens Knudsen","name":"Wilkens Knudsen, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicolai J","key":"weweralbrechtsenpau","last":"Wewer Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"a4bee617-45cc-4a85-a58a-817fb06a5525","name":"Møller, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise Lotte","key":"gluudpau","last":"Gluud","locid":"5f316a6f-fef0-44ac-ad8d-522731684721","name":"Gluud, Lise Lotte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Srdan","key":"novovicpau","last":"Novovic","locid":"e7b83607-f699-4ed0-88df-3347f7db66e2","name":"Novovic, Srdan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35546222"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365521.2022.2072176","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00365521"],"issue":"10","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"1257-1263","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130260062"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4cd4392e-5193-4795-98a8-53b56c95b5bd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term changes of pancreatic function in patients with complicated walled-off necrosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-439268","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorder (PTLD) in solid organ transplant recipients has a high mortality and may present early (<2 years) or late (≥2 years) posttransplantation. We investigated the clinical characteristics of early and late PTLD among kidney and liver transplant recipients. Methods: Recipients, transplanted at Rigshospitalet, with PTLD development as adults from January 2010 to August 2020, were included. Clinical characteristics, laboratory parameters, and pathology of early and late PTLD were compared. Results: Thirty-one PTLD cases were detected where 10 (32%) were early and 21 (68%) were late PTLD. EBV DNA in plasma was detected in 78% versus 28% in early and late PTLD (p =.037). None of the recipients with early PTLD and nine recipients with late PTLD (47%) had Ann Arbor stage IV at the time of their diagnosis (p =.006). Cyclophosphamid–Hydroxyrubicin–Oncovin–Prednisolon was used for treatment in 10 (48%) recipients with late PTLD (p = 0.032) only. There was no difference in mortality between the two groups. Conclusions: Recipients with late PTLD had a lower prevalence of detectable EBV DNA in plasma, were diagnosed with more advanced disease, and were more frequently treated with chemotherapy compared to recipients with early PTLD.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Abdulovski, Ranya","Møller, Dina Leth","Knudsen, Andreas D.","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Rasmussen, Allan","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Wareham, Neval E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-447698"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Kidney Transplantation","Liver Transplantation","Solid organ transplantation","posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorder"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early and late onset posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorders among adult kidney and liver transplant recipients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.13815","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-447698","identifier":[{"id":"85133967171","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35719018","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9543731","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-5aaf185b-d73b-448f-94e4-5732e058102f"],"keyword":["kidney transplantation","liver transplantation","posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorder","solid organ transplantation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2E36FA0C2AEFE713ED6A7283D91836C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.13815","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320651421/European_J_of_Haematology_2022_Abdulovski_Early_and_late_onset_posttransplant_lymphoproliferative_disorders_among.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ranya","key":"abdulovskipau","last":"Abdulovski","name":"Abdulovski, Ranya","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dina L.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"8d5cc577-14db-4efa-9db9-72b979611644","name":"Møller, Dina Leth","name_org":"Møller, Dina L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas D.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"fbeb64c3-4995-4397-8457-b4c20c93dc7a","name":"Knudsen, Andreas D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren S.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","name_org":"Sørensen, Søren S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Allan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","name_org":"Nielsen, Susanne D.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Neval E.","key":"warehampau","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Neval E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35719018"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejh.13815","issn":["09024441","09024506"],"issn_org":["09024441"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Haematology","pages":"343-350","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Haematology","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133967171"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5aaf185b-d73b-448f-94e4-5732e058102f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early- and late-onset posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorders among adult kidney and liver transplant recipients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-447698","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Concurrent anxiety is frequent in major depressive disorder and a shared pathophysiological mechanism between anxiety and other depressive symptoms is plausible. The serotonin 4 receptor (5-HT4R) has been implicated in both depression and anxiety. This is the first study to investigate the association between the cerebral 5-HT4R binding and anxiety in patients with depression before and after antidepressant treatment and the association to treatment response. Ninety-one drug-free patients with depression were positron emission tomography scanned with the 5-HT4R ligand [11C]-SB207145. Depression severity and concurrent anxiety was measured at baseline and throughout 8 weeks of antidepressant treatment. Anxiety measures included four domains: anxiety/somatization factor score; Generalized Anxiety Disorder 10-items (GAD-10) score; anxiety/somatization factor score ≥7 (anxious depression) and syndromal anxious depression. Forty patients were rescanned at week 8. At baseline, we found a negative association between global 5-HT4R binding and both GAD-10 score (p < 0.01) and anxiety/somatization factor score (p = 0.06). Further, remitters had a higher baseline anxiety/somatization factor score compared with non-responders (p = 0.04). At rescan, patients with syndromal anxious depression had a greater change in binding relative to patients with non-syndromal depression (p = 0.04). Concurrent anxiety in patients with depression measured by GAD-10 score and anxiety/somatization factor score is negatively associated with cerebral 5-HT4R binding. A lower binding may represent a subtype with reduced natural resilience against anxiety in a depressed state, and concurrent anxiety may influence the effect on the 5-HT4R from serotonergic antidepressants. The 5-HT4R is a promising neuroreceptor for further understanding the underpinnings of concurrent anxiety in patients with depression.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Köhler-Forsberg, Kristin","Ozenne, Brice","Larsen, Søren V.","Poulsen, Asbjørn S.","Landman, Elizabeth B.","Dam, Vibeke H.","Ip, Cheng Teng","Jorgensen, Anders","Svarer, Claus","Knudsen, Gitte Moos","Frokjaer, Vibe G.","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-500517"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concurrent anxiety in patients with major depression and cerebral serotonin 000000000004 receptor binding a neuropharm 000000000001 study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-022-02034-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-500517","identifier":[{"id":"85133901443","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9276803","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35821015","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b34ce426-41f6-4ec3-bd73-79249da57ba0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0005C4F022CAA6AF03741E72D2DFDD02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-022-02034-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/314432484/Concurrent.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristin","key":"köhlerforsbergkristinpau","last":"Köhler-Forsberg","name":"Köhler-Forsberg, Kristin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Brice","key":"ozennebricepau","last":"Ozenne","locid":"52e17fb0-a702-4384-bb59-a3a09619877c","name":"Ozenne, Brice","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Søren V.","key":"larsensørenvpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15f7f99a-0254-46d1-a47d-c8d6628f04b1","name":"Larsen, Søren V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asbjørn S.","key":"poulsenasbjørnspau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Asbjørn S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elizabeth B.","key":"landmanelizabethbpau","last":"Landman","name":"Landman, Elizabeth B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke H.","key":"damvibekehpau","last":"Dam","name":"Dam, Vibeke H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Cheng Teng","key":"ipchengtengpau","last":"Ip","locid":"6ad86471-9e4f-4bb6-8af2-1317d90b1271","name":"Ip, Cheng Teng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anders","key":"jorgensenanderspau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"46015f76-041c-4177-aa3a-8bcfd13eda19","name":"Jorgensen, Anders","name_org":"Jørgensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-6012-6965","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"svarerclauspau","last":"Svarer","name":"Svarer, Claus","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Gitte M.","key":"knudsengittemoospau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f02aee9e-69cf-491a-9765-ff062f734db8","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Moos","name_org":"Knudsen, Gitte M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1508-6866","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Vibe G.","key":"frokjaervibegpau","last":"Frokjaer","locid":"ab1287b2-e920-4656-b4bc-1b7d3dffd2dc","name":"Frokjaer, Vibe G.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Martin B.","key":"jørgensenmartinbalslevpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"dfc70acd-d15d-44f9-891e-6a7646d1727d","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","name_org":"Jørgensen, Martin B.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35821015"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41398-022-02034-5","issn":["21583188"],"issue":"1","journal":"Translational Psychiatry","paperid":"273","status":"p","title":"Translational Psychiatry","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133901443"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b34ce426-41f6-4ec3-bd73-79249da57ba0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Concurrent anxiety in patients with major depression and cerebral serotonin 4 receptor binding : A NeuroPharm-1 study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-500517","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Magnetic resonance enterocolonography (MREC) and pan-enteric capsule endoscopy (CE) offers visualization of the entire gastrointestinal tract in a single examination. We examined the diagnostic accuracy of MREC and CE in patients with suspected Crohn's disease (CD). METHOD: In a prospective, blinded, multicenter study, we included patients with clinically suspected CD. Patients were examined with MREC, CE, and ileocolonoscopy (IC) within 2 weeks. The primary outcome was per patient sensitivity, specificity, and diagnostic accuracy for ileocolonic CD. IC served as reference standard. RESULTS: 153 patients were included in the study and IC, MREC, and CE was performed in 152, 151, 133 patients, respectively. CD was diagnosed with IC in 59 (39%) patients (terminal ileum (TI) 22, colon 20, TI and colon 17). The sensitivity and specificity for diagnosing ileocolonic CD with MREC was 67.9% (CI 53.7-80.1) and 76.3% (CI 65.2-85.3) (TI 76.9% and 85.6%; colon 27% and 93%) compared to 87.5% (CI 73.2-95.8) and 87.8% (CI 78.2-94.3) with CE (TI 96.6% and 87.5%; colon 75.0% and 93.0%). The sensitivity of CE was superior to that of MREC (p = 0.02). The patient experienced discomfort was equal with CE and MREC and significantly less than with IC. CONCLUSION: In patients with suspected CD, CE has a high sensitivity for diagnosing CD in the TI and colon, which is superior to that of MREC. The sensitivity of MREC for diagnosing CD in the colon is poor. CE could be a patient-friendly alternative to IC in selected patients with suspected CD. Registered at ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT03134586.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brodersen, Jacob Broder","Knudsen, Torben","Kjeldsen, Jens","Agerbæk Juel, Mie","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Jensen, Michael Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-618798"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brodersen, Jacob Broder"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic accuracy of pan enteric capsule endoscopy and magnetic resonance enterocolonography in suspected crohn s disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.12307","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-618798","identifier":[{"id":"85137531977","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36069336","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9731660","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-9f30b75b-f47b-4b7a-91a0-6c7f80c85829"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D175EC21723D0F8EDAD9AD7925E6E965"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.12307","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/216177532/UEG_Journal_2022_Brodersen_Diagnostic_accuracy_of_pan_enteric_capsule_endoscopy_and_magnetic_resonance.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Medical gastroenterology-hepatology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Broder","key":"brodersenpau","last":"Brodersen","locid":"6848c9c8-cad2-4000-9a02-d73415b277cd","name":"Brodersen, Jacob Broder","orcid":"0000-0003-2530-7554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"afa15e36-ab82-4894-89c0-b8802310b50b","name":"Knudsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0003-0726-0115","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Agerbaek","key":"juelpau","last":"Juel","locid":"e100aceb-82b9-479a-9365-f89a179d0d75","name":"Agerbæk Juel, Mie","name_org":"Juel, Mie Agerbaek","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Dam","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a6ef46da-3165-4804-9599-4a6cd9f1bbaa","name":"Jensen, Michael Dam","orcid":"0009-0004-8432-1764","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36069336"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ueg2.12307","issn":["20506406","20506414"],"issn_org":["20506406"],"issue":"9","journal":"United European Gastroenterology Journal","pages":"973-982","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"United European Gastroenterology Journal","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137531977"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9f30b75b-f47b-4b7a-91a0-6c7f80c85829"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diagnostic accuracy of pan-enteric capsule endoscopy and magnetic resonance enterocolonography in suspected Crohn's disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=si