journal":"Cells","paperid":"2005","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Cells","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132421701"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","All University Colleges","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","VIA University College","allarity therapeutics europe (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-43da996e-31c8-474b-8a27-516dbd7b49b0","ku-13a5aece-4a24-4e9a-9565-a0682b9e1086","sdu-a3ab033d-b495-4a9d-9d66-101c68f77322","ucl-7c9e8d65-039f-49a4-9a35-60dd51339f37","via-27e77f56-d226-4f1e-90f6-90f6d6b275b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","VIA University College"],"title":"A Signature of Exaggerated Adipose Tissue Dysfunction in Type 2 Diabetes Is Linked to Low Plasma Adiponectin and Increased Transcriptional Activation of Proteasomal Degradation in Muscle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-098.34-017599","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The recurrence rate of colorectal liver metastases (CRLM) patients treated with curative intent is above 50%. Standard of care surveillance includes intensive computed tomographic (CT) imaging as well as carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) measurements. Nonetheless, relapse detection often happens too late to resume curative treatment. This longitudinal cohort study enrolled 115 patients with plasma samples (N = 439) prospectively collected before surgery, postoperatively at day 30 and every third month for up to 3 years. Droplet digital PCR (ddPCR) was used to monitor serial plasma samples for somatic mutations. Assessment of ctDNA status either immediately after surgery, or serially during surveillance, stratified the patients into groups of high and low recurrence risk (hazard ratio [HR], 7.6; 95% CI, 3.0-19.7; P <.0001; and HR, 4.3; 95% CI, 2.3-8.1; P <.0001, respectively). The positive predictive value (PPV) of ctDNA was 100% in all postoperative analyses. In multivariable analyses, postoperative ctDNA status was the only consistently significant risk marker associated with relapse (P <.0001). Indeterminate CT findings were observed for 30.8% (21/68) of patients. All patients (9/21) that were ctDNA positive at the time of the indeterminate CT scan later relapsed, contrasting 42.6% (5/12) of those ctDNA negative (P =.0046). Recurrence diagnoses in patients with indeterminate CT findings were delayed (median 2.8 months, P <.0001). ctDNA status is strongly associated with detection of minimal residual disease and early detection of relapse. Furthermore, ctDNA status can potentially contribute to clinical decision-making in case of indeterminate CT findings, reducing time-to-intervention.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Reinert, Thomas","Petersen, Lena Marie Skindhøj","Henriksen, Tenna Vesterman","Larsen, Marie Øbo","Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Frydendahl, Amanda","Øgaard, Nadia","Knudsen, Michael","Nordentoft, Iver","Vang, Søren","Krag, Søren Rasmus Palmelund","Knudsen, Anders Riegels","Mortensen, Frank Viborg","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-207785"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"keyword":["Biomarkers Tumor genetics","Circulating Tumor DNA genetics","Colorectal Neoplasms diagnosis","Colorectal cancer liver metastases","Droplet digital PCR","Humans","Liver Neoplasms genetics","Longitudinal Studies","Minimal residual disease","Neoplasm Recurrence Local epidemiology","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Recurrence surveillance","circulating tumor DNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating tumor dna for prognosis assessment and postoperative management after curative intent resection of colorectal liver metastases","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.33924","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-207785","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9303459","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34994972","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122933499","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8981151a-7114-47f2-9de3-3de3a3064715"],"keyword":["Biomarkers, Tumor/genetics","Circulating Tumor DNA/genetics","Circulating tumor DNA","Colorectal Neoplasms/diagnosis","Colorectal cancer liver metastases","Droplet digital PCR","Humans","Liver Neoplasms/genetics","Longitudinal Studies","Minimal residual disease","Neoplasm Recurrence, Local/epidemiology","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Recurrence surveillance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2838AC7BC4FBD7ABCFC8C770DC5865DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.33924","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9303459/pdf/IJC-150-1537.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"reinertthomaspau","last":"Reinert","locid":"22f4f867-bf80-4a55-89ac-be06f063db03","name":"Reinert, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4835-4804","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena Marie Skindhøj","key":"petersenlenamarieskindhøjpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"662ca33b-5b25-4e51-9243-dd5dc6262446","name":"Petersen, Lena Marie Skindhøj","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tenna Vesterman","key":"henriksentennavestermanpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"3861b20b-cac4-4754-bb98-8ae8cca5ac57","name":"Henriksen, Tenna Vesterman","orcid":"0000-0002-8541-1735","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Øbo","key":"larsenmarieøbopau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Marie Øbo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Heilskov","key":"rasmussenmadsheilskovpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3285e14f-ef19-480d-97ff-c95d6a90b354","name":"Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","orcid":"0000-0001-5723-6303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amanda Frydendahl Boll","key":"frydendahlamandapau","last":"Johansen","locid":"f36c28b3-