{"abstract":"Data visualization can be powerful in enabling us to make sense of complex data. Expressive data representation – where individuals have control over the nature of the output – is hard to incorporate into existing frameworks and techniques for visualization. The power of informal, rough, expressive sketches in working out ideas is well documented. This points to an opportunity to better understand how expressivity can exist in data visualization creation. We explore the expressive potential of Data Painting through a study aimed at improving our understanding of what people need and make use of in creating novel examples of data expression. Participants use exact measures of paint for data-mapping and then explore the expressive possibilities of free-form data representation. Our intentions are to improve our understanding of expressivity in data visualization; to raise questions as to the creation and use of non-traditional data visualizations; and to suggest directions for expressivity in visualization.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sturdee, Miriam","Knudsen, Søren","Carpendale, Sheelagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381890"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lancaster University","Simon Fraser University"],"keyword":["Data Painting","Data visualization","Expressive Data Representation","Informal Sketches","Non Traditional Visualizations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data painting expressive free form visualisation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2022.257","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381890","ids":["itu-296eaf2c-7b35-4aca-a9ae-4906a419bc69"],"keyword":["Data Painting","Data Visualization","Expressive Data Representation","Informal Sketches","Non-Traditional Visualizations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B5D2F812A9B455A709CD9DF5308B2FEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2022.257","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"lancaster university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lancaster University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"simon fraser university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simon Fraser University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miriam","key":"sturdeepau","last":"Sturdee","name":"Sturdee, Miriam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2575c800-642d-4984-9c56-41601cf07a26","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheelagh","key":"carpendalepau","last":"Carpendale","name":"Carpendale, Sheelagh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2022.257","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of DRS2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-296eaf2c-7b35-4aca-a9ae-4906a419bc69"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data-Painting: Expressive Free-Form Visualisation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381890","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper draws together nine strategies for creative visualization activities. Teaching visualization often involves running learning activities where students perform tasks that directly support one or more topics that the teacher wishes to address in the lesson. As a group of educators and researchers in visualization, we reflect on our learning experiences. Our activities and experiences range from dividing the tasks into smaller parts, considering different learning materials, to encouraging debate. With this paper, our hope is that we can encourage, inspire, and guide other educators with visualization activities. Our reflections provide an initial starting point of methods and strategies to craft creative visualisation learning activities, and provide a foundation for developing best practices in visualization education.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Roberts, Jonathan C.","Bach, Benjamin","Boucher, Magdalena","Chevalier, Fanny","Diehl, Alexandra","Hinrichs, Uta","Huron, Samuel","Kirk, Andy","Knudsen, Søren","Meirelles, Isabel","Noonan, Rebecca","Pelchmann, Laura","Rajabiyazdi, Fateme","Stoiber, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382349"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","France","Germany","Ireland","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bangor University","Carleton University","Institut Polytechnique de Paris","Munster Technological University","OCAD University","St. Pölten University of Applied Sciences","University of Cologne","University of Edinburgh","University of Toronto","University of Zurich","Visualising Data Ltd"],"keyword":["FOS Computer and information sciences","Graphics cs GR","Human Computer Interaction cs HC","I 3 8","K 3 0"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reflections and considerations on running creative visualization learning activities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2209.09807","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382349","identifier":[{"id":"85146361467","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4878cf8f-5241-4c8b-a50d-07b061998a34"],"keyword":["FOS: Computer and information sciences","Graphics (cs.GR)","Human-Computer Interaction (cs.HC)","I.3.8","K.3.0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EF8EF4DD1D59E0C21166B75112D973F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2209.09807","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"bangor university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Bangor University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"st pölten university of applied sciences","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"St. Pölten University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"institut polytechnique de paris","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut Polytechnique de Paris","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"visualising data ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Visualising Data Ltd","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"itu it university of copenhage