://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381794","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Several tissues produce and release interleukin-6 (IL-6) in response to beta2-adrenergic stimulation with selective agonists (beta2-agonists). Moreover, exercise stimulates muscle IL-6 production, but whether beta2-agonists regulate skeletal muscle production and release of IL-6 in humans, in association with exercise remains to be clarified. Thus, we investigated leg IL-6 release in response to beta2-agonist salbutamol in lean young men at rest and in recovery from resistance exercise. Design: The study employed a randomized controlled crossover design, where 12 men ingested either salbutamol (16 mg) or placebo for 4 days, followed by the last dose (24 mg) administered 1½ h before exercise. Arterial and femoral venous plasma IL-6 as well as femoral artery blood flow was measured before and ½-5 h in recovery from quadriceps muscle resistance exercise. Furthermore, vastus lateralis muscle biopsies were collected ½ and 5 h after exercise for determination of mRNA levels of IL-6 and Tumor Necrosis Factor (TNF)-α. Results: Average leg IL-6 release was 1.7-fold higher (p=0.01) for salbutamol than placebo, being 138±76 and 79±66 pg∙min-1 (mean±SD) for salbutamol and placebo, respectively, but IL-6 release was not significantly different between treatments within specific sampling points at rest and after exercise. Muscle IL-6 mRNA was 1.5 and 1.7-fold higher (p=0.001) for salbutamol than placebo ½ and 5 h after exercise, respectively, whereas no significant treatment differences were observed for TNF-α mRNA. Conclusions: Beta2-adrenergic stimulation with high doses of the selective beta2-agonist salbutamol, preceeded by 4 consecutive daily doses, induces transcription of IL-6 in skeletal muscle in response to resistance exercise and increases muscle IL-6 release in lean individuals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hostrup, Morten","Knudsen, Jakob G.","Maag Kristensen, Caroline","Jessen, Søren","Pilegaard, Henriette","Bangsbo, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393728"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beta adrenoceptor","Beta2 adrenoceptor","Cytokine","Faculty of Science","SABA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beta sub 000000000002 sub agonist increases skeletal muscle interleukin 000000000006 production and release in response to resistance exercise in men","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14171","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-393728","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9545867","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35460295","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129139360","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-006c1985-795c-4204-877e-b99039a8bdd1"],"keyword":["Beta-adrenoceptor","Beta2","Beta2-adrenoceptor","Cytokine","Faculty of Science","SABA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F17F00C38E3EA2D3E24517A5A95A5127"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14171","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/310230034/Hostrup_et_al_Scandinavian_Journal_of_Medicine_Science_in_Sports_2022_Vol_32_7_1099_1108.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"hostruppau","last":"Hostrup","locid":"2c96b73f-d427-45db-af64-9caf29101092","name":"Hostrup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-6201-2483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grunnet","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"820c7a12-b0e8-45d5-b8f7-35af01f74d37","name":"Knudsen, Jakob G.","name_org":"Knudsen, Jakob Grunnet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"maagkristensenpau","last":"Maag Kristensen","locid":"944bae46-3f36-45d0-9284-4ea2bc689b57","name":"Maag Kristensen, Caroline","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"5c391a38-0386-4839-8779-9ba06caaa6e0","name":"Jessen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-1264","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henriette","key":"pilegaardpau","last":"Pilegaard","locid":"bca00b25-e11a-407d-936f-6982a39ef1d8","name":"Pilegaard, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-1071-0327","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35460295"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sms.14171","issn":["09057188","16000838"],"issn_org":["09057188"],"issue":"7","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","pages":"1099-1108","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129139360"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-006c1985-795c-4204-877e-b99039a8bdd1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beta<sub>2</sub>-agonist increases skeletal muscle interleukin 6 production and release in response to resistance exercise in men","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-393728","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Perennial grain crops could make a valuable addition to sustainable agriculture, potentially even as an alternative to their annual counterparts. The ability of perennials to grow year after year significantly reduces the number of agricultural inputs required, in terms of both planting and weed control, while reduced tillage improves soil health and on-farm biodiversity. Presently, perennial grain crops are not grown at large scale, mainly due to their early stages of domestication and current low yields. Narrowing the yield gap between perennial and annual grain crops will depend on characterizing differences in their life cycles, resource allocation, and reproductive strategies and understanding the trade-offs between annualism, perennialism, and yield. The genetic and biochemical pathways controlling plant growth, physiology, and senescence should be analyzed in perennial crop plants. This information could then be used to facilitate tailored genetic improvement of selected perennial grain crops to improve agronomic traits and enhance yield, while maintaining the benefits associated with perennialism.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Chapman, Elizabeth A.","Thomsen, Hanne Cecilie","Tulloch, Sophia","Correia, Pedro M P","Luo, Guangbin","Najafi, Javad","DeHaan, Lee R.","Crews, Timothy E.","Olsson, Lennart","Lundquist, Per-Olof","Westerbergh, Anna","Pedas, Pai Rosager","Knudsen, Søren","Palmgren, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-465361"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","The Land Institute, Salinas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perennials as future grain crops opportunities and challenges","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2022.898769","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-465361","identifier":[{"id":"85135935670","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000840742800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35968139","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9372509","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-7825cdb3-bb6e-4451-912b-2e617841c172"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CDB8410F4609769180EC4E2B4D7431CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2022.898769","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318545082/fpls_13_898769.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"carlsberg foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CARL","l3nn":"Carlsberg Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Carlsberg Foundation","namevar":["Carlsberg Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CARL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Transport Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"the land institute salinas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The Land Institute, Salinas","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","ke