ass to biobased growing media as substitute for peat","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-196702","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction This post hoc pooled analysis of four real-world studies (SURE Canada, Denmark/Sweden, Switzerland and UK) aimed to characterize the use of once-weekly (OW) semaglutide, a glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist (GLP-1RA), in patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D). Research design and methods The Semaglutide Real-world Evidence (SURE) studies had a duration of ∼30 weeks. Changes in glycated hemoglobin (HbA 1c) and body weight (BW) were analyzed for the overall population and the following baseline subgroups: GLP-1RA-naïve/GLP-1RA switchers; body mass index <25/≥25-<30/≥30-<35/≥35 kg/m 2; age <65/≥65 years; HbA 1c <7%/≥7-≤8%/>8-≤9%/>9%; T2D duration <5/≥5-<10/≥10 years. Data for patients achieving treatment targets were analyzed in the overall population and the baseline HbA 1c ≥7% subgroup. Results Of 1212 patients, 960 were GLP-1RA-naïve and 252 had switched to semaglutide from another GLP-1RA. In the overall population, HbA 1c was reduced from baseline to end of study (EOS) by -1.1% point and BW by -4.7 kg; changes were significant for all subgroups. There were significantly larger reductions of HbA 1c and BW in GLP-1RA-naïve versus GLP-1RA switchers and larger reductions in HbA 1c for patients with higher versus lower baseline HbA 1c. At EOS, 52.6% of patients in the overall population achieved HbA 1c <7%. No new safety concerns were identified in any of the completed SURE studies. Conclusions In this pooled analysis, patients with T2D initiating OW semaglutide showed significant improvements from baseline to EOS in HbA 1c and BW across various baseline subgroups, including patients previously treated with a GLP-1RA other than semaglutide, supporting OW semaglutide use in clinical practice. Trail registration numbers NCT03457012; NCT03631186; NCT03648281; NCT03876015.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Yale, Jean François","Bodholdt, Ulrik","Catarig, Andrei Mircea","Catrina, Sergiu","Clark, Alice","Ekberg, Neda Rajamand","Erhan, Umut","Holmes, Patrick","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Liutkus, Joanne","Sathyapalan, Thozhukat","Schultes, Bernd","Rudofsky, Gottfried"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255122"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Yale, Jean François"],"country":["Canada","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Academic Specialist Center","All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","McGill University","Olten Cantonal Hospital","University of Hull"],"keyword":["Glucagon Like Peptide 1","Glycated Hemoglobin A","Incretins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real world use of once weekly semaglutide in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes pooled analysis of data from four sure studies by baseline characteristic subgroups","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjdrc-2021-002619","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255122","identifier":[{"id":"85127661855","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8984040","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35383100","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-dc62361f-bcd8-4aa9-9d42-7eb2a48fea0b"],"keyword":["glucagon-like peptide 1","glycated hemoglobin A","incretins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-645BF50ABDA56F3C92075B83EA4DC225"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjdrc-2021-002619","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Private practice - Denmark (medical)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"academic specialist center","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Academic Specialist Center","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - SDCA-Steno Diabetes Center Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"university of hull","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hull","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"ch","key":"olten cantonal hospital","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Olten Cantonal Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean François","key":"yalepau","last":"Yale","name":"Yale, Jean François","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"bodholdtpau","last":"Bodholdt","name":"Bodholdt, Ulrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrei Mircea","key":"catarigpau","last":"Catarig","name":"Catarig, Andrei Mircea","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergiu","key":"catrinapau","last":"Catrina","name":"Catrina, Sergiu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"clarkpau","last":"Clark","name":"Clark, Alice","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Neda Rajamand","key":"ekbergpau","last":"Ekberg","name":"Ekberg, Neda Rajamand","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Umut","key":"erhanpau","last":"Erhan","name":"Erhan, Umut","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"holmespau","last":"Holmes","name":"Holmes, Patrick","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanne","key":"liutkuspau","last":"Liutkus","name":"Liutkus, Joanne","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Thozhukat","key":"sathyapalanpau","last":"Sathyapalan","name":"Sathyapalan, Thozhukat","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernd","key":"schultespau","last":"Schultes","name":"Schultes, Bernd","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Gottfried","key":"rudofskypau","last":"Rudofsky","name":"Rudofsky, Gottfried","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35383100"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjdrc-2021-002619","issn":["20524897"],"issue":"2","journal":"BMJ Open Diabetes Research & Care","paperid":"e002619","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open Diabetes Research & Care","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127661855"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Novo Nordisk","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","private practice - denmark (medical)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dc62361f-bcd8-4aa9-9d42-7eb2a48fea0b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Real-world use of once-weekly semaglutide in patients with type 2 diabetes : Pooled analysis of data from four SURE studies by baseline characteristic subgroups","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255122","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We take the well-established use of physical scale models in architecture and identify new opportunities for using them to interactively visualize and examine multiple streams of geospatial data. Overlaying, comparing, or integrating visualizations of complementary data sets in the same physical space is often challenging given the constraints of various data types and the limited design space of possible visual encodings. Our vision of \"simultaneous worlds\" uses physical models as a substrate upon which visualizations of multiple data streams can be dynamically and concurrently integrated. To explore the potential of this concept, we created three design explorations that use an illuminated campus model to integrate visualizations about building energy use, climate, and movement paths on a university campus. We use a research through design approach, documenting how our interdisciplinary collaborations with domain experts, students, and architects informed our designs. Based on our observations, we characterize the benefits of models for 1) situating visualizations, 2) composing visualizations, and 3) manipulating and authoring visualizations. Our work highlights the potential of physical models to support embodied exploration of spatial and non-spatial visualizations through fluid interactions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hull, Carmen","Knudsen, Søren","Carpendale, Sheelagh","Willett, Wesley"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381719"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Simon Fraser University","University of Calgary"],"keyword":["Collaborative design","Data overlays","Embodied exploration","Geospatial data visualization","Illuminated models","Interactive visualizations","Physical scale models","Research through Design","Spatial data integration","Visualization techniques"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simultaneous worlds supporting fluid exploration of multiple data sets via physical models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92556945/hull2022simultaneous.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381719","ids":["itu-1e51d6bc-186a-4209-baaf-8b308b167e20"],"keyword":["Collaborative design","Data overlays","Embodied exploration","Geospatial data visualization","Illuminated models","Interactive visualizations","Physical scale models","Research through design","Spatial data integration","Visualization techniques"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC051D3C289129B09E81931078CCD1FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92556945/hull2022simultaneous.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of calgary","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Calgary","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"simon fraser university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simon Fraser University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carmen","key":"hullpau","last":"Hull","name":"Hull, Carmen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2575c800-642d-4984-9c56-41601cf07a26","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheelagh","key":"carpendalepau","last":"Carpendale","name":"Carpendale, Sheelagh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wesley","key":"willettpau","last":"Willett","name":"Willett, Wesley","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Graphics Interface 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e51d6bc-186a-4209-baaf-8b308b167e20"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simultaneous Worlds: Supporting Fluid Exploration of Multiple Data Sets via Physical Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381719","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The International Classification of Diseases (ICD) is widely used by clinical coders worldwide for clinical coding morbidity data into administrative health databases. Accordingly, hospital data quality largely depends on the coders’ skills acquired during ICD training, which varies greatly across countries.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Otero Varela, Lucia","Doktorchik, Chelsea","Wiebe, Natalie","Southern, Danielle A","Knudsen, Søren","Mathur, Pallavi","Quan, Hude","Eastwood, Cathy A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384937"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Calgary"],"keyword":["Clinical Coding","Data Accuracy","Data quality","Education","Health Information Management","International Classification of Diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"international classification of diseases clinical coding training an international survey","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101333700/otero-varela-et-al-2022-international-classification-of-diseases-clinical-coding-training-an-international-survey.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384937","identifier":[{"id":"85134320376","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f8f6877c-5a41-4c68-b57c-e04c5af986b2"],"keyword":["clinical coding","data accuracy","data quality","education","health information management","international classification of diseases"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59918F4DE2D3262085900987630639B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-N