{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Brodersen, Jacob Broder","Kjeldsen, Jens","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Knudsen, Torben","Juel, M. A.","ensen, M.D. J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-595359"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-23","start":"2021-10-22","title":"29th United European Gastroenterology Week Virtual","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brodersen, Jacob Broder"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the diagnostic performance of pan enteric capsule endoscopy and magnetic resonance enterocolonography in patients with suspected crohn s disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.12144","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-595359","ids":["sdu-4d3e980c-a337-454b-8a13-764e3539715c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AA622BB52877875F409CAEFFCCF5DA0D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Medical gastroenterology-hepatology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"broderbrodersenpau","last":"Broder Brodersen","locid":"6848c9c8-cad2-4000-9a02-d73415b277cd","name":"Brodersen, Jacob Broder","name_org":"Broder Brodersen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-2530-7554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"afa15e36-ab82-4894-89c0-b8802310b50b","name":"Knudsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0003-0726-0115","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. A.","key":"juelpau","last":"Juel","name":"Juel, M. A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.D. J","key":"ensenpau","last":"ensen","name":"ensen, M.D. J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["20506406","20506414"],"issn_org":["20506406"],"issue":"Suppl. 8","journal":"United European Gastroenterology Journal","paperid":"P1041","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"United European Gastroenterology Journal","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4d3e980c-a337-454b-8a13-764e3539715c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The diagnostic performance of pan-enteric capsule endoscopy and magnetic resonance enterocolonography in patients with suspected crohn's disease","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-595359","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background The vast majority of patients with advanced ovarian cancer experience disease recurrence after primary treatment. Objective To explore the diagnostic accuracy of repeated measurement of patient-reported outcomes and quality-of-life scores in relation to ovarian cancer recurrence. Methods Patients with ovarian cancer were recruited to the PROMova study by the end of their primary treatment at eight centers in Denmark. The purpose of the PROMova study was to explore the applicability of repeated use of patient-reported outcomes, which consisted of the European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer generic questionnaire and the ovarian specific questionnaire. The patient-reported outcomes were completed 3, 6, 9, 12, and 15 months after enrollment or until recurrence. The 3-month interval between completions was the period in which recurrence was assessed. Imaging and the biomarker CA125 were used as reference modality for recurrence. Mixed effects logistic regression was used to investigate the association between mean patient-reported outcome scores and recurrence. Receiver operating curves were used to establish cut-off scores. The diagnostic accuracy of patient-reported outcomes, including sensitivity, specificity, and positive and negative predictive values was estimated based on the Youden index. For combined scales, diagnostic accuracy was investigated based on multivariate analysis. Results The analysis included 196 patients with an overall recurrence rate of 50.5% and an overall mean time to recurrence of 302 days. With imaging as reference, patients with recurrence reported significantly lower global health, worse physical functioning, and more abdominal symptoms preceding recurrence. With CA125 as reference, global health, physical and emotional functioning were impaired. Despite the worsening of a number of symptoms prior to recurrence whichever reference modality was applied, the patient-reported outcome scores did not provide adequate diagnostic accuracy. Conclusion Repeated use of patient-reported outcomes during surveillance of ovarian cancer was not of diagnostic value. Future efforts should be directed at improving the administration of patient-reported outcomes as well as exploring the potential of using these outcomes as an indicator of clinical relevance.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kargo, Anette Stolberg","Jensen, Pernille Tine","Lindemann, Kristina","Hjøllund, Niels Henrik Ingvar","Liposits, Gabor Istvan","Raaschou-Jensen, Nicoline","Knudsen, Bettina Mølri","Möller, Sören","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Steffensen, Karina Dahl"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-027987"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kargo, Anette Stolberg"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo University Hospital","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Medical Oncology","Ovarian Neoplasms","quality of life PRO palliative care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of patient reported outcomes and ovarian cancer recurrence","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85108567815","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-027987","identifier":[{"id":"85108567815","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34489355","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d36dcbbd-1fd6-40f4-a9c5-825f901afb17","sdu-1dcf1e90-361d-4011-b39a-6ddc6d506a93"],"keyword":["medical oncology","ovarian neoplasms","quality of life (pro)/palliative care"],"lang":"Englis