order : results from the NeuroPharm 1 study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-413507","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To determine the prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 at a Danish tertiary referral otorhinolaryngology clinic during the first wave of the COVID-19 pandemic among patients with suspected acute upper airway infection (UAI) and patients operated for head and neck cancer (HNC), respectively. To monitor changes in the number of patient encounters for acute UAI and the number of referrals for the workup of HNC. Trial registration: NCT-04356560 (Clinicaltrials.gov). Methods: Prospective enrolled case series of all patients with suspected acute UAI (n = 88) and of patients undergoing surgery for HNC (n = 96), respectively, from March 23rd to May 5th, 2020, at a public tertiary referral otorhinolaryngology clinic in Denmark. SARS-CoV-2 was diagnosed with nasopharyngeal and oropharyngeal swabbing. Patients with suspected acute UAI had symptoms and definitive diagnoses registered in a database. Trends in the number of referrals and patient encounters were retrieved from an electronic patient journal system and analyzed retrospectively. Results: Eighty-eight patients with acute UAI were enrolled including 55 men and 34 women, median age of 31 years (range: 10 months to 82 years). One patient (1.1%) tested positive. Among 96 patients operated for HNC, zero tested positive. The number of referrals for HNC workup, and patient encounters for peritonsillar abscesses, decreased markedly in the first 3 weeks. Conclusion: The prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 during the first 6 weeks of the first wave was minimal among patients with acute UAI and zero among patients operated for HNC. The decrease in referrals for the workup of HNC may increase time to treatment initiation and patient morbidity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen, Peter Anders","Rasmussen, Kasper Møller Boje","Channir, Hani Ibrahim","von Buchwald, Christian","Cayé-Thomasen, Per","Klokker, Mads","Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","Kirkby, Nikolai Søren","Aanaes, Kasper","Jensen, Ramon Gordon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453863"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Otolaryngology","Respiratory tract infections","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","Tertiary Care Centers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact and prevalence of sars cov 000000000002 in patients with head and neck cancer and acute upper airway infection in a tertiary otorhinolaryngology referral center in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7778690/pdf/405_2020_Article_6514.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453863","identifier":[{"id":"33388982","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85098710040","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7778690","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-65231263-8170-4f02-90e8-6a3757aa1648"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Head and neck neoplasms","Otolaryngology","Respiratory tract infections","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","Tertiary care centers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25A17490263347864F8C5B12E310B281"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7778690/pdf/405_2020_Article_6514.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Peter Anders","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Peter Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper Møller Boje","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Kasper Møller Boje","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hani Ibrahim","key":"channirpau","last":"Channir","name":"Channir, Hani Ibrahim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"cayéthomasenpau","last":"Cayé-Thomasen","locid":"51411e35-b4a9-4e04-b2ef-538ebf70b337","name":"Cayé-Thomasen, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"klokkerpau","last":"Klokker","locid":"be74f452-48e9-4e56-8de1-f0ed083b9c77","name":"Klokker, Mads","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jenny Dahl","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"ace82a97-ed40-44ae-9619-37b98fdaf285","name":"Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolai Søren","key":"kirkbypau","last":"Kirkby","name":"Kirkby, Nikolai Søren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"aanaespau","last":"Aanaes","locid":"8bf39677-0bde-4163-ae14-19cf5b84d4bf","name":"Aanaes, Kasper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ramon Gordon","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bbbd5d78-5cb2-4f8a-9cf2-e19601100ef9","name":"Jensen, Ramon Gordon","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33388982"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00405-020-06514-6","issn":["09374477","09428992"],"issn_org":["09374477"],"issue":"9","journal":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","pages":"3409-3415","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","volume":"278"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098710040"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-65231263-8170-4f02-90e8-6a3757aa1648"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The impact and prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 in patients with head and neck cancer and acute upper airway infection in a tertiary otorhinolaryngology referral center in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453863","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bacterial and fungal bloodstream infections (BSI) are common after pediatric liver and kidney transplantations and associated with morbidity and mortality. However, knowledge about incidence rates, pathogen composition, and resistance patterns is limited. We aimed to describe the pattern of bacterial and fungal BSI in a cohort of pediatric liver and kidney transplant recipients. Methods: A prospective study of 85 pediatric liver and kidney transplant recipients transplanted from 2010 to 2017 with a total of 390 person-years of follow-up. Clinical characteristics and BSI were retrieved from national registries assuring nationwide follow-up for at least 1 year. BSI incidence rates and pathogen composition were investigated and stratified by the time post-transplantation and type of transplanted organ. Results: A total of 29 BSI were observed within the first 5 years post-transplantation with 16 different pathogens. The overall incidence rate of first BSI was 1.91 per 100 recipients per month (95% CI, 1.1–3.1) in the first year post-transplantation. The most common pathogens were Enterococcus faecium, Candida albicans, Escherichia coli, and Klebsiella pneumoniae. The pathogen composition depended on the transplanted organ with a higher proportion of BSI with Enterobacterales in kidney transplant recipients than in liver transplant recipients (67% vs. 20%, p = 0.03), while multiple pathogens were detected in the liver transplant recipients. Conclusions: BSI were common in pediatric liver and kidney transplant recipients and the pathogen composition differed between liver and kidney transplant recipients. Guidelines for empiric antibiotic therapy should consider the type of transplanted organ as well as the local resistance patterns.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Møller, Dina Leth","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Wareham, Neval Ete","Rezahosseini, Omid","Knudsen, Andreas D.","Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","Rasmussen, Allan","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462853"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bacteremia","Fungemia","Kidney Transplantation","Liver Transplantation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bacterial and fungal bloodstream infections in pediatric liver and kidney transplant recipients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12879-021-06224-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462853","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8188646","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85107603618","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34103013","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7410862a-a464-499c-888a-c7c9cbdb3ae0"],"keyword":["Bacteremia","Fungemia","Kidney transplantation","Liver transplantation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FFDA31754BBC3A9E4D6E20107A3DF03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12879-021-06224-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273016184/s12879_021_06224_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Dina Leth","key":"møllerdinalethpau","last":"Møller","locid":"8d5cc577-14db-4efa-9db9-72b979611644","name":"Møller, Dina Leth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Schwartz","key":"sørensensørenschwartzpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Neval Ete","key":"warehamnevaletepau","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Neval Ete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Omid","key":"rezahosseiniomidpau","last":"Rezahosseini","locid":"25f086c7-0215-450d-a148-0fd4745377ea","name":"Rezahosseini, Omid","orcid":"0000-0003-2198-1904","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Dehlbæk","key":"knudsenandreasdpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"fbeb64c3-4995-4397-8457-b4c20c93dc7a","name":"Knudsen, Andreas D.","name_org":"Knudsen, Andreas Dehlbæk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jenny Dahl","key":"knudsenjennydahlpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"ace82a97-ed40-44ae-9619-37b98fdaf285","name":"Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"rasmussenallanpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Allan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsensusannedampau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34103013"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12879-021-06224-2","issn":["14712334"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Infectious Diseases","paperid":"541","status":"p","title":"BMC Infectious Diseases","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107603618"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7410862a-a464-499c-888a-c7c9cbdb3ae0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bacterial and fungal bloodstream infections in pediatric liver and kidney transplant recipients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462853","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Several electroencephalogram (EEG) biomarkers for prediction of drug response in major depressive disorder (MDD) have been proposed, but validations in larger independent datasets are missing. In the current study, we investigated the prognostic value of previously suggested EEG biomarkers. We gathered data that matched prior studies in terms of EEG methodology, clinical criteria for MDD, and statistical approach as closely as possible. The NeuroPharm study is a non-randomized and open label prospective clinical trial. One hundred antidepressant free patients with MDD were enrolled in the study and 79 (57 female) were included in the per-protocol analysis. The biomarkers candidates for cross-validation were derived from prior studies such as iSPOT-D and EMBARC and include frontal and occipital alpha power and asymmetry and delta and theta activity at anterior cingulate cortex (ACC). The alpha asymmetry, reported in two out of six prior studies, could be partially validated. We found that in female patients, larger right than left frontal alpha power prior to drug treatment was associated with better clinical outcome 8 weeks later. Moreover, female non-responder had higher central left alpha power relative to the right. In contrast to prior reports, we found that lower theta activity at ACC was present in remitters and was associated with greater improvement at week 8. We provide evidence that in women with MDD, alpha asymmetry seems to be the most promising EEG biomarker for prediction of treatment response. Registration number: NCT02869035.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Ip, Cheng Teng","Olbrich, Sebastian","Ganz, Melanie","Ozenne, Brice","Köhler-Forsberg, Kristin","Dam, Vibeke H.","Beniczky, Sándor","Jørgensen, Martin B.","Frokjaer, Vibe G.","Søgaard, Birgitte","Christensen, Søren R.","Knudsen, Gitte M."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026775"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Knudsen, Gitte M."],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["Major depressive disorder","Pretreatment biomarker","Treatment response","qEEG"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-FILA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-FILA","DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pretreatment qeeg biomarkers for predicting pharmacological treatment outcome in major depressive disorder independent validation from the neuropharm study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85104712384","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026775","identifier":[{"id":"33910154","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85104712384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c24a3d7f-8214-4d49-8b65-5cb6a097295f","ku-88e84680-75db-4a19-8653-170612574e81"],"keyword":["Major depressive disorder","Pretreatment biomarker","Treatment response","qEEG"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-282B3CBADA77386509E50B8323C81AB0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Neurophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"filadelfia danish epilepsy hospital","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-FILA","l3nn":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","namevar":["Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-FILA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Cheng Teng","key":"ippau","last":"Ip","locid":"6ad86471-9e4f-4bb6-8af2-1317d90b1271","name":"Ip, Cheng Teng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"olbrichpau","last":"Olbrich","name":"Olbrich, Sebastian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Melanie","key":"ganzpau","last":"Ganz","locid":"a0225c8e-a6e9-4116-a301-a65b1d7a7b5b","name":"Ganz, Melanie","orcid":"0000-0002-9120-8098","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Brice","key":