{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Mumps, measles, rubella, and varicella-zoster viruses (MMRV) may cause severe infections in seronegative adult solid organ transplant (SOT) recipients but can be prevented by vaccination. We aimed to determine MMRV serostatus in adult SOT recipients before and one-year post-transplantation as well as evidence of MMRV infections in a large, prospective cohort of SOT recipients. METHODS: A prospective study of 1182 adult SOT recipients included in the Management of Posttransplant Infections in Collaborating Hospitals (MATCH) cohort from 2011 to 2017 with a one-year follow-up. Systematic monitoring of MMRV serology was performed prior to transplantation and one-year post-transplantation. PCR was used to confirm viral replication in SOT-recipients presenting with clinical evidence of infection. RESULTS: Among 1182 adult SOT recipients, 28 (2.4%), 77 (6.5%), 65 (5.5%), and 22 (1.9%) were seronegative for measles, mumps, rubella, and VZV, respectively, and 165 (14%) were seronegative for at least one of the MMRV viruses. One-year post-transplantation, 29/823 (3.5%) of seropositive SOT recipients had seroreverted, and 63/111 (57%) of seronegative SOT recipients seroconverted for at least one MMRV virus. No evidence of MMR infections was found, but 8 (0.7%) SOT recipients developed symptoms and had a positive VZV PCR. CONCLUSIONS: A large proportion of SOT recipients were seronegative for at least one of the MMRV viruses. MMRV infections in SOT recipients may disseminate and become fatal, and although only few cases of VZV infection were detected, results from this study suggest increase attention towards vaccination of patients waiting for SOT.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rezahosseini, Omid","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Perch, Michael","Ekenberg, Christina","Møller, Dina Leth","Knudsen, Andreas Dehlbæk","Kirkby, Nikolai","Lundgren, Jens","Lodding, Isabelle P","Wareham, Neval Ete","Gustafsson, Finn","Rasmussen, Allan","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-487154"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measles mumps rubella and varicella zoster virus serology and infections in solid organ transplant recipients during the first year posttransplantation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-487154","identifier":[{"id":"32564061","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122546613","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9cceba04-307c-4b7b-874e-b96e69f0255a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7245C0E6BB69965DC3380718C8F624F2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Omid","key":"rezahosseinipau","last":"Rezahosseini","locid":"25f086c7-0215-450d-a148-0fd4745377ea","name":"Rezahosseini, Omid","orcid":"0000-0003-2198-1904","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Schwartz","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"perchpau","last":"Perch","locid":"e0a136a6-8b36-4735-9db2-8847ce581fc6","name":"Perch, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"ekenbergpau","last":"Ekenberg","name":"Ekenberg, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dina Leth","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Dina Leth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas Dehlbæk","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Andreas Dehlbæk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikolai","key":"kirkbypau","last":"Kirkby","name":"Kirkby, Nikolai","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Isabelle P","key":"loddingpau","last":"Lodding","name":"Lodding, Isabelle P","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Neval Ete","key":"warehampau","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Neval Ete","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"5f442b2b-52d8-4795-a132-165b9f2d68b1","name":"Rasmussen, Allan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c5f21a63-fdc5-49ce-8c0f-97e2c623fbc4","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32564061"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cid/ciaa824","issn":["10584838","15376591"],"issn_org":["10584838"],"issue":"11","journal":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","status":"p","title":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122546613"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9cceba04-307c-4b7b-874e-b96e69f0255a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measles, Mumps, Rubella, and Varicella Zoster Virus Serology and Infections in Solid Organ Transplant Recipients During the First Year Posttransplantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-487154","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Recently, we demonstrated that whey protein (WP) combined with low dietary fiber improved lipemia, a risk factor for cardiovascular disease in subjects with abdominal obesity. In the present study, we investigated the effects of intake of WP and dietary fiber from enzyme-treated wheat bran on other metabolic parameters of the metabolic syndrome. Methods: The study was a 12-week, double-blind, randomized, controlled, parallel intervention study. We randomized 73 subjects with abdominal obesity to 1 of 4 iso-energetic dietary interventions: 60 g per day of either WP hydrolysate or maltodextrin (MD) combined with high-fiber (HiFi; 30 g dietary fiber/day) or low-fiber (LoFi; 10 g dietary fiber/day) cereal products. We assessed changes in insulin sensitivity, gut hormones (GLP-1, GLP-2, GIP, and peptide YY), body composition, 24-h BP, resting energy expenditure and respiratory exchange ratio (RER), and appetite. Results: Sixty-five subjects completed the trial. Subjective hunger ratings were lower after 12 weeks of WP compared with MD, independent of fiber content (P = 0.02). We found no effects on ratings of satiety, fullness or prospective food consumption for either of the interventions. Intake of WP combined with LoFi increased the postprandial peptide YY response. There were no effects of WP or fiber on insulin sensitivity, body composition, energy expenditure, incretins, or 24-h BP. Conclusions: WP consumption for 12 weeks reduced subjective ratings of hunger in subjects with abdominal obesity. Neither WP nor dietary fiber from wheat bran affected insulin sensitivity, 24-h BP, gut hormone responses, body composition, or energy expenditure compared with MD and low dietary fiber.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Fuglsang-Nielsen, Rasmus","Rakvaag, Elin","Langdahl, Bente Lomholt","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Hermansen, Kjeld","Gregersen, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-098.38-028002"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Fuglsang-Nielsen, Rasmus"],"keyword":["CEREAL FIBER","Cardiovascular disease","Dairy foods","Glucose tolerance","Milk","Overweight","Risk Factors","Vascular function","Weight loss","Whole grain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of whey protein and dietary fiber intake on insulin sensitivity body composition energy expenditure blood pressure and appetite in subjects with abdominal obesity","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85091022172","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.38-028002","identifier":[{"id":"85091022172","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000571665600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"32948867","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d3b2a469-49b9-4c23-b884-6498db5bba17","ku-f271c39a-1ccd-4ba4-b129-d54a64d9b69c"],"keyword":["CARDIOVASCULAR-DISEASE","CEREAL FIBER","DAIRY FOODS","GLUCOSE-TOLERANCE","MILK","OVERWEIGHT","RISK-FACTORS","VASCULAR FUNCTION","WEIGHT-LOSS","WHOLE-GRAIN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F037100FFE6ED16FA82700D09632EBDC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of C