{"abstract":"In this study, a comparative study was conducted on the three reactor types (the adiabatic, water-cooled and gas-cooled reactor) employed for the traditional syngas to methanol (STM) process to investigate their potential applications to the STM process with the CO 2-rich feed gas or the CO 2 hydrogenation to methanol (CTM) process. The temperature profiles in the axial and radial directions particularly the hot-spot temperatures, operating conditions and methanol yields for the reactors have been investigated using the thermodynamic analysis, the CFD method and the pseudo-homogeneous model. The capital costs for CTM process with the three reactor types have also been evaluated. Compared with the traditional STM process, the STM process with the CO 2-rich feed gas and CTM process exhibited reduced hot-spot temperatures. The simulation results showed that the single-bed adiabatic (without internal cooling) reactor and the gas-cooled reactor exhibited potentials for the CTM process, where the hot-spot temperatures the hot-spot temperatures in the reactors can be within the typical operating temperature range (e.g., 220–280 °C) for the catalyst. Regarding the comparison of the three reactor types for the CTM process, the water-cooled reactor showed advantages in terms of efficient heat removal, low hot-spot temperature and relatively wide range of inlet temperature for control. The adiabatic reactor and the gas-cooled reactor demonstrated a relatively low and medium performance, and also a relatively low and medium capital cost, respectively, which indicates the potentials of the two reactor types in a small-scale CTM process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059181"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Methanol synthesis","Thermodynamic analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparative study on three reactor types for methanol synthesis from syngas and co000000000002","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448880495/Manu_for_VBN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059181","identifier":[{"id":"85081202267","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1f3f897c-c9a8-4c84-b597-5cece3117552"],"keyword":["Adiabatic reactor","CO hydrogenation to methanol","CO2 hydrogenation to methanol","Gas-cooled reactor","Methanol synthesis","Thermodynamic analysis","Water-cooled reactor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F46E4294E333291DC570689A94B4C52C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448880495/Manu_for_VBN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2020.124632","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"124632","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","volume":"393"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081202267"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1f3f897c-c9a8-4c84-b597-5cece3117552"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A comparative study on three reactor types for methanol synthesis from syngas and CO2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059181","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this corrigendum, the authors would like to make a correction in the Section of Experimental, Single cell assembly, the second sentence: “The components of the MEA from anode to cathode are Ti felt (350 mm thick, porosity of 81%, fiber diameter of 20 mm) that was employed as the anode porous transport layer” should be corrected to “The components of the MEA from anode to cathode are Ti felt (350 μm thick, porosity of 81%, fiber diameter of 20 μm) that was employed as the anode porous transport layer”. The authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Li, Na","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Li, Na"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"corrigendum to the effect of fe sup 000000000003 sup contamination in feed water on proton exchange membrane electrolyzer performance international journal of hydrogen energy 000000002019 000000000044 000000000026 000000012952 000000012957 s360319919313825 000000000010 000000001016 j ijhydene 000000002019 000000000004 000000000015","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85076231388&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113207","identifier":[{"id":"85076231388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d95539be-9a17-4f43-9abe-9878aee12471"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C1C112F1F2EC02080764D7D95046B7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","