{"abstract":"Vores pointe er, at konkurrence bliver en fristelse for elever i folkeskolen i dag. Det aktuelle ideal er 'maksimeret læring', hvor eleven konstant er opmærksom på sin egen læring og på at overgå sig selv I den situation kan det være en lettelse at glemme sig selv et øjeblik og 'bare' forsøge at vinde over de andre. Folkeskolens fællesskab bliver et 'sammen hver for sig', et foran-bagved. Var det det, vi ville? - spørger vi i kroniken, måske lidt retorisk.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, Hanne","Christensen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-245341"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"er konkurrence blevet folkeskolens fællesskab","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://politiken.dk/debat/kroniken/art7855546/Konkurrencementaliteten-er-g%C3%A5et-amok-i-folkeskolen?shareToken=v_RiqWAASEiw","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-245341","ids":["au-cb097f6d-dab9-4ad1-96b4-f879e7a305b3"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DC9BC1D08E7BFC0A892C553216043B22"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"64613f11-d8e3-46a7-9eae-4a4a50cf9fdc","name":"Knudsen, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0003-3879-0629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c6bf7b94-cdf4-4abe-8e80-5526aacfd66c","name":"Christensen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1335-0806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09071814"],"newspaper":"Politiken","pages":"7-8","publisher":"JP/Politikens Hus AS","publisher_org":"JP/Politikens Hus A/S","status":"p","title":"Politiken","title_org":"Politiken, kroniken"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cb097f6d-dab9-4ad1-96b4-f879e7a305b3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Er konkurrence blevet folkeskolens fællesskab?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-245341","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Next to the widely studied glycation and Maillard reaction cascade, the heat treatment of milk during production of long shelf-life products may induce side reactions where serine, phosphoserine, glycoserine, cysteine or cystine can be converted into dehydroalanine, which in turn can further react with lysine, histidine or cysteine to yield lysinoalanine (LAL), histidinoalanine (HAL) or lanthionine (LAN) cross-links. The nutritional value, digestibility and functionality of the proteins may be affected by the introduction of covalent cross-links, modified amino acid residues and eventually aggregation. In this study, a liquid chromatography triple quadrupole based method was developed to directly quantify LAL and LAN using multiple reaction monitoring. The method was validated and applied to investigate the content of these cross-links in different dairy products. The level of LAL and LAN was below quantification in raw milk and pasteurised milk, but increasing amounts were measured in ultra-high temperature milk and micellar casein isolate.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","Le, Thao Thi Thu","Knudsen, Lotte Juul","Rauh, Valentin","Poulsen, Nina Aagaard","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-275211"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Edith Cowan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and application of a multiple reaction monitoring mass spectrometry method for absolute quantification of lysinoalanine and lanthionine in dairy products","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85081966518","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-275211","identifier":[{"id":"85081966518","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ffa2d123-205f-441d-be46-bbf1d1aaf11c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EE08D1F458EFAC0A85C9E539705284F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"edith cowan university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Edith Cowan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"030ede5c-2e12-40c1-9d0c-543f0c5ffadf","name":"Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","name_org":"Nielsen, Søren D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thao T.","key":"lepau","last":"Le","locid":"f114fe35-c2f1-437d-b00b-8beded4747a9","name":"Le, Thao Thi Thu","name_org":"Le, Thao T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte J.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7ee04b01-4825-401c-93b0-64ffaa7e3452","name":"Knudsen, Lotte Juul","name_org":"Knudsen, Lotte J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentin","key":"rauhpau","last":"Rauh","name":"Rauh, Valentin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina A.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"c6f00bcb-f900-41bb-98ee-c685ea6f8894","name":"Poulsen, Nina Aagaard","name_org":"Poulsen, Nina A.","orcid":"0000-0001-9983-9663","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","name_org":"Larsen, Lotte B.","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.idairyj.2020.104693","issn":["09586946","18790143"],"issn_org":["09586946"],"journal":"International Dairy Journal","paperid":"104693","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Dairy Journal","volume":"105"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081966518"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ffa2d123-205f-441d-be46-bbf1d1aaf11c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Development and application of a multiple reaction monitoring mass spectrometry method for absolute quantification of lysinoalanine and lanthionine in dairy products","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-275211","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A significant drop of 2.4-2.9 percentage-points (%-p) in crude protein content (on dry matter basis) in Danish grain crops was observed from around 1990 to 2015. The aim of the analysis was to quantify the effect of the change in N-response of varieties of winter wheat (WW) and spring barley (SB) under farmers’ conditions based on approx. 1000 fertilizer trials with WW and 500 with SB carried out in farmers’ fields from 1987 to 2015. Results indicated that for WW receiving 129-190 kg N/ha, DM yield increased 0.8-0.9 Mg/ha. The amount of harvested N in grain increased 5-11 kg N/ha, and % N in grain dropped by 0.1-0.05 %-points; the largest drop was found for low N-additions. For SB, receiving 93-129 kg N/ha, DM yield increased by 0.9-1.1 Mg/ha. The amount of harvested N in grain increased by 4-6 kg while the N % in grain dropped 0.2-0.24 %-points. For both crops, the effect of plant breeding is likely to be confounded with the effect of increased CO2. Adding up effects of changed N-response and fertilizer rates only explained part of the observed reduction in crude protein content.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Styczen, Merete Elisabeth","Abrahamsen, Per","Hansen, Søren","Knudsen, Leif"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463792"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Det Natur og Biovidenskabelige Fakultet","Fertilization","Plant Breeding","Protein content","Spring barley","Winter wheat"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of the significant drop in protein content in danish grain crops from 000000001990 000000002015 based on n response in fertilizer trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-463792","identifier":[{"id":"000528197200006","type":"wos"},{"id":"85079125496","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-75a40e2c-417b-4013-9345-995c910d2082"],"keyword":["Det Natur- og Biovidenskabelige Fakultet","Fertilization","Plant breeding","Protein content","Winter wheat","spring barley"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6844B2869D9F1FC4753353B0DF0435AB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Environmental Chemistry and Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish agriculture food council","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-AAF","l3nl":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","l3nn":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","namevar":["Danish Agriculture & Food Council"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-AAF","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Merete Elisabeth","key":"styczenpau","last":"Styczen","locid":"ff480289-c8d9-48f2-8481-ea97bcdea046","name":"Styczen, Merete Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0003-0420-2577","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"890129b9-995a-458c-bc5d-203846210934","name":"Abrahamsen, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-4804-2758","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95884c00-416a-4f9f-8b62-c02d5fdf0faf","name":"Hansen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5483-6853","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Leif","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Leif","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eja.2020.126013","issn":["11610301","18737331"],"issn_org":["11610301"],"journal":"European Journal of Agronomy","paperid":"126013","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Agronomy","volume":"115"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079125496"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danish Agriculture & Food Council","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-75a40e2c-417b-4013-9345-995c910d2082"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of the significant drop in protein content in Danish grain crops from 1990-2015 based on N-response in fertilizer trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463792","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present PixelClipper, a tool built for facilitating data engagement events. PixelClipper supports conversations around visualizations in public settings through annotation and commenting capabilities. It is recognized that understanding data is important for an informed society. However, even when visualizations are available on the web, open data is not yet reaching all audiences. Public facilitated events centered around data visualizations may help bridge this gap. PixelClipper is designed to promote discussion and engagement with visualizations in public settings. It allows viewers to quickly and expressively extract visual clippings from visualizations and add comments to them. Ambient and facilitator displays attract attention by showing clippings. They function as entry points to the full visualizations while supporting deeper conversations about the visualizations and data. We describe the design goals of PixelClipper, share our experiences from deploying it, and discuss its future potential in supporting data visualization engagement events.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Walny, Jagoda","Storteboom, Sarah","Pusch, Richard","Hwang, Steven Munsu","Knudsen, Søren","Carpendale, Sheelagh","Willett, Wesley"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-496319"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Calgary"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pixelclipper supporting public engagement and conversation about visualizations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290397039/PixelClipper_Walny_2020_early_version.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-496319","identifier":[{"id":"31985410","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85078471979","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ac3e5ded-c688-4faf-99e0-e7da4c84a7eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-382673EA81EB952D736C5C4881685AFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290397039/PixelClipper_Walny_2020_early_version.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of calgary","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Calgary","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jagoda","key":"walnypau","last":"Walny","name":"Walny, Jagoda","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"storteboompau","last":"Storteboom","name":"Storteboom, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Richard","key":"puschpau","last":"Pusch","name":"Pusch, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steven Munsu","key":"hwangpau","last":"Hwang","name":"Hwang, Steven Munsu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Soren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"60aa66e8-eac5-4487-94e1-f1379643b27d","name":"Knudsen, Søren","name_org":"Knudsen, Soren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sheelagh","key":"carpendalepau","last":"Carpendale","name":"Carpendale, Sheelagh","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wesley","key":"willettpau","last":"Willett","name":"Willett, Wesley","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31985410"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mcg.2020.2968906","issn":["02721716","15581756"],"issn_org":["02721716"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Computer Graphics and Applications","pages":"57-70","status":"p","title":"IEEE Computer Graphics and Applications","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078471979"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ac3e5ded-c688-4faf-99e0-e7da4c84a7eb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pixelclipper : Supporting public engagement and conversation about visualizations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-496319","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim was to investigate if oncologic treatment decision based on G8 screening followed by comprehensive geriatric assessment (CGA) and a multidisciplinary team conference in patients with G8 ≤ 14 was better than treatment decision based on standard assessment. ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT02671994. Materials and Methods: From January 2016 to June 2018, 96 patients with cancer, aged ≥70 years, were included. Patients were randomized to treatment decision based on the oncologist's clinical judgement (control) or based on screening with G8. If G8 > 14 treatment decision was made as in the control group and if G8 ≤ 14, patients were referred to CGA including intervention as needed and treatment decision after a multidisciplinary team conference (MDT). Results: The study was closed early. 47 patients were randomized to the control group and 49 to the intervention group; 28 had a G8 ≤ 14, 24 of whom attended CGA. In the intervention group 48% completed treatment as planned compared to 54% in the control group (p = .208). Thirty-eight percent experienced grade 3–4 toxicity in the control group compared with only 20% in the intervention group (p = .055). Median overall survival (OS) was 14.2 months in the control group and 19.1 months in the intervention group (p = .911). Median progression-free survival (PFS) was 9.0 months in the control group and 7.8 months for the intervention group (p = .838). Conclusion: Treatment decision based on G8 screening followed by CGA had no impact on completion rate of planned oncologic treatment, OS or PFS, but resulted in a borderline significant lower incidence of grade 3–4 toxicity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nadaraja, Sambavy","Matzen, Lars Erik","Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","Dysager, Lars","Ør Knudsen, Anja","Jeppesen, Stefan Starup","Möller, Sören","Herrstedt, Jørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-595358"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Academy for Geriatric Cancer Research (AgeCare)"],"corresponding_author":["Nadaraja, Sambavy"],"keyword":["Cancer","Comprehensive geriatric assessment","Gynecological cancer","Lung cancer","Older patient","Randomized Controlled Trial","Treatment decision","Urological cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of comprehensive geriatric assessment for optimal treatment of older patients with cancer a randomized parallel group clinical trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jgo.2019.06.019","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We would like to thank the Danish Cancer Society [grant number R90-A6232 ] and The Velux Foundation [grant number 9631 ] for funding this study. The sponsors did not have any role in the study design, the collection and analysis of data; in the interpretation of results; in the writing of the report; or in the decision to submit the article for publication."],"id":"S01-000.00-595358","identifier":[{"id":"31279749","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068206624","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4d3e6265-aa75-4c24-b7b8-b312f528e684"],"keyword":["Cancer","Comprehensive geriatric assessment","Gynecological cancer","Lung cancer","Older patient","Randomized controlled trial","Treatment decision","Urological cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C44AD5CA817CD2A519650E52ABC1FF6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jgo.2019.06.019","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresear