{"abstract":"Purpose: We examined whether diabetic polyneuropathy (DPN) and diabetic foot ulcers in type 2 diabetes can be accurately identified using International Classification of Diseases, 10th revision discharge diagnosis codes, surgery codes, and drug prescription codes. Methods: We identified all type 2 diabetes patients in the Central Denmark region, 2009-2016, who had ≥1 primary/secondary diagnosis code of “diabetes with neurological complication” (E10.4-E14.4), “diabetic polyneuropathy” (G63.2), or “polyneuropathy, unspecified” (G62.9). Patients with potential painful DPN and non-painful DPN were identified based on prescription history for serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors, tricyclic antidepressants, or gabapentinoids. Likewise, type 2 diabetes patients with potential foot ulcers were identified based on diagnosis or surgery codes. We used medical record review as the reference standard and calculated positive predictive values (PPVs). Results: Of 53 randomly selected patients with potential painful DPN, 38 were classified as having DPN when validated against medical records; of these, 18 also had neuropathic pain, yielding a PPV of 72% (95% CI: 58-83%) for DPN and 34% (95% CI: 22-48%) for painful DPN. Likewise, among 54 randomly selected patients with potential non-painful DPN, 30 had DPN based on medical record data; of these, 27 had non-painful DPN, yielding PPVs of 56% (95% CI: 41-69%) and 50% (95% CI: 36-64%), respectively. Secondary E-chapter codes often denoted stroke or mononeuropathies, rather than DPN. Excluding secondary E-chapter codes from the algorithm increased the PPV for DPN to 78% (95% CI: 63-89%) for the painful DPN cohort and to 74% (95% CI: 56-87%) for the non-painful DPN cohort. Of 53 randomly selected patients with potential diabetic foot ulcer, only 18 diagnoses were confirmed; PPV=34% (95% CI: 22-48%). Conclusion: G-chapter and primary E-chapter diagnosis codes can detect type 2 diabetes patients with hospital-diagnosed DPN, and may be useful in epidemiological research. In contrast, our diabetic foot ulcer algorithm did not perform well.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christensen, Diana Hedevang","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Nicolaisen, Sia Kromann","Andersen, Henning","Callaghan, Brian Christopher","Finnerup, Nanna Brix","Jensen, Troels Staehelin","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231296"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Diana Hedevang"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Michigan"],"keyword":["Diabetic foot ulcer","Diabetic polyneuropathy","Epidemiology","Positive predictive value","Registries","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can diabetic polyneuropathy and foot ulcers in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes be accurately identified based on icd 000000000010 hospital diagnoses and drug prescriptions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S197474","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231296","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6503195","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31118819","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85067552913","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b2b89503-191a-456f-9461-72aea0e28c78"],"keyword":["Diabetic foot ulcer","Diabetic polyneuropathy","Epidemiology","Positive predictive value","Registries","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-310732B125160931E752656DF7BEE0EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S197474","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of michigan","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Diana Hedevang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"736d7555-3234-4cec-97fa-6138c22ee99a","name":"Christensen, Diana Hedevang","orcid":"0000-0002-2693-5651","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sia Kromann","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","locid":"955ac2de-afa2-42e6-abe1-aa6f68aeada8","name":"Nicolaisen, Sia Kromann","orcid":"0000-0002-6106-1945","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henning","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c428cd32-44da-4dc0-adc3-018731065131","name":"Andersen, Henning","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian Christopher","key":"callaghanpau","last":"Callaghan","name":"Callaghan, Brian Christopher","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nanna Brix","key":"finneruppau","last":"Finnerup","locid":"96511d27-1bc4-4075-82d7-3382b8b4c167","name":"Finnerup, Nanna Brix","orcid":"0000-0001-5541-0240","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels Staehelin","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e1a6c2c8-3a85-464d-a1b3-53c8bab37d6d","name":"Jensen, Troels Staehelin","orcid":"0000-0002-3487-6380","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reimar Wernich","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"36e7af2c-e02f-48d4-b124-0f1bd95b1748","name":"Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","orcid":"0000-0001-9135-3474","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31118819"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s197474","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"311-321","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","title_org":"Clinical epidemiology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067552913"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b2b89503-191a-456f-9461-72aea0e28c78"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Can diabetic polyneuropathy and foot ulcers in patients with type 2 diabetes be accurately identified based on ICD-10 hospital diagnoses and drug prescriptions?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-231296","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
