{"abstract":"High temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cells (HT-PEMFC) have phosphoric acid doped membranes. Acid in the membrane is mobile and tends to move out of the membrane depending on the acid doping. The migration of acid (when the doping is high) towards the anode at high current density >0.4Acm−2 causes gas diffusion layer (GDL) and catalyst flooding which thereby results higher hydrogen transport resistance. Thus, it is important to determine the acid doping level, which is optimal. In this study, transient changes in hydrogen mass transport is investigated as a function of doping level and current density. Three doping levels 11, 8.3 and 7 molecules of H2PO4 per PBI repeat unit are investigated. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) was modified to a single frequency measurement and time constant are calculated for resistance change with current density using a linear fit. The time constants are 2.0 ± 0.5, 3.4 ± 0.3, 8.2 ± 0.2 min for low and 2.5 ± 0.8, 4.9 ± 0.3 and 4.5 ± 0.2 min for high current densities, for the respective doping levels. The resistance decreases at high and increases at low current densities for all the doping levels with a varying time constant. This change in time constant is attributed to low doping level having lower capillary pressure to push the acid from reaching GDL pores from the membrane and/or catalyst layer.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thomas, Sobi","Araya, Samuel Simon","Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Steenberg, Thomas","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101765"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomas, Sobi"],"keyword":["EIS","Fuel cell","High temperature PEM","Load cycling","Phosphoric acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrogen mass transport resistance changes in a high temperature polymer membrane fuel cell as a function of current density and acid doping","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/331043330/Hydrogen_mass_transport_resistance_changes_in_a_high_temperatu_2019_Electroc.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the Innovation Fund Denmark for funding the work through the 4 M project. The authors are also thankful to Danish Power Systems for providing the MEA used in the experiment."],"id":"S01-000.00-101765","identifier":[{"id":"85067068353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b2223f4c-e825-4e30-ada6-0161e3f76a83"],"keyword":["EIS","Fuel cell","High temperature PEM","Load cycling","Phosphoric acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CCF6756F336B9EA88DD0C4FB766AC14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/331043330/Hydrogen_mass_transport_resistance_changes_in_a_high_temperatu_2019_Electroc.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Danish Power Systems Ltd."],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"steenbergpau","last":"Steenberg","name":"Steenberg, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.electacta.2019.06.021","issn":["00134686","18733859"],"issn_org":["00134686"],"journal":"Electrochimica Acta","pages":"521-527","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electrochimica Acta","volume":"317"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067068353"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","danish power systems ltd."],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b2223f4c-e825-4e30-ada6-0161e3f76a83"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Hydrogen mass transport resistance changes in a high temperature polymer membrane fuel cell as a function of current density and acid doping","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101765","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Chemotherapy resistance remains a challenge in the clinical management of metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC). Here, early changes in cell-free circulating tumour DNA (ctDNA) levels were explored as a marker of therapeutic efficacy. Twenty-four mCRC patients were enrolled and treated with FOLFIRI based first-line therapy. Blood samples collected pre-treatment, at day 7, 14, 21, 60 and at progression were analysed for cell-free DNA (cfDNA) and ctDNA levels using digital droplet PCR. A subset of samples were additionally analysed by targeted sequencing. Patients with high pre-treatment ctDNA or cfDNA levels (≥75th centile) had significantly shorter progression free survival (PFS) than patients with lower levels. Despite an overall decline in ctDNA levels from pre-treatment to first CT-scan, serial analysis identified seven patients with temporary increases in ctDNA consistent with growth of resistant cells. These patients had shorter PFS and shorter overall survival. Targeted sequencing analyses of cfDNA revealed dramatic changes in the clonal composition in response to treatment. Our study suggests that increasing ctDNA levels during the first cycles of first-line FOLFIRI treatment is a predictor of incipient progressive disease and poorer survival. Thus, we demonstrate the importance of monitoring ctDNA levels as early as one week after treatment onset to enable early detection of treatment failure.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Lyskjær, Iben","Kronborg, Camilla","Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Sorensen, Boe Sandahl","Demuth, Christina","Rosenkilde, Mona","Frydendahl, Amanda","Knudsen, Michael","Vang, Søren","Krag, Søren Rasmus Palmelund","Spindler, Karen-Lise Garm","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146361"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"keyword":["Acquired resistance","Digital PCR","Guidelines","Mutations","Plasma","Survival","Therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correlation between early dynamics in circulating tumour dna and outcome from folfiri treatment in metastatic colorectal cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-47708-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146361","identifier":[{"id":"000479187800048","type":"wos"},{"id":"31395942","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6687711","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85070574523","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1dbbe85b-988f-4267-b47a-7d774e50c4a6"],"keyword":["ACQUIRED-RESISTANCE","DIGITAL PCR","GUIDELINES","MUTATIONS","PLASMA","SURVIVAL","THERAPY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D0B3A087986AACBEC4F82FF6F8D4254"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-47708-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Iben","key":"lyskjærpau","last":"Lyskjær","locid":"03ec53bc-fe20-4591-b2fc-ed0d89bc3a53","name":"Lyskjær, Iben","orcid":"0000-0003-3446-1182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla Skovhus","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","loci