g, Camilla","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"22","corresponding":null,"first":"Kári","key":"stefánssonkáripau","last":"Stefánsson","name":"Stefánsson, Kári","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30988515"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-019-0391-1","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"924-930","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064555172"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ec8b6a7b-4b08-4d4b-813b-cf75e61b74ed","ku-fcc7544e-30e9-4f99-9348-fa334c927368"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Roadmap for a precision-medicine initiative in the Nordic region","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.44-029822","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Children with mental and physical disabilities are less often participating in school PE in Danish primary and secondary schools. Engagement in physical activity is equal important for all children, and the exclusion from PE can have negative consequences for their current physical and mental health and future possibilities for an active and healthy life. The purpose of the current study is to conceptualize a practical framework to ensure the inclusion of all children regardless of mental and physical abilities in school PE. Methods: The development of the conceptual framework is based on three methodological approaches. Firstly, the current evidence base is systematically reviewed for practical approaches and guidelines for inclusion in sport and PE. Secondly, qualitative interviews are conducted with PE teachers to identify needs, constraints and opportunities for inclusion. And finally, the framework is developed and reviewed by a coalition of scientific and practical experts in the area. Results: The framework consists of two levels: a strategic level focusing on prioritization, communication and organizational preparation; and a practical level focusing on didactical and pedagogical approaches for PE. Fundamentally, all children should be able to learn from each PE lesson regardless of physical and metal condition. Teachers must therefore plan, present and accomplish PE there meet individual needs in relation to the curriculum demands. This approach entails: 1) Setting a clear focus on both physical and social learning outcome of the lessons; 2) Selecting activities there are adaptable to meet the individual needs; 3) structuring lessons and communication to decrease disturbing noise and interruptions; 4) focus on positive peer-to-peer feedback to promote supportive social climate; and 5) meet all children with a positive and understanding attitude and focus on their abilities and motivational drivers. Conclusions: The conceptual framework will be available for all Danish PE teachers from august 2019 at the educational platform hosted by the Ministry of Education. At the same time an educational strategy is planned to include the conceptual framework in the teacher education and professional development. The conceptual framework will increase the inclusion of children with physical and mental disabilities as well as other children with special needs regarding PE. This will ground the foundation for their health and well-being. Support/Funding Source: The study is funded by the Danish Ministry of Education","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christiansen, Lars Breum","Knudsen, Louise Stjerne","Skovgaard, Thomas","Smedegaard, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-049621"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-30","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2019-08-28","title":"HEPA Europe 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inclusion of children with mental and physical disabilities in ordinary school pe a conceptual framework","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-049621","ids":["sdu-e51dcd1e-96a8-4cd6-8014-d7f36690956f","ucl-d476a2f6-0880-49e0-898c-2e23f8952bc6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-806DC22881B6D9A0BA98B1B63B2AA3DB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Active Living"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Pædagogik og Samfund, Anvendt Forskning i Pædagogik og Samfund","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Pædagogik og Samfund, Læreruddannelsen i Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Breum Skov","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c168a51e-682a-42f8-8a57-fa705d9749e9","name":"Christiansen, Lars Breum","name_org":"Christiansen, Lars Breum Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-5142-3623","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Stjerne","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"82021dca-c7e0-4f60-8f0e-da84ddc9ee77","name":"Knudsen, Louise Stjerne","orcid":"0000-0003-4028-7125","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c6eebd4-6fdf-4819-bf31-6ae3c7e0b582","name":"Skovgaard, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6729-4988","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"smedegaardpau","last":"Smedegaard","locid":"1f611d29-034f-4665-9a21-2e53d6a07f16","name":"Smedegaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5451-9743","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e51dcd1e-96a8-4cd6-8014-d7f36690956f","ucl-d476a2f6-0880-49e0-898c-2e23f8952bc6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Inclusion of children with mental and physical disabilities in ordinary school PE – a conceptual framework","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-049621","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper compares the performance over time of seven different operation modes with the scope of investigating realistic degradation responses of a polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis (PEM WE) to different operation modes for grid-balancing services. Among these modes are constant current and constant voltage operations at different temperatures and current cycling operations, including a solar profile. It was found that faster current cycling improved the overall cell performance over the test period of 500 h, mainly due to a decrease in total ohmic resistance, which is also observed during the break-in phase preceding the experiments. Dynamic operation led to more severe fluoride emission from the catalyst binder, which improved the performance in terms of cell potential but could be a concern for long term degradation as membrane thinning promotes higher gas crossover. All other operation modes on the other hand suffered from an increase in total ohmic resistance, leading to an overall performance decrease, which is suspected to be due to the passivation of the Ti components. Higher operating temperatures were found to enhance cell performance, but are detrimental from a durability point of view since they exacerbate both membrane thinning and passivation processes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Fouda-Onana, Frédéric","Serre, Guillaume","Thoby, Dominique","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057987"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Frensch, Steffen Henrik"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Commissariat à l’énergie atomique et aux énergies alternatives"],"keyword":["Durability","Polymer electrolyte membrane","Water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of the operation mode on pem water electrolysis degradation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85073979737&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to acknowledge the support by Innovation Fund Denmark through the e-STORE project , Grant 4106-00025B ."],"id":"S01-000.00-057987","identifier":[{"id":"85073979737","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1b1a5e4a-73d2-4a1f-86af-0ecc95ce44d2"],"keyword":["Durability","Dynamic operation mode","Membrane degradation","Polymer electrolyte membrane","Water electrolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9CED2787411808CDF9327A74303E0B5C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"commissariat à l énergie atomique et aux énergies alternatives","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Commissariat à l’énergie atomique et aux énergies alternatives","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frédéric","key":"foudaonanapau","last":"Fouda-Onana","name":"Fouda-Onana, Frédéric","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guillaume","key":"serrepau","last":"Serre","name":"Serre, Guillaume","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominique","key":"thobypau","last":"Thoby","name":"Thoby, Dominique","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2019.09.169","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"57","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"29889-29898","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073979737"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1b1a5e4a-73d2-4a1f-86af-0ecc95ce44d2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Influence of the operation mode on PEM water electrolysis degradation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-057987","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Methanol is a liquid fuel that can be produced by renewable means and used in HT-PEM fuel cells, where a steam methanol reformer is used to provide a hydrogen rich mixture to the fuel cell. A steady-state non-isothermal model of the methanol steam reformer has been developed to predict the reformate contaminants and methanol conversion of the reformer. Kinetic reactions were based on a Langmuir-Hinshelwood model considering the methanol steam reforming (MSR), water gas shift (WGS) and methanol decomposition (MD) reactions. Heat transfer between hot air and catalyst bed, as well as heat and mass transfer phenomena inside reformer were considered. The performance of the reformer in terms of methanol conversion and CO concentration has also been examined to study the effect of different operating conditions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhu, Jimin","Araya, Samuel Simon","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Pedersen, Thomas Egsgaard","Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072210"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-30","place":"Duisburg, de","start":"2019-08-27","title":"6th CARISMA International Conference on Medium and High Temperature Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cells","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CO concentration","HT PEMFC system","Methanol conversion","Methanol steam reforming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and experimental characterization of a methanol steam reformer for a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane ht pem fuel cell system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316715790/Poster.pptx","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-072210","ids":["aau-4c6ca6ca-0881-4995-8ef7-4cc9b9aeb25f"],"keyword":["CO concentration","HT-PEMFC system","Methanol conversion","Methanol steam reforming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-995DE6123162A0B833BDBDD38704EBA3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316715790/Poster.pptx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jimin","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"646bbb27-0236-46fb-9e23-beb875af834f","name":"Zhu, Jimin","orcid":"0000-0001-7889-4233","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Egsgaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8709485e-ae53-4a02-8991-90ce43b7e445","name":"Pedersen, Thomas Egsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4c6ca6ca-0881-4995-8ef7-4cc9b9aeb25f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and experimental characterization of a methanol steam reformer for a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane (HT-PEM) fuel cell system","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072210","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Polymer electrolyte membrane (PEM) degradation in electrolysis mode is simulated through a Fenton model that includes all major involved electrochemical reactions. Supportive experimental investigations on the effect of hydrogen peroxide and iron impurities are carried out in an ex-situ set-up, where the results are utilized to fit model parameters. The experiments reveal a high dependence of fluoride emission on iron concentration, which catalyzes the reaction, and identifies hydrogen peroxide as a necessary precursor for destructive hydroxyl radical formation. Simulations of in-situ operation reveal that elevated current is favorable in terms of lower fluoride emission, as the radicals are depleted by side reactions. Temperatures above 80∘C significantly accelerate membrane thinning, where the step from 80∘C to 90∘C more than doubles thinning after 500 h.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Serre, Guillaume","Fouda-Onana, Frédéric","Jensen, Henriette Casper","Christensen, Morten Lykkegaard","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089819"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CEA, LITEN, DEHT, F-38054, Grenoble, France"],"keyword":["Hydrogen peroxide"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of iron and hydrogen peroxide on membrane degradation for polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis computational and experimental investigation on fluoride emission","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/297983449/JPS_memdegrad.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-089819","identifier":[{"id":"85062429403","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-88b86351-a679-4ed4-833a-96105b685ce2"],"keyword":["Fenton reaction model","Fluoride emission rate","Hydrogen Peroxide","Membrane degradation modelling","PEM water electrolysis aging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-051ED3A7519EAD044E1ECBFF183C9850"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/297983449/JPS_memdegrad.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"cea liten deht f 38054 grenoble france","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CEA, LITEN, DEHT, F-38054, Grenoble, France","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guillaume","key":"serrepau","last":"Serre","name":"Serre, Guillaume","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frédéric","key":"foudaonanapau","last":"Fouda-Onana","name":"Fouda-Onana, Frédéric","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henriette Casper","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ee119ae1-3b5d-4f5a-82ee-f1860c46cb7a","name":"Jensen, Henriette Casper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Lykkegaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"098b901d-fa2d-422d-ade3-d2cd21cb5a60","name":"Christensen, Morten Lykkegaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7671-817X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2019.02.076","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"54-62","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"420"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062429403"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88b86351-a679-4ed4-833a-96105b685ce2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of iron and hydrogen peroxide on membrane degradation for polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis : Computational and experimental investigation on fluoride emission","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089819","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In order to understand the thermal behaviour of a lithium-ion battery, the heat generation within the cell should be determined. The entropic heat coefficient is necessary to determine for the heat generation calculation. The entropic heat coefficient is one of the most important factors, which affects the magnitude of the reversible heat. The purpose of this research is to analyze and investigate the effect of different parameters on the entropic coefficient of lithium titanate oxide batteries. In this research, a lithium ion pouch cell was examined in both charging and discharging situations. The state of charge levels range was considered from 10% to 90%, and vice versa, in 10% increments. The temperature levels vary from 5 °C to 55 °C and the voltage levels vary from 1.5 V to 2.8 V. The effect of different parameters such as initial temperature, state of charge, thermal cycle, time duration for thermal cycles, and procedure prior to the thermal cycle on the entropic coefficient of lithium titanate oxide batteries were investigated. It was concluded that there is a strong influence of the battery cell state of charge on the entropic heat coefficient compared with other parameters.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091351"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Madani, Seyed Saeed"],"keyword":["Entropic heat coefficient","Lithium titanate oxide batteries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an experimental analysis of entropic coefficient of a lithium titanate oxide battery","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en12142685","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091351","identifier":[{"id":"85068825243","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8e109717-0bda-42a3-9e36-df7483b8f336"],"keyword":["Entropic heat coefficient","Lithium titanate oxide batteries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-255185B64FAD87EBFB64CB85EA779030"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/311597907/energies_12_02685.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en12142685","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en12142685","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"14","journal":"Energies","pages":"1-10","paperid":"2685","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068825243"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8e109717-0bda-42a3-9e36-df7483b8f336"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An experimental analysis of entropic coefficient of a lithium titanate oxide battery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091351","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The resistance is one of the parameters that describes the performance of Lithium-ion (Li-ion) batteries, as it offers information about the battery efficiency and its power capability. However, similar to other performance parameters of Li-ion batteries, the resistance is dependent on the operating conditions and increases while the battery is aging. Traditionally, to capture these dependencies, Li-ion cells are aged at different conditions using synthetic mission profiles and periodically the aging tests are stopped in order to measure the resistance at standard conditions. Most of the times, even though accurate information about the resistance behavior is obtained, they do not reflect the behavior from real-life applications. Thus, in this work we propose a method for extracting, modelling, and predicting the resistance directly from the battery dynamic mission profile. While the extraction mainly relied on data manipulation and bookkeeping, the modelling and subsequent prediction of the resistance used a log-linear model.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vilsen, Søren Byg","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-105401"],"event":{"end":"2019-10-03","place":"Baltimore, us","start":"2019-09-29","title":"2019 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery degradation","Dynamic aging profile","Lithium ion battery","Log linear model","Resistance estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting lithium ion battery resistance degradation using a log linear model","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316557646/PID6006633_7.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-105401","identifier":[{"id":"85076772349","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bef26f15-17d0-4b86-99b3-44573a658eb2"],"keyword":["Battery Degradation","Dynamic aging profile","Lithium-ion battery","Log-linear model","Resistance estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FEE5A7109A2F1281124222A02F1A600"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316557646/PID6006633_7.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences, Statistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Byg","key":"vilsenpau","last":"Vilsen","locid":"b5209c84-7990-4da8-9a0b-684bbd14a377","name":"Vilsen, Søren Byg","orcid":"0000-0002-9718-8147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce.2019.8912770","eisbn":["9781728103952"],"isbn":["9781728103969"],"issn":["23293721"],"pages":"1136-1143","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2019 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076772349"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bef26f15-17d0-4b86-99b3-44573a658eb2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Predicting Lithium-ion Battery Resistance Degradation using a Log-Linear Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-105401","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The world-wide increasing demand for protein has lead to intensive search for sustainable alternative protein sources for monogastrics. Protein extracted from grass and forage legumes have the potential to become such source. However, the nutritional quality may depend on plant source, harvest-and processing conditions. Two studies with ileal-cannulated pigs fed concentrates with crude protein (CP) contents of 33-38% of DM separated from perennial ryegrass (PRG), red clover (RC), and lucerne (LU) had standardized ileal digestibilities of indispensable amino acids of 62-81, except Cys which ranged 13-37%; lower than of reference soybean meal (SBM). Higher CP content of the concentrates by improved harvest and processing technology may increase the nutritional quality. Such optimization is required for green biomass to be both environmentally and economically competitive as feed protein","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lærke, Helle Nygaard","Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","Ambye-Jensen, Morten","Jensen, Søren Krogh","Sørensen, J. F.","Nørgaard, Jan Værum","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-176554"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lærke, Helle Nygaard"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DuPont - US"],"keyword":["Amino acids","Biorefinery","Digestibility","Protein quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extracts of green biomass as source of protein for pigs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85101943343","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-176554","identifier":[{"id":"85101943343","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-52c9308e-f3fa-4c1a-8841-4e5e514d2007"],"keyword":["amino acids","biorefinery","digestibility","monogastric","protein quality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7722DB9F50259FD2626BFA8CA405C53B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"dupont us","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DuPont - US","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H. N.","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","name_org":"Lærke, H. N.","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"stødkildepau","last":"Stødkilde","locid":"7edb699b-a75e-48cd-a351-9ee9e1321d4d","name":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","name_org":"Stødkilde, L.","orcid":"0000-0001-9434-0118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"ambyejensenpau","last":"Ambye-Jensen","locid":"9f74b922-bac9-44db-b3a3-31c9b450ebe8","name":"Ambye-Jensen, Morten","name_org":"Ambye-Jensen, M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Krogh","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7e493d39-1152-46c0-a822-c46e6ed914f3","name":"Jensen, Søren Krogh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J. F.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, J. F.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. V.","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"c19af48d-12e9-41fe-bb23-5435a0ff19a7","name":"Nørgaard, Jan Værum","name_org":"Nørgaard, J. V.","orcid":"0000-0002-0580-0184","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. E.Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","name_org":"Knudsen, K. E.Bach","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3920/978-90-8686-891-9_28","issn":["00712477"],"journal":"EAAP scientific series","pages":"177-178","publisher":"Wageningen Academic Publishers","status":"p","title":"EAAP scientific series","volume":"138"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101943343"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-52c9308e-f3fa-4c1a-8841-4e5e514d2007"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Extracts of green biomass as source of protein for pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-176554","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Novel sensitive methods for detection and monitoring of residual disease can improve postoperative risk stratification with implications for patient selection for adjuvant chemotherapy (ACT), ACT duration, intensity of radiologic surveillance, and, ultimately, outcome for patients with colorectal cancer (CRC). Objective: To investigate the association of circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) with recurrence using longitudinal data from ultradeep sequencing of plasma cell-free DNA in patients with CRC before and after surgery, during and after ACT, and during surveillance. Design, Setting, and Participants: In this prospective, multicenter cohort study, ctDNA was quantified in the preoperative and postoperative settings of stages I to III CRC by personalized multiplex, polymerase chain reaction-based, next-generation sequencing. The study enrolled 130 patients at the surgical departments of Aarhus University Hospital, Randers Hospital, and Herning Hospital in Denmark from May 1, 2014, to January 31, 2017. Plasma samples (n = 829) were collected before surgery, postoperatively at day 30, and every third month for up to 3 years. Main Outcomes and Measures: Outcomes were ctDNA measurement, clinical recurrence, and recurrence-free survival. Results: A total of 130 patients with stages I to III CRC (mean [SD] age, 67.9 [10.1] years; 74 [56.9%] male) were enrolled in the study; 5 patients discontinued participation, leaving 125 patients for analysis. Preoperatively, ctDNA was detectable in 108 of 122 patients (88.5%). After definitive treatment, longitudinal ctDNA analysis identified 14 of 16 relapses (87.5%). At postoperative day 30, ctDNA-positive patients were 7 times more likely to relapse than ctDNA-negative patients (hazard ratio [HR], 7.2; 95% CI, 2.7-19.0; P <.001). Similarly, shortly after ACT ctDNA-positive patients were 17 times (HR, 17.5; 95% CI, 5.4-56.5; P <.001) more likely to relapse. All 7 patients who were ctDNA positive after ACT experienced relapse. Monitoring during and after ACT indicated that 3 of the 10 ctDNA-positive patients (30.0%) were cleared by ACT. During surveillance after definitive therapy, ctDNA-positive patients were more than 40 times more likely to experience disease recurrence than ctDNA-negative patients (HR, 43.5; 95% CI, 9.8-193.5 P <.001). In all multivariate analyses, ctDNA status was independently associated with relapse after adjusting for known clinicopathologic risk factors. Serial ctDNA analyses revealed disease recurrence up to 16.5 months ahead of standard-of-care radiologic imaging (mean, 8.7 months; range, 0.8-16.5 months). Actionable mutations were identified in 81.8% of the ctDNA-positive relapse samples. Conclusions and Relevance: Circulating tumor DNA analysis can potentially change the postoperative management of CRC by enabling risk stratification, ACT monitoring, and early relapse detection..","author_count":38,"contributors":["Reinert, Thomas","Henriksen, Tenna Vesterman","Christensen, Emil","Sharma, Shruti","Salari, Raheleh","Sethi, Himanshu","Knudsen, Michael","Nordentoft, Iver","Wu, Hsin-Ta","Tin, Antony S","Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Vang, Søren","Shchegrova, Svetlana","Frydendahl, Amanda","Srinivasan, Ramya","Assaf, Zoe","Balcioglu, Mustafa","Olson, Alexander","Dashner, Scott","Hafez, Dina","Navarro, Samantha","Goel, Shruti","Rabinowitz, Matthew","Billings, Paul","Sigurjonsson, Styrmir","Dyrskjøt, Lars","Swenerton, Ryan","Aleshin, Alexey","Laurberg, Søren","Madsen, Anders Husted","Kannerup, Anne-Sofie","Stribolt, Katrine","Krag, Søren Rasmus Palmelund","Iversen, Lene Hjerrild","Gotschalck, Kåre Andersson","Lin, Cheng-Ho Jimmy","Zimmermann, Bernhard G","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-184836"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adjuvant chemotherapy","Colon cancer","Fluorouracil","Recurrence","Risk","Surgery","Surveillance","Survival"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of plasma cell free dna by ultradeep sequencing in patients with stages i to iii colorectal cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/197692926/jamaoncology_reinert_2019_oi_190019.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-184836","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6512280","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85065571391","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31070691","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000480303500008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-61388ffa-fcf7-4e48-962b-06f335d2c982"],"keyword":["ADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY","COLON-CANCER","FLUOROURACIL","RECURRENCE","RISK","SURGERY","SURVEILLANCE","SURVIVAL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CD4559FDECF8A163253D27D0C7A66945"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/197692926/jamaoncology_reinert_2019_oi_190019.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT",