"Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ed7d0f31-30f0-4658-aed3-5a8e36f9a481"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Obesity and metabolic risk factors associated with non-painful and painful diabetic polyneuropathy: a nationwide prevalence study of 5,249 patients in the Danish DD2 cohort","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-641259","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The Plan-Do-Study-Act (PDSA) method is widely used in quality improvement (QI) strategies. However, previous studies have indicated that methodological problems are frequent in PDSA-based QI projects. Furthermore, it has been difficult to establish an association between the use of PDSA and improvements in clinical practices and patient outcomes. The aim of this systematic review was to examine whether recently published PDSA-based QI projects show self-reported effects and are conducted according to key features of the method. METHODS: A systematic literature search was performed in the PubMed, Embase and CINAHL databases. QI projects using PDSA published in peer-reviewed journals in 2015 and 2016 were included. Projects were assessed to determine the reported effects and the use of the following key methodological features; iterative cyclic method, continuous data collection, small-scale testing and use of a theoretical rationale. RESULTS: Of the 120 QI projects included, almost all reported improvement (98%). However, only 32 (27%) described a specific, quantitative aim and reached it. A total of 72 projects (60%) documented PDSA cycles sufficiently for inclusion in a full analysis of key features. Of these only three (4%) adhered to all four key methodological features. CONCLUSION: Even though a majority of the QI projects reported improvements, the widespread challenges with low adherence to key methodological features in the individual projects pose a challenge for the legitimacy of PDSA-based QI. This review indicates that there is a continued need for improvement in quality improvement methodology.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren Valgreen","Laursen, Henrik Vitus Bering","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Bartels, Paul Daniel","Ehlers, Lars Holger","Mainz, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-094.74-011788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Knudsen, Søren Valgreen"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Haifa"],"keyword":["Delivery of Health Care standards","Health services research","Humans","PDSA","Plan do study act","Quality","Quality Improvement","Quality Improvement standards","Research Design standards"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Danish Clinical Registries, Denmark, Nrd. Fasanvej 57, 2000, Frederiksberg, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can quality improvement improve the quality of care a systematic review of reported effects and methodological rigor in plan do study act projects","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-019-4482-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The review was funded by Aalborg University, Denmark. The funding body had no influence on the study design, on the collection, analysis and interpretation of data or on the design of the manuscript."],"id":"S02-094.74-011788","identifier":[{"id":"31585540","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6778385","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85072942450","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f6b437fa-ca7c-4f3f-9d5e-892b13eaf929","sdu-af354b84-f9c3-46dc-a4fb-b35b0649f01e"],"keyword":["Delivery of Health Care/standards","Health services research","Humans","PDSA","Plan-do-study-act","Quality","Quality Improvement/standards","Quality improvement","Research Design/standards"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-189700CA11CFA17EE0FF496A574FC487"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/313316704/Knudsen_et_al_2919_Can_quality_improvement_improve_the_quality_of_care","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-019-4482-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/161194822/s12913_019_4482_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Clinical Health Services Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management, Danish Center for Healthcare Improvements (Business)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Clinical Registries, Denmark, Nrd. Fasanvej 57, 2000, Frederiksberg, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"il","key":"university of haifa","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"University of Haifa","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Valgreen","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"d59094b5-44a6-4398-9acf-f3f530e0504b","name":"Knudsen, Søren Valgreen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Vitus Bering","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"79f3767c-c51c-4756-95f3-2e1decc71e29","name":"Laursen, Henrik Vitus Bering","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Paaske","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"c3e8b374-a343-484a-a10d-e6550efbb8dc","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","orcid":"0000-0002-2787-0271","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul Daniel","key":"bartelspau","last":"Bartels","name":"Bartels, Paul Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Holger","key":"ehlerspau","last":"Ehlers","locid":"2ceddc99-bbe0-4721-8040-b4253e22468f","name":"Ehlers, Lars Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-6512-5566","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"mainzpau","last":"Mainz","locid":"fadbea42-81be-48a2-afb2-c868f9dfa4f5","name":"Mainz, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-0242-9233","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31585540"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12913-019-4482-6","issn":["14726963"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Health Services Research","pages":"1-10","paperid":"683","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Health Services Research","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072942450"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f6b437fa-ca7c-4f3f-9d5e-892b13eaf929","sdu-af354b84-f9c3-46dc-a4fb-b35b0649f01e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Can quality improvement improve the quality of care? : A systematic review of reported effects and methodological rigor in plan-do-study-act projects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.74-011788","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Recently, new augmented recording techniques have entered archaeological fieldwork. We review a major urban excavation in Ribe, Denmark, which has adopted a systematic use of 3D laser scanning and intensive soil and sediment micromorphological sampling as part of the excavation recording practice. Both methods represent a major advance in field documentation, achieving a higher degree of detail and precision for the recording of archaeological features. We argue that these technologies also challenge the current paradigm of single-context recording, i.e. the separation of layers and features as all-encompassing units of recording. First, 3D digital recording implies that contexts are defined in a more definite way than previously, with less flexibility for recursive revision. Second, micromorphology demonstrates how the strata separated in excavation are only a subset of those created in deposition. We call for a new approach, which takes into consideration the fact that excavation units do not always mirror depositional events, as assumed by single-context theory, and that different kinds of observations may not overlap, as assumed in single-context practice. Instead, interfaces, matrices and assemblages are restored as separate units to record and feed into the interpretation cycle. This may be described as recording metacontext: observations that go across or between contexts. We demonstrate how a systematic metacontext registration can lead to a manageable and more detailed excavation record, more faithful to the archaeologists’ observations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Feveile, Claus","Croix, Sarah","Knudsen, Maria","Qvistgaard, Sarah Skytte","Sindbæk, Søren Michael","Deckers, Pieterjan Sylvin","Wouters, Barbora"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-020318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["3D laser scanning","Micromorphology","Ribe","Viking Age Scandinavia"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single context metacontext and high definition archaeology integrating new standards of stratigraphic excavation and recording","src":["au","kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85067308490","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-020318","identifier":[{"id":"85067308490","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-691b3ae4-fe92-4f32-aa86-3e7b99761d20","kum-4120d383-7c73-47d6-825a-517203b73632"],"keyword":["3D laser scanning","Excavation methods","Micromorphology","Ribe","Single-context recording","Viking-Age Scandinavia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-618B246D7E556E3052888FEAF512B96C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, Museum of Southwest Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Centre for Urban Network Evolutions (UrbNet)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"feveilepau","last":"Feveile","locid":"d9f06346-e589-42f4-9787-989881636f70","name":"Feveile, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-4872-7909","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah","key":"croixpau","last":"Croix","locid":"85a83b94-b0c4-4abb-9161-cff867a1fa7a","name":"Croix, Sarah","orcid":"0000-0002-3956-6728","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pieterjan Sylvin","key":"deckerspau","last":"Deckers","locid":"9f3e38ce-eb83-42f3-a050-bafa686b274c","name":"Deckers, Pieterjan Sylvin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"4835c02b-468d-4de1-b6e3-72fa34b5548f","name":"Knudsen, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Skytte","key":"qvistgaardpau","last":"Qvistgaard","locid":"44a78936-76ba-422b-b35e-4f709031d3cd","name":"Qvistgaard, Sarah Skytte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Michael","key":"sindbækpau","last":"Sindbæk","locid":"65a936de-6831-47a4-9ce2-86f59dbfb019","name":"Sindbæk, Søren Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1254-1256","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbora","key":"wouterspau","last":"Wouters","locid":"fe531fd2-dc13-495d-b64b-479fab8d87c4","name":"Wouters, Barbora","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10816-019-09417-x","issn":["10725369","15737764"],"issn_org":["10725369"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Archaeological Method and Theory","pages":"1591-1631","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Archaeological Method and Theory","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067308490"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-691b3ae4-fe92-4f32-aa86-3e7b99761d20","kum-4120d383-7c73-47d6-825a-517203b73632"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Single Context, Metacontext, and High Definition Archaeology : Integrating New Standards of Stratigraphic Excavation and Recording","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-020318","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: The long-term effects of stress ulcer prophylaxis with pantoprazole are unknown in ICU patients. We report 1-year mortality outcome in the Stress Ulcer Prophylaxis in the Intensive Care Unit (SUP-ICU) trial. Methods: In the SUP-ICU trial, acutely admitted adult ICU patients at risk of gastrointestinal bleeding were randomised to intravenous pantoprazole 40 mg vs placebo (saline) once daily during their ICU stay. We assessed mortality at 1 year and did sensitivity analyses according to the trial protocol and statistical analysis plan. Results: A total of 3261 of the 3291 patients with available data (99.1%) were followed up at 1 year after randomisation; 1635 were allocated to pantoprazole and 1626 to placebo. At 1 year after randomisation, 610 of 1635 patients (37.3%) had died in the pantoprazole group as compared with 601 of 1626 (37.0%) in the placebo group (relative risk, 1.01; 95% confidence interval 0.92-1.10). The results were consistent in the sensitivity analysis adjusted for baseline risk factors and in those of the per-protocol population. We did not observe heterogeneity in the effect of pantoprazole vs placebo on 1-year mortality in the predefined subgroups, that is, patients with and without shock, mechanical ventilation, liver disease, coagulopathy, high disease severity (SAPS II > 53) or in medical vs surgical ICU patients. Conclusion: We did not observe a difference in 1-year mortality among acutely admitted adult ICU patients with risk factors for gastrointestinal bleeding allocated to stress ulcer prophylaxis with pantoprazole or placebo during the ICU stay. (The SUP-ICU trial was funded by Innovation Fund Denmark and others; ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT02467621).","author_count":25,"contributors":["Marker, Søren","Krag, Mette","Perner, Anders","Wetterslev, Jørn","Lange, Theis","Wise, Matt P","Borthwick, Mark","Bendel, Stepani","Keus, Frederik","Guttormsen, Anne Berit","Schefold, Joerg C","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Elkmann, Thomas","Bestle, Morten","Arenkiel, Bjørn","Laake, Jon H","Kamper, Maj K","Lång, Maarit","Pawlowicz-Dworzanska, Malgorzata B.","Karlsson, Sari","Liisanantti, Janne","Dey, Nilanjan","Knudsen, Heidi","Granholm, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander"],"cuid":["S03-093.62-005917"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["SUP-ICU trial investigators","the SUP-ICU trial investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Marker, Søren"],"country":["Australia","China","Finland","Netherlands","Norway","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiff University","Peking University","Tampere University","University of Bergen","University of Bern","University of Bristol","University of Eastern Finland","University of Groningen","University of Melbourne","University of Oslo","University of Oulu"],"keyword":["All cause mortality","Gastrointestinal bleeding","Intensive care unit","Long term follow up","Stress ulcer prophylaxis","Stress ulceration"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pantoprazole in icu patients at risk for gastrointestinal bleeding 000000000001 year mortality in the sup icu trial","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85069710617&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.62-005917","identifier":[{"id":"000478157900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"8506971061