ddc-f443-468f-906a-27e30a5c509a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pantoprazole in ICU patients at risk for gastrointestinal bleeding—1-year mortality in the SUP-ICU trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.62-005917","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Two different battery thermal management design for a battery cell is presented. The design is intended to represent the cooling procedures and heat transfer phenomena. Computational fluid dynamics were used for both steady-state simulation and time-dependent condition. Inside the battery, a lumped amount of volumetric heat source is considered. The determined heat generations data are taken from isothermal battery calorimeter experiments. Water was considered as cooling liquid. The design is simulated to distinguish the temperature gradient over surfaces of the cell. Furthermore, the temperature evolution outcomes are simulated. It was concluded that by using the liquid at 15 °C, at 8C discharge rate the temperature moderately declines with raising liquid flow rates, recording a maximum of 25 °C for the liquid at 15 °C.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thermal analysis of an indirect liquid cooling with different geometries for a lithium ion battery","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1149/09501.0105ecst","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054809","identifier":[{"id":"85081086703","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-10469d4b-c37a-405f-b20a-992fbd774b23"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7C215C0E0983E484F80C5790A3623565"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/09501.0105ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081086703"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-10469d4b-c37a-405f-b20a-992fbd774b23"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Thermal Analysis of an Indirect Liquid Cooling with Different Geometries for a Lithium-ion Battery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054809","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"CO 2 hydrogenation to methanol via the reverse water-gas shift (the CAMERE process) is an alternative method for methanol synthesis. High operating temperatures (600-800 °C) are required for the reverse water-gas shift (RWGS) process because of the thermodynamic limit. In this study, moderate temperatures (200-300 °C) were used for the RWGS part of the CAMERE process by the application of in situ water removal (ISWR). Thermodynamic analyses were conducted on this process using the Gibbs-free-energy-minimization method. The analyses show that by using ISWR with high water-removal fractions (e.g., 0.80-0.99), the CO 2 conversion of the RWGS part can be significantly improved at moderate operating temperatures. One-step CO 2 hydrogenation to methanol (CTM) with ISWR was also investigated, and it resulted in similar methanol yields. Both processes showed high potential and the ability to promote CO 2 hydrogenation to methanol through the use of ISWR.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-075451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CO2 hydrogenation","Membrane reactor","Methanol synthesis","Thermodynamic analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thermodynamic analyses of a moderate temperature process of carbon dioxide hydrogenation to methanol via reverse water gas shift with in situ water removal","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.iecr.9b01312","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-075451","identifier":[{"id":"85066989795","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5787a755-3c8a-47df-8292-fba5addccb57"],"keyword":["CAMERE process","CO2 hydrogenation","In situ water removal","Membrane reactor","Methanol synthesis","Sorption-enhanced reaction process","Thermodynamic analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4063B0E669984AE9D879E33424965425"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448877764/Thermodynamic_analyses_of_a_moderate_temperature_process_of_carbon_dioxide_hydrogenation_to_methanol_via_reverse_water_gas_shift_with_in_situ_water_removal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.iecr.9b01312","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.iecr.9b01312","issn":["08885885","15205045"],"issn_org":["08885885"],"issue":"24","journal":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","pages":"10559-10569","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066989795"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5787a755-3c8a-47df-8292-fba5addccb57"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Thermodynamic Analyses of a Moderate-Temperature Process of Carbon Dioxide Hydrogenation to Methanol via Reverse Water–Gas Shift with In Situ Water Removal","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-075451","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Cooling of the lithium-Ion batteries is an important issue in electric vehicles industries. This paper introduces a simple analytical solution for the battery cooling by considering different parameters that affect the air and liquid cooling of lithium-Ion batteries. It was assumed that the cell dimension is 204mm*129mm.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-079260"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-28","place":"Brno, cz","start":"2019-08-25","title":"20th International Conference on Advanced Batteries, Accumulators and Fuel Cells, ABAF 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an analytical solution for lithium ion batteries cooling","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85081083856&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-079260","identifier":[{"id":"85081083856","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-64979d39-d202-4189-86e0-90e188f0f837"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-341A80F9BEEC1E21BB6C7707434DF605"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/09501.0075ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"75-79","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081083856"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-64979d39-d202-4189-86e0-90e188f0f837"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An Analytical Solution for Lithium-Ion Batteries Cooling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-079260","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The determination of coulombic efficiency of the lithium-ion batteries can contribute to comprehend better their degradation behavior. In this research, the coulombic efficiency and capacity loss of three lithium-ion batteries at different current rates (C) were investigated. Two new battery cells were discharged and charged at 0.4 C and 0.8 C for twenty times to monitor the variations in the aging and coulombic efficiency of the battery cell. In addition, prior cycling was applied to the third battery cell which consist of charging and discharging with 0.2 C, 0.4 C, 0.6 C, and 0.8 C current rates and each of them twenty times. The coulombic efficiency of the new battery cells was compared with the cycled one. The experiments demonstrated that approximately all the charge that was stored in the battery cell was extracted out of the battery cell, even at the bigger charging and discharging currents. The average capacity loss rates for discharge and charge during 0.8 C were approximately 0.44% and 0.45% per cycle, correspondingly.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-082511"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Madani, Seyed Saeed"],"keyword":["Capacity loss","Coulombic efficiency","Lithium ion batteries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of current rate and prior cycling on the coulombic efficiency of a lithium ion battery","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries5030057","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-082511","identifier":[{"id":"85071735732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6f8a7983-fd4d-4d82-b7fd-18c597d6e7f5"],"keyword":["Capacity loss","Coulombic efficiency","Lithium-ion batteries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8C4206570178DB6FBAA5F3223F00A16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/310247968/batteries_05_00057.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries5030057","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/batteries5030057","issn":["23130105"],"issue":"3","journal":"Batteries","paperid":"57","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Batteries","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071735732"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6f8a7983-fd4d-4d82-b7fd-18c597d6e7f5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Effect of Current Rate and Prior Cycling on the Coulombic Efficiency of a Lithium-Ion Battery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-082511","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The effect of ferric ions on cell performance of proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer (PEM WE)was studied by injecting Fe2(SO4)3 solution into DI water to prepare different Fe3+ concentrations contamination (1, 10, 100 parts per million (ppm, molar ratio)). Results showed that there was clear cell performance decay with increasing Fe3+ concentrations, and the cell stopped running at 100 ppm Fe3+ concentration in feed water. With increasing temperature, the cell performance increased for a short period. With low Fe3+ concentrations, cell performance decreased with increasing current density, but with 10 ppm Fe3+ concentration and higher current density of 2A/cm2 , cell performance was enhanced. Therefore, both temperature and current density can make positive contributions to improve cell performance under the condition of contaminated feed water.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Li, Na","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114378"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Li, Na"],"keyword":["PEM electrolysis","Performance degradation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of fe sup 000000000003 sup contamination in feed water on proton exchange membrane electrolyzer performance","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448878859/paper_A.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to acknowledge the financial support from Innovation Fund Denmark through the e-STORE project, Grant No. 4106-00025B . Na Li appreciates China Scholarship Council for the financial support. Appendix A"],"id":"S01-000.00-114378","identifier":[{"id":"85064539380","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dd330c67-d837-4533-86b1-554309972693"],"keyword":["Ferric ion contamination","PEM electrolysis","Performance degradation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6DDC0EE9AB9C700A7B1767EC7DEECF86"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448878859/paper_A.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Na","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"a89f75fa-7daa-406c-b5ea-5307f875cdf0","name":"Li, Na","orcid":"0000-0002-1267-6185","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2019.04.015","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"26","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"12952-12957","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064539380"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dd330c67-d837-4533-86b1-554309972693"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The effect of Fe <sup>3+</sup> contamination in feed water on proton exchange membrane electrolyzer performance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-114378","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
