opment research - an innovative research design for school based physical activity","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649929","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"One of the reasonable possibilities to investigate the battery behaviour under various temperature and current conditions is the development of a model of the lithium-ion batteries and then by employing the simulation technique to anticipate their behaviour. This method not only can save time but also they can predict the behaviour of the batteries through simulation. In this investigation, a three-dimensional model is developed to simulate thermal and electrochemical behaviour of a 13Ah lithium-ion battery. In addition, the temperature dependency of the battery cell parameters was considered in the model in order to investigate the influence of temperature on various parameters such as heat generation during battery cell operation. Maccor automated test system and isothermal battery calorimeter were used as experimental setup to validate the thermal model, which was able to predict the heat generation rate and temperature at different positions of the battery. The three-dimensional temperature distributions which were achieved from the modelling and experiment were in well agreement with each other throughout the entire of discharge cycling at different environmental temperatures and discharge rates.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069535"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lithium titanate oxide batteries","Thermal behaviour","Thermal modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulation of thermal behaviour of a lithium titanate oxide battery","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en12040679","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-069535","identifier":[{"id":"000460667700105","type":"wos"},{"id":"85061962375","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-43528b75-fc0f-4f09-837e-ded89ba983fa"],"keyword":["Lithium titanate oxide batteries","Thermal behaviour","Thermal modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B880D17EB1B89463DDE963C915C5175C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/329218931/energies_12_00679.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en12040679","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en12040679","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"4","journal":"Energies","pages":"1-15","paperid":"679","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061962375"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-43528b75-fc0f-4f09-837e-ded89ba983fa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Simulation of Thermal Behaviour of a Lithium Titanate Oxide Battery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069535","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) have gained considerable attention owing to their unique structures with tunable three-dimensional porous frameworks and numerous applications. The large surface area and great porosity make MOFs a potential electrode material for lithium-ion batteries (LIBs). However, the impact of lithiation/delithiation on structures of MOFs have been investigated to very limited extent. In this presentation, we report our initial advances in understanding the relationship between the structure of MOFs and the electrochemical performances. We prepared Al-MOF and combined it with graphene sheets by a facile self-assembly process. Compared with pristine MOFs, the composite showed a prolonged orderdisorder transition and greatly enhanced electrochemical performances. During the lithiation/delithiation process, the bulk MOFs crystal particles were transformed into fine amorphous powders, which were protected by the graphene sheets from detaching from the electrical current collector. The enhancement of the electrochemical performances is ascribed to the effect of the synergy between the order-disorder transition in MOF particles and the addition of graphene sheets. The order-disorder transition remarkably increased the capacity of the composite from 60 to 400 mAh g-1 at a current density of 100 mA g-1 after 100 cycles. At the current density of 1000 mA g-1, the composite experienced an order-disorder transition (activation process) in the first 500 cycles and then the capacity exhibited a decay of 0.02% per cycle in the subsequent 500 cycles, suggesting its high cycling stability. This work implies that the order-disorder engineering concept can be used to improve both the capacity and the cycling stability of anode materials with great volume changes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gao, Chengwei","Wang, Peixing","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Zhang, Yanfei","Yue, Yuanzheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094342"],"event":{"end":"2019-06-17","place":"Beijing, cn","start":"2019-06-15","title":"4th International Conference on Nanoenergy and Nanosystems 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qilu University of Technology"],"keyword":["Anode","Lithium ion batteries","Metal organic framework","Order disorder transition"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mof graphene composite with long order disorder process for high performance lithium ion batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309411355/Abstract_for_NENS_2019_Chengwei_Gao.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094342","ids":["aau-98cc2063-416c-4864-946f-f40ee6c00060"],"keyword":["Anode","Lithium ion batteries","Metal-organic Framework","Order-Disorder Transition"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-78D74A5DA7F269C6888D5C14026DB0CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309411355/Abstract_for_NENS_2019_Chengwei_Gao.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Disordered Materials","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"qilu university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qilu University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chengwei","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","locid":"901c925a-036f-4f5e-98f2-26f6c905f793","name":"Gao, Chengwei","orcid":"0000-0001-7105-2121","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peixing","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Peixing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanfei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yanfei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yuanzheng","key":"yuepau","last":"Yue","locid":"613ef41c-8216-4aa7-b1c9-b24d1fccfdbc","name":"Yue, Yuanzheng","orcid":"0000-0002-6048-5236","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-98cc2063-416c-4864-946f-f40ee6c00060"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"MOF-graphene composite with long order-disorder process for high-performance lithium ion batteries","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094342","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"It is known that impurities, especially metal ions in feed water, can cause significant performance degradation of proton exchange membrane water electrolyser (PEM WE). In this study, the long-term effect of iron ion contamination on single cell performance is investigated by introducing Fe2 (SO4)3 into deionized water fed in PEM WE. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) and polarization curve results were recorded during the test. Results show that with 1 parts per million (ppm, molar ratio) Fe3+ contamination at the test condition of 0.5 A/cm2 and 60 °C, the cell performance degrades severely, especially the charge and mass transfer resistances increase significantly with time. Resistance values obtained through fitting the experiment data with equivalent circuit model were used to better describe the results. The results of Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM) and Energy Dispersive X-ray Spectroscopy (EDX) test illustrate that the existence of Fe3+ promote the Fenton reaction, leading to the production of chemical radicals, which degrade the membrane and anode catalyst layer severely.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Li, Na","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095685"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Li, Na"],"keyword":["Long term operation","PEM water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term contamination effect of iron ions on cell performance degradation of proton exchange membrane water electrolyser","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448878924/paper_B.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to acknowledge the financial support from Innovation Fund Denmark through the e-STORE project, Grant No. 4106-00025B . Na Li appreciates China Scholarship Council for the financial support."],"id":"S01-000.00-095685","identifier":[{"id":"85067796547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9d522188-aa4b-4b5d-8a30-c410ba63c16e"],"keyword":["Fe contamination","Fluoride emission","Long-term operation","MEA degradation mechanism","PEM water electrolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-913EAC07E1030042EAF95543B4978B9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448878924/paper_B.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermofluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Na","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"a89f75fa-7daa-406c-b5ea-5307f875cdf0","name":"Li, Na","orcid":"0000-0002-1267-6185","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2019.226755","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"1-7","paperid":"226755","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"434"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067796547"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9d522188-aa4b-4b5d-8a30-c410ba63c16e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Long-term contamination effect of iron ions on cell performance degradation of proton exchange membrane water electrolyser","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-095685","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
