{"abstract":"IntroductionThe stable, ultra-long duration of action of insulin degludec (degludec) minimizes fluctuations in glucose-lowering activity over the daily (24-h) dosing period, and comparative studies with other basal insulins suggest that these properties translate into a lower risk of hypoglycemia at equivalent levels of glycemic control. Results from the real-world European multicenter, retrospective chart review study of 2550 patients with type 1 and type 2 diabetes (T1D and T2D) in routine clinical care EU-TREAT (NCT02662114) showed that patients benefited from improved glycemic control and significantly reduced rates of hypoglycemia following a switch to degludec.MethodsIn this post hoc analysis, EU-TREAT patients were stratified into good (7.5% HbA1c), intermediate (>7.5 to 8.5% HbA1c), and poor (>8.5% HbA1c) glycemic control at baseline to investigate the possibility of differential benefits, either improved control or reduced risk of hypoglycemia, whichever the need. Changes in HbA1c, overall hypoglycemia, and total insulin dose from baseline to 6 and 12months follow-up were assessed for each group.ResultsFor both T1D and T2D patients, those in good initial control experienced significant reductions in rates of hypoglycemia and total insulin dose following the switch, without compromising control. Those in poor initial control achieved significant improvements in HbA1c with no change in rates of hypoglycemia or total insulin dose.ConclusionThis analysis expands the findings of EU-TREAT by showing differential changes in the clinical endpoints depending on particular need. It introduces the possibility that the differential benefits of degludec could address two of the renowned clinical challenges faced when treating diabetes: improving glycemic control for optimal management of T1D and titrating insulin dose in T2D, both without fear of increased hypoglycemia.Trial RegistrationClinicalTrials.gov, NCT02662114.FundingNovo Nordisk A/S.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tentolouris, Nikolaos","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Lapolla, Annunziata","Wolden, Michael Lyng","Haldrup, Steffen","Schultes, Bernd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-207720"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tentolouris, Nikolaos"],"country":["Greece","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Athens","University of Padova"],"keyword":["Glycemic control","Hypoglycemia","IMPACT","Insulin degludec","Observational Study","Post hoc analysis","Productivity","Type 1 diabetes","Type 2","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"switching real world diabetes patients to degludec from other basal insulins provides different clinical benefits according to their baseline glycemic control","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12325-019-00916-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-207720","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6824376","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85063058770","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000466110000019","type":"wos"},{"id":"30879256","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-89658eec-5e3c-4208-bdad-26d4a1ee0198"],"keyword":["EU-TREAT study","GLARGINE U100","Glycemic control","Hypoglycemia","IMPACT","Insulin degludec","Long-acting insulin","Observational study","PRODUCTIVITY","Post hoc analysis","TYPE-2","Type 1 diabetes","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-68E65938361980A0545ADDC2FFD34A6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12325-019-00916-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/195876760/Tentolouris2019_Article_SwitchingReal_WorldDiabetesPat.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gr","key":"university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - SDCA-Steno Diabetes Center Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of padova","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padova","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaos","key":"tentolourispau","last":"Tentolouris","name":"Tentolouris, Nikolaos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Soren T.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","name_org":"Knudsen, Soren T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Annunziata","key":"lapollapau","last":"Lapolla","name":"Lapolla, Annunziata","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Lyng","key":"woldenpau","last":"Wolden","name":"Wolden, Michael Lyng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"haldruppau","last":"Haldrup","name":"Haldrup, Steffen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernd","key":"schultespau","last":"Schultes","name":"Schultes, Bernd","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30879256"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12325-019-00916-7","issn":["0741238X","18658652"],"issn_org":["0741238X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Advances in Therapy","pages":"1201-1210","publisher":"Adis","status":"p","title":"Advances in Therapy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063058770"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Novo Nordisk","Other Research","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-89658eec-5e3c-4208-bdad-26d4a1ee0198"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Switching \"Real-World\" Diabetes Patients to Degludec from Other Basal Insulins Provides Different Clinical Benefits According to Their Baseline Glycemic Control","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-207720","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Aging is among the most complex phenotypes that occur in humans. Identifying the interplay between different age-associated features is undoubtedly critical to our understanding of aging and thus age-associated diseases. Nevertheless, what constitutes human aging is not well characterized. Towards this end, we mined millions of PubMed abstracts for age-associated terms, enabling us to generate a detailed description of the human aging phenotype. We discovered age-associated features in clusters that can be broadly associated with previously defined hallmarks of aging, consequently identifying areas where interventions could be pursued. Importantly, we validated the newly discovered features by manually verifying the prevalence of these features in combined cohorts describing 76 million individuals, allowing us to stratify features in aging that appear to be the most prominent. In conclusion, we propose a comprehensive landscape of human aging: the human aging phenome.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andreassen, Søren Norge","Ezra, Michael Ben","Scheibye-Knudsen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-420222"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aging","Data mining","Phenome","Phenotype"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a defined human aging phenome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/aging.102166","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-420222","identifier":[{"id":"31408848","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85071011874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2ced35e0-7a93-4f2a-b902-2c2f14644ec3"],"keyword":["Aging","Data mining","Phenome","Phenotype"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C486D7B88DFC287D72D2211B685B1D37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/226792015/erfctPCCz3afLYYtF.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/aging.102166","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Norge","key":"andreassenpau","last":"Andreassen","locid":"4dc31e1f-cb7c-44bd-a979-a4118879b801","name":"Andreassen, Søren Norge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Ben","key":"ezrapau","last":"Ezra","locid":"3ec9f908-e99d-4aab-9dee-6dec99d08ce8","name":"Ezra, Michael Ben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"scheibyeknudsenpau","last":"Scheibye-Knudsen","locid":"161fd11a-45bf-427a-8307-f111b06510bb","name":"Scheibye-Knudsen, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31408848"],"pub":{"doi":"10.18632/aging.102166","issn":["19454589"],"issue":"15","journal":"Aging","pages":"5786-5806","status":"p","title":"Aging","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071011874"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ced35e0-7a93-4f2a-b902-2c2f14644ec3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A defined human aging phenome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-420222","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present PADE, a visual analytics tool for collaboratively exploring data from patient administrative systems on large touch displays in meeting contexts. Large touch displays are becoming commercially available, but we have limited knowledge about how they might be used in such a context. We designed PADE based on inquiries with healthcare data analysts tasked with understanding expenses in a healthcare system that serve about six million residents. Our goals in designing the system were to enable the analysts to collaboratively construct hypotheses, quickly generate and execute strategies, and support ad hoc discussions and QA sessions during meetings. We created a set of interaction techniques that let users create new visualizations and combine parts of existing ones. We illustrate these possibilities through a collaborative analysis scenario. Finally, we discuss the possibilities and limitations of PADE, its interaction techniques, and future work in this direction.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren","Hornbæk, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505501"],"event":{"end":"2019-10-20","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2019-10-20","title":"10th IEEE Workshop on Visual Analytics in Healthcare, VAHC 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human centered computing","Information visualization","Interaction techniques","Large displays","Multi touch","Visualization systems and tools","multiple views"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pade supporting collaborative visual analysis of patient administrative systems data with a large touch display system","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-505501","identifier":[{"id":"85078203338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bbc4ff0c-eea2-4b6d-a57e-b3e64bfaf227"],"keyword":["Human-centered computing","Information visualization","Interaction techniques","Large displays","Visualization systems and tools","multi-touch","multiple views"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC1F52E1E035FCBB6C1C651B487538B1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"hornbækpau","last":"Hornbæk","locid":"148d1e88-e306-46e1-9218-f420470b1ce1","name":"Hornbæk, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0001-8742-1198","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vahc47919.2019.8945039","eisbn":["9781728124230"],"pages":"9-16","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE Workshop on Visual Analytics in Healthcare, VAHC 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078203338"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bbc4ff0c-eea2-4b6d-a57e-b3e64bfaf227"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PADE : Supporting Collaborative Visual Analysis of Patient Administrative Systems Data with a Large Touch Display System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505501","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Despite the high number of frozen embryo transfer (FET) cycles being conducted (190 000 cycles/year) in Europe, the timing of blastocyst transfer and the use of luteal phase progesterone support in modified natural cycle FET (mNC-FET) in assisted reproductive technologies are controversial. In mNC-FET, the timing of blastocyst warming and transfer is determined according to the time of implantation in a natural cycle, aiming to reach blastocyst endometrial synchronicity. However, the optimal day of blastocyst transfer following ovulation trigger is not determined. In addition, the value of luteal phase support to maintain the endometrium remains uncertain. Thus, there is a need to identify the optimal timing of blastocyst warming and transfer and the effect of luteal phase support in a randomised controlled trial design. The aim of this randomised controlled trial is to investigate if progesterone supplementation from the early luteal phase until gestational age 8 weeks is superior to no progesterone supplementation and to assess if blastocyst warming and transfer 6 days after ovulation trigger is superior to 7 days after ovulation trigger in mNC-FET with live birth rates as the primary outcome. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: Multicentre, randomised, controlled, single-blinded trial including 604 normo-ovulatory women aged 18-41 years undergoing mNC-FET with a high-quality blastocyst originating from their first to third in vitro fertilisation/intracytoplasmic sperm injection cycle. Participants are randomised (1:1:1:1) to either luteal phase progesterone or no luteal phase progesterone and to blastocyst warming and transfer on day 6 or 7 after human chorionic gonadotropin trigger. Only single blastocyst transfers will be performed. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study is approved by the Danish Committee on Health Research Ethics (H-18025839), the Danish Medicines Agency (2018061319) and the Danish Data Protection Agency (VD-2018-381). The results of the study will be publicly disseminated. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: The study is registered in EudraCT (2018-002207-34) and on ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT03795220); Pre-results.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Saupstad, Marte","Freiesleben, Nina La Cour","Skouby, Sven Olaf","Andersen, Lars Franch","Knudsen, Ulla Breth","Petersen, Kathrine Birch","Husth, Merete","Egeberg, Anne","Petersen, Morten Rønn","Ziebe, Søren","Andersen, Anders Nyboe","Løssl, Kristine","Pinborg, Anja"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-004580"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technologies","Endometrial preparation","Frozen embryo transfer","Progesterone","Subfertility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Kvindeafdelingen, Aarhus University Hospital, Horsens Hospital and the Institute of Clinical Medicine, Horsens, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preparation of the endometrium and timing of blastocyst transfer in modified natural cycle frozen thawed embryo transfers mnc fet a study protocol for a randomised controlled multicentre trial","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-031811","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.97-004580","identifier":[{"id":"85076676549","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6924851","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31843833","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-5e62e9dc-8206-4908-bb03-1879ee596fad","au-bebff87b-7cea-4933-8842-d073362fa29d","ku-946063b3-211e-429a-8599-f111dc2d98cb"],"keyword":["assisted reproductive technologies","endometrial preparation","frozen embryo transfer","progesterone","subfertility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B570BA0027CE50E2BD50B7A2600A7CB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-031811","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/240197658/e031811.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/319869175/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medici