{"abstract":"I rapporten evalueres, hvorvidt BOLIG+ i Søborg lever op til målet om at være Danmarks første reelt energineutrale etageboligbyggeri. Evalueringen bygger på målinger af energi og indeklima i bygningen gennem halvandet år samt interview af beboerne. Desuden vurderes, om det projekterede energibehov er sammenligneligt med det målte energiforbrug. Rapporten er afslutningen på en lang udvikling og realisering af BOLIG+ konceptet, som startede under Energy Camp 2005.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Søren Østergaard","Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054090"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energiforbrug","Etageboliger","Evaluering","Indeklima","Målinger","energineutralt byggeri"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bolig energineutrale etageboliger måling og evaluering","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/682577616/SBi_2018-12.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054090","ids":["aau-0ddd3632-90b1-4246-80a9-c53112a2cce9"],"keyword":["Målinger","energiforbrug","energineutralt byggeri","etageboliger","evaluering","indeklima"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7AE702610CCB46C4A8CA3333952BA6C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/682577616/SBi_2018-12.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Department of Energy Performance, Indoor Environment and Sustainability of Buildings (EIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Energy Efficiency Research Group (SBi)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Energy and Sustainability in Buildings","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Energy and Buildings Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Østergaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Søren Østergaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Bjarne","key":"wittchenpau","last":"Wittchen","locid":"4cf412e5-ace3-40f6-8f0c-dfef37eac83d","name":"Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","orcid":"0000-0002-3305-5409","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik N.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7f5e707b-235a-4e71-ae71-e9278e7aa2ba","name":"Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","name_org":"Knudsen, Henrik N.","orcid":"0000-0002-3196-7279","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["05739985"],"issue":"12","pages":"140","place":"København","publisher":"Statens Byggeforskningsinstitut, Aalborg Universitet","repno":"SBI-rapport, No. 12","series":"SBI-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0ddd3632-90b1-4246-80a9-c53112a2cce9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"BOLIG+ Energineutrale etageboliger : Måling og evaluering","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054090","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates the influence of the cell compression of a PEM water electrolysis cell. A small single cell is therefore electrochemically analyzed by means of polarization behavior and impedance spectroscopy throughout a range of currents (0.01 A cm−2 to 2.0 A cm−2) at two temperatures (60°C and 80°C) and eight compressions (0.77 MPa–3.45 MPa). Additionally, a computational model is utilized to support the analysis. The main findings are that cell compression has a positive effect on overall cell performance due to decreased contact resistances, but is subject to optimization. In this case, no signs of severe mass transport problems due to crushed transport layers are visible in either polarization curves or impedance plots, even at high currents. However, a Tafel plot analysis revealed more than one slope throughout the current range. The change in the Tafel slope is therefore discussed and connected to the electrochemical reaction or an ohmic contribution from a non-electrode component.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Olesen, Anders Christian","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-066006"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Contact resistance","Impedance spectroscopy","Model validation","PEM water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model supported characterization of a pem water electrolysis cell for the effect of compression","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/268292085/Frensch_model_supported_characterization_2017_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-066006","identifier":[{"id":"85040682266","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-36eb5a2c-15e4-4c7a-976b-ee96901d90a8"],"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Contact resistance","Impedance spectroscopy","Model validation","PEM water electrolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18A20D8CE8CFA8D0DA34AD01D8E37194"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/268292085/Frensch_model_supported_characterization_2017_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.electacta.2018.01.040","issn":["00134686","18733859"],"issn_org":["00134686"],"journal":"Electrochimica Acta","pages":"228-236","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electrochimica Acta","volume":"263"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040682266"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-36eb5a2c-15e4-4c7a-976b-ee96901d90a8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Model-supported characterization of a PEM water electrolysis cell for the effect of compression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-066006","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Instrumental knowledge utilization is the process whereby knowledge influences political decision making. Such processes are complex and, consequently, hard to measure. Nevertheless, knowing what determines degrees of knowledge utilization is a prerequisite for fostering more evidence-based policy making. Numerous factors that contribute to, and co-determine, knowledge utilization are beyond the reach of researchers, but among the factors that researchers can influence, one variable has been presented as being crucial: the degree to which researchers adapt their research to meet the demands of intended knowledge users. In other words, making their research comprehensible, operational, realistic in terms of interventions and implications, and appealing to users. Drawing on the conceptual work of Landry, Amara, and Lamari, this paper develops a new, and more direct, measurement of adaptation. This measurement is subsequently applied in an analysis employing the Degrees of Knowledge Utilization (DoKU) scale and, thus, extending Knudsen’s five-year meta-evaluation related to the Danish pesticide area. Surprisingly, the statistical tests show that degrees of adaptation have no significant influence on degrees of knowledge utilization.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Bøllingtoft Knudsen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-134962"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evidence based policy making","Research adaptation"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testing whether adaptation to use increases degrees of instrumental knowledge utilization from evaluation reports","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85050256561","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-134962","identifier":[{"id":"85050256561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-09f1ffa2-cdb7-4b3d-889c-0edc57a06ef7"],"keyword":["evidence-based policy making","instrumental knowledge utilization","knowledge-to-policy","research adaptation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBAD516600FD43465600AA86FBD041FD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"bøllingtoftknudsenpau","last":"Bøllingtoft Knudsen","locid":"2439dd14-a6dd-434d-89bd-8970f3126ced","name":"Bøllingtoft Knudsen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1936724418786341","issn":["19367244"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Applied Social Science","pages":"98-112","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Social Science","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050256561"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-09f1ffa2-cdb7-4b3d-889c-0edc57a06ef7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Testing Whether Adaptation to Use Increases Degrees of Instrumental Knowledge Utilization from Evaluation Reports","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-134962","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
