e":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"ramharterpau","last":"Ramharter","name":"Ramharter, Michael","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitta Ruth","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"50fca07c-ced4-453a-a26a-0d664c9a1491","name":"Knudsen, Birgitta R.","name_org":"Knudsen, Birgitta Ruth","orcid":"0000-0002-3484-3802","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29515150"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-018-22378-7","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","pages":"4122","paperid":"4122","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048288590"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","zymonostics aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2a17249a-104b-4cc2-8cf9-8d951db0858e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Detection of the Malaria causing Plasmodium Parasite in Saliva from Infected Patients using Topoisomerase I Activity as a Biomarker","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-153457","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: In 2011, the role of Point of Care Ultrasound (POCUS) was defined as one of the top five research priorities in physician-provided prehospital critical care and future research topics were proposed; the feasibility of prehospital POCUS, changes in patient management induced by POCUS and education of providers. This systematic review aimed to assess these three topics by including studies examining all kinds of prehospital patients undergoing all kinds of prehospital POCUS examinations and studies examining any kind of POCUS education in prehospital critical care providers. Methods and results: By a systematic literature search in MEDLINE, EMBASE, and Cochrane databases, we identified and screened titles and abstracts of 3264 studies published from 2012 to 2017. Of these, 65 studies were read in full-text for assessment of eligibility and 27 studies were ultimately included and assessed for quality by SIGN-50 checklists. No studies compared patient outcome with and without prehospital POCUS. Four studies of acceptable quality demonstrated feasibility and changes in patient management in trauma. Two studies of acceptable quality demonstrated feasibility and changes in patient management in breathing difficulties. Four studies of acceptable quality demonstrated feasibility, outcome prediction and changes in patient management in cardiac arrest, but also that POCUS may prolong pauses in compressions. Two studies of acceptable quality demonstrated that short (few hours) teaching sessions are sufficient for obtaining simple interpretation skills, but not image acquisition skills. Three studies of acceptable quality demonstrated that longer one- or two-day courses including hands-on training are sufficient for learning simple, but not advanced, image acquisition skills. Three studies of acceptable quality demonstrated that systematic educational programs including supervised examinations are sufficient for learning advanced image acquisition skills in healthy volunteers, but that more than 50 clinical examinations are required for expertise in a clinical setting. Conclusion: Prehospital POCUS is feasible and changes patient management in trauma, breathing difficulties and cardiac arrest, but it is unknown if this improves outcome. Expertise in POCUS requires extensive training by a combination of theory, hands-on training and a substantial amount of clinical examinations - a large part of these needs to be supervised.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bøtker, Morten Thingemann","Jacobsen, Lars","Rudolph, Søren Steemann","Knudsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240754"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bøtker, Morten Thingemann"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian Air Ambulance Foundation"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Critical care","Dyspnea","Education","Point of care","Prehospital","Systematic review","Trauma","Ultrasound"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of point of care ultrasound in prehospital critical care a systematic review","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85049076885","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240754","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6019293","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29940990","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85049076885","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c34b8f8c-e571-4312-a553-4a6d982dc3ab"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Critical care","Dyspnea","Education","Point of care","Prehospital","Systematic review","Trauma","Ultrasound"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D58E1ECC762B2AF86D634DCEC72A600E"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Præhospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian air ambulance foundation","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Air Ambulance Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Emergency Medical Services","National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Thingemann","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"626b3aff-f412-4560-a703-9ad54f701c09","name":"Bøtker, Morten Thingemann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Steemann","key":"rudolphpau","last":"Rudolph","name":"Rudolph, Søren Steemann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"6522c177-3a63-48df-bf6f-ed3dc9761ec1","name":"Knudsen, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29940990"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13049-018-0518-x","issn":["17577241"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","paperid":"51","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049076885"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c34b8f8c-e571-4312-a553-4a6d982dc3ab"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The role of point of care ultrasound in prehospital critical care : A systematic review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240754","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, there has been an increasing interest in immunomodulatory therapy as a means to treat various conditions, including infectious diseases. For instance, Toll-like receptor (TLR) agonists have been evaluated for treatment of genital herpes. However, although the TLR7 agonist imiquimod was shown to have antiviral activity in individual patients, no significant effects were observed in clinical trials, and the compound also exhibited significant side effects, including local inflammation. Cytosolic DNA is detected by the enzyme cyclic GMP-AMP (2'3'-cGAMP) synthase (cGAS) to stimulate antiviral pathways, mainly through induction of type I interferon (IFN)s. cGAS is activated upon DNA binding to produce the cyclic dinucleotide (CDN) 2'3'-cGAMP, which in turn binds and activates the adaptor protein Stimulator of interferon genes (STING), thus triggering type I IFN expression. In contrast to TLRs, STING is expressed broadly, including in epithelial cells. Here we report that natural and non-natural STING agonists strongly induce type I IFNs in human cells and in mice in vivo, without stimulating significant inflammatory gene expression. Systemic treatment with 2'3'-cGAMP reduced genital herpes simplex virus (HSV) 2 replication and improved the clinical outcome of infection. More importantly, local application of CDNs at the genital epithelial surface gave rise to local IFN activity, but only limited systemic responses, and this treatment conferred total protection against disease in both immunocompetent and immunocompromised mice. In direct comparison between CDNs and TLR agonists, only CDNs acted directly on epithelial cells, hence allowing a more rapid and IFN-focused immune response in the vaginal epithelium. Thus, specific activation of the STING pathway in the vagina evokes induction of the IFN system but limited inflammatory responses to allow control of HSV2 infections in vivo.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Skouboe, Morten Kelder","Knudsen, Alice","Reinert, Line S.","Boularan, Cedric","Lioux, Thierry","Perouzel, Eric","Thomsen, Martin K.","Paludan, Søren R"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-248326"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Invivogen Europe"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sting agonists enable antiviral cross talk between human cells and confer protection against genital herpes in mice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85046497048","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-248326","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5897032","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85046497048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29608601","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d04836e7-d37b-4712-9d4f-9757fa85a4ef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CDF1E2D08C56FAA20E34C07DACCDBAC"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"invivogen europe","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Invivogen Europe","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten K","key":"skouboepau","last":"Skouboe","locid":"4478c894-2e40-4156-a638-eda3af306e66","name":"Skouboe, Morten Kelder","name_org":"Skouboe, Morten K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alice","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"9710e8a8-9e26-4f5d-8d16-9c3df83fcc4b","name":"Knudsen, Alice","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line S","key":"reinertpau","last":"Reinert","locid":"6395427d-ea95-403c-9322-fe41de8e0021","name":"Reinert, Line S.","name_org":"Reinert, Line S","orcid":"0000-0002-8317-0886","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cedric","key":"boularanpau","last":"Boularan","name":"Boularan, Cedric","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thierry","key":"liouxpau","last":"Lioux","name":"Lioux, Thierry","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eric","key":"perouzelpau","last":"Perouzel","name":"Perouzel, Eric","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin K","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f96a0a95-170a-4113-ae44-38ecf582517b","name":"Thomsen, Martin K.","name_org":"Thomsen, Martin K","orcid":"0000-0002-5055-7531","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren R","key":"paludanpau","last":"Paludan","locid":"1322e859-c715-4278-8805-ea36e987dd5e","name":"Paludan, Søren R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29608601"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.ppat.1006976","issn":["15537366","15537374"],"issn_org":["15537366"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLoS Pathogens","paperid":"e1006976","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLoS Pathogens","title_org":"P L o S Pathogens","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046497048"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d04836e7-d37b-4712-9d4f-9757fa85a4ef"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"STING agonists enable antiviral cross-talk between human cells and confer protection against genital herpes in mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-248326","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this study we present the test-retest reliability of pre-intervention EEG/ERP (electroencephalogram/event-related potentials) data across four recording intervals separated by a washout period (18-22 days). POz-recording-reference EEG/ERP (28 sites, average reference) were recorded from thirty-two healthy male participants. Participants were randomly allocated into different intervention sequences, each with four intervention regimens: 10 mg vortioxetine, 20 mg vortioxetine, 15 mg escitalopram and Placebo. We report classical EEG spectra: δ (1-4 Hz), θ (4-8 Hz), α (8-12 Hz), β (12-30 Hz), γ1 (30-45 Hz) and γ2 (45-80 Hz) of resting state and vigilance-controlled, and of auditory steady state response, as well as ERP components N100, P200 and P300 in auditory oddball task and error related negativity (ERN) and error positivity (Pe) in hybrid flanker task. Reliability was quantified using intra-class correlation coefficient (ICC). We found that θ, α and β of continuous EEG were highly reliable (ICCs ≥ 0.84). Evoked power of other tasks demonstrated larger variability and less reliability compared to the absolute power of continuous EEG. Furthermore, reliabilities of ERP measures were lower compared to those of the EEG spectra. We saw fair to excellent reliability of the amplitude of the components such as Pe (0.60-0.82) and P300 (0.55-0.80). Moreover, blood tests confirmed that there was no measurable drug carry-over from the previous intervention. The results support that EEG/ERP is reliable across four recording intervals, thus it can be used to assess the effect of different doses and types of drugs with CNS effects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ip, Cheng-Teng","Ganz, Melanie","Ozenne, Brice","Sluth, Lasse B","Gram, Mikkel","Viardot, Geoffrey","l'Hostis, Philippe","Danjou, Philippe","Knudsen, Gitte M","Christensen, Søren R"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-006564"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Biotrial"],"keyword":["Crossover design","EEG","ERP","Repeated measurements","Test retest reliability"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Coaze IVS, Kronhjorten 129, DK-9530 Støvring, Denmark"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pre intervention test retest reliability of eeg and erp over four recording intervals","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpsycho.2018.09.007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-006564","identifier":[{"id":"85055038708","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30253197","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-87b6bb89-ab82-489b-bfc9-cda546f0853f","ku-10cf3551-49a5-4b94-8031-27efb7b4d2d0"],"keyword":["Crossover design","EEG","ERP","Repeated measurements","Test-retest reliability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C03E31DF0BF66286481336F9BDA367FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpsycho.2018.09.007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/210835141/1_s2.0_S0167876018300606_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/294253248/1_s2.0_S0167876018300606_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSu