{"abstract":"In this study, a small PEM water electrolysis single cell set up is utilized to extract information about degradation mechanisms. The major parameter of interest is the operational condition, which is changed from constant to cycling current input signal throughout a period of just over 1000h. The cell shows a high reversible share of the voltage increase at constant operation, which builds up slowly and can be recovered through a short interruption of cell operation. Impedance measurements reveal a considerable change in ohmic contributions as well as electrochemical performance over time. The model supported IV curve analysis backs the impedance data and reveals an increase in contact resistances. At the same time, the electrochemical surface area on both electrodes is reduced. The results suggest that dynamic operation may be beneficial for cell performance and therefore operational cost, while a degradation rate of 164.1µV*h−1 was calculated.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Olesen, Anders Christian","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058451"],"event":{"end":"2018-05-17","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2018-05-13","title":"Symposium on Oxygen or Hydrogen Evolution Catalysis for Water Electrolysis 4 - 233rd ECS Meeting","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model supported analysis of degradation phenomena of a pem water electrolysis cell under dynamic operation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85050405416&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-058451","identifier":[{"id":"85050405416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1cc8d2bd-59de-46d2-ae4a-78a735828646"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D246C524FE8D5306066E9C37E98F159"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H.","key":"xupedh","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, H.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"K. E.","key":"ayerspedh","last":"Ayers","name":"Ayers, K. E.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"P. J.","key":"kuleszapedh","last":"Kulesza","name":"Kulesza, P. J.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"G.","key":"wupedh","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, G.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08511.0037ecst","edition":"11","eisbn":["9781607685395"],"issn":["19386737"],"pages":"37-45","publisher":"Electrochemical Society Inc.","series":"ECS Transactions","status":"p","subtitle":"Oxygen or Hydrogen Evolution Catalysis for Water Electrolysis 4","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050405416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1cc8d2bd-59de-46d2-ae4a-78a735828646"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Model-supported analysis of degradation phenomena of a PEM water electrolysis cell under dynamic operation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058451","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The water balance of a proton exchange membrane fuel cell (PEMFC) can provide valuable insight into the state of the fuel cell. The most commonly applied method to measure the water balance is the knock-out method where the flaw gas of anode and/or cathode is cooled down and the condensed amount of water is weighed and compared to the amount of product water, while over the past years our group has developed a new method by applying hot wire anemometry at the anode outlet. In this work, a comparison between the knock-out and hot wire methods is experimentally demonstrated for 3.8 kW water-cooled PEMFC stack. The stack is run under wet conditions at different current densities and stoichiometric ratios. The hot-wire method has shown a higher sensitivity and an instant response for the measured water balance. Meanwhile, the knock-out method showed less sensitivity, much slower time response, and higher inaccuracies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Liso, Vincenzo","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063432"],"event":{"end":"2018-10-04","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2018-09-30","title":"ECS and SMEQ Joint International Meeting","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparison of the proton exchange membrane fuel cell water balance measured simultaneously with the water knock out method and hot wire anemometry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85058280706&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-063432","identifier":[{"id":"85058280706","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2e2997a8-5624-42e7-a14d-a9ce51864de8"],"keyword":["Diagnostics and Characterization Methods","MEA Design","Modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E526B0FAFEE4ACA99B1BFCB873B8870"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vincenzo","key":"lisopau","last":"Liso","locid":"c3a177b3-f874-40d3-984a-f1587412ec79","name":"Liso, Vincenzo","orcid":"0000-0002-7597-3849","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08613.0199ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"13","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"199-209","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058280706"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2e2997a8-5624-42e7-a14d-a9ce51864de8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Comparison of the Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell Water Balance Measured Simultaneously with the Water Knock-out Method and Hot Wire Anemometry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063432","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"State of charge (SOC) is one of the most important parameters in battery management systems, as it indicates the available battery capacity at every moment. There are numerous battery model-based methods used for SOC estimation, the accuracy of which depends on the accuracy of the model considered to describe the battery dynamics. The SOC estimation method proposed in this paper is based on an Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) and nonlinear battery model which was parameterized using extended laboratory tests performed on several 13 Ah lithium titanate oxide (LTO)-based lithium-ion batteries. The developed SOC estimation algorithm was successfully verified for a step discharge profile at five different temperatures and considering various initial SOC initialization values, showing a maximum SOC estimation error of 1.16% and a maximum voltage estimation error of 44 mV. Furthermore, by carrying out a sensitivity analysis it was showed that the SOC and voltage estimation error are only slightly dependent on the variation of the battery model parameters with the SOC.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stroe, Ana-Irina","Meng, Jinhao","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Teodorescu, Remus","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071016"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian"],"keyword":["Equivalent electrical circuit","Extended Kalman filter","Hybrid pulse power characterization test","Lithium ion batteries","Model parametrization","State of charge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of battery parametric uncertainties on the state of charge estimation of lithium titanate oxide based batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en11040795","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-071016","identifier":[{"id":"85045388412","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4852b8c1-aefc-4914-bae9-5972a5c2d0eb"],"keyword":["Equivalent electrical circuit","Extended Kalman Filter","Hybrid pulse power characterization test","Lithium titanate oxide (LTO) batteries","Lithium-ion batteries","Model parametrization","State of charge"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE9EB1CE5E9C3F742760289A5F007902"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en11040795","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/11/4/795","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/286918960/energies_11_00795.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ana-Irina","key":"stroeanairinapau","last":"Stroe","locid":"e6ff6bac-362f-4fd1-b46c-d5f62d1e2c1a","name":"Stroe, Ana-Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-8254","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinhao","key":"mengjinhaopau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Jinhao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroedanielioanpau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskimaciejjozefpau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescuremuspau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærsørenknudsenpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en11040795","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"4","journal":"Energies","pages":"1-19","paperid":"795","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045388412"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4852b8c1-aefc-4914-bae9-5972a5c2d0eb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Influence of Battery Parametric Uncertainties on the State-of-Charge Estimation of Lithium Titanate Oxide-Based Batteries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071016","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The present work focuses on reducing the complexities involved in the mass production of HT-PEM fuel cell systems integrated with a methanol reformer. Different break-in procedures are investigated on a single HT-PEMFC. The work is divided into two parts, the first in which different break-in times are tested in order to reduce the usual break-in time of around 100 h, and the second one, where simulated reformed fuel is tested during and after break-in to understand the impact on degradation over time. In this study, two set of tests are carried out with different break-in times, the normal break-in (100 h), intermediate break-in (30 and 50 h) and no break-in (0 h). After break-in, all the cells were subjected to a load cycling profile between 0.2 and 0.6 A cm−2 with 5 min at each current density. The test was then carried out to compare the cell performance over time when the break-in is carried out with simulated reformed gas having a composition of 64.7% H2, 21.3% CO2, 12% H2O and 2% CH3OH. The break-in time for this test was 100 h. The cells are operated at 0.2 A cm−2 during break-in and thereafter at 0.6 A cm−2 under normal operation. The cell performance and impedance change over time is analyzed. The different resistances are deduced using equivalent circuit models and analyzed to understand the changes occurring in the MEA during break-in and how they affect the durability of an HT-PEMFC. The degradation rate for the different operating strategy is calculated from the voltage trajectory over time. The comparison of degradation and break-in time suggests that the normal break-in induces a uniform ohmic resistance changes in the cell over time, while the fast cycling leads to non-uniform changes in resistances. However, the performance and degradation are not significantly affected over 750 h test. The test with simulated reformed fuel indicates that the break-in with pure H2 is important for longer durability when operation thereafter is with reformed fuel. The cell with reformed fuel break-in degrades much faster compared to the cell with H2 break-in.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomas, Sobi","Araya, Samuel Simon","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088361"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomas, Sobi"],"keyword":["Break in","EIS","HT PEMFC","Load cycling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating different break in procedures for reformed methanol high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85048962212&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the Innovation Fund Denmark for funding the work through the 4M project (Project no. 845010 ). The authors are also thankful to Serenergy for providing the MEA used in the experiments."],"id":"S01-000.00-088361","identifier":[{"id":"85048962212","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-83a9a761-ea59-4f6d-ba98-317422233fc6"],"keyword":["Break-in","EIS","HT-PEMFC","Load cycling","Reformed fuel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-645166C5182D676DDFA5A0C2C7709B37"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2018.05.166","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"31","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"14691-14700","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048962212"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-83a9a761-ea59-4f6d-ba98-317422233fc6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Investigating different break-in procedures for reformed methanol high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088361","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"To comprehend the thermal behaviour, performance and the dependency of the affecting parameters such as state-of-charge and C-rates on the heat loss, efficiency, heat flux and maximum temperature of a commercial pouch type lithium-ion battery under various working conditions, different loading were applied to the battery. The capacity of the battery is 13Ah, which has a lithium titanate oxide based anode from Altairnano. Surface temperatures and heat flux of the Lithium-ion battery cell were measured by means of isothermal battery calorimeter. Different charge and discharge current pulses with different C-rates at ten state of charge (SOC) levels from 10% to 90% SOC were applied to the battery by using Maccor automated test system. It was concluded that heat losses demonstrated approximately decreasing pattern from 10 % SOC to 90% SOC.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092100"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of the effect of state of charge and c rates on the heat loss and efficiency of a lithium ion battery","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-092100","identifier":[{"id":"85061041022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-90b2aa9b-524e-4673-9ad8-b35fd3a32953"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-199FD741C497B5C1E9FB1FD4A0152D1E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08701.0051ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"51-58","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061041022"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-90b2aa9b-524e-4673-9ad8-b35fd3a32953"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Investigation of the Effect of State-of-Charge and C-Rates on the Heat Loss and Efficiency of a Lithium-Ion Battery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092100","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The cocoa industry in Ghana is the second largest in the world, and it generates huge amounts of cocoa pod husks, which currently represent a disposal problem as no significant use has been found for them. The husks are rich in potassium, which may be used for alkaline hydrocolloid extraction from red seaweeds. Chemical and rheological properties of κ-carrageenan from Kappaphycus alvarezii and the Ghanaian red seaweed Hypnea musciformis extracted by KOH (benchmark) or by a cocoa pod husk ash solution were compared. Similar extraction yields and successful modification of the seaweed hydrocolloids with 3,6-anhydro-galactopyranose and sulfate contents of 37–38 and 16–17%, respectively, were obtained with cocoa pod husk ash and KOH extraction. Gel strengths of the κ-carrageenans were also similar: G′ at 25 °C were 5780 Pa with cocoa pod husk ash and 5930 Pa with KOH. These findings have implications for industrial waste biomass utilization and sustainable green growth development of seaweed hydrocolloid processing in Ghana.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rhein-Knudsen, Nanna","Ale, Marcel Tutor","Rasmussen, Søren","Kamp, Simon Kjær","Bentil, Joseph A.","Meyer, Anne S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327887"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rhein-Knudsen, Nanna"],"keyword":["Carrageenan","Circular economy","Potassium","Rheology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alkaline extraction of seaweed carrageenan hydrocolloids using cocoa pod husk ash","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/151915361/Rhein_Knudsen_et_al_2018_Biomass_Conversion_and_Biorefinery.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327887","identifier":[{"id":"85051245892","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4e4cbfc2-8656-4996-a000-5834369db515"],"keyword":["Carrageenan","Circular economy","Hypnea","Potassium","Rheology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF876AB60DFB17E14AE929B7613E6142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/151915361/Rhein_Knudsen_et_al_2018_Biomass_Conversion_and_Biorefinery.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nanna","key":"rheinknudsenpau","last":"Rhein-Knudsen","locid":"2dad40ef-2cde-4133-a1e3-6e5036c45ebc","name":"Rhein-Knudsen, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0001-6695-346X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marcel Tutor","key":"alepau","last":"Ale","locid":"b60ff798-327e-4caa-ab83-5e000a4081b1","name":"Ale, Marcel Tutor","orcid":"0000-0001-6417-0891","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon Kjær","key":"kamppau","last":"Kamp","name":"Kamp, Simon Kjær","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joseph A.","key":"bentilpau","last":"Bentil","locid":"c1f51758-3a3b-4f3b-b1ce-bacdc2ff0a13","name":"Bentil, Joseph A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne S.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"1e9f4759-72d8-4d52-94ec-ce192ffca184","name":"Meyer, Anne S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8910-9931","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13399-018-0305-y","issn":["21906815","21906823"],"issn_org":["21906815"],"issue":"3","journal":"Biomass Conversion and Biorefinery","pages":"577-583","publisher":"Springer Verlag","status":"p","title":"Biomass Conversion and Biorefinery","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051245892"],"sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","8. Decent Work and Economic Growth","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4e4cbfc2-8656-4996-a000-5834369db515"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Alkaline extraction of seaweed carrageenan hydrocolloids using cocoa pod husk ash","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327887","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Anthracyclines remain a cornerstone in the treatment of primary and advanced breast cancer (BC). This study has evaluated the predictive value of a multigene mRNA-based drug response predictor (DRP) in the treatment of advanced BC with epirubicin. The DRP is a mathematical method combining in vitro sensitivity and gene expression with clinical genetic information from > 3000 clinical tumor samples. METHODS: From a DBCG cohort, 140 consecutive patients were treated with epirubicin between May 1997 and November 2016. After patient informed consent, mRNA was isolated from archival formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded primary breast tumor tissue and analyzed using Affymetrix arrays. Using time to progression (TTP) as primary endpoint, the efficacy of epirubicin was analyzed according to DRP combined with clinicopathological data collected retrospectively from patients' medical records. Statistical analysis was done using Cox proportional hazards model stratified by treatment line. RESULTS: Median TTP was 9.3 months. The DRP was significantly associated to TTP (P = 0.03). The hazard ratio for DRP scores differing by 50 percentage points was 0.55 (95% CI -0.93, one-sided). A 75% DRP was associated with a median TTP of 13 months compared to 7 months following a 25% DRP. Multivariate analysis showed that DRP was independent of age and number of metastases. CONCLUSION: The current study prospectively validates the predictive capability of DRP regarding epirubicin previously shown retrospectively allowing the patients predicted to be poor responders to choose more effective alternatives. Randomized prospective studies are needed to demonstrate if such an approach will lead to increased overall survival.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Buhl, Anna Sofie Kappel","Christensen, Troels Dreier","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Nelausen, Knud Mejer","Balslev, Eva","Knoop, Ann Søegaard","Brix, Eva Harder","Svensson, Else","Glavicic, Vesna","Luczak, Adam Andrzej","Langkjer, Sven Tyge","Linnet, Søren","Jakobsen, Erik Hugger","Bogovic, Jurij","Ejlertsen, Bent","Rasmussen, Annie","Hansen, Anker","Knudsen, Steen","Nielsen, Dorte","Jensen, Peter Buhl"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-007424"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Buhl, Anna Sofie Kappel"],"keyword":["Adult","Advanced breast cancer","Aged","Biomarkers Pharmacological","Breast Neoplasms drug therapy","Disease Free Survival","Disease Progression","Epirubicin","Epirubicin administration dosage","Female","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic drug effects","Humans","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Proteins genetics","Precision medicine","Predictive biomarker","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","RNA Messenger genetics","Retrospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting efficacy of epirubicin by a multigene assay in advanced breast cancer within a danish breast cancer cooperative group dbcg cohort a retrospective prospective blinded study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-018-4918-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-007424","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6208899","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000447497300013","type":"wos"},{"id":"85051496722","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30099635","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["