","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Impact of red and processed meat and fibre intake on treatment outcomes among patients with chronic inflammatory diseases: protocol for a prospective cohort study of prognostic factors and personalised medicine.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-095.87-011719","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, a simplified model of a Polymer Electrolyte Membrane (PEM) water electrolysis cell is presented and compared with experimental data at 60 °C and 80 °C. The model utilizes the same modelling approach used in previous work where the electrolyzer cell is divided in four subsections: cathode, anode, membrane and voltage. The model of the electrodes includes key electrochemical reactions and gas transport mechanism (i.e., H2, O2 and H2O) whereas the model of the membrane includes physical mechanisms such as water diffusion, electro osmotic drag and hydraulic pressure. Voltage was modelled including main overpotentials (i.e., activation, ohmic, concentration). First and second law efficiencies were defined. Key empirical parameters depending on temperature were identified in the activation and ohmic overpotentials. The electrodes reference exchange current densities and change transfer coefficients were related to activation overpotentials whereas hydrogen ion diffusion to Ohmic overvoltages. These model parameters were empirically fitted so that polarization curve obtained by the model predicted well the voltage at different current found by the experimental results. Finally, from the efficiency calculation, it was shown that at low current densities the electrolyzer cell absorbs heat from the surroundings. The model is not able to describe the transients involved during the cell electrochemical reactions, however these processes are assumed relatively fast. For this reason, the model can be implemented in system dynamic modelling for hydrogen production and storage where components dynamic is generally slower compared to the cell electrochemical reactions dynamics.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liso, Vincenzo","Savoia, Giorgio","Araya, Samuel Simon","Cinti, Giovanni","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061002"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Perugia"],"keyword":["Hydrogen production","PEM electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling and experimental analysis of a polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis cell at different operating temperatures","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en11123273","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-061002","identifier":[{"id":"85059317419","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-25b2cbbd-7eab-4236-ae64-89f23eabd8f6"],"keyword":["PEM electrolysis","hydrogen production","modelling of experimental validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-13C47C77DA296FFFE22D168B3D4AFEE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/293736112/energies_11_03273_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en11123273","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of perugia","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Perugia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vincenzo","key":"lisopau","last":"Liso","locid":"c3a177b3-f874-40d3-984a-f1587412ec79","name":"Liso, Vincenzo","orcid":"0000-0002-7597-3849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giorgio","key":"savoiapau","last":"Savoia","name":"Savoia, Giorgio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"cintipau","last":"Cinti","name":"Cinti, Giovanni","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en11123273","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"12","journal":"Energies","pages":"1-18","paperid":"3273","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059317419"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-25b2cbbd-7eab-4236-ae64-89f23eabd8f6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modelling and Experimental Analysis of a Polymer Electrolyte Membrane Water Electrolysis Cell at Different Operating Temperatures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061002","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper reviews different methods for determination of thermal parameters of lithium ion batteries. Lithium ion batteries are extensively employed for various applications owing to their low memory effect, high specific energy, and power density. One of the problems in the expansion of hybrid and electric vehicle technology is the management and control of operation temperatures and heat generation. Successful battery thermal management designs can lead to better reliability and performance of hybrid and electric vehicles. Thermal cycling and temperature gradients could have a considerable impact on the lifetime of lithium ion battery cells. Thermal management is critical in electric vehicles (EVs) and good thermal battery models are necessary to design proper heating and cooling systems. Consequently, it is necessary to determine thermal parameters of a single cell, such as internal resistance, specific heat capacity, entropic heat coefficient, and thermal conductivity in order to design suitable thermal management system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064580"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lithium ion batteries","Thermal modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"review of parameter determination for thermal modeling of lithium ion batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries4020020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064580","identifier":[{"id":"000436154600007","type":"wos"},{"id":"85048166540","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-322c63da-5be8-4d96-a601-e8db7a996ef5"],"keyword":["Lithium ion batteries","Parameter determination","Thermal modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-56FDAB6CD099894F7B364EF8623BD76A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/282779325/Review_of_Parameter_Determination_for_Thermal_Modeling_of_Lithium_Ion_Batterie.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries4020020","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed","key":"saeedmadanipau","last":"Saeed Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","name_org":"Saeed Madani, Seyed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/batteries4020020","issn":["23130105"],"issue":"2","journal":"Batteries","pages":"1-16","paperid":"20","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Batteries","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048166540"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-322c63da-5be8-4d96-a601-e8db7a996ef5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Review of Parameter Determination for Thermal Modeling of Lithium Ion Batteries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064580","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"A single polymer electrolyte membrane (PEM) water electrolyzer cell is operated under cathode no flow, co flow and counter flow water recirculation configurations in this work. The polarization curve, electrochemical impedance spectrum (EIS) and current and temperature distribution of the PEM water electrolyzer cell are measured under different water recirculation configurations and different applied current. The experimental results show that the counter flow configuration brings about slightly better cell performance and lower polarization resistance. The current and temperature distribution pattern are similar under different water recirculation configurations and different applied current. However, the current and temperature distribution is more uniform under counter flow water recirculation, which could be related with smaller different between inlet and outlet water temperature under counter flow configuration.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zhou, Fan","Al Shakhshir, Saher","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076495"],"event":{"end":"2018-05-17","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2018-05-13","title":"233rd ECS Meeting","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"current and temperature distribution measurement in a polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolyzer cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-076495","identifier":[{"id":"85056830103","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5b200c0b-84d7-402a-b885-f9aaaa75d643"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-022FDF07D8087A2CE8CFEAC47B96DEB4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"874642c9-fe83-4b87-9b5e-9b8088c39e6a","name":"Zhou, Fan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08513.1005ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"13","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"1005-1012","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"85"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056830103","2-s2.0-85056836578"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5b200c0b-84d7-402a-b885-f9aaaa75d643"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Current and Temperature Distribution Measurement in a Polymer Electrolyte Membrane Water Electrolyzer Cell","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076495","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Present research explores the impact of operation temperature of a 13 Ah Lithium Titanate Oxid (LTO) battery cell on its thermal behaviour, heat generation, efficiency and maximum temperature. To accomplish this, different loading patterns were applied to the battery. The experiments were accomplished at several charge and discharge cycles with different C-rates. Temperature is one of the most important parameters, which have considerable impacts on the capacity, cycle lifetime, safety and heat generation of lithium-ion batteries. Notwithstanding, the comprehensive and detail effects of temperature on the heat generation of lithium-ion batteries is necessary to be found. The findings allow us to have a better understanding of the effect of temperature on different aspect of the battery ell. The results will assists on a precise thermal model of the battery. In addition it can improve the thermal management systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Schaltz, Erik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101365"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study of temperature impacts on a lithium ion battery thermal behaviour by employing isothermal calorimeter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-101365","identifier":[{"id":"85061067356","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b0db64e0-fc74-406a-9341-fe6aa4e1e542"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5044702DD4A9AB97A8C80CEEF0C91983"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seyed Saeed","key":"madanipau","last":"Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08701.0295ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"295-305","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061067356"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b0db64e0-fc74-406a-9341-fe6aa4e1e542"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Study of Temperature Impacts on a Lithium-Ion Battery Thermal Behaviour by Employing Isothermal Calorimeter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101365","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"A major challenge in affluent societies is the increase in disorders related to gut and metabolic health. Chronic over nutrition by unhealthy foods high in energy, fat, and sugar, and low in dietary fibre is a key environmental factor responsible for this development, which may cause local and systemic inflammation. A low intake of dietary fibre is a limiting factor for maintaining a viable and diverse microbiota and production of short-chain fatty acids in the gut. A suppressed production of butyrate is crucial, as this short-chain fatty acid (SCFA) can play a key role not only in colonic health and function but also at the systemic level. At both sites, the mode of action is through mediation of signalling pathways involving nuclear NF-κB and inhibition of histone deacetylase. The intake and composition of dietary fibre modulate production of butyrate in the large intestine. While butyrate production is easily adjustable it is more variable how it influences gut barrier function and inflammatory markers in the gut and periphery. The effect of butyrate seems generally to be more consistent and positive on inflammatory markers related to the gut than on inflammatory markers in the peripheral tissue. This discrepancy may be explained by differences in butyrate concentrations in the gut compared with the much lower concentration at more remote sites.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Lærke, Helle Nygaard","Hedemann, Mette Skou","Nielsen, Tina Skau","Ingerslev, Anne Krog","Nielsen, Ditte Søvsø Gundelund","Theil, Peter Kappel","Purup, Stig","Hald, Stine","Schioldan, Anne Grethe","Marco, Maria L.","Gregersen, Søren","Hermansen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-136406"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at Davis"],"keyword":["Butyrate","Dietary fibre","Gut inflammation","Systemic inflammation","gut barrier function"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of diet modulated butyrate production on intestinal barrier function and inflammation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85054888648","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-136406","identifier":[{"id":"85054888648","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30322146","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6213552","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0c55857d-1822-4a93-904d-f20d0efb0778"],"keyword":["butyrate","dietary fibre","gut barrier function","gut inflammation","systemic inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2AE1239FB46195DE6E4B8B075A95627E"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at davis","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Davis","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Erik","key":"bachknudsenpau","last":"Bach Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","name_org":"Bach Knudsen, Knud Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408f