tion","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"2","eisbn":["9788772100043"],"pages":"41-64","place":"Aalborg, Danmark","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Studies in history, archives and cultural heritage","status":"p","subtitle":"The Great War and its Impacts","title":"World War 1","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-93eb2e76-f963-4179-b708-78bfc02025a9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The origins of World War 1","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092941","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The durability and lifetime of the proton exchange membrane water electrolysis (PEMWE) is directly affected by local current distribution (LCD). Uniform LCD indicates uniform electrochemical reaction and vice versa. LCD might be affected by the mechanical properties of the bipolar plate (BP) such as the elasticity and bristliness. In this work, the LCD is measured at the cathode side using S segmented plate with 100 segments over the 50 cm active area. To study the effect of BP mechanical properties on LCD of the PEMWE, graphite and titanium BPs materials are used in this work. The titanium BP has shown a non-uniform LCD at higher clamping torque (CT), and a uniform LCD at lower one. Meanwhile, the graphite BP has shown a uniform LCD at higher CT and less uniform LCD at lower CT. Also, it is concluded that higher PEMWE cell performance not necessary means more uniform LCD.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Zhou, Fan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-117143"],"event":{"end":"2018-10-04","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2018-09-30","title":"ECS and SMEQ Joint International Meeting","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Current distribution","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the effect of bipolar plate mechanical properties on the current distribution of proton exchange membrane water electrolysis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85058352706&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-117143","identifier":[{"id":"85058352706","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e6e05e0e-ab37-4c3f-a918-db4b28bc8bb9"],"keyword":["Bipolar plate materials","Current distribution","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-512633C14EF84A2187550F9673F60CE4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"874642c9-fe83-4b87-9b5e-9b8088c39e6a","name":"Zhou, Fan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08613.0683ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"13","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"683-693","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"86"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058352706"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e6e05e0e-ab37-4c3f-a918-db4b28bc8bb9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"On the Effect of Bipolar Plate Mechanical Properties on the Current Distribution of Proton Exchange Membrane Water Electrolysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-117143","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis (PEMEC) is a high-yield technique for hydrogen generation from renewable energy. One challenge for commercialisation of the technology is a low-cost and highly efficient flow plate. Flow plates are one of the most expensive parts of an electrolysis system, therefore a thorough study on alternative flow plate manufacturing methods pays off. Expanded metals have low manufacturing cost. Even though they are being used in different industries from electrochemistry to ventilation and air conditioning systems, there is little information available on their fluid flow behaviour. In this paper, the distribution of gas and liquid flow in expanded metal is analysed. Expanded metal flow resistance properties such as porosity, permeability and inertial resistance for two different sizes in both horizontal and vertical directions are determined. Alongside the experiments, two different computational fluid dynamic (CFD) simulations of flow in the experimental setup and the structure of the expanded metal was done.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","Müller, Martin","Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121565"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Forschungszentrum Jülich"],"keyword":["CFD","Flow field","Gas liquid flow","PEM water electrolysis","Pressure loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental and numerical study of flow in expanded metal plate for water electrolysis applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85049607230&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121565","identifier":[{"id":"85049607230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f61686b1-1643-4ae4-9b24-cc740add6d72"],"keyword":["CFD","Expanded metal mesh","Flow field","Gas-liquid flow","PEM water electrolysis","Pressure loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5453E1B9297A8A93AEF7A5E44568BC39"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"forschungszentrum jülich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Forschungszentrum Jülich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saeed Sadeghi","key":"lafmejanipau","last":"Lafmejani","locid":"db40a4cb-554f-4515-aaa1-724aa7c708a0","name":"Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","orcid":"0000-0002-1780-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2018.07.032","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"334-342","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"397"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049607230"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f61686b1-1643-4ae4-9b24-cc740add6d72"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental and numerical study of flow in expanded metal plate for water electrolysis applications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121565","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Of the patients undergoing radical cystectomy, 20–80% experience relapse. Minimally invasive methods for early detection of metastatic relapse after cystectomy and for monitoring ongoing therapy are urgently needed to improve individualised follow-up and treatment. Therefore, we evaluated the use of circulating tumour DNA (ctDNA) in plasma and urine to detect metastatic relapse after cystectomy and measure treatment efficacy. We exome sequenced tumour and germline DNA from patients with muscle-invasive bladder cancer and monitored ctDNA in 370 liquid biopsies throughout the disease courses by 84 personalised digital droplet polymerase chain reaction assays targeting 61 genes. Patients were prospectively recruited between 2013 and 2017. Patients with metastatic relapse had significantly higher ctDNA levels compared with disease-free patients (p < 0.001). The median positive lead time between ctDNA detection in plasma and diagnosis of relapse was 101 d after cystectomy (range 0–932 d). Early detection of metastatic relapse and treatment response using liquid biopsies represents a novel, highly sensitive tool for monitoring patients, supporting clinicians, and guiding treatment decisions. Patient summary: Measurement of tumour-specific mutations in plasma and urine may be a powerful tool to monitor response during treatment and identify early signs of metastatic disease. Liquid biopsy analysis of tumour-specific mutations is a highly sensitive method for monitoring early signs of metastatic disease in patients with bladder cancer. Furthermore, liquid biopsy monitoring methods may help inform clinicians on treatment efficacy.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Birkenkamp-Demtröder, Karin","Christensen, Emil","Nordentoft, Iver","Knudsen, Michael","Taber, Ann","Høyer, Søren","Lamy, Philippe","Agerbæk, Mads","Jensen, Jørgen Bjerggaard","Dyrskjøt, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-148379"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomarker","Cell free DNA","Liquid biopsy","Neoadjuvant chemotherapy","Plasma","Treatment response"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monitoring treatment response and metastatic relapse in advanced bladder cancer by liquid biopsy analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eururo.2017.09.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-148379","identifier":[{"id":"85029904678","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28958829","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-213df835-7195-4a30-8c2d-27f2afa5b739"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Cell-free DNA","Droplet digital polymerase chain reaction","Liquid biopsy","Minimally invasive monitoring","Neoadjuvant chemotherapy","Personalised analysis","Plasma","Reservoir urine","Treatment response"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2191DC9D91909BAD8F9762AB51BEB7E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eururo.2017.09.011","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"birkenkampdemtröderpau","last":"Birkenkamp-Demtröder","locid":"77abb58a-ad4f-4f04-a992-b61a599a15e7","name":"Birkenkamp-Demtröder, Karin","rank