Bon","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lindsay","key":"macdonaldvermeulenpau","last":"MacDonald Vermeulen","locid":"6698df59-a9e0-4d5f-b297-3d54d1bf9d45","name":"Macdonald Vermeulen, Lindsay","name_org":"MacDonald Vermeulen, Lindsay","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles","key":"perinpau","last":"Perin","name":"Perin, Charles","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lien","key":"quachpau","last":"Quach","name":"Quach, Lien","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bukpau","last":"Buk","name":"Buk, Peter","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrina","key":"tabulipau","last":"Tabuli","name":"Tabuli, Katrina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shreya","key":"choprapau","last":"Chopra","name":"Chopra, Shreya","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wesley","key":"willettpau","last":"Willett","name":"Willett, Wesley","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheelagh","key":"carpendalepau","last":"Carpendale","name":"Carpendale, Sheelagh","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Regan","key":"mandrykpedh","last":"Mandryk","name":"Mandryk, Regan","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark","key":"hancockpedh","last":"Hancock","name":"Hancock, Mark","rank":17,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3170427.3186539","eisbn":["9781450356206","9781450356213"],"isbn":["9781450356213"],"place":"ACM New York, NY","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Engage with CHI","title":"CHI 2018 - Extended Abstracts of the 2018 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052026361"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c50533ff-e4d1-41a8-a759-8261deec82c7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Democratizing Open Energy Data for Public Discourse Using Visualization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-241793","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Introduced in 2014, Danish public schools are obliged to ensure that all pupils are physically active at least 45 minutes on average per day. Research shows that many schools have incorporated more physical activities, but it is challenging to include all children and ensuring sufficient quality of activities. The purpose of this presentation is to outline the preparation of an intervention with the aim of supporting schools and teachers implementing a physical active school day for everyone. Methods Randomised controlled trials are recognised as the most valid design to obtain knowledge on ways to promote new approaches in different settings. However, this design can be criticised for not taking enough consideration of the complexity of the setting. Furthermore, many scientific school interventions are too detached from practice, which makes the value for society small. The design of the current research intervention is based on theoretical concepts of implementation, innovation and psychosocial well-being and will adopt a compatible, adaptable and scalable approach to school based physical activity promotion. Results Research results will be targeted practical actions and applicable to in-class activity, activity breaks and PE. It will include outcomes on students’ physical activity, motivation, well-being and learning ability as well as outcomes relevant to school management and development of teaching practices Conclusion It is crucial to consider the complex reality of school settings when conducting real-life interventions, and innovative study designs must","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Lise Sohl","Smedegaard, Søren","Knudsen, Louise Stjerne","Runge, Lisbeth","Skovgaard, Thomas","Christiansen, Lars Breum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587329"],"event":{"end":"2018-10-17","place":"London, gb","start":"2018-10-15","title":"7th ISPAH Congress","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from randomised controlled trials to compatible adaptable and scalable school development research an innovative research design for school based physical activity","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-587329","ids":["sdu-3149342a-6b70-43da-828b-46c5b93b3f06"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A8E96F716F6A845093F78765B2AA51C6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Active Living"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Sohl","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"5ecb4ee1-55e2-48d1-a743-86c50e450ac0","name":"Jeppesen, Lise Sohl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"smedegaardpau","last":"Smedegaard","locid":"1f611d29-034f-4665-9a21-2e53d6a07f16","name":"Smedegaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5451-9743","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Stjerne","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"82021dca-c7e0-4f60-8f0e-da84ddc9ee77","name":"Knudsen, Louise Stjerne","orcid":"0000-0003-4028-7125","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Runge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f8ec914f-7057-4cec-907a-ea5e23bef6e0","name":"Runge, Lisbeth","name_org":"Larsen, Lisbeth Runge","orcid":"0000-0002-4378-7785","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c6eebd4-6fdf-4819-bf31-6ae3c7e0b582","name":"Skovgaard, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6729-4988","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Breum Skov","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c168a51e-682a-42f8-8a57-fa705d9749e9","name":"Christiansen, Lars Breum","name_org":"Christiansen, Lars Breum Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-5142-3623","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3149342a-6b70-43da-828b-46c5b93b3f06"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"From randomised controlled trials to compatible, adaptable and scalable school development research - an innovative research design for school based physical activity","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-587329","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper gives insight into the discharge behavior of lithium-ion batteries based on the investigations, which have been done by the researchers [1– 19]. In this article, the battery's discharge behaviour at various discharge rates is studied and surface monitor, discharge curve, volume monitor plot of maximum temperature in the domain and maximum temperature in the area are illustrated. Additionally, an external and internal short-circuit treatment for three cases have been studied. The Dual-Potential Multi-Scale Multi-Dimensional (MSMD) Battery Model (BM) was used by ANSYS FLUENT software to analysis the discharge behaviour of lithium-ion batteries. The results show that surface monitor plot of discharge curve at 1 C has a decreasing trend and volume monitor plot of maximum temperature in the domain has slightly increasing pattern over the simulation time. For the curves of discharge and maximum temperature in the domain, lowest and the highest rate of changes were seen for 0.5C and 5C respectively.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-067754"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-13","place":"Monte-Carlo, mc","start":"2017-04-11","title":"2017 Twelfth International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lithium ion batteries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the discharge behavior of lithium ion batteries using the dual potential multi scale multi dimensional msmd battery model","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-067754","identifier":[{"id":"85021332431","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000403212100054","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-3d15ad08-318d-4498-ab34-c2f8225d76d9"],"keyword":["Discharge behavior","Dual-Potential MSMD Battery model","ECM model","Lithium-ion batteries","NTGK model","Newman's model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31B3572BDE8ADD943DDE1A4235120B65"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seyed","key":"saeedmadanipau","last":"Saeed Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","name_org":"Saeed Madani, Seyed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ever.2017.7935915","isbn":["9781538616925"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 Twelfth International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021332431"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3d15ad08-318d-4498-ab34-c2f8225d76d9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The discharge behavior of lithium-ion batteries using the Dual-Potential Multi-Scale Multi-Dimensional (MSMD) Battery Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-067754","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Decreasing of fossil fuel sources and ecological worries has spurred global attention in the expansion of developing energy storing systems for electric vehicles (EVs). As a consequence of escalating appeal on new dependable power supplier for hybrid electric vehicles, lithium-ion (Li-ion) batteries have obtained much considerations in the previous decade. Their highest production rate among other types of batteries is because of their superior characteristics. Greater energy efficiency, lesser self-discharge rate, more lifespan and the nonexistence of the memory effect are the main reasons that make them interesting for researchers and producers. Thermal problem related to electric vehicle (EV) battery packs has been a matter of contention and can considerably influence battery functioning and life cycle. Temperature variations from module to module in a battery pack could result in reduced performance. Therefore,thermal management of batteries is essential for various purposes containing thermal runaway and longstanding of cell functioning period. The favorable outcome of electricdriven vehicles (EDVs) depends on the lithium-ion battery technology. Notwithstanding, the safety concern is a considerable technical problem and has become an important factor which might postpones subsequent extension of lithium-ion batteries. This paper reviews different methods for thermal management of lithium-ion batteries. Various methods such as using Phase change materials and using air cooling, straight liquid cooling, ancillary liquid cooling, fin cooling have been considered to assess their usefulness from the viewpoint of coolant energy utilization, highest temperature growth, temperature alteration, and extra mass required for the cooling scheme.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100336"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-13","place":"Monte-Carlo, mc","start":"2017-04-11","title":"2017 Twelfth International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lithium ion batteries","Thermal management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a review of thermal management and safety for lithium ion batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-100336","identifier":[{"id":"000403212100053","type":"wos"},{"id":"85021383641","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ad4c6261-c7df-471a-8ee0-a25bb75cd8c3"],"keyword":["Lithium ion batteries","Thermal management","Thermal safety of cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C4BD1770619073315EDF1FA40AD60CC5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seyed","key":"saeedmadanipau","last":"Saeed Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","name_org":"Saeed Madani, Seyed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swiercz