:"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"mainzpau","last":"Mainz","locid":"fadbea42-81be-48a2-afb2-c868f9dfa4f5","name":"Mainz, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-0242-9233","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bf011362-0e0e-4089-bf19-b8653fc9a603"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"There is Need for Improvement of Quality Improvement : A Systematic Review of the PDSA Method in QI Studies","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-105417","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Competition in education has two functions: selection and motivation. How do these two functionscorrelate, contradict or co-exist? How has the educational system reflected on the relation betweencompetition as motivational technology and as a technology for selection? The aim of this paper isto formulate the problem of competition in education as a relation between selection and motivationand provide an analytical strategy to grasp this problem. Our ambition is to theorize the problemand give empirical illustrations of how the connection between selection and motivation has beenarticulated in various educational institutions and programs.We start out in a system’s theoretical vocabulary in order to understand how competition may beobserved from within the system of education and from other systems. Then we turn to GeorgSimmel and Theodor Geiger to build up analytical concepts on competition. After this we sketchout different ways in which competition as motivation and selection has been articulated ineducational programs and institutions. <p/>","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, Hanne","Christensen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-171570"],"event":{"end":"2017-07-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2017-07-06","title":"33rd EGOS Colloquium","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"competition in education selection and motivation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/426606844/CompetitionShortPaperEGOS2017.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-171570","identifier":[{"id":"85013482361","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4a12504b-f125-4248-92fa-e553e239e753"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-379BCF9415A26153A5F2B1A84680A765"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/426606844/CompetitionShortPaperEGOS2017.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"64613f11-d8e3-46a7-9eae-4a4a50cf9fdc","name":"Knudsen, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0003-3879-0629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c6bf7b94-cdf4-4abe-8e80-5526aacfd66c","name":"Christensen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1335-0806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4a12504b-f125-4248-92fa-e553e239e753"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Competition in education : Selection and motivation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-171570","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"De danske nyhedsmediers hjemmesider indgår i et skjult og hyperkomplekst netværk af tjenester og virksomheder, som sender data mellem hinanden, når borgerne bruger nyheder. Et privat dansk nyhedssite har i gennemsnit 102 eksterne partnere knytet til sig. Google er den altdominerende af dem. De mange partnere underminerer medievirksomhedernes kommercielle fundament.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Flyverbom, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-299618"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de skjulte datastrømme i nyhedsproduktionen","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://hdl.handle.net/10398/9538","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-299618","ids":["cbs-fd50a5b0-0e08-435b-8dc2-2e56e90dbb40"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-069C55E01B7E8F6AEBC80D4EDCD14C3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://hdl.handle.net/10398/9538","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.altinget.dk/misc/Mediernes%20udvikling%20i%20Danmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"flyverbompau","last":"Flyverbom","locid":"85ddabd4-7915-496a-81e1-41610119ef88","name":"Flyverbom, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-9465-6219","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisbeth","key":"knudsenpedh","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Lisbeth","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Schultz","key":"jørgensenpedh","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Søren Schultz","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["2445852X"],"pages":"52-65","place":"København","publisher":"Slots- og Kulturstyrelsen","series":"Mediernes udvikling i Danmark","status":"p","subtitle":"Analyser af internationale aktørers betydning for det danske mediemarked, danske medieudbydere og dansk medieindhold","title":"Globaliseringen af den danske mediebranche"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-fd50a5b0-0e08-435b-8dc2-2e56e90dbb40"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"De skjulte datastrømme i nyhedsproduktionen","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-299618","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Results from animal and human studies suggest that lithium in therapeutic doses may improve learning and memory and modify the risk of developing dementia. Additional preliminary studies suggest that subtherapeutic levels, including microlevels of lithium, may influence human cognition. OBJECTIVE: To investigate whether the incidence of dementia in the general population covaries with long-term exposure to microlevels of lithium in drinking water. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: This Danish nationwide, population-based, nested case-control study examined longitudinal, individual geographic data on municipality of residence and data from drinking water measurements combined with time-specific data from all patients aged 50 to 90 years with a hospital contact with a diagnosis of dementia from January 1, 1970, through December 31, 2013, and 10 age- and sex-matched control individuals from the Danish population. The mean lithium exposure in drinking water since 1986 was estimated for all study individuals. Data analysis was performed from January 1, 1995, through December 31, 2013. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: A diagnosis of dementia in a hospital inpatient or outpatient contact. Diagnoses of Alzheimer disease and vascular dementia were secondary outcome measures. In primary analyses, distribution of lithium exposure was compared between patients with dementia and controls. RESULTS: A total of 73 731 patients with dementia and 733 653 controls (median age, 80.3 years; interquartile range, 74.9-84.6 years; 44 760 female [60.7%] and 28 971 male [39.3%]) were included in the study. Lithium exposure was statistically significantly different between patients with a diagnosis of dementia (median, 11.5 μg/L; interquartile range, 6.5-14.9 μg/L) and controls (median, 12.2 μg/L; interquartile range, 7.3-16.0 μg/L; P < .001). A nonlinear association was observed. Compared with individuals exposed to 2.0 to 5.0 μg/L, the incidence rate ratio (IRR) of dementia was decreased in those exposed to more than 15.0 μg/L (IRR, 0.83; 95% CI, 0.81-0.85; P < .001) and 10.1 to 15.0 μg/L (IRR, 0.98; 95% CI, 0.96-1.01; P = .17) and increased with 5.1 to 10.0 μg/L (IRR, 1.22; 95% CI, 1.19-1.25; P < .001). Similar patterns were found with Alzheimer disease and vascular dementia as outcomes. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: Long-term increased lithium exposure in drinking water may be associated with a lower incidence of dementia in a nonlinear way; however, confounding from other factors associated with municipality of residence cannot be excluded.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kessing, Lars Vedel","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Voutchkova, Denitza","Erntsen, Vibeke","Schullehner, Jörg","Hansen, Birgitte","Andersen, Per Kragh","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær"],"cuid":["S02-086.13-793207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, South","Nordic"],"country":["Greenland","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","National University of Singapore"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of lithium in drinking water with the incidence of dementia","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85030639982","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.13-793207","identifier":[{"id":"28832877","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5710473","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85030639982","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-37143c5c-780d-4db2-934d-18a2c5a7c1d6","ku-6577482f-6d8f-4e1a-8c86-566075fb4805"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-839A8B91BB78A6C7E2B9ED3A0BB756BF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Vedel","key":"kessingpau","last":"Kessing","locid":"93a97a97-e9d8-464b-8eed-1244a0a9ee56","name":"Kessing, Lars Vedel","orcid":"0000-0001-9377-9436","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas Alexander","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","locid":"b87ed711-194a-48dc-b83a-3c7aad18a00d","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikoline Nygård","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Flindt","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Munch","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Denitza","key":"voutchkovapau","last":"Voutchkova","locid":"3ca8a082-f717-4a20-a043-48e33b88a7bb","name":"Voutchkova, Denitza","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"erntsenpau","last":"Erntsen","name":"Erntsen, Vibeke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vibeke","key":"ernstsenpau","last":"Ernstsen","name":"Ernstsen, Vibeke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörg","key":"schullehnerpau","last":"Schullehner","name":"Schullehner, Jörg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Birgitte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per Kragh","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"6d37a601-0e0d-4507-85dd-1539366656c9","name":"Andersen, Per Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-0490-0885","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28832877"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2017.2362","issn":["15383636","2168622X"],"issn_org":["0003990X"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA Psychiatry","pages":"1005-1010","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Psychiatry","title_org":"J A M A Psychiatry","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030639982"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-37143c5c-780d-4db2-934d-18a2c5a7c1d6","ku-6577482f-6d8f-4e1a-8c86-566075fb4805"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association of Lithium in Drinking Water With the Incidence of Dementia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.13-793207","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Energy transition can be led by more hydrogen production. Hydrogen offers a clean, sustainable, and flexible option for overcoming different obstacles that face the low-carbon economy [1]. PEMWE is one of the most promising candidate technologies to produce hydrogen from renewable energy sources. PEMWE cell splits water into hydrogen and oxygen when an electric current is passed through it. Electrical current forces the positively charged ions to migrate to negatively charged cathode, where hydrogen is reduced. Meanwhile, oxygen is produced at the anode side electrode and escapes as a gas with the circulating water. In the recent few years, PEMWE’s R&D has inched towards; operating conditions; such as increased operating temperature and cathode-anode high differential pressure operation, flow field design, stack development, and numerical modelling [2,3]. In this work the effect of clamping pressure on the PEMWE cell characteristics’; performance, conductivity, hydrogen and water cross-over through the membrane electrode assembly (MEA) is studied. A 50 cm2 active area PEMWE cell with double serpentine flow field channels for the anode and cathode side is used. Measurements are carried out at constant cell temperature (70°C) and atmospheric pressure. Early results for IV curve predict that the PEMWE cell performance increases with increasing the clamping pressure at fixed temperature and current density. This can be elucidated by the EIS measurements which predict an increment in ohmic and activation resistance at lower clamping pressure values at the same temperature and current density. Furthermore, early results have not shown any significant change in the amount of hydrogen crossing-over from cathode to anode and water from anode to cathode. This might be attributed to the membrane properties which might not be changed significantly with changing the clamping pressure.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Cui, Xiaoti","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059088"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-15","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2017-06-13","title":"1st International Conference on Electrolysis","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Polarization curve","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental study on the influence of clamping pressure on proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer pemwe cell s characteristics","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-059088","ids":["aau-1ee92ecf-e202-4959-9628-45659c9bdbb9"],"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Hydrogen cross-over","Polarization curve","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer","Water cross-over"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D6E2BBECD88C48D3E44555ED39F8628C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1ee92ecf-e202-4959-9628-45659c9bdbb9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental study on the influence of clamping pressure on proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer (PEMWE) cell’s characteristics","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059088","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Lithium-ion batteries have already gained acceptability for Electric Vehicles (EVs) and Hybrid Electric Vehicles (HEVs) applications because of several reasons such as high theoretical capacity, their cycle-life, and high specific energy density. The intention of this experimental research is to study the surface temperature evolution of a 13 Ah Nano Lithium-Titanate battery cell for the usage of rechargeable energy storage system under fast charging conditions. The nominal voltage of the cell is 2.26V and the nominal capacity is 13.4 Ah. In this research, contact thermocouples were employed in order to measure the surface temperature evolution of the cell. A relatively non-uniform temperature distribution was observed over the cell surface.The position of the maximum temperature was seen around the negative tab of the cell.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063772"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-13","place":"Brno, cz","start":"2017-09-10","title":"18th International Conference on Advanced Batteries, Accumulators and Fuel Cells","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolution of surface temperature of a 000000000013 amp hour nano lithium titanate battery cell under fast charging","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-063772","identifier":[{"id":"85046036197","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2f5502e5-c69d-4c68-b74a-5472593c16b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85D9034CCE4D6DAA8B52310776742FE4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seyed","key":"saeedmadanipau","last":"Saeed Madani","locid":"2b964c98-f205-4a96-8e1c-e2433090f82a","name":"Madani, Seyed Saeed","name_org":"Saeed Madani, Seyed","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/08101.0271ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"271-279","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046036197"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2f5502e5-c69d-4c68-b74a-5472593c16b9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Evolution of Surface Temperature of a 13 Amp Hour Nano Lithium-Titanate Battery Cell under Fast Charging","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063772","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The prevailing standards and scientific literature offer a wide range of options for the construction of a battery thermal management system (BTMS). The design of an innovative yet well-functioning BTMS requires strict supervision, quality audit and continuous improvement of the whole process. It must address all the current quality and safety (Q&S) standards. In this review article, an effective battery thermal management is sought considering the existing battery Q&S standards and scientific literature. The article contains a broad overview of the current existing standards and literature on a generic compliant BTMS. The aim is to assist in the design of a novel compatible BTMS. Additionally, the article delivers a set of recommendations to make an effective BTMS.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-097240"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Batteries","Battery thermal management system BTMS","Calorimetry","Isothermal Calorimeter","Li ion batteries","Thermal imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards an ultimate battery thermal management system a review","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries3010009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-097240","identifier":[{"id":"85035131115","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000408137800009","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-a2dbbb9d-2fa9-4115-867d-4e7f49d71c5c"],"keyword":["Batteries","Battery management systems (BMSs)","Battery thermal management system (BTMS","Calorimetry","Isothermal calorimeter","Li-ion batteries","Quality and safety (Q&S) standards","Thermal imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F6B6DE12E13F3F8CF4F53E67F6B7C42A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries3010009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/280768675/batteries_03_00009_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/batteries3010009","issn":["23130105"],"issue":"1","journal":"Batteries","paperid":"9","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Batteries","volume":"3"},"review"