{"abstract":"Importance: Results from animal and human studies suggest that lithium in therapeutic doses may improve learning and memory and modify the risk of developing dementia. Additional preliminary studies suggest that subtherapeutic levels, including microlevels of lithium, may influence human cognition. Objective: To investigate whether the incidence of dementia in the general population covaries with long-term exposure to microlevels of lithium in drinking water. Design, Setting, and Participants: This Danish nationwide, population-based, nested case-control study examined longitudinal, individual geographic data on municipality of residence and data from drinking water measurements combined with time-specific data from all patients aged 50 to 90 years with a hospital contact with a diagnosis of dementia from January 1, 1970, through December 31, 2013, and 10 age- and sex-matched control individuals from the Danish population. The mean lithium exposure in drinking water since 1986 was estimated for all study individuals. Data analysis was performed from January 1, 1995, through December 31, 2013. Main Outcomes and Measures: A diagnosis of dementia in a hospital inpatient or outpatient contact. Diagnoses of Alzheimer disease and vascular dementia were secondary outcome measures. In primary analyses, distribution of lithium exposure was compared between patients with dementia and controls. Results: A total of 73 731 patients with dementia and 733 653 controls (median age, 80.3 years; interquartile range, 74.9-84.6 years; 44 760 female [60.7%] and 28 971 male [39.3%]) were included in the study. Lithium exposure was statistically significantly different between patients with a diagnosis of dementia (median, 11.5 µg/L; interquartile range, 6.5-14.9 µg/L) and controls (median, 12.2 µg/L; interquartile range, 7.3-16.0 µg/L; P < .001). A nonlinear association was observed. Compared with individuals exposed to 2.0 to 5.0 µg/L, the incidence rate ratio (IRR) of dementia was decreased in those exposed to more than 15.0 µg/L (IRR, 0.83; 95% CI, 0.81-0.85; P < .001) and 10.1 to 15.0 µg/L (IRR, 0.98; 95% CI, 0.96-1.01; P = .17) and increased with 5.1 to 10.0 µg/L (IRR, 1.22; 95% CI, 1.19-1.25; P < .001). Similar patterns were found with Alzheimer disease and vascular dementia as outcomes. Conclusions and Relevance: Long-term increased lithium exposure in drinking water may be associated with a lower incidence of dementia in a nonlinear way; however, confounding from other factors associated with municipality of residence cannot be excluded.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kessing, Lars Vedel","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Voutchkova, Denitza","Ernstsen, Vibeke","Schullehner, Jörg","Hansen, Birgitte","Andersen, Per Kragh","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-802736"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Alzheimer Disease","Case Control Studies","Dementia","Dementia Vascular","Denmark","Drinking water","Environmental Exposure","Female","Humans","Incidence","Journal Article","Lithium","Male","Statistics as Topic","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of lithium in drinking water with the incidence of dementia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85030639982","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-802736","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5710473","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85030639982","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28832877","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b357319a-3563-4d8f-a3ff-d78ae972989b"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Alzheimer Disease","Case-Control Studies","Dementia","Dementia, Vascular","Denmark","Drinking Water","Environmental Exposure","Female","Humans","Incidence","Journal Article","Lithium","Male","Statistics as Topic","Time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-839A8B91BB78A6C7E2B9ED3A0BB756BF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Vedel","key":"kessingpau","last":"Kessing","name":"Kessing, Lars Vedel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Alexander","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikoline Nygård","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"42deac4a-cdd7-47dd-9738-d5801af12a4a","name":"Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Flindt","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Munch","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Denitza","key":"voutchkovapau","last":"Voutchkova","name":"Voutchkova, Denitza","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"ernstsenpau","last":"Ernstsen","name":"Ernstsen, Vibeke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörg","key":"schullehnerpau","last":"Schullehner","name":"Schullehner, Jörg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Birgitte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kragh","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Per Kragh","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28832877"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2017.2362","issn":["15383636","2168622X"],"issn_org":["2168622X"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA Psychiatry","pages":"1005-1010","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Psychiatry","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030639982"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b357319a-3563-4d8f-a3ff-d78ae972989b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Lithium in Drinking Water With the Incidence of Dementia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-802736","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Chronic inflammatory diseases (CIDs), including Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis (inflammatory bowel diseases, IBD), rheumatoid arthritis, psoriasis, psoriatic arthritis, spondyloarthritides, hidradenitis suppurativa, and immune-mediated uveitis, are treated with biologics targeting the pro-inflammatory molecule tumour necrosis factor-α (TNF) (i.e., TNF inhibitors). Approximately one-third of the patients do not respond to the treatment. Genetics and lifestyle may affect the treatment results. The aims of this multidisciplinary collaboration are to identify (1) molecular signatures of prognostic value to help tailor treatment decisions to an individual likely to initiate TNF inhibitor therapy, followed by (2) lifestyle factors that support achievement of optimised treatment outcome. This report describes the establishment of a cohort that aims to obtain this information. Clinical data including lifestyle and treatment response and biological specimens (blood, faeces, urine, and, in IBD patients, intestinal biopsies) are sampled prior to and while on TNF inhibitor therapy. Both hypothesis-driven and data-driven analyses will be performed according to pre-specified protocols including pathway analyses resulting from candidate gene expression analyses and global approaches (e.g., metabolomics, metagenomics, proteomics). The final purpose is to improve the lives of patients suffering from CIDs, by providing tools facilitating treatment selection and dietary recommendations likely to improve the clinical outcome.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Andersen, Vibeke Normann","Holmskov, Uffe","Sørensen, Signe Bek","Jawhara, Mohamad","Andersen, Karina W","Bygum, Anette","Sylvester Hvid, Lone","Grauslund, Jakob","Wied, Jimmi","Glerup, Henning","Fredberg, Ulrich","Villadsen, Jan Alexander","Kjær, Søren Geill","Fallingborg, Jan","Moghadd, Seyed A G R","Knudsen, Torben","Brodersen, Jacob","Frøjk, Jesper","Dahlerup, Jens Frederik","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Christensen, Robin","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Thiel, Steffen","Færgeman, Nils J","Brandslund, Ivan","Stensballe, Allan","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Franke, Andre","Ellinghaus, David","Rosenstiel, Philip","Raes, Jeroen","Heitmann, Berit","Boye, Mette","Lindgaard Nielsen, Charlotte","Werner, Lars","Kjeldsen, Jens","Ellingsen, Torkell"],"cuid":["S05-099.47-002802"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Christian-Albrechts-University of Kiel","Kiel University","University of Leuven","VIB","Vlaams Instituut voor Biotechnologie (VIB)"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Biomarkører","CID","Exercise","Food","Journal Article","Kronisk inflammatorisk sygdom","Molecular epidemiology","Motion","Patient related outcome measures PROMs","Personalized medicine","Red meat","Rygning","Smoking","Treatment Outcome","Western style diet WSD"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Diagnostic Centre, Silkeborg Regional Hospital, University of Aarhus, 8600 Silkeborg, Denmark. Henning.Glerup@silkeborg.rm.dk."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a proposal for a study on treatment selection and lifestyle recommendations in chronic inflammatory diseases a danish multidisciplinary collaboration on prognostic factors and personalised medicine","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license"