{"abstract":"The intermittent renewable and power energy sources can be effectively utilized usinghydrogen energy storage technology. Hydrogen has the highest energy capacity per unitweight of any known other fuel. Also it is considered as a promising energy carrier and a futurereplacement for fossil fuel energy sources. The proton exchange membrane water electrolyser(PEMWE) is the most candidate technology to produce hydrogen from renewable energysources. PEMWE cell splits water into hydrogen and oxygen when an electric current is passedthrough it. Electrical current forces the positively charged ions to migrate to negatively chargedcathode, where hydrogen is reduced. Meanwhile, oxygen is produced at the anode sideelectrode and escape as a gas with the circulating water. In the recent few years, PEMWE’s R&D has inched towards; operating conditions; such asincreased operating temperature and cathode-anode high differential pressure operation, flowfield design, stack development, and modeling. In this work the effect of clamping pressure onthe PEMWE cell performance is studied. A 50 cm2 active area PEMWE cell with doubleserpentine flow field channels for the anode and cathode side is used. The standardelectrochemical technique to characterize the performance of electrochemical cells is thepolarization curve. Thus, the IV curves are measured at different clamping pressures. Also, the electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) is used as a non-invasive technique tocharacterize the electrochemical processes at different clamping pressures. All thesemeasurements are conducted at constant cell temperature (70°C) and atmospheric pressure.Furthermore, to ensure a high confidence level in the obtained data, experiments are repeatedfew times. Early results for polarization curve predict that the PEMWE cell performance increases withincreasing the clamping pressure at fixed temperature and current density. This can beelucidated by the EIS measurements which predict an increment in ohmic and activation","author_count":3,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076989"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-01","place":"New Orleans, LA, us","start":"2017-05-28","title":"231st ECS Meeting","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Polarization curve","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the experimental investigation of the clamping pressure effects on the proton exchange membrane water electrolyser cell performance","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/250869514/Abstract_98990_On_the_Experimental_Investigation_of_the_Clamping_Pressure_Effects_on_the_Proton_Exchange_Membrane_Water_Electrolyser_Cell_Performance_Saher.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-076989","identifier":[{"id":"000432420500128","type":"wos"},{"id":"85030559217","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5cc02b57-7b58-4aa3-a23e-743b07131a16"],"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Polarization Curve","Proton exchange membrane water electrolyzer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-98700C2C10AEE0FDBB39D09B03DA6A25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/250869514/Abstract_98990_On_the_Experimental_Investigation_of_the_Clamping_Pressure_Effects_on_the_Proton_Exchange_Membrane_Water_Electrolyser_Cell_Performance_Saher.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/07711.1409ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"11","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"1409-1421","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030559217"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5cc02b57-7b58-4aa3-a23e-743b07131a16"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"On the Experimental Investigation of the Clamping Pressure Effects on the Proton Exchange Membrane Water Electrolyser Cell Performance","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076989","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Electric vehicles (EVs) represent one of the solutions for reducing the carbon emissions worldwide. Even though EVs have recently gained more and more popularity, their adoption at a large scale is mainly prevented by several factors, such as range anxiety and battery degradation. The range of an EV is mainly limited by the energy density and specific energy of the battery, while the battery degradation is determined by the driving manner (i.e., the mission profile) to which the EV is subjected to. In this paper we analyze the EV-battery degradation, in terms of both capacity fade and internal resistance increase (power decrease), by performing laboratory accelerated ageing tests for a period of eleven months. To perform this analysis, we used a standardized driving cycle – the Worldwide harmonized Light vehicles Test Cycle (WLTC) and a real-life temperature profile, characteristic to a European city. Furthermore, the study is performed for a Lithium-ion battery chemistry, which is nowadays very popular for EVs, the nickel manganese cobalt oxide-chemistry.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Martinez-Laserna, Egoitz","Sarasketa-Zabala, Elixabet"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091244"],"event":{"end":"2017-10-05","place":"Cincinnati, Ohio, us","start":"2017-10-01","title":"2017 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","IKERLAN-IK4, Technological Research Center"],"keyword":["Accelerated ageing","Capacity","Driving cycle","Electric vehicle","Internal Resistance","Lithium ion battery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accelerated aging of lithium ion batteries based on electric vehicle mission profile","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/263630081/DIS_Batt2020_final_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091244","identifier":[{"id":"000426847405133","type":"wos"},{"id":"85041477444","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8db74fe5-2c43-40ac-8118-d85afa9e376a"],"keyword":["Accelerated ageing","Capacity","Driving cycle","Electric vehicle","Internal resistance","Lithium-ion battery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C27937AA21D1B8515466142BC9724246"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/263630081/DIS_Batt2020_final_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"ikerlan ik4 technological research center","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"IKERLAN-IK4, Technological Research Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Egoitz","key":"martinezlasernapau","last":"Martinez-Laserna","name":"Martinez-Laserna, Egoitz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elixabet","key":"sarasketazabalapau","last":"Sarasketa-Zabala","name":"Sarasketa-Zabala, Elixabet","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce.2017.8096937","issn":["23293721"],"pages":"5631-5637","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2017 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041477444"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8db74fe5-2c43-40ac-8118-d85afa9e376a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Accelerated Aging of Lithium-Ion Batteries based on Electric Vehicle Mission Profile","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091244","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This work presents a comprehensive mapping of electrochemical impedance measurements under the influence of CO and methanol vapor contamination of the anode gas in a high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell, at varying load current. Electrical equivalent circuit model parameters based on experimental evaluation of electrochemical impedance spectroscopy measurements were used to quantify the changes caused by different contamination levels. The changes are generally in good agreement with what is found in the literature. It is shown that an increased level of CO contamination resulted in an increase in the high frequency and intermediate frequency impedances. When adding CO and methanol to the anode gas, the low frequency part of the impedance spectrum is especially affected at high load currents, which is clearly seen as a result of the high load current resolution used in this work. The negative effects of methanol vapor are found to be more pronounced on the series resistance. When CO and methanol vapor are both present in anode gas, the entire frequency spectrum and thereby all the equivalent circuit model parameters are affected. It is also shown that the trends of contamination effects are similar for all the test cases, namely, CO alone, methanol alone and a mix of the two, suggesting that effects of methanol may include oxidation into CO on the catalyst layer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Christian","Polverino, Pierpaolo","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Araya, Samuel Simon","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Pianese, Cesare","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095785"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Salerno"],"keyword":["CO","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Equivalent electrical circuit","Fuel cell","PBI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impedance characterization of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell stack under the influence of carbon monoxide and methanol vapor","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85026390121&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095785","identifier":[{"id":"000411545300034","type":"wos"},{"id":"85026390121","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9db1055f-3aa9-489e-9c51-246c23eac7db"],"keyword":["CO","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Equivalent electrical circuit","Fuel cell","Methanol vapor","PBI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F99BCA6B08E69F66BDF710327FEE8C1"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of salerno","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Salerno","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SerEnergy"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"0e062d6c-eeae-49d3-ae56-d750f51b90b7","name":"Jeppesen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0297-6854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierpaolo","key":"polverinopau","last":"Polverino","name":"Polverino, Pierpaolo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cesare","key":"pianesepau","last":"Pianese","name":"Pianese, Cesare","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2017.07.094","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"34","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"21901-21912","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026390121"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","serenergy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9db1055f-3aa9-489e-9c51-246c23eac7db"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impedance characterization of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell stack under the influence of carbon monoxide and methanol vapor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-095785","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
