":"Ehlers, Lars Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-6512-5566","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"mainzpau","last":"Mainz","locid":"fadbea42-81be-48a2-afb2-c868f9dfa4f5","name":"Mainz, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-0242-9233","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9f5702ae-a102-4079-aad4-c1bba052ca29"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Can quality improvement improve the quality of care?","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-096242","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper gives insight into the cooling simulation and thermal abuse modeling of lithium-ion batteries by ANSYS FLUENT. Cooling strategies are important issues in the thermal management of lithium-ion battery systems, and it is essential to investigate them attentively in order to maintain the functioning temperature of batteries within an optimum range. The high temperature is able not only to decrease the efficiency of batteries but also may lead to the thermal runaway. To comprehend further, the thermal abuse behavior of lithium-ion batteries based on The Newman, Tiedemann, Gu, and Kim (NTGK) model has been implemented in ANSYS FLUENT software. The results show that to achieve an optimum energy consumption for battery cooling, a minimum value of average heat transfer coefficient can be selected in order to keep the functioning temperature of batteries within an optimum range.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madani, Seyed Saeed","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102336"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-13","place":"Brno, cz","start":"2017-09-10","title":"18th International Conference on Advanced Batteries, Accumulators and Fuel Cells","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cooling simulation and thermal abuse modeling of lithium ion batteries using the newman tiedemann gu and kim ntgk model","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-102336","identifier":[{"id":"85046026543","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b409a145-e7e1-4cb0-86ff-06f715ab5bd4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0325CD48528DAE73F65FB3F668996ED"],"oai":