Newman, Tiedemann, Gu, and Kim (NTGK) Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102336","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"With the increasing interest in producing hydrogen through water electrolysis, the importance of understanding the transport phenomena governing its operation increases. To ensure optimal operating conditions for PEM electrolysis, it is particularly important to understand how the liquid feed-water distributes. Water not only serves a reactant, it also aids in cooling due to its high specific heat capacity. The movement of liquid water at the anode is difficult to model, since it is highly coupled to the formation of gas bubbles. To capture the complex two-phase flow behaviour that takes place within micro-channels and porous media, our research group has developed an Euler-Euler model in the computational fluid dynamics modelling framework of ANSYS CFX. In addition to two-phase flow, the model accounts for turbulence, species transport in the gas phase, heat transport in all three phases (i.e. solid, gas and liquid), as well as charge transport of electrons and ions. Our recent improvements have focused on the models ability to account for phase change and electrochemistry as well as the modelling of two-phase flow regimes. For comparison, an interdigitated and parallel channel flow field will be investigated with regard to how well they distribute gas and heat. To obtain a high durability when operating at high current densities, it is essential that liquid water and temperature is evenly distribution over the entire active surface area. In Figure 1, a contour plot of the temperature distribution within an interdigitated flow field is presented as an example. The axis-symmetric simulation shows that the formation of hot spots in the order of 8◦C above the inlet temperature can occur for a current density of 3 A/cm2 and a water stoichiometry of 350. These spots are primarily located underneath the outlet channels. To avoid them, an in-depth design and simulation study is necessary.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113028"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-15","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2017-06-13","title":"1st International Conference on Electrolysis","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flow field design for high pressure pem electrolysis cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260750023/ICE2017_Olesen_Anders_Christian.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113028","ids":["aau-d8b41121-5423-428a-9b4b-d87f4eb3bb6b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A6398881F926A7E19135E1DBDA43BC9F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260750023/ICE2017_Olesen_Anders_Christian.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d8b41121-5423-428a-9b4b-d87f4eb3bb6b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Flow field design for high-pressure PEM electrolysis cells","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113028","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"DC capacitors in power electronic converters are a major constraint on improvement of power density as well as reliability. In this paper, according to the degradation data of electrolytic capacitors through the accelerated test, the time-to-failure of the capacitor cell is acquired and it can be further extended to lower stress levels. Then, in a case study of a fuel cell backup power application, the mission profile based lifetime expectancy of the individual capacitor and the capacitor bank is estimated in terms of the standby mode and operation mode. The lifetime prediction of the capacitor banks can be obtained and compared with and without the degradation effect.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Dao","Wang, Huai","Blaabjerg, Frede","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Hansen, Daniel Blom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118821"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-07","place":"Kaohsiung, tw","start":"2017-06-03","title":"2017 IEEE 3rd International Future Energy Electronics Conference and ECCE Asia (IFEEC 2017 - ECCE Asia)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"degradation effect on reliability evaluation of aluminum electrolytic capacitor in backup power converter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260687579/PID4650829.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-118821","identifier":[{"id":"85034055556","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000426696300036","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-ec98f347-5e98-4c09-82d5-8d10eca70ecb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DDCC7DBA689C90FF5B3109A51235042A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260687579/PID4650829.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dantherm Power A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dao","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"8cf08fe2-24d6-4224-aaa2-f7e03a45debb","name":"Zhou, Dao","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-4309","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Huai","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"e8606356-85bc-4d6c-a091-e91dce99441a","name":"Wang, Huai","orcid":"0000-0002-5404-3140","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Blom","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Daniel Blom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ifeec.2017.7992443","eisbn":["9781509051571"],"pages":"202-207","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 IEEE 3rd International Future Energy Electronics Conference and ECCE Asia (IFEEC 2017 - ECCE Asia)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034055556"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dantherm power a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ec98f347-5e98-4c09-82d5-8d10eca70ecb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Degradation Effect on Reliability Evaluation of Aluminum Electrolytic Capacitor in Backup Power Converter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118821","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: We investigated whether detection of ctDNA after resection of colorectal cancer identifies the patients with the highest risk of relapse and, furthermore, whether longitudinal ctDNA analysis allows early detection of relapse and informs about response to intervention.Experimental Design: In this longitudinal cohort study, we used massively parallel sequencing to identify somatic mutations and used these as ctDNA markers to detect minimal residual disease and to monitor changes in tumor burden during a 3-year follow-up period.Results: A total of 45 patients and 371 plasma samples were included. Longitudinal samples from 27 patients revealed ctDNA postoperatively in all relapsing patients (n = 14), but not in any of the nonrelapsing patients. ctDNA detected relapse with an average lead time of 9.4 months compared with CT imaging. Of 21 patients treated for localized disease, six had ctDNA detected within 3 months after surgery. All six later relapsed compared with four of the remaining patients [HR, 37.7; 95% confidence interval (CI), 4.2-335.5; P < 0.001]. The ability of a 3-month ctDNA analysis to predict relapse was confirmed in 23 liver metastasis patients (HR 4.9; 95% CI, 1.5-15.7; P = 0.007). Changes in ctDNA levels induced by relapse intervention (n = 19) showed good agreement with changes in tumor volume (κ = 0.41; Spearman ρ = 0.4).Conclusions: Postoperative ctDNA detection provides evidence of residual disease and identifies patients at very high risk of relapse. Longitudinal surveillance enables early detection of relapse and informs about response to intervention. These observations have implications for the postoperative management of colorectal cancer patients. Clin Cancer Res; 23(18); 5437-45. ©2017 AACR.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Schøler, Lone Vedel","Reinert, Thomas","Ørntoft, Mai-Britt Worm","Kassentoft, Christine Gaasdal","Árnadóttir, Sigrid Salling","Vang, Søren","Nordentoft, Iver","Knudsen, Michael","Lamy, Philippe","Andreasen, Ditte","Mortensen, Frank Viborg","Knudsen, Anders Riegels","Stribolt, Katrine","Sivesgaard, Kim","Mouritzen, Peter","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Laurberg, Søren","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-098.63-019749"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical implications of monitoring circulating tumor dna in patients with colorectal cancer","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85029517104","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.63-019749","identifier":[{"id":"28600478","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85029517104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-619e0d07-8df2-42d1-aefb-be96323050a5","ku-9a0c3f71-c8cd-424d-a06a-6d6d1ab70e01"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BB32A6AB1749A0F8040E4700FD5F5819"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Comp