rsen","name":"Andersen, Claus L","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28600478"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-17-0510","issn":["10780432","15573265"],"issn_org":["10780432"],"issue":"18","journal":"Clinical Cancer Research","pages":"5437-5445","publisher":"American Association for Cancer Research Inc.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Cancer Research","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029517104"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","exiqon a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-619e0d07-8df2-42d1-aefb-be96323050a5","ku-9a0c3f71-c8cd-424d-a06a-6d6d1ab70e01"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Clinical Implications of Monitoring Circulating Tumor DNA in Patients with Colorectal Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.63-019749","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this study, the gaseliquid flow through an interdigitated anode flow field of a PEM water electrolysis cell (PEMEC) is analysed using a three-dimensional, transient, computational fluid dynamics (CFD) model. To account for two-phase flow, the volume of fluid (VOF) method in ANSYS Fluent 17.2 is used. The modelled geometry consists of the anode channels and the anode transport layer (ATL). To reduce the complexity of the phenomena governing PEMEC operation, the dependence upon electro-chemistry is disregarded. Instead, a fixed source of the gas is applied at the interface between the ATL and the catalyst layer. An important phenomenon that the model is able to capture is the gaseliquid contact angle on both the channel wall and ATL-channel interface. Particularly, the latter interface is crucial in capturing bubble entrainment into the channel. To validate the numerical simulation, photos taken of the gaseliquid flow in a transparent micro-channel, are qualitative compared against the simulation results. The experimental observations confirm the models prediction of long Taylor bubbles with small bubbles in between. From the simulation results, further intriguing details of the flow are revealed. From the bottom to the top of the outgoing channel, the film thickness gradually increases from zero to 200 mm. This increase in the film thickness is due to the particular superficial velocity field that develops in an interdigitated flow. Here both the superficial velocities change along the length of the channel. The model is capable of revealing effect of different bubble shapes/lengths in the outgoing channel. Shape and the sequence of the bubbles affect the water flow distribution in the ATL. The model presented in this work is the first step in the development of a comprehensive CFD model that comprises multiphase flow in porous media and micro-channel, electro-chemistry in catalyst layers, ion transport in membrane, hydrogen evolution, etc. The model can aid in the study of gaseliquid flow and its impact on the performance of a PEMEC.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086191"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CFD","Gas liquid flow","PEMEC","Water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vof modelling of gas liquid flow in pem water electrolysis cell micro channels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260540169/CFD_VOF_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-086191","identifier":[{"id":"000405160400003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85020469782","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7c4a9db4-6cd5-4c39-81b6-080901b02a99"],"keyword":["CFD","Gas-liquid flow","PEMEC","Single-fluid VOF","Taylor flow","Water electrolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-60407393B391292764F4CB830B053BA9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260540169/CFD_VOF_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saeed Sadeghi","key":"lafmejanipau","last":"Lafmejani","locid":"db40a4cb-554f-4515-aaa1-724aa7c708a0","name":"Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","orcid":"0000-0002-1780-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2017.05.079","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"26","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"16333-16344","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020469782"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7c4a9db4-6cd5-4c39-81b6-080901b02a99"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"VOF modelling of gas–liquid flow in PEM water electrolysis cell micro-channels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086191","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"With the novel possibilities for detecting molecules of interest with extreme sensitivity also comes the risk of encountering hitherto negligible sources of error. In life science, such sources of error might be the broad variety of additives such as dithiothreitol (DTT) used to preserve enzyme stability during in vitro reactions. Using two different assays that can sense strand interruptions in double stranded DNA, we here show that DTT is able to introduce nicks in the DNA backbone. DTT was furthermore shown to facilitate the immobilization of fluorescent DNA on an NHS-ester functionalized glass surface. Such reactions may in particular impact the readout from single molecule detection studies and other ultrasensitive assays. This was highlighted by the finding that DTT markedly decreased the signal to noise ratio in a DNA sensor based assay with single molecule resolution.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Fjelstrup, Søren","Andersen, Marie Bech","Thomsen, Jonas","Wang, Jing","Stougaard, Magnus","Pedersen, Finn Skou","Ho, Yi-Ping","Hede, Marianne Smedegaard","Knudsen, Birgitta R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-193156"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese University of Hong Kong"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of dithiothreitol on dna","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s17061201","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-193156","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5492665","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28538659","ty