9c5-a96c-41ec-a5df-b3d541b67239"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Time-of-Flight Three Dimensional Neutron Diffraction in Transmission Mode for Mapping Crystal Grain Structures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.40-032890","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Seeds of Barley (Hordeum vulgare) are infected by a high number of fungi, including pathogens such as Fusarium graminearum, F. culmorum, F. poae, F. avenaceum and Pyrenophora teres. Fusarium spp. is a widely distributed fungus causing yield reduction in a range of agricultural crops and many species in the genus produce mycotoxins responsible for serious quality deterioration. In malting barley, Fusarium also has a negative effect by causing gushing in beer. A number of barley seeds (app. 200) assumed to be infected by fungal from different origins and years of cultivation were tested by NGS sequencing the ITS (Internal Transcribed Spacer) region from total DNA. Approximately 2-4000 sequences were obtained from each seed and these were subsequently identified to species level in order to give an exact identification of fungal genera on each seed. The main fungal genera identified were Fusarium, Pyrenophora, Epicoccum, Didymella, Alternaria, Bipolaris and Microdochium. The fungal composition and quantities on each seed varied significantly. Some were infected mainly by a single fungus and some were infected by multiple fungi. All seeds were prior to this evaluated by multispectral imaging on the dorsal and ventral sides by the VideometerLab multispectral imaging system (Videometer A/S, Hørsholm, Denmark). This system is an instrument equipped with 19 different light emitting diodes at wavelengths ranging from 375 to 970nm (ultraviolet, visual and lower wavelength of the near-infrared region) in the reflectance mode (5 Mpix per band, pixel size app. 45 μm x 45 μm). Spectral information over the surface of seeds may be combined with information about size, shape, and texture of the seeds. This information links detection of fungal infection with other seed characteristics known from general seed testing. Analytical separation of the identified fungi was based on mean pixel intensity and a normalized Canonical Discriminant Analysis (nCDA) using the images of infected and healthy seeds. The potential of using spectral characteristics of the fungal species as a way to provide a fast optical screening method for fungal contamination of barley on the fungal species level was investigated by comparing results from the next generation sequencing and multispectral imaging.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Johannes Ravn","Carstensen, Jens Michael","Søren, Knudsen","Shrestha, Santosh","Nicolaisen, Mogens"],"cuid":["S02-096.67-029129"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-15","place":"København, dk","start":"2017-06-11","title":"ICNIRS 18th International Conference on Near Infrared Spectroscopy","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Fusarium","Multispectral imaging","Next generation sequencing","Seed health","barley Hordeum vulgare L"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of barley grain mycoflora by next generation sequencing and videometer multispectral imaging","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-096.67-029129","ids":["au-e3176fba-11d3-40a3-a2a5-156442a81c39","dtu-2fa99aed-e84d-4aa4-acc9-614dc6c5e79b"],"keyword":["Barley (Hordeum vulgare L)","FUSARIUM","Multispectral imaging","Next generation sequencing","Seed health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-E29A1E23DBAF07C0C0C93F83A2E909F2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"carlsberg foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CARL","l3nn":"Carlsberg Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Carlsberg Foundation","namevar":["Carlsberg Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CARL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes Ravn","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"20741068-2b9e-49c0-b7d5-551e049b45b2","name":"Jørgensen, Johannes Ravn","orcid":"0000-0003-3133-2350","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Michael","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"81e6af6e-2673-4f75-a894-82a7506ef55f","name":"Carstensen, Jens Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2535-3908","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Knudsen","key":"sørenpau","last":"Søren","name":"Søren, Knudsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Santosh","key":"shresthapau","last":"Shrestha","locid":"406d55e4-bbab-4f2c-9153-9eb0a5b6cf0a","name":"Shrestha, Santosh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","locid":"9f0ee31a-5e77-4716-abdb-d0215f9bc220","name":"Nicolaisen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-0407-2488","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e3176fba-11d3-40a3-a2a5-156442a81c39","dtu-2fa99aed-e84d-4aa4-acc9-614dc6c5e79b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Identification Of Barley Grain Mycoflora By Next Generation Sequencing And Videometer Multispectral Imaging","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.67-029129","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To examine if monocyte and macrophage activity may be on the mechanistic pathway to non-AIDS comorbidity by investigating the associations between plasma-soluble CD163 (sCD163) and incident non-AIDS comorbidities in well treated HIV-infected individuals. DESIGN: Prospective single-center cohort study. METHODS: Plasma sCD163 was quantified by ELISA technique at study entry in 2004/2005, and non-AIDS comorbidity was identified by International Classification of Disease Tenth revision diagnosis codes and registry linkage in 2014/2015. Associations between sCD163 and incident comorbidity was examined using multivariable Cox proportional hazards models adjusted for pertinent covariates. RESULTS: In HIV-1-infected individuals (n = 799), the highest quartile of plasma sCD163 was associated with incident chronic lung disease [adjusted hazard ratio (aHR), 3.2; 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.34; 7.46] and incident chronic kidney disease (aHR, 10.94; 95% CI: 2.32; 51.35), when compared with lowest quartiles. Further, (every 1 mg) increase in plasma sCD163 was positively correlated with incident liver disease (aHR, 1.12; 95% CI: 1.05; 1.19). The sCD163 level was not associated with incident cancer, cardiovascular disease or diabetes mellitus. CONCLUSION: sCD163 was independently associated with incident chronic kidney disease, chronic lung disease and liver disease in treated HIV-1-infected individuals, suggesting that monocyte/macrophage activation may be involved in the pathogenesis of non-AIDS comorbidity and a potential target for therapeutic intervention.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kirkegaard-Klitbo, Ditte M","Mejer, Niels","Knudsen, Troels B","Møller, Holger Jon","Moestrup, Søren Kragh","Poulsen, Susanne D","Kronborg, Gitte","Benfield, Thomas"],"cuid":["S03-093.87-013861"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Kirkegaard-Klitbo, Ditte M."],"keyword":["Adult","Antigens CD blood","Antigens Differentiation Myelomonocytic blood","Chronic Disease epidemiology","Enzyme Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Female","HIV 1","HIV Infections complications","Humans","Incidence","Journal Article","Kidney Diseases epidemiology","Kidney disease","Liver Diseases epidemiology","Liver disease","Lung Diseases epidemiology","Lung disease","Macrophage","Male","Middle Aged","Monocyte","Prospective Studies","Receptors Cell Surface blood","sCD163"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"soluble cd000000000163 predicts incident chronic lung kidney and liver disease in hiv infection","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014113888","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.87-013861","identifier":[{"id":"85014113888","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28252527","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-11b0dc9b-802b-4071-b3af-e95a3bc6f613","ku-bea6887f-f03c-40d6-9a6f-cb3ddd0afd4d","sdu-ce166fca-e9c8-4ee8-8d42-26048d462dac"],"keyword":["Adult","Antigens, CD/blood","Antigens, Differentiation, Myelomonocytic/blood","Chronic Disease/epidemiology","Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Female","HIV Infections/complications","HIV-1","Humans","Incidence","Journal Article","Kidney Diseases/epidemiology","Kidney disease","Liver Diseases/epidemiology","Liver disease","Lung Diseases/epidemiology","Lung disease","Macrophage","Male","Middle Aged","Monocyte","Prospective Studies","Receptors, Cell Surface/blood","SCD163"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E9F5719D890ABEE04C94