{"abstract":"Objective: Animal data suggest that subtherapeutic doses, including micro doses, of lithium may influence mood, and lithium levels in drinking water have been found to correlate with the rate of suicide. It has never been investigated whether consumption of lithium may prevent the development of bipolar disorder (primary prophylaxis). In a nation-wide population-based study, we investigated whether long-term exposure to micro levels of lithium in drinking water correlates with the incidence of bipolar disorder in the general population, hypothesizing an inverse association in which higher long-term lithium exposure is associated with lower incidences of bipolar disorder. Methods: We included longitudinal individual geographical data on municipality of residence, data from drinking water lithium measurements and time-specific data from all cases with a hospital contact with a diagnosis of mania/bipolar disorder from 1995 to 2013 (N=14 820) and 10 age- and gender-matched controls from the Danish population (N= 140 311). Average drinking water lithium exposure was estimated for all study individuals. Results: The median of the average lithium exposure did not differ between cases with a diagnosis of mania/bipolar disorder (12.7 μg/L; interquartile range [IQR]: 7.9-15.5 μg/L) and controls (12.5 μg/L; IQR: 7.6-15.7 μg/L; P=.2). Further, the incidence rate ratio of mania/bipolar disorder did not decrease with higher long-term lithium exposure, overall, or within age categories (0-40, 41-60 and 61-100 years of age). Conclusion: Higher long-term lithium exposure from drinking water was not associated with a lower incidence of bipolar disorder. The association should be investigated in areas with higher lithium levels than in Denmark.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kessing, Lars Vedel","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Knudsen, Nikoline N.","Jørgensen, Lisbeth F.","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Voutchkova, Denitza","Ernstsen, Vibeke","Schullehner, Jörg","Hansen, Birgitte","Andersen, Per K","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-666096"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, South","Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Kessing, Lars V."],"country":["Greenland","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Bipolar disorder","Drinking water","Incidence","Lithium","Low dose","micro dose"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lithium in drinking water and the incidence of bipolar disorder a nation wide population based study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85024479585","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-666096","identifier":[{"id":"28714553","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85024479585","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-136df1ab-6b8a-4252-945f-82230ae84bdb","ku-a5cbf3a5-ac6b-479d-b43b-7fa7521254cf","sdu-703e27b3-1573-4126-a711-776ae5ced980"],"keyword":["bipolar disorder","drinking water","incidence","lithium","low dose","micro dose"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B262CAC2F0D57E9E06432AB40ACF1F4C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Economics and Business Economics","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - National Centre for Register-based Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars V","key":"kessingpau","last":"Kessing","locid":"93a97a97-e9d8-464b-8eed-1244a0a9ee56","name":"Kessing, Lars Vedel","name_org":"Kessing, Lars V","orcid":"0000-0001-9377-9436","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas A","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","locid":"b87ed711-194a-48dc-b83a-3c7aad18a00d","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","name_org":"Gerds, Thomas A","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikoline N.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"42deac4a-cdd7-47dd-9738-d5801af12a4a","name":"Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","name_org":"Knudsen, Nikoline N.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth F.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Lisbeth F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Munch","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Denitza","key":"voutchkovapau","last":"Voutchkova","locid":"3ca8a082-f717-4a20-a043-48e33b88a7bb","name":"Voutchkova, Denitza","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"ernstsenpau","last":"Ernstsen","name":"Ernstsen, Vibeke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jörg","key":"schullehnerpau","last":"Schullehner","locid":"f7647c26-21ff-4d28-8645-ac66742707e9","name":"Schullehner, Jörg","orcid":"0000-0002-1153-6885","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Birgitte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per K","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"6d37a601-0e0d-4507-85dd-1539366656c9","name":"Andersen, Per Kragh","name_org":"Andersen, Per K","orcid":"0000-0003-0490-0885","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette K.","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","name_org":"Ersbøll, Annette K.","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28714553"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bdi.12524","issn":["13985647","13992406"],"issn_org":["13995618"],"issue":"7","journal":"Bipolar Disorders","pages":"563-567","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Bipolar Disorders","title_org":"Bipolar Disorders (English Edition, Online)","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85024479585"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-136df1ab-6b8a-4252-945f-82230ae84bdb","ku-a5cbf3a5-ac6b-479d-b43b-7fa7521254cf","sdu-703e27b3-1573-4126-a711-776ae5ced980"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Lithium in drinking water and the incidence of bipolar disorder: A nation-wide population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-666096","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The objective of this paper is to develop a new operational strategy to increase the lifetime of a high temperature proton exchange membrane (HT-PEMFCs) fuel cell system by using load cycling patterns to reduce the phosphoric acid loss from the fuel cell. Four single cells were operated under different current cycling profile, while one cell was operated at constant current density for comparison. Polarization curves and electrochemical impedance spectroscopy measurements were recorded during the course of the tests and analysed. Two different current densities, 0.2 Acm-2 for the lower end and 0.8 Acm-2 for the higher end, were selected for the load cycling operation. The relaxation time, which is the period of time spent at low current density operation, is varied to understand how the performance over prolonged period behaves. The duration of the high current density operation is selected based on the relaxation time in order to have the same average current density of (0.55 Acm-2 ) for all the cells. Cell 5, with a relaxation time of 2 min performs best and shows lower degradation rate of 36 μVh-1 compared to other load cycling cells with smaller relaxation times. The cell operated at constant current density shows a degradation rate of 57 μVh-1, which is 1.5 times higher than the degradation rate of cell 5.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thomas, Sobi","Jeppesen, Christian","Steenberg, Thomas","Araya, Samuel Simon","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061250"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomas, Sobi"],"keyword":["Fuel cell","High temperature PEM","Impedance","Load cycling","Phosphoric acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new load cycling strategy for enhanced durability of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85030660801&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-061250","identifier":[{"id":"85030660801","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000415768200025","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-2696bc57-b14f-4e81-abd7-1a5f7f31b028"],"keyword":["Fuel cell","High temperature PEM","Impedance","Load cycling","Phosphoric acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2319A369E33E702787584E864A172DDD"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Danish Power Systems Ltd."],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"0e062d6c-eeae-49d3-ae56-d750f51b90b7","name":"Jeppesen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0297-6854","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"steenbergpau","last":"Steenberg","name":"Steenberg, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2017.09.018","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"44","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"27230-27240","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030660801"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","danish power systems ltd."],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2696bc57-b14f-4e81-abd7-1a5f7f31b028"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"New load cycling strategy for enhanced durability of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061250","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents an experimental characterization of a high temperature protonexchange membrane fuel cell (HT-PEMFC) short stack carried out by means of impedance spectroscopy. Selected operating parameters; temperature, stoichiometry and reactant compositions were varied to investigate their effects on a reformate-operated stack. Polarization curves were also recorded to complement the impedance analysis of the researched phenomena. An equivalent circuit model was used to estimate the different resistances at varying parameters. It showed a significantly higher low frequency resistance at lower stoichiometry. Both anode and cathode stoichiometric ratios had significant effects on the stack performance during the dry hydrogen and reformate operation modes. In both cases the effects faded away when sufficient mass transport was achieved, which took place at λanode= 1.3 for dry hydrogen, λanode= 1.6 for reformate operation and λcathode= 4.The work also compared dry hydrogen, steam reforming and autothermal reforming gas feeds at160 ◦Cand showed appreciably lower performance in the case of autothermal reforming at the same stoichiometry, mainly attributable to mass transport related issues. In a CO poisoning analysis the stack showed good tolerance to concentration up to 1% CO in the fuel stream.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Araya, Samuel Simon","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063913"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Degradation","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Fuel cell","HTPEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrochemical impedance spectroscopy eis characterization of reformate operated high temperature pem fuel cell stack","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22606/ijper.2017.11003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-063913","ids":["aau-2fd6f589-8273-4465-9001-719e2f6bc324"],"keyword":["Degradation","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Fuel cell","HTPEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7D362DB6F0FD819E5DD1914AFC5E847B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260053438/PER_100005_2017052510532439866.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22606/ijper.2017.11003","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22606/ijper.2017.11003","issn":["25210343"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Power and Energy Research","pages":"20-40","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Power and Energy Research","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2fd6f589-8273-4465-9001-719e2f6bc324"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy (EIS) Characterization of Reformate-operated High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell Stack","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063913","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In order to analyze the dynamic behavior of a Lithium-ion (Li-ion) battery and to determine their suitability for various applications, battery models are needed. An equivalent electrical circuit model is the most common way of representing the behavior of a Li-ion battery. There are different circuit models proposed and various techniques for parameterization of these models available in literature. Nevertheless, in this paper a second order equivalent circuit is proposed and the current pulse technique is used for its parameterization. This study shows results of extensive experimental characterization tests performed for a wide range of operating conditions (temperature, load current and state-of-charge) on a commercial available 13Ah high-power lithium titanate oxide battery cell. The obtained results were used to parametrize the proposed dynamic model of the battery cell. To assess the accuracy of the proposed dynamic model, simulation results are presented and compared against laboratory measurements, performed for different conditions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Stroe, Ana-Irina","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Teodorescu, Remus","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069735"],"event":{"end":"2017-05-27","place":"Brasov, ro","start":"2017-05-25","title":"Joint International Conference OPTIM-ACEMP Optimization of Electrical and Electronic Equipment Aegean Conference on ELectrical Machines and Power Electronics","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dynamic model","Lithium ion battery","Simulation","Voltage estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lithium ion battery dynamic model for wide range of operating conditions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=7975044","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-069735","identifier":[{"id":"000426909600100","type":"wos"},{"id":"85027694687","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-44017f71-cca1-44b4-b045-106cbd0f306e"],"keyword":["Dynamic model","Lithium-ion battery","Simulation","Voltage estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FC46360B0229FF920B4AC49A0B53E6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=7975044","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana-Irina","key":"stroeanairinapau","last":"Stroe","locid":"e6ff6bac-362f-4fd1-b46c-d5f62d1e2c1a","name":"Stroe, Ana-Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-8254","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroedanielioanpau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskimaciejjozefpau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescuremuspau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærsørenknudsenpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/optim.2017.7975044","eisbn":["9781509044894"],"pages":"660-666","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2017 International Conference on Optimization of Electrical and Electronic Equipment (OPTIM) &amp; 2017 Intl Aegean Conference on Electrical Machines and Power Electronics (ACEMP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027694687"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-44017f71-cca1-44b4-b045-106cbd0f306e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Lithium-ion battery dynamic model for wide range of operating conditions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069735","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Lithium-ion battery second life usage might be an interesting solution for certain applications and it can bring not only environmental benefits but also e.g. lower electric vehicles or hybrid electric vehicles total cost of ownership. However, the electrical performance and performance degradation of the battery systems in the second life application are still unknown what brings significant economic risk and hinders second life battery usage. This work investigates the capacity and power degradation of the 2.5Ah nanophosphate LiFePO4/C cells under different the second life calendar ageing regimes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085609"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-14","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2017-09-11","title":"19th European Conference on Power Electronics and Applications, EPE'17 ECCE Europe","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Calendar ageing","Degradation","Lithium batteries","Second life"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calendar ageing of lifepo000000000004 c batteries in the second life applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-085609","identifier":[{"id":"000418374404040","type":"wos"},{"id":"85042154407","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7a61c582-da21-4fdd-8e29-47e1269da134"],"keyword":["Lithium batteries","calendar ageing","degradation","second life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54DF67610F490F743E632A19C6AF13E2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/epe17ecceeurope.2017.8099173","eisbn":["9789075815276"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2017 19th European Conference on Power Electronics and Applications (EPE'17 ECCE Europe)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042154407"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7a61c582-da21-4fdd-8e29-47e1269da134"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Calendar Ageing of LiFePO4/C Batteries in the Second Life Applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-085609","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Current lithium-ion battery research aims in not only increasing their energy density but also power density. Emerging applications of lithium-ion batteries (hybrid electric vehicles, plug-in hybrid electric vehicles, grid support) are becoming more and more power demanding. The increasing charging and discharging power capability rates of lithium-ion batteries raises safety concerns and requires thermal management of the entire battery system. Moreover, lithium-ion battery's temperature influences both battery short term (capacity, efficiency, self-discharge) and long-term (lifetime) behaviour. Thus, thermal modelling of lithium-ion battery cells and battery packs is gaining importance. Equivalent thermal circuits' models have proven to be relatively accurate with a low computational burden for the price of low spatial resolution; nevertheless, they usually require expensive equipment for parametrization. Recent research initiated by Barsoukov et al. proposed electrothermal impedance spectroscopy as a novel and non-destructive method of characterizing the thermal properties of batteries by defining frequency dependent thermal impedance. Despite its usefulness, the electrothermal impedance spectroscopy method can be still improved in terms of e.g. accuracy and measurement time and it has a potential to be extended to new applications. Performed review indicates that the electrothermal impedance spectroscopy is a very promising, non-destructive, simple and especially cost-efficient method for thermal characterization of batteries. The scientific intention of this paper is to collect and systematize the state of knowledge about electrothermal impedance spectroscopy and present different measurement methods on the example of a high-power lithium battery cell and finally to discuss the prospect.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Stanciu, Tiberiu","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092605"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery thermal model","Lithium ion battery","Thermal impedance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrothermal impedance spectroscopy as a cost efficient method for determining thermal parameters of lithium ion batteries prospects measurement methods and the state of knowledge","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0959652616314500","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-092605","identifier":[{"id":"84994409980","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000401887700009","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-927b777d-dde9-4c9b-9566-04b8484d2da1"],"keyword":["Battery thermal model","Electrothermal impedance spectroscopy","Lithium-ion battery","Thermal impedance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-034316A928CADF100B73CC24DD8A39A3"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tiberiu","key":"stanciupau","last":"Stanciu","locid":"f16625ba-f630-4152-b06a-7bfbb0561d5e","name":"Stanciu, Tiberiu","orcid":"0000-0003-2447-5257","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jclepro.2016.09.109","issn":["09596526"],"issue":"Part 1","journal":"Journal of Cleaner Production","pages":"63-71","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cleaner Production","volume":"155"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994409980"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-927b777d-dde9-4c9b-9566-04b8484d2da1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Electrothermal impedance spectroscopy as a cost efficient method for determining thermal parameters of lithium ion batteries : Prospects, measurement methods and the state of knowledge","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092605","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper a method for estimating the fuel cell impedance is presented, namely the current pulse injection (CPI) method, which is well suited for online implementation. This method estimates the fuel cell impedance and unlike electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS), it is simple to implement at a low cost. This makes it appealing as a characterization method for on-line diagnostic algorithms. In this work a parameter estimation method for estimation of equivalent electrical circuit (EEC) parameters, which is suited for on-line use is proposed. Tests on a 10 cell high temperature PEM fuel cell show that the method yields consistent results in estimating EEC parameters for different current pulse at different current loads, with a low variance. A comparison with EIS shows that despite its simplicity the response of CPI can reproduce well the impedance response of the high and intermediate frequencies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Christian","Araya, Samuel Simon","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-097928"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jeppesen, Christian"],"keyword":["Characterization","EIS","Fuel cell","PEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an eis alternative for impedance measurement of a high temperature pem fuel cell stack based on current pulse injection","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260479252/20170509_FUCE16_paper_chj.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-097928","identifier":[{"id":"000405043000016","type":"wos"},{"id":"85020083939","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a514d4c5-989d-4737-b915-3159a18bd48d"],"keyword":["CPI","Characterization","Current pulse injection","EIS","Fuel cell","PEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0996543934E6B3BE98605B1F28090F1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260479252/20170509_FUCE16_paper_chj.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SerEnergy"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"0e062d6c-eeae-49d3-ae56-d750f51b90b7","name":"Jeppesen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0297-6854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2017.05.066","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"24","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"15851-15860","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020083939"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","serenergy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a514d4c5-989d-4737-b915-3159a18bd48d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An EIS alternative for impedance measurement of a high temperature PEM fuel cell stack based on current pulse injection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-097928","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The objective of this paper is to separate out the effects of methanol and water vapour on a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell under different temperatures (160°C and 180°C) and current densities (0.2Acm-2, 0.4Acm-2 and 0.6Acm-2). The degradation rates at the different current densities and temperatures are analysed and discussed. The results are supported by IV curves and impedance spectroscopy. The individual resistance variations are extracted by equivalent circuit model fitting of the impedance spectra. The presence of water in the anode feed enhances the performance while the presence of 5% methanol tends to degrade the cell performance. However, the presence of H2O mitigates some of the adverse effects of methanol. The effect of varying fuel compositions was found to be more prominent at lower current densities. The voltage improves significantly when adding water vapour to the anode after pure hydrogen operation at 180°C. A decrease in the total resistance corresponding to the voltage improvement is observed from the impedance spectra. There is minimal variation in performance with the introduction of 3% and 5% methanol along with water vapour in the anode feed at all current densities and operating temperatures. The overall degradation over a period of 1915h is -44μVh-1. The test time includes 595h of test with pure H2 and 300h test each with 15% H2O, 3% CH3OH+15% H2O and 5% CH3OH+15% H2O at varying current densities and temperatures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomas, Sobi","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomas, Sobi"],"keyword":["Equivalent circuit model","HT PEMFC","Impedance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental study to distinguish the effects of methanol slip and water vapour on a high temperature pem fuel cell at different operating conditions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85009165631&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-123625","identifier":[{"id":"85009165631","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000396950300034","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-fd7097f4-582d-4445-b35f-fef5b3b3884f"],"keyword":["Equivalent circuit model","HT-PEMFC","Impedance","Reformed methanol"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5FCA338538CADBA1E36A50A42CA66BE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2016.11.063","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","pages":"422-436","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"192"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009165631"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fd7097f4-582d-4445-b35f-fef5b3b3884f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental study to distinguish the effects of methanol slip and water vapour on a high temperature PEM fuel cell at different operating conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123625","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Perturbations in the insulin-like growth factor (IGF) system may contribute to the accelerated cardiovascular disease (CVD) that occurs in patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D). However, it remains unknown whether the IGF system is also involved in the development of early, subclinical CVD. We characterised the IGF system in T2D patients and matched controls and examined the associations with markers of subclinical target organ damage. Methods: The study included 99 patients with recently diagnosed T2D and 99 age- and sex-matched controls. IGF-1 and IGFBP-1 to -4 were measured by immunoassays, as were pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A) and the PAPP-A-generated N-terminal (NT) and C-terminal (CT) IGFBP-4 fragments, which are novel CVD risk markers. Arterial stiffness was evaluated by carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity (PWV). Cerebral white matter lesions (WMLs) and carotid artery remodelling were determined by MRI. Results: After multivariate adjustments, patients with T2D had lower concentrations of IGFBP-2, IGFBP-4, NT- and CT-IGFBP-4, when compared with controls. IGFBP-2 was inversely correlated to PWV in all subjects in multivariate analysis (P < 0.05), and IGFBP-3 was inversely associated with severity of WMLs (P < 0.05). The NT-IGFBP-4 fragment was associated with the degree of carotid artery remodelling among all subjects (regression coefficient (95% CI): 2.95 (0.70, 5.16), P = 0.011). Levels of NT- and CT-IGFBP-4 were reduced in T2D patients receiving metformin compared to those in controls and patients not receiving metformin. Conclusions: Even in recently diagnosed and well-controlled T2D patients, IGF protein levels are altered and associated with CVD risk factors.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hjortebjerg, Rikke","Laugesen, Esben","Høyem, Pernille","Oxvig, Claus","Stausbøl-Grøn, Brian","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Kim, Won Yong","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","Hansen, Troels Krarup","Bjerre, Mette","Frystyk, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-149169"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the igf system in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes associations with markers of cardiovascular target organ damage","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85015591740","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-149169","identifier":[{"id":"85015591740","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28179448","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-22970e29-9afa-48b1-bcc0-e470effcbbbd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-555362923338B8F2E8F1AD135FF03042"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","locid":"d7f05783-92a6-4c22-9d46-9bd0128122b4","name":"Hjortebjerg, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"laugesenpau","last":"Laugesen","locid":"e06ca9b7-d51f-40f2-b042-696ca2b18492","name":"Laugesen, Esben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"høyempau","last":"Høyem","locid":"cbd0d45d-3fcf-4208-93ca-d5f580739f1a","name":"Høyem, Pernille","rank":