{"abstract":"De danske medieudbyderes vilkår, værdikæder og forretningsmodeller har på 30 år ændret sig fundamentalt gennem en globalisering, en digitalisering og en datafcering af mediemarkedet. Udviklingen er drevet af aktører, der ikke selv er en del af den gamle mediebranche: de udenlandske teknologivirksomheder.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Flyverbom, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-298493"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mediebranchens transformation fra analog indhegning til digital grænseløshed","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58900408/Afsluttende_rapport_Globalisering_af_den_danske_mediebranche_13_09_2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-298493","ids":["cbs-f216e48a-8c4e-4873-8e2b-0155e391536a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CE9BD0820472C6FAD3944CACCF2028A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58900408/Afsluttende_rapport_Globalisering_af_den_danske_mediebranche_13_09_2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"flyverbompau","last":"Flyverbom","locid":"85ddabd4-7915-496a-81e1-41610119ef88","name":"Flyverbom, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-9465-6219","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisbeth","key":"knudsenpedh","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Lisbeth","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Schultz","key":"jørgensenpedh","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Søren Schultz","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["2445852X"],"pages":"19-26","place":"København","publisher":"Slots- og Kulturstyrelsen","series":"Mediernes udvikling i Danmark","status":"p","subtitle":"Analyser af internationale aktørers betydning for det danske mediemarked, danske medieudbydere og dansk medieindhold","title":"Globaliseringen af den danske mediebranche"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-f216e48a-8c4e-4873-8e2b-0155e391536a"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Mediebranchens transformation : Fra analog indhegning til digital grænseløshed","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-298493","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Suicide is a major public health concern. High-dose lithium is used to stabilize mood and prevent suicide in patients with affective disorders. Lithium occurs naturally in drinking water worldwide in much lower doses, but with large geographical variation. Several studies conducted at an aggregate level have suggested an association between lithium in drinking water and a reduced risk of suicide; however, a causal relation is uncertain. Individual-level register-based data on the entire Danish adult population (3.7 million individuals) from 1991 to 2012 were linked with a moving five-year time-weighted average (TWA) lithium exposure level from drinking water hypothesizing an inverse relationship. The mean lithium level was 11.6 µg/L ranging from 0.6 to 30.7 µg/L. The suicide rate decreased from 29.7 per 100,000 person-years at risk in 1991 to 18.4 per 100,000 person-years in 2012. We found no significant indication of an association between increasing five-year TWA lithium exposure level and decreasing suicide rate. The comprehensiveness of using individual-level data and spatial analyses with 22 years of follow-up makes a pronounced contribution to previous findings. Our findings demonstrate that there does not seem to be a protective effect of exposure to lithium on the incidence of suicide with levels below 31 µg/L in drinking water.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Knudsen, Nikoline N.","Schullehner, Jörg","Hansen, Birgitte","Jørgensen, Lisbeth F.","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Voutchkova, Denitza","Gerds, Thomas A.","Andersen, Per K.","Bihrmann, Kristine","Grønbæk, Morten","Kessing, Lars Vedel","Kjær Ersbøll, Annette"],"cuid":["S03-098.99-030927"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, South","Nordic"],"country":["Greenland","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Denmark","Drinking water","Exposure assessment","Individual level data","Journal Article","Lithium","Spatial analysis","Suicide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lithium in drinking water and incidence of suicide a nationwide individual level cohort study with 000000000022 years of follow up","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph14060627","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.99-030927","identifier":[{"id":"85020768130","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5486313","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28604590","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-fe5be094-dc85-4fd1-bf40-6e65bf4c9a05","ku-481b8d2c-0f2e-4cfa-b3fa-de18543e8acc","sdu-fd91c1c4-687f-4b3b-a6d8-94b96e17ee68"],"keyword":["Denmark","Drinking water","Exposure assessment","Individual-level data","Journal Article","Lithium","Spatial analysis","Suicide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-260BA44577C2D6B4DD39D596FF3DE357"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/188963757/Lithium_in_Drinking_Water_and_Incidence_of_Suicide_A_Nationwide_Individual_Level_Cohort_Study_with_22_Years_of_Follow_Up.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph14060627","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129631871/Lithium_in_Drinking_Water_and_Incidence_of_Suicide.pdf","version":