1c4-687f-4b3b-a6d8-94b96e17ee68"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Lithium in Drinking Water and Incidence of Suicide : A Nationwide Individual-Level Cohort Study with 22 Years of Follow-Up","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.99-030927","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The recent acceleration in hydrogen production’s R&D will lead the energy transition. Low temperature polymer electrolyte membrane electrolysis (LT-PEME) is one of the most promising candidate technologies to produce hydrogen from renewable energy sources, and for synthetic fuel production. LT-PEME splits water into hydrogen and oxygen when the voltage is applied between anode and cathode. Electrical current forces the positively charged ions to migrate to negatively charged cathode through PEM, where hydrogen is produced. Meanwhile, oxygen is produced at the anode side electrode and escapes as a gas with the circulating water. The effects of clamping pressure (Pc) on the LT-PEME cell performance, polarization resistances, and hydrogen and water crossover through the membrane, and hydrogen and oxygen production rate are studied. A 50 cm2 active area LT-PEME cell designed and manufactured in house is utilized in this work. Higher Pc has shown higher cell performance this refers to lower ohmic and activation resistances. Water crossover from anode to cathode is slightly decreased at higher Pc resulting in a slight decrease in hydrogen crossover from cathode to anode. Also, the percentage of hydrogen in the produced oxygen at the anode side is significantly reduced at higher Pc and at lower current density.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Cui, Xiaoti","Frensch, Steffen Henrik","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064056"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Polarization curve","Polarization resistances","Proton exchange membrane electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in situ experimental characterization of the clamping pressure effects on low temperature polymer electrolyte membrane electrolysis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448950741/In_situ_experimental_characterization_of_theclamping_pressure_effects_on_low_temperaturepolymer_electrolyte_membrane_electrolysis.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064056","identifier":[{"id":"000411545300003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85026519919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-30673898-06d7-416a-98d4-02e0dff865ad"],"keyword":["Clamping pressure","Hydrogen crossover rate","Polarization curve","Polarization resistances","Proton exchange membrane electrolysis","Water crossover rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBF71FA45AD3A8F3E2CAF9985B766A75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/448950741/In_situ_experimental_characterization_of_theclamping_pressure_effects_on_low_temperaturepolymer_electrolyte_membrane_electrolysis.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoti","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","locid":"569f8898-f768-496f-8fc3-c93d917ef238","name":"Cui, Xiaoti","orcid":"0000-0001-6514-0280","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen Henrik","key":"frenschpau","last":"Frensch","locid":"81f53416-7408-4e66-9964-11ce7c6aafc9","name":"Frensch, Steffen Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2017.07.059","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"34","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"21597-21606","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026519919"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-30673898-06d7-416a-98d4-02e0dff865ad"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"In-situ experimental characterization of the clamping pressure effects on low temperature polymer electrolyte membrane electrolysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064056","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This study proposes a data-drive impedance-based methodology for fault detection and isolation of low and high cathode stoichiometry, high CO concentration in the anode gas, high methanol vapour concentrations in the anode gas and low anode stoichiometry, for high temperature PEM fuel cells. The fault detection and isolation algorithm is based on an artificial neural network classifier, which uses three extracted features as input. Two of the proposed features are based on angles in the impedance spectrum, and are therefore relative to specific points, and shown to be independent of degradation, contrary to other available feature extraction methods in the literature. The experimental data is based on a 35 day experiment, where 2010 unique electrochemical impedance spectroscopy measurements were recorded. The test of the algorithm resulted in a good detectability of the faults, except for high methanol vapour concentration in the anode gas fault, which was found to be difficult to distinguish from a normal operational data. The achieved accuracy for faults related to CO pollution, anode- and cathode stoichiometry is 100% success rate. Overall global accuracy on the test data is 94.6%.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Christian","Araya, Samuel Simon","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Thomas, Sobi","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089639"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jeppesen, Christian"],"keyword":["Classification","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy EIS","Fault diagnosis","Fuel cell","PEM","Pattern recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fault detection and isolation of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell stack under the influence of degradation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260486163/20170627_1500_HTPEM_FDI_chj.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-089639","identifier":[{"id":"000403548200005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85019879701","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8800f802-ebff-476b-b436-cf014adfc03d"],"keyword":["Classification","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS)","Fault diagnosis","Fuel cell","PEM","Pattern recognition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-916B76BD1477269C54E2A5DCBC4C2E33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/260486163/20170627_1500_HTPEM_FDI_chj.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SerEnergy"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"0e062d6c-eeae-49d3-ae56-d750f51b90b7","name":"Jeppesen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0297-6854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2017.05.021","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"37-47","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"359"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019879701"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","serenergy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8800f802-ebff-476b-b436-cf014adfc03d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Fault detection and isolation of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell stack under the influence of degradation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089639","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The modern civilization is working based on a secure, sustainable, and economic energy. With the increasing share of renewable energies like solar and wind power, the secure and sustainable energy production will go under threat due to highly fluctuating electricity generated from these energy sources. An opportunity is to store energy as a means of energy surplus absorption. Polymer Electrolyte Membrane Electrolysis Cell (PEMEC) as a method of long term (more than an hour) energy storage, converts the unstable generated electricity to hydrogen. It is a key technology for closing the renewable energy economical system loop. It converts water to oxygen and high pressure hydrogen using electricity with a fast response rate that suits to damp grid fluctuations. One of the issues within these electrolysers is their high cost. One means of the cost reduction is to increase production from the existing cell by increasing its current density from 1 (A/cm2) (at the existing conventional cells) to 5 (A/cm2). At high current densities, due to high rate of oxygen generation and concentrated heat generation in the cell, issues related to heat and gas management come up which must be managed. In this study, an experimental setup is made of plexiglass, Titanium-felt (Ti-felt) and nano-porous ceramic. The setup demonstrates a similar gas-liquid flow encounters in PEM water electrolysis micro-channels and anode porous media. The nano-porous ceramic plate simulates small bubbles generation on the real membrane electrode assembly (MEA) surface. The movement of gas-liquid flow upward in the micro-channel at several water stoichiometric numbers are analysed and compared with a transparent PEMEC.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","Olesen, Anders Christian","Al Shakhshir, Saher","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095507"],"event":{"end":"2017-10-05","place":"National Harbor, us","start":"2017-10-01","title":"232nd ECS Meeting","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysing gas liquid flow in pem electrolyser micro channels using a micro porous ceramic as gas permeable wall","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1149/08008.1107ecst","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095507","identifier":[{"id":"85049634092","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000425016500113","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-9cba6e68-d061-4133-aa32-d00c2fd1673f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33C2C20778C921479C87D64A0996F215"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1149/08008.1107ecst","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ecst.ecsdl.org/content/80/8/1107.abstract","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/269826783/Sadeghi_Lafmejani_et_al._2017_Analysing_Gas_Liquid_Flow_in_PEM_Electrolyser_Micro_Channels_Using_a_Micro_Porous_Ceramic_as_Gas_Perme.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","us