{"abstract":"How can gardening in the eighteenth century be compared with contemporary tendencies and hallenges, first and foremost with regards to the influence of climate changes: urban gardens, guerilla gardens, biodiversity, and so on? Gardens have from the early modern period been regarded as a third nature: artificial, formed by man, and different from wilderness - the first nature - as well as agricultural land - the second nature. This special interaction between nature and human beings makes gardens special kinds of places. Michel Foucault categorizes gardens as contradictory sites, the so called heterotopias. From ancient times gardens have been places of the acres, of ideas of Paradise, Arcadia, Elysium - but also of political power and control. They have been metaphors of religious, philosophical, and political ideas. In addition to these conceptual and cultural levels there is a level of concrete practice. The paradise of the garden is the place of care (Robert Pugue Harrison 2008). This chapter examines how the ideas of vita activa (Hanna Arendt 1958) occur in the eighteenth century in 'how-to' gardening books and in the practice of the Danish garden enthusiast Johan Bülow, who created the garden of Sanderumgaard.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Knudsen, Karin Esmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"johan bülows spade havepraksis i 000000001700 tallet","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-638159","ids":["sdu-e2bc863e-c329-40e0-b8e7-a71e68180132"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-62DEF1F5B28BB85C10367B58378F0793"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Literature"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin Esmann","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"1092fb7d-a253-484b-8294-3ff955c787da","name":"Knudsen, Karin Esmann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"bredsdorffpedh","last":"Bredsdorff","name":"Bredsdorff, Thomas","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Peter","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Søren Peter","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793060524"],"place":"København","publisher":"U Press","status":"p","subtitle":"2000-tals spørgsmål, 1700-tals svar","title":"Det lange lys"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e2bc863e-c329-40e0-b8e7-a71e68180132"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Johan Bülows spade : Havepraksis i 1700-tallet","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-638159","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"PEM water electrolysis is a key component for closing the loop of the renewable energy eco-system. In particular, these high response water electrolysers are suitable for fluctuating power sources. Conventional PEM water electrolysers are typically operated at a current density of around 1 A/cm2 and are fairly expensive. One means of increasing the hydrogen yield to cost ratio of such systems, is to increase the operating current density. However, at high current densities, management of heat and mass transfer in the anode current collector and channel becomes crucial. This entails that further understanding of the gas-liquid flow in both the porous media and the channel is necessary for insuring proper oxygen, water and heat management of the electrolysis cell. In this work, the patterns of vertical upward gas-liquid flow in a 5×1×94 mm micro-channel are experimentally analysed. A sheet of titanium felt is used as a permeable wall for permeation of air through a column of water similar to the phenomenon encountered at the anode. The transparent setup is operated ex-situ and the gas-liquid flow regimes are identified using a camera.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056859"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysing gas liquid flow in pem electrolyser micro channels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-056859","identifier":[{"id":"84991735445","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-172c7c4f-9599-4eca-ba05-b005e10f7836"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-360A751DC52C8AC3245532BF8CCC1F24"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saeed Sadeghi","key":"lafmejanipau","last":"Lafmejani","locid":"db40a4cb-554f-4515-aaa1-724aa7c708a0","name":"Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","orcid":"0000-0002-1780-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/07514.1121ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"14","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"1121-1127","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991735445"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-172c7c4f-9599-4eca-ba05-b005e10f7836"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analysing Gas-Liquid Flow in PEM Electrolyser Micro-Channels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056859","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Lithium-ion batteries are regarded as the key energy storage technology for both e-mobility and stationary renewable energy storage applications. Nevertheless, the Lithium-ion batteries are complex energy storage devices, which are characterized by a complex degradation behavior, which affects both their capacity and internal resistance. This paper investigates, based on extended laboratory calendar ageing tests, the degradation of the internal resistance of a Lithium-ion battery. The dependence of the internal resistance increase on the temperature and state-of-charge level have been extensive studied and quantified. Based on the obtained laboratory results, an accurate semi-empirical lifetime model, which is able to predict with high accuracy the internal resistance increase of the Lithium-ion battery over a wide temperature range and for all state-of-charge levels was proposed and validated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Teodorescu, Remus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085370"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-22","place":"Milwaukee, WI, us","start":"2016-09-18","title":"8th Annual IEEE Energy Conversion Congress &amp; Exposition","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Calendar ageing","Degradation","Internal Resistance","Lithium ion battery","Modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comprehensive study on the degradation of lithium ion batteries during calendar ageing the internal resistance increase","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-085370","identifier":[{"id":"85015417847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-799e3949-8bf8-4712-8883-062b23af19ae"],"keyword":["Calendar Ageing","Degradation","Internal Resistance","Lithium-ion Battery","Modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FCC1A8ACCA842353B832B37F8C45EC4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescupau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce.2016.7854664","eisbn":["9781509007370"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 8th Annual IEEE Energy Conversion Congress &amp; Exposition (ECCE), 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015417847"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-799e3949-8bf8-4712-8883-062b23af19ae"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Comprehensive Study on the Degradation of Lithium-Ion Batteries during Calendar Ageing : The Internal Resistance Increase","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-085370","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Proton exchange membrane fuel cells (PEMFC’s) are becoming increasingly popular for uninterrupted power supply especially in remote areas. In the case of telecom back-up operations, PEMFC systems are often placed in areas of extreme climates, e.g. in Norway or Canada where the temperatures drop below -20 °C in the winter which make liquid-cooled fuel cells impossible. In such cases, air-cooled fuel cell systems are deployed where the air that is fed to the fuel cell serves both as reactant supplier and coolant to remove the waste heat that is generated during fuel cell operation. In some cases the warmer exhaust air is used to pre-heat and also humidify the incoming colder and dryer air stream using an enthalpy wheel. It is important to thermodynamically understand such a fuel cell system, and in this work the enthalpy streams and the humidity stream are followed throughout the fuel cell system in order to optimize the operating conditions and the performance of such a system. The adjustable parameters include the fan speed that determines the amount of air that is brought into the system, and the size and rotating speed of the rotating enthalpy wheel. In addition, computational fluid dynamics simulations have been carried out to better understand the distribution of the reactant air over the fuel cell stack and the resulting temperature distribution across the stack. These results suggest that the humidifying function of the current enthalpy wheel is negligible and a smaller enthalpy wheel or an ordinary heat exchanger can fulfill the heat recovery demand. Despite the fact that the air enters the stack at a cold temperature, even the forefront of the stack is at a much elevated and desired stack temperature with the help of supplying an acceptable amount of power to an electric stack heater. So a preheating of the air stream by the enthalpy wheel might be unnecessary during steady-state operation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gao, Xin","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090792"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-07","place":"Honolulu, Hawaii, us","start":"2016-10-02","title":"PRiME 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enthalpy analysis and heat exchanger sizing of an air cooled proton exchange membrane fuel cell system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266665319/PRiME_2016_Enthalpy_analysis_and_Heat_Exchanger_Sizing_torsten_xga.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090792","ids":["aau-8c3227e0-0760-4184-83a0-13987cb019e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2DABF4B322ED1FF631925475C72BA62D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266665319/PRiME_2016_Enthalpy_analysis_and_Heat_Exchanger_Sizing_torsten_xga.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xin","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8c3227e0-0760-4184-83a0-13987cb019e1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Enthalpy analysis and Heat Exchanger Sizing of an Air-cooled Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell System","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-090792","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In PEM water electrolysis, a gaseous oxygen phase inherently develops and prevails the liquid water phase from uniformly distributing throughout the catalytic porous layer of the anode. An even distribution of liquid water not only ensures good mass transport characteristics of the reactant specie, it also secures an even heat removal of the cell. In a previous research effort, the gas-liquid, two-phase flow was investigated in the commercial CFD framework of ANSYS CFX using the Euler-Euler model. Particularly, the treatment of gas-liquid flow in a porous medium domain subject to capillary pressure was shown to push the limits of the codes ca-pabilities. In order to improve simulation stability and time, a new model is developed in the open source CFD software OpenFOAM. The customizability of this code not only allows for specific relaxation strategies, it also permits the implementation of various boundary conditions at porous-porous or porous-fluid interfaces found in the membrane electrode assembly. Particularly the treatment of a discontinuous phase volume fraction at the porous-porous interface, and the merging of two pressures fields into a single dominating at the porous-fluid interface influence the convergence stability of the solver.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093235"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-27","place":"Firenze, it","start":"2016-05-22","title":"The 9th International Conference on Multiphase Flow","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling of gas liquid two phase flow in porous media and channels of a pem water electrolysis cell using the euler euler framework of openfoam","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-093235","ids":["aau-94d91ee8-b00e-4ec2-a82f-0ed23385dd25"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-558F658A79EA850A0D7EFC5C5B40FF14"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94d91ee8-b00e-4ec2-a82f-0ed23385dd25"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modelling of gas-liquid, two-phase flow in porous media and channels of a PEM water electrolysis cell using the Euler-Euler framework of OpenFOAM","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093235","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"e-Cigarettes have gained worldwide popularity as a substitute for smoking, but concern has been raised regarding the long-term effects associated with their use. We report a case of a 45-yearold female consumer of e-cigarettes who presented with 4 months of abdominal pain and fever. Initial imaging discoveredmultiple pulmonary nodules and liver lesions suspicious of widespread metastases; however, an extensive evaluation found no evidence of malignancy. Results of a lung biopsy revealed an area withmultinucleated giant cells suggestive of a foreign body reaction to a lipophilic material. Upon cessation of e-cigarette use (known as vaping), the lung nodules disappeared, and the liver lesions regressed. Our case report suggests that vaping can induce an inflammatory reaction mimicking metastatic cancer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Madsen, Lene Margrethe Ring","Vinther Krarup, Niels Henrik","Bergmann, Troels Korshøj","Baerentzen, Steen","Neghabat, Shadman","Duval, Lone","Knudsen, Søren Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-152157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chest imaging","Foreign Bodies","Inflammation","Smoking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a cancer that went up in smoke pulmonary reaction to e cigarettes imitating metastatic cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960325435","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-152157","identifier":[{"id":"84960325435","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26965975","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-27c8c22b-b91a-469b-9a7c-6c1d51fdc381"],"keyword":["Biopsy (lung)","Chest imaging","Foreign bodies","Inflammation","Smoking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACE8A9FB377BA1BB293690428B67AF5B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism C"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Margrethe Ring","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Lene Margrethe Ring","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"vintherkraruppau","last":"Vinther Krarup","name":"Vinther Krarup, Niels Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels Korshøj","key":"bergmannpau","last":"Bergmann","locid":"18388434-1c3d-4d46-8bc9-9b1885a5ab2b","name":"Bergmann, Troels Korshøj","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen","key":"bærentzenpau","last":"Bærentzen","locid":"da87051c-cbe8-419a-92c8-0700c7f40899","name":"Baerentzen, Steen","name_org":"Bærentzen, Steen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shadman","key":"neghabatpau","last":"Neghabat","name":"Neghabat, Shadman","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"duvalpau","last":"Duval","locid":"119d0202-6a61-48b1-ab64-7c58ba736597","name":"Duval, Lone","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26965975"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.chest.2015.09.003","issn":["00123692","19313543"],"issn_org":["00123692"],"issue":"3","journal":"Chest","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Chest","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960325435"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-27c8c22b-b91a-469b-9a7c-6c1d51fdc381"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Cancer That Went Up in Smoke: Pulmonary Reaction to e-Cigarettes Imitating Metastatic Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-152157","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
