{"abstract":"High efficient and less pollutant fuel cell stacks are emerging and strong candidates of the power solution used for mobile base stations. In the application of the backup power, the availability and reliability hold the highest priority. This paper considers the reliability metrics from the component-level to the system-level for the power stage used in a fuel cell application. It starts with an estimation of the annual accumulated damage for the key power electronic components according to the real mission profile of the fuel cell system. Then, considering the parameter variations in both the lifetime model and the stress levels, the Weibull distribution of the power semiconductors lifetime can be obtained by using Monte Carlo analysis. Afterwards, the reliability block diagram can further be adopted to evaluate the reliability of the power stage based on the estimated power semiconductor reliability. In a case study of a 5 kW fuel cell power stage, the parameter variations of the lifetime model prove that the exponential factor of the junction temperature fluctuation is the most sensitive parameter. Besides, if a 5-out-of-6 redundancy is used, it is concluded both the B10 and the B1 system-level lifetime can be remarkably increased compared to when no redundancy is used.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Dao","Wang, Huai","Blaabjerg, Frede","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Hansen, Daniel Blom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-070260"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-22","place":"Milwaukee, WI, us","start":"2016-09-18","title":"8th Annual IEEE Energy Conversion Congress &amp; Exposition","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"system level reliability assessment of power stage in fuel cell application","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/327228074/PID4353245.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-070260","identifier":[{"id":"85015424281","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-45c2b269-f6f8-4c94-a79a-379934b544a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-79152C01EBF050F8CAC6464A1B13D7BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/327228074/PID4353245.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dantherm Power A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dao","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"8cf08fe2-24d6-4224-aaa2-f7e03a45debb","name":"Zhou, Dao","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-4309","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Huai","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"e8606356-85bc-4d6c-a091-e91dce99441a","name":"Wang, Huai","orcid":"0000-0002-5404-3140","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Blom","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Daniel Blom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce.2016.7855492","eisbn":["9781509007370"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015424281"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dantherm power a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-45c2b269-f6f8-4c94-a79a-379934b544a7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"System-level Reliability Assessment of Power Stage in Fuel Cell Application","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-070260","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The current status on the understanding of the various operational aspects of high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cells (HT-PEMFC) has been summarized. The paper focuses on phosphoric acid-doped polybenzimidazole (PBI)-based HT-PEMFCs and an overview of the common practices of their design and characterization techniques at single cell, stack and system levels is given. The state-of-the-art concepts of different degradation mechanisms and methods of their mitigation are also discussed. Moreover, accelerated stress testing (AST) procedures for HT-PEMFCs available in literature are outlined. Catalyst degradation and electrolyte loss take place at higher rates in the beginning of life of the fuel cell. This is due to the smaller size of Pt particles and the presence of excess phosphoric acid in the beginning of life that favor the respective degradation. Therefore, the redistribution of phosphoric acid in the membrane and the electrodes is crucial for the proper activation of the fuel cell, and a startup procedure should take this into account in order to avoid beginning of life degradation. On-line monitoring of the fuel cell system's state of health using diagnostic tools can help detect fuel cell faults for targeted interventions based on the observed conditions to prevent sudden failures and to prolong the fuel cell's lifetime. However, the technology is still under development and robust on-line diagnostics tools are hardly available. Currently, mitigation is mainly done based on favorable operating conditions and techniques to recover degradation and the development of more resistant components that can withstand the known degradation mechanisms.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Araya, Samuel Simon","Zhou, Fan","Liso, Vincenzo","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Thomas, Sobi","Gao, Xin","Jeppesen, Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Characterization","Degradation","Fuel cell","High temperature PEM fuel cell","PBI","Phosphoric acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comprehensive review of pbi based high temperature pem fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-107403","identifier":[{"id":"84997751523","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000389089600026","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-c59d4db2-7949-42a4-bec7-c04ff68f8bee"],"keyword":["Characterization","Degradation","Fuel cell","High temperature PEM fuel cell","PBI","Phosphoric acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B95BF9832441C2E939726809AFC5A55A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"simonarayapau","last":"Simon Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","name_org":"Simon Araya, Samuel","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"F