{"abstract":"In this paper, we explore the potential of using visual representations to support people in managing, organizing, and understanding relations between multiple visualization views. Multiple views can help people understand different facets of data and data processing, and are a crucial part of data analysis particularly when it is done collaboratively. Both the growing use of multiple views and the increasing display sizes have amplified the need to explore how to better help people to understand the relations between many views. To improve our understanding of how to visualize view relations, we invited visualization and interaction designers to critique and sketch representations of view relations. The participants provided design critiques, and sketched their own relation representations. Our findings expand the range and palette of ways of visually linking visualization views and suggest new directions for designing view relation representations to better support analysis with multiple views.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren","Carpendale, Sheelagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-487385"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","end":"2016-10-27","place":"Göteborg, se","start":"2016-10-23","title":"9th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Calgary"],"keyword":["Qualitative study","Visualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"view relations an exploratory study on between view meta visualizations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84997541822&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-487385","identifier":[{"id":"84997541822","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9d2c7634-f377-46e2-9dcb-e4a6035dff09"],"keyword":["Meta-visualization","Multiple and coordinated views","Qualitative study","View relations","Visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D8CB8B4F36C66DA70B94456845334E8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of calgary","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Calgary","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"60aa66e8-eac5-4487-94e1-f1379643b27d","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sheelagh","key":"carpendalepau","last":"Carpendale","name":"Carpendale, Sheelagh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2971485.2971566","eisbn":["9781450347631"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84997541822"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9d2c7634-f377-46e2-9dcb-e4a6035dff09"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"View relations : an exploratory study on between-view meta-visualizations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-487385","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Khuzestan, Iran is heavily industrialised with petrochemical and refinery companies. Herein, sediment and soil samples were collected from Hendijan coast, Khore Mosa and Arvandroud River. The CHEMSIC (CHEmometric analysis of Selected Ion Chromatograms) method was used to assign the main sources of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon (PAH) pollution. A four-component principal component analysis (PCA) model was obtained. While principal component 1 (PC1) was related to the total concentration of PAHs, the remaining PCs described three distinct sources: PC2 and PC3 collectively differentiate between weathered petrogenic and pyrogenic, and PC4 is indicative for a diagenetic input. The sources of PAHs in the Arvandroud River were mainly relatively fresh oil with some samples corresponding to a weathered oil input. Further, perylene (indicator for diagenetic source) was identified. Samples from Khore Mosa revealed a mixture with high proportions of high-molecular-weight PAHs, indicating a pyrogenic/weathered petrogenic source. Samples from Hendijan coast contained low relative concentrations of PAHs, thus only little information on pollution sources.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lübeck, Josephine S.","Poulsen, Kristoffer Gulmark","Knudsen, Sofie B.","Soleimani, Mohsen","Furbo, Søren","Tomasi, Giorgio","Christensen, Jan H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501013"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Natural Resources, Isfahan University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"source apportionment of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons pahs in sediments from khuzestan province iran","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-501013","identifier":[{"id":"84990960968","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27289289","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b41db275-d751-4250-85ef-236acc256244"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47210E4533831907AC5FA0022E08E28A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Environmental Chemistry and Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"department of natural resources isfahan university of technology","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Department of Natural Resources, Isfahan University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Josephine","key":"lübeckpau","last":"Lübeck","locid":"a831a649-ee78-4c6f-aca7-7b48c60419c8","name":"Lübeck, Josephine S.","name_org":"Lübeck, Josephine","orcid":"0000-0001-8124-6229","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristoffer Gulmark","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"91956feb-c80e-4ad3-9da9-33c3230c194e","name":"Poulsen, Kristoffer Gulmark","orcid":"0000-0002-9799-1175","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie B.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Sofie B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mohsen","key":"soleimanipau","last":"Soleimani","name":"Soleimani, Mohsen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"furbopau","last":"Furbo","locid":"343e8c6c-3f60-48b4-9099-50090a675b02","name":"Furbo, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-2044-7438","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Giorgio","key":"tomasipau","last":"Tomasi","locid":"3cd3a1d2-cdfb-4d74-9b3a-cf0ff9a329a5","name":"Tomasi, Giorgio","orcid":"0000-0003-0576-6868","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"9a1c0725-fbc4-4f5d-a42d-1f7c063c89c6","name":"Christensen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0003-1414-1886","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27289289"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marpolbul.2016.05.057","issn":["0025326X","18793363"],"issn_org":["0025326X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","pages":"584-590","status":"p","title":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84990960968"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b41db275-d751-4250-85ef-236acc256244"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Source apportionment of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) in sediments from Khuzestan province, Iran","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-501013","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":10,"contributors":["Madsen, Anne Marie Rosendahl","Uldum, Søren Anker","Holm, Anette","Kjelsø, Charlotte","Knudsen, Elisa","Løgstrup, Lene","Trunjer Kusk Nielsen, Marc","Skov, Marianne Nielsine","Jensen, Thøger Gorm","Kemp, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-574522"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-12","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2016-04-09","title":"26th European Congress of Clinical Microbiology and Infectious Diseases","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an outbreak of community acquired legionnaires disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-574522","ids":["sdu-049bc3b4-8910-4bdd-a3a5-fba5e7945879"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CF9E6FAFDA4CF185D91E69B3253E14E7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Marie","key":"rosendahlmadsenpau","last":"Rosendahl Madsen","locid":"ef92475a-7386-454d-9c19-215f4e8b3835","name":"Madsen, Anne Marie Rosendahl","name_org":"Rosendahl Madsen, Anne Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-3396-3554","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Anker","key":"uldumpau","last":"Uldum","name":"Uldum, Søren Anker","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"bf236581-7ff9-4735-9100-9e863e41e609","name":"Holm, Anette","orcid":"0000-0001-7794-2846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"kjelsøpau","last":"Kjelsø","name":"Kjelsø, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"cf03ebba-5e50-4c3d-8841-d71ab876d41a","name":"Knudsen, Elisa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"løgstruppau","last":"Løgstrup","name":"Løgstrup, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"trunjerkusknielsenpau","last":"Trunjer Kusk Nielsen","locid":"1f7690d9-c93e-4437-8890-83f03f03f528","name":"Trunjer Kusk Nielsen, Marc","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Nielsine","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"5b2553ab-dfde-4995-8c58-7840a16be668","name":"Skov, Marianne Nielsine","orcid":"0000-0002-2619-0864","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thøger Gorm","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5ef769d5-da5b-468a-b80a-75fcc537c166","name":"Jensen, Thøger Gorm","orcid":"0000-0002-3889-0016","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"kemppau","last":"Kemp","locid":"d28a28b7-cbe0-42f1-b2c6-ff6a89cafcf8","name":"Kemp, Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-5989-0421","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-049bc3b4-8910-4bdd-a3a5-fba5e7945879"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"An outbreak of community-acquired Legionnaires’ disease","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-574522","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background. CD163, a monocyte- and macrophage-specific scavenger receptor, is shed as soluble CD163 (sCD163) during the proinflammatory response. Here, we assessed the association between plasma sCD163 levels and progression to AIDS and all-cause mortality among individuals infected with human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV). Methods. Plasma sCD163 levels were measured in 933 HIV-infected individuals. Hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) associated with mortality were computed by Cox proportional hazards regression. Results. At baseline, 86% were receiving antiretroviral treatment, 73% had plasma a HIV RNA level of <50 copies/mL, and the median CD4 + T-cell count was 503 cells/μL. During 10.5 years of follow-up, 167 (17.9%) died. Plasma sCD163 levels were higher in nonsurvivors than in survivors (4.92 mg/L [interquartile range {IQR}, 3.29-8.65 mg/L] vs 3.16 mg/L [IQR, 2.16-4.64 mg/L]; P =. 0001). The cumulative incidence of death increased with increasing plasma sCD163 levels, corresponding to a 6% or 35% increased risk of death for each milligram per liter or quartile increase, respectively, in baseline plasma sCD163 level (adjusted HR, 1.06 [95% CI, 1.03-1.09] and 1.35 [95% CI, 1.13-1.63], respectively). Conclusions. Plasma sCD163 was an independent marker of all-cause mortality in a cohort of HIV-infected individuals, suggesting that monocyte/macrophage activation may play a role in HIV pathogenesis and be a target of intervention.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Knudsen, Troels Bygum","Ertner, Gideon","Petersen, Janne","Møller, Holger Jon","Moestrup, Søren Kragh","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Kronborg, Gitte","Benfield, Thomas"],"cuid":["S03-098.81-015207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["HIV","Inflammation","Journal Article","Mortality","Outcome","Soluble CD163"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma soluble cd000000000163 level independently predicts all cause mortality in hiv 000000000001 infected individuals","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84990946697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-098.81-015207","identifier":[{"id":"27354366","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84990946697","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000386147200015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-23e8192d-ffe5-4792-b41b-b9ba81adc4f6","ku-00a626a2-0d83-4d02-9b54-a2028d2d2f0c","sdu-5f7d85f7-c7a3-4b72-b141-6111d4dbe5b7"],"keyword":["HIV","Inflammation","Journal Article","Mortality","Outcome","Soluble CD163"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-7C4AA6B02BEE300597A4E66A6A8AA949"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Troels Bygum","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Troels Bygum","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gideon","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","name":"Ertner, Gideon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Janne","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1cb72724-54f8-4ca1-a201-bfa4a354a129","name":"Petersen, Janne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger Jon","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b08dc9ce-d595-49c6-833a-4ec9b4223a05","name":"Møller, Holger Jon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Kragh","key":"moestruppau","last":"Moestrup","locid":"84b91217-5ed8-4507-8a92-00c1815e2c81","name":"Moestrup, Søren Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-3862-2107","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"benfieldpau","last":"Benfield","locid":"03fdbbba-4bc0-41aa-845b-81ba0bded9ba","name":"Benfield, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-0698-9385","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27354366"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jiw263","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"8","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"1198-204","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","title_org":"Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"214"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84990946697"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-23e8192d-ffe5-4792-b41b-b9ba81adc4f6","ku-00a626a2-0d83-4d02-9b54-a2028d2d2f0c","sdu-5f7d85f7-c7a3-4b72-b141-6111d4dbe5b7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Plasma Soluble CD163 Level Independently Predicts All-Cause Mortality in HIV-1-Infected Individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.81-015207","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cells are getting growing interest in industrial areas like backup systems for telecom applications or power source for electric vehicles. Although these systems are characterized by long periods of inactivity, they must be able to start at any instant in the shortest time. However, the membrane of which PEMFCs are made of tends to dry out when not in use. This increases the time interval required to start the system up and could lead to the destruction of the fuel cell. In this article a start-up time measurement setup is presented, which is part of a larger project, the membrane hydration status estimator for monitoring the humidity of a fuel cell stack during standby. The fuel cell has been placed in a climatic chamber, connected to hydrogen and the start-up time has been measured with different environmental conditions. Based on the previous results and the ones presented in this paper a correlation between the start-up time and relative humidity of the membrane can be derived.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Török, Lajos","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Bidoggia, Benoit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055200"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-10","place":"Florence, it","start":"2016-06-07","title":"16th International Conference on Environment and Electrical Engineering, EEEIC 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Impedance","Relative humidity","Temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of membrane hydration status for active proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems by impedance measurement start up time measurements","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-055200","identifier":[{"id":"84988353031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-11a5dad6-d20d-4736-a43a-609d24bd9053"],"keyword":["Hydrogen (H2) start-up time","Impedance","Low temperature PEM fuel cell","Temperature","relative humidity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FDE31F7B7E0137794D22F2A5B63AD66B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["FLSmidth"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lajos","key":"törökpau","last":"Török","locid":"78d77d48-7ba5-4ad5-9ba9-8dc41019b8a5","name":"Török, Lajos","orcid":"0000-0002-4668-0588","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Benoit","key":"bidoggiapau","last":"Bidoggia","name":"Bidoggia, Benoit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/eeeic.2016.7555842","eisbn":["9781509023202"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of IEEE 16th International Conference on Environment and Electrical Engineering (EEEIC), 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988353031"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","flsmidth"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-11a5dad6-d20d-4736-a43a-609d24bd9053"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of membrane hydration status for active proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems by impedance measurement : Start-up time measurements","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055200","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this experiment-based research, the performance and behaviour of a pouch type Li-ion battery cell are reported. The commercial test cell has a Lithium Titanate Oxide (LTO) based anode with 13Ah capacity. It is accomplished by measuring the evolution of surface temperature distribution, and the heat flux of the battery cell at the same time. Temperatures on the surface of the cell are measured using contact thermocouples, whereas, the heat flux is measured simultaneously by the isothermal calorimeter. This heat flux measurement is used for determining the heat generation inside the cell. Consequently, using the heat generation result the important performance constituent of the battery cell efficiency is calculated. Those are accomplished at different temperature levels (-5&#x000B0;C, 10&#x000B0;C, 25&#x000B0;C and 40&#x000B0;C) of continuous charge and discharge constant current rate (1C,2C,4C,8C,10C (maximum)). There is a significant change in heat generation in both charge and discharge events on different temperature and C-rate. The heat flux change level is non-linear. This nonlinear heat flux is responsible for the nonlinear change of efficiency in different C-rate in a particular temperature. The presented experimental technique is a very precise determination to profile the battery cell. The result of the research can be incorporated in constructing a precise datasheet for a battery cell which can assist the researchers, engineers, and different stakeholders to enhance different aspects of battery research.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065672"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-20","place":"cn","start":"2016-10-17","title":"2016 IEEE Vehicle Power and Propulsion Conference (VPPC)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery behaviour","Battery efficiency","Battery thermal management","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Key performance indicator KPI","Spatial distribution","Surface temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of battery heat generation and key performance indicator efficiency using isothermal calorimeter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/251892097/Investigation_of_Battery_Heat_Generation_and_Key_Performance_Indicator_Efficiency_using_Isothermal_Calorimeter.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-065672","identifier":[{"id":"85011019670","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-35c62d35-66ed-4f9b-826a-a3826fed3f8e"],"keyword":["Battery behaviour","Battery efficiency","Battery thermal management","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Key performance indicator (KPI)","Lithium Titanate Oxide (LTO)","Spatial distribution","Surface temperature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3269C10CE737536ADE038688117106CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/251892097/Investigation_of_Battery_Heat_Generation_and_Key_Performance_Indicator_Efficiency_using_Isothermal_Calorimeter.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vppc.2016.7791713","eisbn":["9781509035281"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 IEEE Vehicle Power and Propulsion Conference (VPPC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011019670"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-35c62d35-66ed-4f9b-826a-a3826fed3f8e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Investigation of Battery Heat Generation and Key Performance Indicator Efficiency Using Isothermal Calorimeter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065672","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Proton exchange membrane fuel cells (PEMFC’s) are currently being commercialized for various applications ranging from automotive to stationary such as powering telecom back-up units. In PEMFC’s, oxygen from air is internally combined with hydrogen to form water and produce electricity and heat. This product heat has to be effectively removed from the fuel cell, and while automotive fuel cells are usually liquid-cooled using a secondary coolant loop similar to the internal combustion engines, stationary fuel cell systems as they are used for telecom back-up applications often rely on excessive air fed to the fuel cell cathode to remove the heat. Thereby, the fuel cell system is much simpler and cheaper while the fuel cell performance is substantially lower compared to automotive fuel cells. This work presents a computational fluid dynamics analysis on the heat management of an air-cooled fuel cell powered commercial telecom back-up system produced by Dantherm Power A/S, Denmark. The analysis is carried out with the commercial CFD solver Fluent (ANSYS Inc.). The fuel cell stack is modeled as a porous medium to accurately match the pressure drop, and it includes a heat source to account for the product heat. An important result is the predicted distribution of the temperature over the fuel cell stack, and a comparison between the modeling results and experimental validation will be made. Finally, the effect of various operating parameters on the temperature distribution in the telecom back-up power box will be investigated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gao, Xin","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080449"],"event":{"end":"2016-03-17","place":"Waikoloa Beach, Hawaii, us","start":"2016-03-13","title":"The First Pacific Rim Thermal Engineering Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational fluid dynamics","Fuel cell","Heat management","Optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a computational fluid dynamics analysis of air flow through a telecom back up unit powered by an air cooled proton exchange membrane fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266665284/CFD_Telecom_back_up_System_TBE_extended.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-080449","ids":["aau-689421a5-8317-4ca8-bdae-8fae222f498f"],"keyword":["Air-cooled","Computational fluid dynamics","Fuel cell","Heat management","Optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B700A22F51811EB7B1865B5408871D91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266665284/CFD_Telecom_back_up_System_TBE_extended.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xin","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"The First Pacific Rim Thermal Engineering Conference"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-689421a5-8317-4ca8-bdae-8fae222f498f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A COMPUTATIONAL FLUID DYNAMICS ANALYSIS OF AIR FLOW THROUGH A TELECOM BACK-UP UNIT POWERED BY AN AIR-COOLED PROTON EXCHANGE MEMBRANE FUEL CELL","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080449","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Lithium-ion (Li-ion) batteries are complex energy storage devices with their performance behavior highly dependent on the operating conditions (i.e., temperature, load current, and state-of-charge (SOC)). Thus, in order to evaluate their techno-economic viability for a certain application, detailed information about Li-ion battery performance behavior becomes necessary. This paper proposes a comprehensive seven-step methodology for laboratory characterization of Li-ion batteries, in which the battery’s performance parameters (i.e., capacity, open-circuit voltage (OCV), and impedance) are determined and their dependence on the operating conditions are obtained. Furthermore, this paper proposes a novel hybrid procedure for parameterizing the batteries’ equivalent electrical circuit (EEC), which is used to emulate the batteries’ dynamic behavior. Based on this novel parameterization procedure, the performance model of the studied Li-ion battery is developed and its accuracy is successfully verified (maximum error lower than 5% and a mean error below 8.5 mV) for various load profiles (including a real application profile), thus validating the proposed seven-step characterization methodology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Ana-Irina","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091537"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Characterization","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","Lithium ion battery","Methodology","Performance modeling","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generalized characterization methodology for performance modelling of lithium ion batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries2040037","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091537","identifier":[{"id":"000408137500008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85054843925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8ec83414-5256-4b89-af35-0116e2407a3e"],"keyword":["Characterization","DC pulses","Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy","Lithium-ion battery","Methodology","Performance Modeling","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5FDF02136CB4C57E1CA882D0EAA9CB7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/batteries2040037","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/2313-0105/2/4/37","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266391003/batteries_02_00037.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroedanielioanpau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskimaciejjozefpau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ana-Irina","key":"stroeanairinapau","last":"Stroe","locid":"e6ff6bac-362f-4fd1-b46c-d5f62d1e2c1a","name":"Stroe, Ana-Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-8254","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærsørenknudsenpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/batteries2040037","issn":["23130105"],"issue":"4","journal":"Batteries","paperid":"37","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Batteries","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054843925"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8ec83414-5256-4b89-af35-0116e2407a3e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Generalized Characterization Methodology for Performance Modelling of Lithium-Ion Batteries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091537","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background The Arteriograph is a cuff-based oscillometric device for non-invasive assessment of central systolic blood pressure (cSBP), aortic augmentation index (Aix) and aortic pulse wave velocity (PWV). Reproducibility of Arteriograph measurements and the agreement with SphygmoCor in diabetic patients has never been assessed. Methods We compared Arteriograph reproducibility and agreement with SphygmoCor with data from two study populations: Study 1 (n = 17) was conducted in a research laboratory and Study 2 (n = 19) in a catheter lab. SphygmoCor PWV data was only available in study 1. Results Reproducibility: Mean differences (±Standard deviation of the difference (SDD)) between duplicate cSBP, Aix and PWV Arteriograph measurements were −0.6 ± 6.6 mmHg, −1.1 ± 3.3% and 0.1 ± 0.5 m/s in study 1 and −0.01 ± 4.3 mmHg, 1.5 ± 3.2% and −0.2 ± 0.6 m/s in study 2, all differences non-significant. Agreement: Mean differences between SphygmoCor and Arteriograph were −14 ± 10 mmHg, −8 ± 7% and 2.4 ± 1.8 m/s, (p < 0.001 for all) in Study 1 and −5 ± 10 mmHg, p = 0.04 and −10 ± 8%, p = <0.001 in Study 2. In study 1, a significant correlation was observed between the mean and the difference for cSBP, r = −0.75, p < 0.001 and for Aix, r = −0.67, p < 0.001. Conclusions In type 2 diabetics, Arteriograph data were reproducible yet systematically overestimated cSBP, Aix and PWV compared with SphygmoCor. Hence, the two devices cannot be used interchangeably in type 2 diabetics.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Krogager, Christoffer","Rossen, Niklas B","Hansen, Klavs Würgler","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Peters, Christian Daugaard","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","Laugesen, Esben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-188599"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Arterial stiffness","Augmentation index","Central blood pressure","Diabetes","Reproducibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimates of arterial stiffness and central blood pressure in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes a comparison of sphygmocor and arteriograph","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84989888660","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-188599","identifier":[{"id":"84989888660","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-67bd3e9a-9bd6-42e0-869d-18b33011337b"],"keyword":["Arterial stiffness","Arteriograph","Augmentation index","Central blood pressure","Diabetes","Reproducibility","SphygmoCor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-A13BE0CDE9F379E26F0C67504106F8BB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"krogagerpau","last":"Krogager","locid":"943a0742-f4b1-4c62-86d0-daf7fade444e","name":"Krogager, Christoffer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niklas Blach","key":"rossenpau","last":"Rossen","locid":"fde04f7b-b73f-42bb-8fed-7ced5a87b6fc","name":"Rossen, Niklas B","name_org":"Rossen, Niklas Blach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klavs Würgler","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2dc4053-a6dd-47ea-bfeb-e689b3b6fc94","name":"Hansen, Klavs Würgler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Daugaard","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","locid":"02fa09b3-c04d-41e2-a9b0-0f23130799f4","name":"Peters, Christian Daugaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4917-1535","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Løgstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"laugesenpau","last":"Laugesen","locid":"e06ca9b7-d51f-40f2-b042-696ca2b18492","name":"Laugesen, Esben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18729312"],"journal":"Artery Research","pages":"18-24","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Artery Research","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84989888660"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-67bd3e9a-9bd6-42e0-869d-18b33011337b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Estimates of arterial stiffness and central blood pressure in patients with type 2 diabetes: A comparison of SphygmoCor and Arteriograph","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-188599","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Post project summary suitable for web publication Background Plant breeding is crucial in creating organic crop production systems that can better cope with interacting stresses such as pests and diseases (especially seed-borne diseases), weeds and the increasingly erratic and unpredictable variation in climate and weather. In this context, COBRA aimed to support and develop organic plant breeding and seed production with a focus on increasing the use and potential of plant material with high genetic diversity in cereals (wheat and barley) and grain legumes (pea and faba bean), through coordinating, linking and expanding existing breeding and research. Although systems based on high, within-crop diversity have shown promising results in organic systems and are now subject to intensive research, their benefits cannot be exploited currently, due to agronomic, regulatory and other hurdles. Also, it is currently unclear which plant breeding approaches, high diversity or otherwise, are most efficient to breed varieties for organic agriculture. To help these aims, COBRA's work was arranged into a management workpackage to coordinate the work and the following five sub-programmes: (1) To improve methods ensuring seed quality and health Progress was made in handling individual seeds in terms of their actual and potential resistance to seed-borne disease. One of the most important problems, bunt of wheat, was advanced considerably in terms of the 'gene for gene' interaction between host and pathogen and in observing the performance of the, currently, most effective resistance genes. Wheat populations, grown over two generations, did not change in their response to bunt. In barley, progress was made in identifying and confirming known and novel resistances to a range of the most important seed-borne diseases. Benign sprays were confirmed as potentially useful for Ascochyta blight control in peas. (2) To determine the potential to increase resilience, adaptability, and overall performance in organic systems by using crop diversity at various levels Valuable progress was made in confirming, expanding and understanding the resilience of the performance of composite cross populations of wheat. A wide range of molecular markers were identified in barley which will help in selecting genotypes adapted to expected future changes in climate and weather. Progress was also made with organic trials of grain legumes. The early 6 of 54 development stages of composite cross populations in the field is now better understood in relation to nutrient use efficiency. (3) To improve breeding efficiency and to develop novel breeding methods to enhance and maintain crop diversity A range of different technologies has been improved for selecting within composite cross populations using NIR spectrometry, colour markers and molecular markers; many of these are non-destructive. Of more immediate value, new composite cross populations involving winter and spring wheat genotypes and including bunt resistant genotypes have now been made. Progress has also been made with bulk breeding of peas, although single genotypes may still be preferred for cropping applications. (4) To identify and remove structural barriers to organic plant breeding and seed production It was important to bring together interested individuals and groups from different European countries to cover available experience and discuss further developments. Most importantly, this was also done directly in consultation with DGSanco, and booklets on the discussions and findings were published and distributed. (5) To improve networking and dissemination in organic plant breeding COBRA successfully established and utilised its website, produced regular newsletters and undertook training and farm days throughout the life of the project to raise the awareness of the project and to also communicate and discuss the finds and outcomes of the work undertaken by its various partners. Conclusion. COBRA’s strength is its focus on coordinating, linking and expanding ongoing organic breeding activities in cereals and grain legumes across Europe, drawing together experts from previously separated areas.","author_count":42,"contributors":["Pearce, Bruce","Kir, Alev","Andersen, Rikke Thomle","Borgen, Anders","D’Oppido, Dalila","Jørgensen, Johannes Ravn","Løes, Anne-Kristin","Buerstmayr, Hermann","Rasmussen, Søren K.","Annicchiarico, Paolo","Evers, Danièle","Delanote, Lieven","Chable, Veronique","Rey, Frederic","Slabe, Anamarija","Knudsen, Jens Chr.","Finckh, Maria","Olesen, Annette","Peltonen-Sainio, Pirjo","Jahoor, Ahmed","Walker, Robin","Andersen, Ole","Bertholdsson, Nils-Ove","Bagger Jørgensen, Rikke","Baresel, Peter","Pedersen, Tove Mariegaard","Killermann, Berta","Miceli, Fabiano","Bavec, Franci","Haesaert, Geert","Andersen, Regine","Messmer, Monika","Reitan, Lars","Tamm, Ilmar","Wyartt, Roger","Legzdina, Linda","Bleidere, Mara","Bedő, Zoltán","Loeschenberger, Franziska","Rasmussen, Morten","Nuijten, Edwin","Döring, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-329878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Estonia","Finland","France","Germany","Hungary","Italy","Latvia","Luxembourg","Netherlands","Norway","Slovenia","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aegean Agricultural Research Institute","All Global Affiliations","Bavarian State Research Center for Agriculture","Centre de Recherche Public Gabriel Lippmann","Centro di Ricerca p. l. Produzioni Foraggere e Lattiero-Case","Estonian Crop Research Institute","Forschungsinstitut fur Biologischen Landbau","Graminor AS","Humboldt University of Berlin","Hungarian Academy of Sciences","INRAE","Inagro","Institute for Sustainable Development","Institute of Agricultural Resources and Economics","Louis Bolk Institute","L’Associazione