scellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0a0e6951-2e43-49a4-8c7c-9403952620e9","au-e79d9ea0-11e8-4248-8b6f-2857beaa5c50","sdu-eb0191d9-e129-43c2-9ecf-494d5d82d4c1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Invasively Measured Aortic Systolic Blood Pressure and Office Systolic Blood Pressure in Cardiovascular Risk Assessment: A Prospective Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.87-000524","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Polymer electrolyte membrane (PEM) fuel cells require good hydration in order to deliver high performance and ensure long life operation. Water is essential for proton conductivity in the membrane which increases by nearly six orders of magnitude from dry to fully hydrated. Adequate water management in PEM fuel cell is crucial in order to avoid an imbalance between water production and water removal from the fuel cell. In the present study, a novel mathematical zero-dimensional model has been formulated for the water mass balance and hydration of a polymer electrolyte membrane. This model incorporates all the essential fundamental physical and electrochemical processes occurring in the membrane electrolyte and considers the water adsorption/desorption phenomena in the membrane. The effect of diffusivity model, surface roughness and water content driving force is considered. The model is validated against experimental data. In the results it is shown that the fuel cell water balance calculated by this model shows better fit with experimental data-points compared with model where only steady state operation were considered. We conclude that this discrepancy is due a different rate of water transport when membrane absorption/ desorption is considered in the model. The model becomes useful in system modelling when studying fuel cells in dynamic conditions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liso, Vincenzo","Araya, Samuel Simon","Olesen, Anders Christian","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-075342"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["PEM fuel cell","Water balance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and experimental validation of water mass balance in a pem fuel cell stack","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-075342","identifier":[{"id":"000370306300093","type":"wos"},{"id":"84957842902","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-571c4654-8dcc-4e28-a62c-c09f8013662f"],"keyword":["Membrane hydration","PEM fuel cell","Water balance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1023E8D1335DE49B39C51E0FA06AA207"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vincenzo","key":"lisopau","last":"Liso","locid":"c3a177b3-f874-40d3-984a-f1587412ec79","name":"Liso, Vincenzo","orcid":"0000-0002-7597-3849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2015.10.095","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"3079-3092","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957842902"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-571c4654-8dcc-4e28-a62c-c09f8013662f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and experimental validation of water mass balance in a PEM fuel cell stack","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-075342","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A novel method to obtain an ad-hoc and real time electrical signal of the PEMFC water balance by employing a constant temperature hot wire anemometry has been developed by our fuel cell research group. In this work, the effect of nitrogen-cross over on this method is experimentally demonstrated by introducing 1% of nitrogen concentration to the dry and humidified hydrogen flow simulating the PEMFC anode outlet. The hot wire voltage is measured with and without nitrogen and it was slightly lower with the presence of nitrogen. The effect of the voltage reduction on the measured water balance is small. This is due to the effect of 1% nitrogen on power law constant’s “m” which can be used in determining the water balance as explained in previous work was extremely low. Thus, the hot wire technique for measuring the PEMFC water balance is still accurate with the nitrogen cross-over","author_count":3,"contributors":["Al Shakhshir, Saher","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080734"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-07","place":"Honolulu, Hawaii, us","start":"2016-10-02","title":"PRiME 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of nitrogen cross over on water balance measurements in proton exchange membrane fuel cell using constant temperature anemometry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-080734","identifier":[{"id":"84991577461","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000406655500009","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-699438a0-1d41-45c6-a100-6b1571033dd7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C11D21038FF5F9396305B1E596D4D626"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saher","key":"alshakhshirpau","last":"Al Shakhshir","locid":"0e7cf7ea-3c90-45b7-acae-48cae2af40e6","name":"Al Shakhshir, Saher","orcid":"0000-0002-5947-8522","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/07514.0101ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"14","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"101-110","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991577461"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-699438a0-1d41-45c6-a100-6b1571033dd7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Effect of Nitrogen Cross-Over on Water Balance Measurements in Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell Using Constant Temperature Anemometry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080734","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The physical and combustion properties of roller-milled and hammer-milled wood pellets for suspension-firing are characterized both experimentally and numerically. The particle size and shape distribution is measured based on dynamical digital image processing. The traditional coal roller mills produce larger biomass particles than hammer mills do. The true density of the particles, measured by ethanol displacement method, does not remarkably vary with the different mills. Combustion tests of the milled biomass particles are performed in a single particle combustion reactor under conditions close to suspension-fired boilers. The ignition, devolatilization and burnout times of the milled particles under different combustion conditions are analysed. A one-dimensional transient model, properly accounting for the particle-ambient flow interaction and appropriately addressing the key sub-processes within the particle, is also developed to predict the combustion behaviours. The good agreement between the model predictions and the experimental results serves as a cross validation of both the tests and the model. Without changes in the infrastructure, biomass pelletizing may not be a viable pre-treatment for large-scale biomass combustion in the existing pulverized coal-fired utility boilers.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Yin, Chungen","Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093059"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-27","place":"Firenze, it","start":"2016-05-22","title":"The 9th International Conference on Multiphase Flow","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hammer mill","Suspension combustion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physical and combustion characteristics of biomass particles prepared by different milling processes for suspension firing in utility boilers","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-093059","ids":["aau-94559dca-c96e-49d7-8621-4e28cad13f7d"],"keyword":["Biomass pellet","Hammer mill","Pulverized fuel boiler","Roller mill","Suspension combustion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F89F717A2ED3832434412EBFCD07E134"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"grundfos","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GFS","l3nl":"Grundfos","l3nn":"Grundfos","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Grundfos","namevar":["Grundfos DK AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GFS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chungen","key":"yinpau","last":"Yin","locid":"a24ca845-2626-44cc-b726-b6c5ec9ddd24","name":"Yin, Chungen","orcid":"0000-0002-9885-7744","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maryam","key":"momenikouchaksaraeipau","last":"Momenikouchaksaraei","name":"Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"International Conference on Multiphase Flow","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 9th International Conference on Multiphase Flow, May 22-27, 2016, Firenze, Italy"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Grundfos","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94559dca-c96e-49d7-8621-4e28cad13f7d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Physical and combustion characteristics of biomass particles prepared by different milling processes for suspension firing in utility boilers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093059","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The pulse power capability (PPC) represents one of the parameters that describe the performance behavior of Lithium-ion batteries independent on the application. Consequently, extended information about the Li-ion battery PPC and its dependence on the operating conditions become necessary. Thus, this paper analyzes the power capability characteristic of a 13Ah high power Lithium Titanate Oxide-based battery and its dependence on temperature, load current and state-of-charge. Furthermore, a model to predict the discharging PPC of the battery cell at different temperatures and load currents for three different state-of-charge levels was proposed and parameterized.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Stroe, Ana-Irina","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Teodorescu, Remus","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093779"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-31","place":"Brno, cz","start":"2016-08-28","title":"17th International Conference Advanced Batteries, Accumulators and Fuel Cells [ABAF 17th]","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pulse power capability estimation of lithium titanate oxide based batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ecst.ecsdl.org/content/74/1/45.full.pdf+html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093779","identifier":[{"id":"85020017578","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000406794300007","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-96ca3e75-8453-48a9-bae6-bc4d6cdf0a8e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CF031389140A45CC0AB0BACB67EC4878"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPu