t":"Rotenberg","locid":"00219c09-8417-495f-96ff-eb34884ad59c","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert","key":"krauthgamerpedh","last":"Krauthgamer","name":"Krauthgamer, Robert","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611974331.ch111","eisbn":["9781611974331"],"pages":"1631-1642","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Twenty-Seventh Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963612588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-293df5ab-4c64-4948-9a9e-0e8a008ec129"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The power of two choices with simple tabulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418062","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"One means of increasing the hydrogen yield to cost ratio of a PEM water electrolyser, is to increase the operating current density. However, at high current densities (higher than 1 A/cm2), management of heat and mass transfer in the anode current collector and channel becomes crucial and can lead to hot spots. Management of heat and fluid flow through the micro-channels play a great role in the capability of PEM water electrolysis when working at high current densities. Despite, many studies have been done on gas-liquid flows; still there is a lack of research on gas-liquid flows in micro-sized channels (hydraulic diameter of 1 mm) of PEM water electrolysis. Precisely controlling all the parameters that affect the gas-liquid flow in a PEM water electrolysis cell is quite challenging, hence a simplified setup is constructed consisting of only a transparent channel with a sheet of titanium felt as a permeable wall.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054946"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-07","place":"Honolulu, Hawaii, us","start":"2016-10-02","title":"PRiME 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gas liquid flow","PEM water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysing gas liquid flow in pem electrolyser micro channels poster","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/242395143/Analysing_Gas_Liquid_Flow_in_PEM_Electrolyser_Micro_Channels_SaeedLafmejani.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054946","ids":["aau-10c5eaf0-126c-40bc-9f2a-0c3f1c982cd5"],"keyword":["Gas-liquid flow","PEM water electrolysis","micro-sized channels"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-83856AEA12A2B20C2651A4FF4A754727"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/242395143/Analysing_Gas_Liquid_Flow_in_PEM_Electrolyser_Micro_Channels_SaeedLafmejani.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saeed Sadeghi","key":"lafmejanipau","last":"Lafmejani","locid":"db40a4cb-554f-4515-aaa1-724aa7c708a0","name":"Lafmejani, Saeed Sadeghi","orcid":"0000-0002-1780-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-10c5eaf0-126c-40bc-9f2a-0c3f1c982cd5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analysing Gas-Liquid Flow in PEM Electrolyser Micro-Channels (Poster)","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054946","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A three-dimensional multiphysics-based thermal model of a battery pack is presented. The model is intended to demonstrate the cooling mechanism inside the battery pack. Heat transfer (HT) and computational fluid dynamics (CFD) physics are coupled for both time-dependent and steady-state simulation. Inside the battery cells in the pack a lumped value of heat generation (HG), that works as a volumetric heat source, is used. The measured HG stems from the cell level isothermal calorimeter experiment. The batteries inside the pack stay in the same initial thermal state in the simulation case. The pack is simulated to find the temperature gradient over the pack surfaces. Moreover, the temperature evolution results are simulated. It is demonstrated that the developed pack model can provide the thermal spatio-temporal behaviour with great detail. The result helps to understand the thermal behavior of the cells inside a battery pack.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065654"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-20","place":"cn","start":"2016-10-17","title":"2016 IEEE Vehicle Power and Propulsion Conference (VPPC)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Isothermal Calorimeter","LTO","Multiphysics model","Spatial distribution","Surface temperature","Thermal management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three dimensional thermal modeling of li ion battery pack based on multiphysics and calorimetric measurement","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/250869926/PapIV_1_Three_Dimensional_Thermal_Modeling_of_Li_Ion_Battery_Pack_based_on_Multiphysics_and_Calorimetric_Measurement.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-065654","identifier":[{"id":"85011082486","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-35b9ece6-8425-4793-953a-a7074c9b2d9c"],"keyword":["Battery Pack Model","Isothermal Calorimeter","LTO","Multiphysics model","Spatial distribution","Surface temperature","Thermal Management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26031AC5120CDF955CDD02FD2060465C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/250869926/PapIV_1_Three_Dimensional_Thermal_Modeling_of_Li_Ion_Battery_Pack_based_on_Multiphysics_and_Calorimetric_Measurement.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vppc.2016.7791803","eisbn":["9781509035281"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of IEEE Vehicle Power and Propulsion Conference (VPPC), 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011082486"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-35b9ece6-8425-4793-953a-a7074c9b2d9c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Three Dimensional Thermal Modeling of Li-Ion Battery Pack Based on Multiphysics and Calorimetric Measurement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065654","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Denmark is participating in IEA EBC Annex 56 “Cost Effective Energy and Carbon Emissions Optimization in Building Renovation”. This paper presents results from the housing complex Traneparken that was chosen as a Danish case for the project. It has undergone a comprehensive energy retrofit including new facades, new windows, additional insulation, mechanical ventilation with heat recovery and a photovoltaic installation on the roof. The measured energy consumption for heating and domestic hot water before and after renovation was 139.1 kWh/m2/year and 95.6 kWh/m2/year respectively, and thereby the project has demonstrated that the renovation resulted in significant energy savings. Furthermore, a questionnaire survey was carried out focusing on the tenants’ overall satisfaction with the retrofitting process and the results of the retrofitting, including e.g. perceived indoor climate before and after the retrofit. In three of the flats in Traneparken measurements of ventilation conditions were performed using passive tracer gas technique together with continuous registration of the room air temperature, the relative humidity and the CO2-concentration using programmable data loggers.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thomsen, Kirsten Engelund","Rose, Jørgen","Christen Mørck, Ove","Jensen, Søren Østergaard","Østergaard, Iben","Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","Bergsøe, Niels Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068121"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energy consumption","Energy retrofit","Indoor climate","Measurements","Residential buildings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy consumption and indoor climate in a residential building before and after comprehensive energy retrofitting","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-068121","identifier":[{"id":"000377739300002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84964727254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3e4e85b8-c9a5-468c-9148-f7b39ac35fcd"],"keyword":["Energy consumption","Energy retrofit","Indoor Climate","Measurements","Residential Buildings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E479C3E36DA2929555B9DB662313829"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Department of Energy Performance, Indoor Environment and Sustainability of Buildings (EIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Energy Efficiency Research Group (SBi)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Energy and Sustainability in Buildings","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Energy and Buildings Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTC