{"abstract":"We explore means of designing and evaluating initial visualization ideas, with concrete and realistic data in cases where data is not readily available. Our approach is useful in exploring new domains and avenues for visualization, and contrasts other visualization work, which typically operate under the assumption that data has already been collected, and is ready to be visualized. We argue that it is sensible to understand data requirements and evaluate the potential value of visualization before devising means of automatic data collection. We base our exploration on three cases selected to span a range of factors, such as the role of the person doing the data collection and the type of instrumentation used. The three cases relate to visualizing sports, construction, and cooking domain data, and use primarily time-domain data and visualizations. For each case, we briefly describe the design case and problem, the manner in which we collected data, and the findings obtained from evaluations. Afterwards, we describe four factors of our data collection approach, and discuss potential outcomes from it.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren","Pedersen, Jeppe Gerner","Herdal, Thor","Larsen, Jakob Eg"],"cuid":["S02-099.76-035746"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-24","place":"Baltimore, us","start":"2016-10-24","title":"6th Workshop on Beyond Time and Errors on Novel Evaluation Methods for Visualization","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Evaluation","InfoVis","Methodology","Personal visualization","Pre design empiricism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using concrete and realistic data in evaluating initial visualization designs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84995477322&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.76-035746","identifier":[{"id":"84995477322","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-892e03da-73d2-4eaf-879a-f26589d2eaca","ku-092e8114-ebfc-4daf-9e09-a8d50e3a9e0d"],"keyword":["Evaluation","InfoVis","Methodology","Personal visualization","Pre-design empiricism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EFFDB4571240B65EA227B2B2A7C979AA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"60aa66e8-eac5-4487-94e1-f1379643b27d","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Gerner","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jeppe Gerner","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thor","key":"herdalpau","last":"Herdal","name":"Herdal, Thor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Eg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"691c8ae7-9a21-4b98-9b91-5e2d9806a4b9","name":"Larsen, Jakob Eg","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-9901","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2993901.2993917","eisbn":["9781450348188"],"isbn":["9781450348188"],"pages":"27-35","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Sixth Workshop on Beyond Time and Errors on Novel Evaluation Methods for Visualization, BELIV '16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995477322"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-892e03da-73d2-4eaf-879a-f26589d2eaca","ku-092e8114-ebfc-4daf-9e09-a8d50e3a9e0d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Concrete and Realistic Data in Evaluating Initial Visualization Designs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.76-035746","year":"2016","yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"In this work, the use of a circular-planar, interdigitated flow field for the anode of a high pressure proton exchange membrane (PEM) water electrolysis cell is investigated in a numerical study. While PEM fuel cells have separated flow fields for reactant transport and coolant, it is possible to operate a PEM electrolysis cell with the anode flow field serving as both. This allows for a simpler system and a thinner design, however sets new and more strict requirements for the flow field to distribute uniformly. For the present study, two computational fluid dynamics models are developed; a single-phase flow model for establishing the effect of geometry and a two-phase flow model for studying the effect of dispersed gas bubbles. Both models account for turbulence and heat transport. By means of the developed models, it is elucidated that the circular-planar shape of the interdigitated flow field causes maldistribution, if land areas of equal width are applied. Moreover, below a water stoichiometry of 350, and at a current density of 1 A/cm2, flow and temperature maldistribution is adversely affected by the presence of the gas phase; particularly gas hold-up near outlet channels can cause excessive formation of hotspots. As the water stoichiometry increases, the flow maldistribution increases as well. Nonetheless, its impact on the temperature distribution is counterbalanced by an overall increase in heat capacity of the flow. Hence, a relative uniform temperature distribution is achieved at and above nominal flow conditions. In a parametric investigation it is further underlined that the predicted formation of hotspots is sensitive to the employed particle diameter of the two-phase channel flow model. The larger the particle size, the more severe the maldistribution of temperature becomes. It is therefore concluded that further experimental validation and research into particle size modeling is necessary.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Rømer, Carsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-052229"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["High pressure","Modeling","PEMEC","Two phase flow","Water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a numerical study of the gas liquid two phase flow maldistribution in the anode of a high pressure pem water electrolysis cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-052229","identifier":[{"id":"000368955300004","type":"wos"},{"id":"84954289243","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-078c9b0f-7e68-4c68-8649-572c11526804"],"keyword":["High pressure","Modeling","PEMEC","Two-phase flow","Water electrolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A4A48F8B5E269E69CAB80B7881BE117"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["IRD A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"rømerpau","last":"Rømer","name":"Rømer, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2015.09.140","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"52-68","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84954289243"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","ird a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-078c9b0f-7e68-4c68-8649-572c11526804"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A numerical study of the gas-liquid, two-phase flow maldistribution in the anode of a high pressure PEM water electrolysis cell","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052229","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The research is focused on the development of a three-dimensional cell level multiphysics battery thermal model. The primary aim is to represent the cooling mechanism inside the unit cell battery pack. It is accomplished through the coupling of heat transfer and computational fluid dynamics (CFD) physics. A lumped value of heat generation (HG) inside the battery cell is used. It stems from isothermal calorimeter experiment. HG depends on current rate and the corresponding operating temperature. It is demonstrated that the developed model provides a deeper understanding of the thermal spatio-temporal behavior of Li-ion battery in different operating conditions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-077226"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-08","place":"Monte-Carlo, mc","start":"2016-04-06","title":"2016 Eleventh International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery performance","Battery thermal management","CFD application","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Lithium Titanate Oxide","Surface temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiphysics based thermal modeling of a pouch lithium ion battery cell for the development of pack level thermal management system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/234317522/PID4224827.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-077226","identifier":[{"id":"84974628252","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5d85a887-e4e7-4a88-a868-ab0282e76efd"],"keyword":["Battery performance","Battery thermal management","CFD application","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Lithium Titanate Oxide","Surface temperature","Temporal temperature distribution","Three dimesional multiphysics model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1763CCBE6A8615D4E6177BA59D222181"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/234317522/PID4224827.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ever.2016.7476442","isbn":["9781509024643"],"pages":"1-9","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 Eleventh International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84974628252"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5d85a887-e4e7-4a88-a868-ab0282e76efd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Multiphysics Based Thermal Modeling of a Pouch Lithium-Ion Battery Cell for the Development of Pack Level Thermal Management System","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-077226","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this experiment-based research, there is an attempt to determine the evolution of surface temperature distribution, thermal behaviour and performance of a battery cell at the same time. The pouch type commercial test cell has a 13Ah capacity and Lithium Titanate Oxide (LTO) based anode. Temperatures on the surface of the cell are measured using contact thermocouples. Additionally, the heat flux is simultaneously measured with the isothermal calorimeter. This heat flux measurement is used for determining the heat generation inside the cell. Consequently, the important performance constituent of the battery cell efficiency is calculated. Those are accomplished at different temperature levels (0??C and 25??C) of continuous constant current 1C charge and discharge. Also, the maximal increase in the battery temperature over the cell surface is found on the battery cell surface. The heat flow calibration and experimentation for calorimetric measurement are deliberated. The experimental procedure is a very precise determination of the heat generation and the efficiency of the battery cell.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-084303"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-08","place":"Monte-Carlo, mc","start":"2016-04-06","title":"2016 Eleventh International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery efficiency","Battery thermal management","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Lithium Titanate Oxide","Performance","Surface temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determination of the behavior and performance of commercial li ion pouch cells by means of isothermal calorimeter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/234317404/PID4221653.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-084303","identifier":[{"id":"84974560062","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-75e413cf-aa15-49ba-aa25-7d918b48fcd1"],"keyword":["Battery behavior","Battery efficiency","Battery thermal management","Heat generation","Isothermal Calorimeter","Lithium Titanate Oxide","Performance","Spatial temperature distribution","Surface temperature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CD81E45736264F99FF31FC3601BDAE65"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/234317404/PID4221653.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ever.2016.7476441","isbn":["9781509024643"],"pages":"1-8","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 Eleventh International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies (EVER)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84974560062"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-75e413cf-aa15-49ba-aa25-7d918b48fcd1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Determination of the behavior and performance of commercial Li-Ion pouch cells by means of isothermal calorimeter","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-084303","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Thermal modeling of lithium-ion batteries is gaining its importance together with increasing power density and compact design of the modern battery systems in order to assure battery safety and long lifetime. Thermal models of lithium-ion batteries are usually either expensive to develop and accurate or equivalent thermal circuit based with moderate accuracy and without spatial temperature distribution. This work presents initial results that can be used as a fundament for the cost-efficient development of the two-dimensional thermal model of lithium-ion battery based on multipoint electrothermal impedance spectroscopy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Knap, Vaclav","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Teodorescu, Remus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094279"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-02","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2016-05-29","title":"229th ECS Meeting","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"two dimensional thermal modeling of lithium ion battery cell based on electrothermal impedance spectroscopy","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241163378/Two_dimensional_Thermal_Modeling_of_Lithium_ion_Battery_Cell_Based_on_Electrothermal_Impedance_Spectroscopy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094279","identifier":[{"id":"85010766701","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9892019b-c7a8-4974-a13d-3bd6968cc96e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A8B7A4C038C86861EA25B88B00BA9FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241163378/Two_dimensional_Thermal_Modeling_of_Lithium_ion_Battery_Cell_Based_on_Electrothermal_Impedance_Spectroscopy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vaclav","key":"knappau","last":"Knap","locid":"d3e7f51b-362b-4876-acb2-53a9bbca7044","name":"Knap, Vaclav","orcid":"0000-0003-0108-1714","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescupau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/07211.0033ecst","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"11","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"33-38","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010766701"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9892019b-c7a8-4974-a13d-3bd6968cc96e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Two-dimensional Thermal Modeling of Lithium-ion Battery Cell Based on Electrothermal Impedance Spectroscopy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094279","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cells are becoming a promising energy source for various applications due to its relatively high efficiency and reliability, and low pollution. They have been applied in backup power systems in telecom applications, where reliability and availability are high priority performance factors. This paper describes a lifetime prediction method for the power semiconductors used in the power conditioning of a fuel cell based backup system, considering both the long-term standby mode and active operation mode. The annual ambient temperature profile is taken into account to estimate its impact on the degradation of MOSFETs during the standby mode. At the presence of power outages, the backup system is activated into the operation mode and the MOSFETs withstand additional thermal stresses due to power losses. A study case of a 1 kW backup system is presented with two annual mission profiles in Denmark and India, respectively. The ambient temperature, occurrence frequency of power outages, active operation time and power levels are considered for the lifetime prediction of the applied MOSFETs. Comparisons of the accumulated lifetime consumptions are performed between standby mode and operation mode, and between Denmark and India, respectively.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Dao","Wang, Huai","Blaabjerg, Frede","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Hansen, Daniel Blom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-105059"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-26","place":"Hefei, cn","start":"2016-05-22","title":"8th IEEE International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference, IPEMC-ECCE Asia 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real mission profile based lifetime estimation of fuel cell power converter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/327229009/PID4198533.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-105059","identifier":[{"id":"84983283827","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bdbee29a-9cd4-47b2-9fdd-049edc736a82"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1C3EAB8F38319A8D7AD087F41EF8968"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/327229009/PID4198533.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dantherm Power A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dao","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"8cf08fe2-24d6-4224-aaa2-f7e03a45debb","name":"Zhou, Dao","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-4309","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Huai","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"e8606356-85bc-4d6c-a091-e91dce99441a","name":"Wang, Huai","orcid":"0000-0002-5404-3140","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Blom","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Daniel Blom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ipemc.2016.7512741","eisbn":["9781509012107"],"pages":"2798-2805","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 IEEE 8th International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference (IPEMC-ECCE Asia)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983283827"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dantherm power a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bdbee29a-9cd4-47b2-9fdd-049edc736a82"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Real Mission Profile Based Lifetime Estimation of Fuel-cell Power Converter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-105059","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Recently, the intestinal microbiota has been emphasised as an important contributor to the development of metabolic syndrome. Dietary fibre may exert beneficial effects through modulation of the intestinal microbiota and metabolic end products. We investigated the effects of a diet enriched with two different dietary fibres, arabinoxylan and resistant starch type 2, on the gut microbiome and faecal short-chain fatty acids. Nineteen adults with metabolic syndrome completed this randomised crossover study with two 4-week interventions of a diet enriched with arabinoxylan and resistant starch and a low-fibre Western-style diet. Faecal samples were collected before and at the end of the interventions for fermentative end-product analysis and 16S ribosomal RNA bacterial gene amplification for identification of bacterial taxa. Faecal carbohydrate residues were used to verify compliance. The diet enriched with arabinoxylan and resistant starch resulted in significant reductions in the total species diversity of the faecal-associated intestinal microbiota but also increased the heterogeneity of bacterial communities both between and within subjects. The proportion of Bifidobacterium was increased by arabinoxylan and resistant starch consumption (P<0.001), whereas the proportions of certain bacterial genera associated with dysbiotic intestinal communities were reduced. Furthermore, the total short-chain fatty acids (P<0.01), acetate (P<0.01) and butyrate concentrations (P<0.01) were higher by the end of the diet enriched with arabinoxylan and resistant starch compared with those resulting from the Western-style diet. The concentrations of isobutyrate (P = 0.05) and isovalerate (P = 0.03) decreased in response to the arabinoxylan and resistant starch enriched diet, indicating reduced protein fermentation. In conclusion, arabinoxylan and resistant starch intake changes the microbiome and short-chain fatty acid compositions, with potential beneficial effects on colonic health and metabolic syndrome.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hald, Stine","Schioldan, Anne Grethe","Moore, Mary E","Dige, Anders","Lærke, Helle Nygaard","Agnholt, Jørgen","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Hermansen, Kjeld","Marco, Maria L.","Gregersen, Søren","Dahlerup, Jens Frederik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-202170"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of arabinoxylan and resistant starch on intestinal microbiota and short chain fatty acids in subjects with metabolic syndrome a randomised crossover study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0159223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-202170","identifier":[{"id":"27434092","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84979289595","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4951149","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-7f50b091-6301-45cd-bde3-044a02a17a74"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE23E1C954AFC8B4227407DCA612C430"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0159223","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hepatology and Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","locid":"ed81f2ac-05a5-4d72-b195-9e6afc4b7800","name":"Hald, Stine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Grethe","key":"schioldanpau","last":"Schioldan","locid":"a710b241-48f9-4926-adb7-f3dbcfeb6a9f","name":"Schioldan, Anne Grethe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary E","key":"moorepau","last":"Moore","name":"Moore, Mary E","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Kirch","key":"digepau","last":"Dige","locid":"c5b7ed9d-4c85-4d70-b215-6b023bdc20f5","name":"Dige, Anders","name_org":"Dige, Anders Kirch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"agnholtpau","last":"Agnholt","locid":"66d6b88f-b5c0-4c2e-b073-056cd18dc1ea","name":"Agnholt, Jørgen","orcid":"0009-0006-4776-0121","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"hermansenpau","last":"Hermansen","locid":"a62f80e1-f33f-47bd-a5e5-87d59477619f","name":"Hermansen, Kjeld","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria L.","key":"marcopau","last":"Marco","name":"Marco, Maria L.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"59b0d84c-a135-49bf-afba-7783f90976c2","name":"Gregersen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1953-8631","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Frederik","key":"dahleruppau","last":"Dahlerup","locid":"0f52b503-fe76-4e51-939a-7a24f226f420","name":"Dahlerup, Jens Frederik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27434092"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0159223","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"7","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0159223","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979289595"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7f50b091-6301-45cd-bde3-044a02a17a74"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of Arabinoxylan and Resistant Starch on Intestinal Microbiota and Short-Chain Fatty Acids in Subjects with Metabolic Syndrome: A Randomised Crossover Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-202170","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Aim Venous thromboembolism (VTE) has long been regarded as a marker of underlying malignancy in the general population. Patients with diabetes mellitus are at increased risk of developing VTE, but it is unclear whether VTE in diabetes patients is also a harbinger of occult cancer. Methods From Danish medical health databases, we identified all diabetes patients (N = 8783) with a first-time diagnosis of VTE during 1978-2011. We followed the patients until a first-time diagnosis of cancer, emigration, death, or study end, whichever came first. We calculated one-year absolute cancer risk and overall and site-specific standardized incidence ratios (SIRs) for cancer based on national cancer incidence. Results During the total study period 878 cancers were observed. The one-year absolute cancer risk was 4.1% and the corresponding SIR was 3.28 (95% confidence interval [CI]: 2.94-3.64). The highest SIRs were observed for cancers of the gallbladder and biliary tract (SIR 13.59; 6.77-24.31), the pancreas (SIR 10.16; 6.85-14.50), the ovary (SIR 9.85; 5.63-16.00), and the liver (SIR 9.39; 4.30-17.84). After the first year of follow-up, the overall cancer SIR associated with VTE and diabetes decreased to 1.05 (95% CI: 0.97-1.15). Conclusions VTE may be a marker of underlying cancer in patients with diabetes mellitus.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christensen, Diana Hedevang","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Dekkers, Olaf M.","Prandoni, Paolo","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239297"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer","Deep venous thrombosis","Diabetes mellitus","Epidemiology","Pulmonary embolism","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"venous thromboembolism and risk of cancer in patients with diabetes mellitus","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84957899908","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239297","identifier":[{"id":"26874682","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84957899908","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c0b41e9b-091d-4fbd-b90f-e1e47fac1f89"],"keyword":["Cancer","Deep venous thrombosis","Diabetes mellitus","Epidemiology","Pulmonary embolism","Venous thromboembolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-176174CA5BF7288409B571F7800FFB57"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Diana Hedevang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"736d7555-3234-4cec-97fa-6138c22ee99a","name":"Christensen, Diana Hedevang","orcid":"0000-0002-2693-5651","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erzsébet","key":"horváthpuhópau","last":"Horváth-Puhó","locid":"20f5c6bd-6ac1-4edb-a393-f34d60db546c","name":"Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","orcid":"0000-0002-3594-2212","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reimar Wernich","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"36e7af2c-e02f-48d4-b124-0f1bd95b1748","name":"Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","orcid":"0000-0001-9135-3474","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"countr