{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Type 2 diabetic patients display significantly higher incidence of cardiovascular (CV) events including stroke compared to non-diabetics. Morning blood pressure surge (MBPS) and blunted systolic night-day (SND) ratio have been associated with CV events in hypertensive patients. No studies have evaluated MBPS in newly diagnosed diabetic patients or studied the association with vascular target organ damage at this early time point of the diabetes disease. METHODS: Ambulatory blood pressure monitoring was performed in 100 patients with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes and 100 age and sex matched controls. MBPS and SND-ratio were calculated. Markers of early vascular target organ damage included pulse wave velocity (PWV), white matter lesions (WML) on brain MRI, and urine albumin/creatinine ratio (UAE). RESULTS: No significant differences in MBPS were found between diabetic patients and controls. Neither MBPS or SND-ratio were associated with PWV, UAE or WML in the diabetic group independently of age, gender and 24-h systolic blood pressure. 40.2 % of diabetic patients and 25.8 % of controls were classified as non-dippers (p = 0.03). CONCLUSION: MBPS and SND-ratio are not associated with subclinical markers of vascular target organ damage in our study sample of newly diagnosed type 2 diabetic patients.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lyhne, Johanne M","Laugesen, Esben","Høyem, Pernille","Cichosz, Simon Lebech","Christiansen, Jens Sandahl","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Hansen, Klavs Würgler","Hansen, Troels Krarup","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-268899"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"morning blood pressure surge and target organ damage in newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetic patients a cross sectional study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84949193348","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-268899","identifier":[{"id":"84949193348","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26630970","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4668664","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f4bdaa28-2d39-4aae-93ea-353c474f31d8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-97D65353CB0EA01CAA899EAE02A5B943"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanne M","key":"lyhnejohannempau","last":"Lyhne","locid":"f632c387-30e9-4d28-8112-4cf9947b6042","name":"Lyhne, Johanne M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"laugesenesbenpau","last":"Laugesen","locid":"e06ca9b7-d51f-40f2-b042-696ca2b18492","name":"Laugesen, Esben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"høyempernillepau","last":"Høyem","locid":"cbd0d45d-3fcf-4208-93ca-d5f580739f1a","name":"Høyem, Pernille","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"cichoszsimonlebechpau","last":"Cichosz","locid":"2e802b07-6f39-4053-a8a4-913f06ad8dd0","name":"Cichosz, Simon Lebech","name_org":"Cichosz, Simon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens S","key":"christiansenjenssandahlpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"3af3a403-0f32-4202-aaec-135d99299f52","name":"Christiansen, Jens Sandahl","name_org":"Christiansen, Jens S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren T","key":"knudsensørentangpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","name_org":"Knudsen, Søren T","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klavs W","key":"hansenklavswürglerpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2dc4053-a6dd-47ea-bfeb-e689b3b6fc94","name":"Hansen, Klavs Würgler","name_org":"Hansen, Klavs W","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels K","key":"hansentroelskraruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4af39f3a-9bb3-4f30-8fee-29a550538de8","name":"Hansen, Troels Krarup","name_org":"Hansen, Troels K","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per L","key":"poulsenperløgstruppau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","name_org":"Poulsen, Per L","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26630970"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12902-015-0068-4","issn":["14726823"],"journal":"BMC Endocrine Disorders","paperid":"77","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Endocrine Disorders","title_org":"B M C Endocrine Disorders","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949193348"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f4bdaa28-2d39-4aae-93ea-353c474f31d8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Morning blood pressure surge and target organ damage in newly diagnosed type 2 diabetic patients: a cross sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-268899","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the field of energy storage devices the pursuit for cheap, high energy density, reliable secondary batteries is at the top of the agenda. The Li-O2battery is one of the possible technologies that, in theory, should be able to close the gap, which exists between the present state-of-the-art Li-ion technologies and the demand placed on batteries by technologies such as electrical vehicles [1]. However, the Li-O2 battery still suffers greatly from high overpotentials during oxygen reduction and evolution reactions (discharge and charge, respectively), poor rechargeability, and decomposition of salts and solvents etc. [2] [3]. In order to improve the electrochemical performance of the Li-O2batteries; it is crucial to understand the fundamental mechanisms that governs and limits the system during electrochemical operation. Here we present a redox probing study of the charge transfer across the deposition product lithium peroxide, Li2O2, using outer-sphere redox shuttles: cobaltocene, ferrocene, and decamethylferrocene. The change in heterogeneous electron transfer exchange rate as a function of the potential and the Li2O2 layer thickness (~state of charge) was determined using electrochemical impedance spectroscopy. The attenuation of the electron transfer exchange rate with film thickness is dependent on the probing potential, indicating that hole tunneling is the dominant process for charge transfer through Li2O2supporting previous work by Luntz et al. [4]. Additionally, this work includes the determination of diffusion coefficients and concentrations of the redox shuttles and the superoxide ion, in a 1,2-dimethoxyethane based electrolyte. References [1] S. A. Freunberger, P. G. Bruce, L. J. Hardwick et J.-M. Tarascon, «Li-O2 and Li-S batteries with high energy storage,» Nature Materials, vol. 11, pp. 19-29, 2012. [2] B. D. McCloskey, A. Valery, A. C. Luntz, S. R. Gowda, G. M. Wallraff, J. M. Garcia, T. Mori et L. E. Krupp, «Combining Accurate O2 and Li2O2 Assays to Separate Discharge and Charge stability Limitations in Nonaqueous Li-O2 Batteries,» J. Phys. Chem. Lett., vol. 4, pp. 2989-2993, 2013. [3] R. Younesi, M. Hahlin, F. Björefors, P. Johansson et K. Edström, «Li-O2 Battery Degradation by Lithium Peroxide (Li2O2): A Model Study,» Chem. Mater., vol. 25, pp. 77-84, 2013. [4] A. C. Luntz, V. Viswanathan, J. Voss, J. B. Varley, J. K. Nørskov, R. Scheffler and A. Speidel, \"Tunneling and Polaron Charge Transport through Li2O2 in Li-O2 Batteries,\" J. Phys. Chem. Lett., vol. 4, pp. 3494-3499, 2013.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Kristian Bastholm","Jensen, Søren Højgaard","Luntz, Alan C.","Hjelm, Johan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-363196"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a study of e sup sup transport through li sub 000000000002 sub o sub 000000000002 sub the main discharge product in the li o sub 000000000002 sub battery","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-363196","ids":["dtu-c419d787-7ea6-41a0-963c-b22d0b9234f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FDAEC1781C068EEC22466177B321877F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Fundamental Electrochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Bastholm","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"dfdc27fb-b2dc-496b-966d-5a763d268b3a","name":"Knudsen, Kristian Bastholm","orcid":"0000-0003-1217-8730","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Højgaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Søren Højgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan C.","key":"luntzpau","last":"Luntz","name":"Luntz, Alan C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"hjelmpau","last":"Hjelm","locid":"1f33d9cb-8387-4672-bfa5-091ef2fc1329","name":"Hjelm, Johan","orcid":"0000-0003-0072-5784","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21512035","21512043"],"issn_org":["21512043"],"issue":"2","journal":"Electrochemical Society. Meeting Abstracts","pages":"20367-367","status":"p","title":"Electrochemical Society. Meeting Abstracts","title_org":"Electrochemical Society. Meeting Abstracts (Online)","volume":"MA2015-01"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c419d787-7ea6-41a0-963c-b22d0b9234f0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Study of e<sup>-</sup> Transport through Li<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>, the Main Discharge Product in the Li-O<sub>2</sub> Battery","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-363196","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Albers, Christian N.","Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","Harder, Christoffer Bugge","Rosendahl, Søren","Knudsen, Berith E.","Ekelund, Flemming","Aamand, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421241"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"groundwater chemistry determines the prokaryotic community structure of waterworks sand filters","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-421241","identifier":[{"id":"84921734107","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000348332400019","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-2eabb7f6-92c9-42d0-a9a6-d78ea865ed04"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47685C808EB8513BDA4EEECAC8185BDD"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian N.","key":"alberspau","last":"Albers","name":"Albers, Christian N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea","key":"ellegaardjensenpau","last":"Ellegaard-Jensen","name":"Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer Bugge","key":"harderpau","last":"Harder","locid":"36d14bf1-76d1-476a-afeb-5d4168d801b7","name":"Harder, Christoffer Bugge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","locid":"25b0aa8d-b223-4ae0-ab6f-26d47230e97d","name":"Rosendahl, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-5202-6585","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Berith E.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Berith E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"ekelundpau","last":"Ekelund","locid":"c62c0d5e-1bc3-45d6-bd62-11bfa9d44c2a","name":"Ekelund, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0002-2144-7659","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Jens","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/es5046452","issn":["0013936X","15205851"],"issn_org":["0013936X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","pages":"839-846","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Technology","title_org":"Environmental Science & Technology (Washington)","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921734107"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2eabb7f6-92c9-42d0-a9a6-d78ea865ed04"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Groundwater chemistry determines the prokaryotic community structure of waterworks sand filters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421241","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This thesis explores information visualizations on large, high-resolution touch displays for analysis of massive amounts of data. The ever increasing rate at which data is collected about everything from peoples’ health, over organisations expenditures, to scientific experiments, necessitates new data analysis techniques. Information visualizations on large, high-resolution touch displays is a promising answer to these needs, and provide abundant display space for people to make sense of data. However, little is known about how to tailor interactive visualizations to abundant display space or about the benefits they might bring. The present thesis draws on the fields of human-computer interaction (HCI) and information visualization (InfoVis) to answer these questions.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does abundant display space support data analysis interaction techniques for information visualizations on large high resolution displays","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.diku.dk/english/event-calendar-2015/soeren_knudsen_phd_thesis_defense/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-425131","ids":["ku-355bf403-d44a-48e6-a6cf-39ed55cb313e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BBF09A431FC164BAB9A3BA9189C73CDB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"60aa66e8-eac5-4487-94e1-f1379643b27d","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"199","publisher":"Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Science, University of Copenhagen","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-355bf403-d44a-48e6-a6cf-39ed55cb313e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Does Abundant Display Space Support Data Analysis? : Interaction Techniques for Information Visualizations on Large, High-Resolution Displays","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425131","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Degradation tests of two phosphoric acid (PA) doped PBI membrane based HT-PEM fuel cells were reported in this paper to investigate the effects of start/stop and the presence of methanol in the fuel to the performance degradation of the HT-PEM fuel cell. Continuous tests with pure dry H2 and methanol containing H2 which was composed of H2, steam and methanol as the fuel were performed on both single cells. After the continuous tests, 12-h-startup/12-h-shutdown dynamic tests were performed on the first single cell with H2 as the fuel and on the second single cell with methanol containing H2 as the fuel. Along with the degradation tests, electrochemical techniques such as polarization curves and electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) were employed to study the degradation mechanisms of the fuel cells. The results of the tests showed that both single cells experienced an increase in the performance during the H2 continuous tests, because of a decrease in the reaction kinetic resistance mainly in the cathode due to the redistribution of PA between the membrane and electrodes. The performance of both single cells decreased in the following tests, with highest performance decay rate in the methanol continuous test, followed by that in the H2 start/stop test and the lowest performance decay rate in the H2 continuous test. EIS measurements for the first fuel cell during the start/stop test showed that the mass transfer resistance and ohmic resistance increased which could be attributed to the corrosion of carbon support in the catalyst layer and degradation of the PBI membrane. During the continuous test with methanol containing H2 as the fuel the reaction kinetic resistance and mass transfer resistance of both single cells increased, which may be caused by the adsorption of methanol decomposition products (CO mainly) on the catalyst surface and dilution of H2 because of the presence of water vapor and methanol in the gas stream. The performance of the second single cell experienced a slight decrease during the start/stop test with methanol containing H2 as the fuel. It is revealed from all the tests that the presence of methanol and start/stop can accelerate the degradation of HT-PEM fuel cell, and the effect of presence of methanol is more significant.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Fan","Araya, Samuel Simon","Grigoras, Ionela","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-082720"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Degradation","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","HT PEMFC","Methanol","PBI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance degradation tests of phosphoric acid doped polybenzimidazole membrane based high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://fuelcellscience.asmedigitalcollection.asme.org/article.aspx?articleid=1936693","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-082720","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000350495700002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84934315944","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-703bebec-a50b-4ac6-9ccb-bc0ba67f921f"],"keyword":["Degradation","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","HT-PEMFC","Methanol","PBI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C3FCDB5FCEC3E095D6D9AC6FC97E6AB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"874642c9-fe83-4b87-9b5e-9b8088c39e6a","name":"Zhou, Fan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ionela","key":"grigoraspau","last":"Grigoras","locid":"1eeff737-15ec-4ee3-a58d-e273ca970287","name":"Grigoras, Ionela","orcid":"0000-0002-1846-6568","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1115/1.4029081","issn":["1550624X","15516989"],"issn_org":["1550624X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Fuel Cell Science and Technology","publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","status":"p","title":"Journal of Fuel Cell Science and Technology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84934315944"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-703bebec-a50b-4ac6-9ccb-bc0ba67f921f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Performance Degradation Tests of Phosphoric Acid Doped Polybenzimidazole Membrane Based High Temperature Polymer Electrolyte Membrane Fuel Cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-082720","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
