{"abstract":"There are currently many different lithium ion (Li-ion) chemistries available on the market, and several new players are in the research and development process; however, none of them is superior to the other chemistries in all aspects. Relatively low price, long cycle and calendar lifetime, and intrinsic safety of the nanophosphate LiFePO4/C Li-ion chemistry make it possible to consider this chemistry for electric vehicle (EV) applications. This paper investigates the lifetime of the nanophosphate LiFePO4/C battery chemistry when it is used for full electrical vehicles. The investigation is performed considering a semiempirical calendar and cycle lifetime model, which was developed based on extended accelerated lifetime tests. Both capacity and power capability degradations during calendar and cycle life aging are considered and quantified. Finally, the developed battery cell lifetime model is used to study the capacity and power capability degradation behavior of the tested nanophosphate LiFePO4/C battery for two EV operational scenarios.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Stroe, Ana-Irina","Teodorescu, Remus","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112053"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Batteries","Life estimation","Lithium","Reliability","Testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lifetime estimation of the nanophosphate lifepo000000000004 c battery chemistry used in fully electric vehicles","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-112053","identifier":[{"id":"84937910073","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000358255700077","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d57aef01-39bc-4a8b-8a43-ed02bda150a5"],"keyword":["Batteries","Life estimation","Lithium","Reliability","Testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7AF26C78ECAD044F06971B1EA1CF7CFB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskimaciejjozefpau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroedanielioanpau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ana-Irina","key":"stroeanairinapau","last":"Stroe","locid":"e6ff6bac-362f-4fd1-b46c-d5f62d1e2c1a","name":"Stroe, Ana-Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-8254","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescuremuspau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærsørenknudsenpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tia.2015.2405500","issn":["00939994"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","pages":"3453-3461","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Industry Applications","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937910073"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d57aef01-39bc-4a8b-8a43-ed02bda150a5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Lifetime Estimation of the Nanophosphate LiFePO4/C Battery Chemistry Used in Fully Electric Vehicles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112053","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The objective is to understand the effect of methanol and water vapor separately on a high temperature PEM fuel cell. An investigation was performed with different anode fuel compositions and results in terms of performance and impedance analyzed. During the initial 1000 h, cell was tested with pure hydrogen under varying current densities of 0.2 A cm-2 and 0.6 A cm-2, followed by hydrogen mixed with 15 % water vapor and then with 1 % methanol. The degradation rates at two current densities 0.2 A cm-2 and 0.6 A cm-2 were analyzed and discussed. The degradation at higher current density is more severe than at lower current density. However, on switching from higher to lower current density, the effect is reversible and the performance is improved. This suggests that some degradation is reversible. The addition of water vapor in the feed improves the performance at high current densities, which suggest an improvement of total cell resistance also supported by the impedance comparison. There is no or minimal variation in performance with the introduction of 1 % methanol along with water vapor in the anode feed at 0.2 A cm-2 and 0.6A cm-2 .","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomas, Sobi","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121534"],"event":{"end":"2015-12-18","place":"Naples, it","start":"2015-12-16","title":"6th European Fuel Cell Technology and Applications Conference - Piero Lunghi Conference, EFC 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["EIS","HTPEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating the effect of water vapor and residual methanol on the anode of high temperature pem fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84994639328&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121534","identifier":[{"id":"84994639328","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f5f945cc-01de-4672-a656-2d6a9572bef2"],"keyword":["EIS","HTPEM","Reformate feed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8854986F1849F962644F638AD02CC5B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sobi","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"33bb2f77-e034-426b-ac72-d921d4354655","name":"Thomas, Sobi","orcid":"0000-0002-2759-3753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788882863241"],"pages":"229-230","publisher":"ENEA, Italian National Agency for New Technologies, Energy and Sustainable Economic Development","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 6th European Fuel Cell - Piero Lunghi Conference, EFC 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994639328"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f5f945cc-01de-4672-a656-2d6a9572bef2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Investigating the Effect of Water Vapor and Residual Methanol on the Anode of High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121534","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The PBI/H3PO4 high temperature (HT) PEM fuel cell is often fueled with H2-rich reformates which typically contain impurities such as CO, CO2 and water vapor. CO in the concentration level of several percent can cause apparent loss in performance of the HT-PEM fuel cell. In this study the influences of CO2 and water content in anode stream on CO poisoning of a HT-PEM fuel cell were investigated. Polarization curves and electrochemical impedance spectra were measured to quantify the performance loss caused by CO poisoning under different conditions. The experimental results suggest that higher anode humidity level reduced the cell performance loss caused by CO poisoning. When the fuel cell was operated with pure H2, the cell performance was not significantly affect by the change in anode dew point temperature in the range of room temperature and 60 °C. CO2 in anode stream resulted in slight decrease in performance of the fuel cell operated with pure H2 due to dilution effect. Whereas it can significantly deteriorate the cell performance loss caused by CO poisoning. Lastly, the CO poisoning effect on cell performance with presence of CO2 was proved to be relieved by anode humidification.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhou, Fan","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Park, Jung O."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-124237"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["South Korea"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Energy Lab, Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["CO poisoning","CO2","High temperature PEM fuel cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental investigation of carbon monoxide poisoning effect on a pbi h000000000003po000000000004 high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell influence of anode humidification and carbon dioxide","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-124237","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000364256500018","type":"wos"},{"id":"84944392744","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ff873ed2-2fe8-4eb1-ac5b-b1b6604e9403"],"keyword":["Anode humidification","CO poisoning","CO2","High temperature PEM fuel cell"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8BECC2CFE54EF611CF0A38FB631D8C60"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"kr","key":"energy lab samsung advanced institute of technology","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Energy Lab, Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"874642c9-fe83-4b87-9b5e-9b8088c39e6a","name":"Zhou, Fan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","la