{"abstract":"Translation elongation factor EF-Tu belongs to the superfamily of guanine-nucleotide binding proteins, which play key cellular roles as regulatory switches. All G-proteins require activation via exchange of GDP for GTP to carry out their respective tasks. Often, guanine-nucleotide exchange factors are essential to this process. During translation, EF-Tu:GTP transports aminoacylated tRNA to the ribosome. GTP is hydrolyzed during this process, and subsequent reactivation of EF-Tu is catalyzed by EF-Ts. The reaction path of guanine-nucleotide exchange is structurally poorly defined for EF-Tu and EF-Ts. We have determined the crystal structures of the following reaction intermediates: two structures of EF-Tu:GDP:EF-Ts (2.2 and 1.8 Å resolution), EF-Tu:PO4:EF-Ts (1.9 Å resolution), EF-Tu:GDPNP:EF-Ts (2.2 Å resolution) and EF-Tu:GDPNP:pulvomycin:Mg(2+):EF-Ts (3.5 Å resolution). These structures provide snapshots throughout the entire exchange reaction and suggest a mechanism for the release of EF-Tu in its GTP conformation. An inferred sequence of events during the exchange reaction is presented.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thirup, Søren Skou","Van, Lan Bich","Nielsen, Tine K","Knudsen, Charlotte Rohde"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-181912"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural outline of the detailed mechanism for elongation factor ts mediated guanine nucleotide exchange on elongation factor tu","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsb.2015.06.011","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-181912","identifier":[{"id":"26073967","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84937627733","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5c2e15ee-5770-4a6e-9ba4-5362832e019d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A23E955E22AF7DEED74A22A7E9D02E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsb.2015.06.011","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Structural Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Skou","key":"thiruppau","last":"Thirup","locid":"58274bd2-99ea-4148-b16d-fb4f744ca9b5","name":"Thirup, Søren Skou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lan Bich","key":"vanpau","last":"Van","locid":"01df2e3c-6a54-4460-b0b6-66035c8233d0","name":"Van, Lan Bich","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine K","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Tine K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte R","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"782aeedc-6bcd-4ce7-867a-57a7cfbcf1bc","name":"Knudsen, Charlotte Rohde","name_org":"Knudsen, Charlotte R","orcid":"0000-0003-2356-4821","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26073967"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jsb.2015.06.011","issn":["10478477","10958657"],"issn_org":["10478477"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Structural Biology","pages":"10-21","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Structural Biology","volume":"191"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937627733"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5c2e15ee-5770-4a6e-9ba4-5362832e019d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Structural outline of the detailed mechanism for elongation factor Ts-mediated guanine nucleotide exchange on elongation factor Tu","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-181912","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Schioldan, Anne Grethe","Gregersen, Søren","Hald, Stine","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Holst, Jens Juul","Hermansen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-186594"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dietary fibres in the prevention of type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-186594","ids":["au-64458643-8978-4ace-94ac-6f1a219f5fc6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7088872CB12372D74A8E2E257EF1DD24"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism C"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Grethe","key":"schioldanpau","last":"Schioldan","locid":"a710b241-48f9-4926-adb7-f3dbcfeb6a9f","name":"Schioldan, Anne Grethe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"59b0d84c-a135-49bf-afba-7783f90976c2","name":"Gregersen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1953-8631","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","locid":"ed81f2ac-05a5-4d72-b195-9e6afc4b7800","name":"Hald, Stine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"hermansenpau","last":"Hermansen","locid":"a62f80e1-f33f-47bd-a5e5-87d59477619f","name":"Hermansen, Kjeld","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/db15-2462-2510","issn":["00121797","1939327X"],"issn_org":["00121797"],"issue":"supplement 1","journal":"Diabetes","publisher":"American Diabetes Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Diabetes","volume":"64"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-64458643-8978-4ace-94ac-6f1a219f5fc6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dietary fibres in the prevention of Type 2 diabetes","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-186594","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The use of distiller dried grains with solubles (DDGS) as alternative to conventional animal feed for non-ruminants is challenged by the high content of non-starch polysaccharides and varying protein quality. In this study the enzymatic degradation of corn- and wheat DDGS was evaluated, in vitro, by use of four xylanases from two different glycoside hydrolase families, GH10 and GH11, along with protease and phytase. Wheat DDGS showed the highest degree of enzymatic degradation due to a lower degree of cell wall complexity compared with that of corn DDGS. For corn DDGS, the combination of xylanase and protease yielded the highest degree of enzymatic degradation, indicating close association of arabinoxylan and protein within the cell wall matrix. Collectively, the GH10 xylanase degraded DDGS more efficiently than the GH11 xylanases, due to the complexity of the substrate and the substrate affinity of this xylanase. The current in vitro results indicate a high potential of xylanase in combination with protease to efficiently degrade DDGS and promote nutrient release in diets for non-ruminant animals.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","Dalsgaard, Søren","Arent, Susan","Lorentsen, Rikke","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Yu, Shukun","Lærke, Helle Nygaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-186596"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Enzymatic activity","Enzymes","Optimization","Protease","Xylanase"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"xylanase and protease increase solubilization of non starch polysaccharides and nutrient release of corn and wheat distillers dried grains with solubles","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bej.2015.02.036","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-186596","identifier":[{"id":"84924045448","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6447a309-57f8-4f61-8d05-e85355a81fb2"],"keyword":["distillers dried grains with solubles","enzymatic activity","enzymes","optimization","protease","xylanase"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D86CD869F875EB49AA073BF465A5F50B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bej.2015.02.036","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Brøgger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4fbc8c90-2c05-4233-a45a-b80c6cbab818","name":"Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan","key":"arentpau","last":"Arent","name":"Arent, Susan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"lorentsenpau","last":"Lorentsen","name":"Lorentsen, Rikke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shukun","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Shukun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bej.2015.02.036","issn":["1369703X","1873295X"],"issn_org":["1369703X"],"journal":"Biochemical Engineering Journal","pages":"99-106","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Biochemical Engineering Journal","volume":"98"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924045448"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6447a309-57f8-4f61-8d05-e85355a81fb2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Xylanase and Protease Increase Solubilization of Non-Starch Polysaccharides and Nutrient Release of Corn- and Wheat Distillers Dried Grains with Solubles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-186596","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Two experiments were performed to study the effect of xylanase on ileal extract viscosity, in vivo fiber solubilization and degradation, and apparent ileal digestibility (AID) of fiber constituents, OM, CP, starch, and crude fat in rye and wheat in ileal-cannulated pigs. In Exp. 1, coarse rye without (NX) or with addition of xylanase from Aspergillus niger (AN), Bacillus subtilis (BS), or Trichoderma reesei (TR) was fed to 8 ileal-cannulated barrows (initial BW 30.9 ± 0.3 kg) for 1 wk each according to a double 4 × 4 Latin square design. In Exp. 2, fine rye, fine wheat, and coarse wheat with or without a combination of xylanase from Bacillus subtilis and Trichoderma reesei were fed to 6 ileal-cannulated barrows (initial BW 33.6 ± 0.5 kg) for 1 wk according to a 6 × 6 Latin square design with a 2 × 3 factorial arrangement of enzyme and cereal matrix. Chromic oxide (0.2%) was used as an inert marker. Ileal effluent was collected for 8 h on d 5 and 7 and pooled for analysis. In Exp. 1, TR reduced intestinal viscosity of pigs fed rye from 9.3 mPa·s in the control diet (NX) to 6.0 mPa·s (P < 0.001), whereas AN and BS had no effect. None of the enzymes changed the concentration of total arabinoxylan, high-molecular-weight arabinoxylan (HMW-AX), or arabinoxylan oligosaccharides (AXOS) in the liquid phase of digesta. In Exp. 2, the enzyme combination reduced intestinal viscosity for all 3 cereal matrices (P < 0.05), but the viscosity was much higher with fine rye (7.6 mPa·s) than with fine and coarse wheat (<1.7 mPa·s). Simultaneously, the total concentration of arabinoxylan in the liquid phase of digesta increased by 82.4% in fine wheat (P < 0.002) and by 45.9% in coarse wheat (P < 0.006), and AXOS increased 16-fold with enzyme addition. Similar effects of enzyme were not seen with rye. The concentration of xylooligosaccharides in the liquid phase of digesta increased with enzyme addition, but for xylose, it was only significant for wheat, for which it increased 3.9-fold (P < 0.001). None of the xylanases affected AID of arabinoxylan of rye in Exp. 1. In Exp. 2, the enzyme combination increased AID of arabinoxylan by 91% to 107% (P < 0.001) across cereal matrices. Enzyme addition did not affect AID of nutrients in any of the experiments except for a higher starch and crude fat digestibility of fine wheat with enzyme addition (P < 0.012) in Exp. 2. Collectively, the results suggest that xylanase is more efficient in degrading arabinoxylan from wheat than from rye.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lærke, Helle Nygaard","Arent, Susan","Dalsgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-273146"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of xylanases on ileal viscosity intestinal fiber modification and apparent ileal fiber and nutrient digestibility of rye and wheat in growing pigs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2527/jas.2015-9096","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-273146","identifier":[{"id":"26440332","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84975833307","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fc17e616-a54d-45bb-87a0-0bbfd6b1e197"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0B3C2652811E3AB449347335C2A1121"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2527/jas.2015-9096","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan","key":"arentpau","last":"Arent","name":"Arent, Susan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26440332"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2527/jas.2015-9096","issn":["00218812","15253163"],"issn_org":["00218812"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Animal Science","pages":"4323-4335","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Animal Science","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84975833307"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fc17e616-a54d-45bb-87a0-0bbfd6b1e197"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of xylanases on ileal viscosity, intestinal fiber modification, and apparent ileal fiber and nutrient digestibility of rye and wheat in growing pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-273146","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Sig dansk vindkraft og de fleste vil umiddelbart tænke på Vestas Wind Systems og Siemens Wind Power. Også de danske vindmølleparker og de investeringer, som især DONG Energy har foretaget, ligger langt fremme i bevidstheden hos mange danskere. Men i skyggen af disse flagskibe trives en meget stor underskov af leverandører. Disse virksomheder, som overvejende er mindre og mellemstore, rummer et meget stort potentiale for vækst. Både den vækst, som de hver især kan opnå. Men i høj grad også den afledte vækst, der kommer hele branchen til gode. Et voksende marked for vindmøller vil betyde flere arbejdspladser, større omsætning og øget konkurrenceevne for de danske virksomheder. Leverandørerne har også en vigtig rolle at spille med hensyn til at gøre vindmøllerne yderligere effektive. Det kan blandt andet ske gennem højere driftssikkerhed. Øgede kompetencer hos leverandørerne fører til færdige produkter og serviceløsninger af højere kvalitet. Samtidig får vindmølleproducenterne mulighed for at koncentrere sig om kerneforretningen, nemlig udvikling og salg af endnu bedre og billigere vindmøller. Med andre ord vil leverandørernes øgede styrke brede sig i hele branchen og dermed yderligere forbedre dansk vindkrafts ry som internationalt førende. I en tid med hård global konkurrence er der imidlertid ingen garanti for, at det fulde potentiale for vækst hos de danske leverandører vil blive indfriet. Industriens Fond, DTU og Vindmølleindustrien har derfor forenet kræfterne gennem det sektorudviklingsprojekt, som ligger bag denne rapport. Både danske og internationale undersøgelser viser, at virksomheder, som er aktive inden for teknologisk udvikling og innovation, opnår højere vækst end andre virksomheder. Især, når indsatsen sker i samarbejde med andre typer af virksomheder og offentlig forskning. Denne rapport beskriver, hvordan sådanne projekter fremover kan finde sted i højere grad end de gør i dag. Samtidig peger projektet på en række bredere problemstillinger, som ikke kan løses gennem enkeltstående fælles forsknings- og udviklingsprojekter. Her leverer rapporten anbefalinger til, hvordan konkurrencekraften hos leverandørerne kan forbedres. Leverandørerne til vindkraften har traditionelt levet uden for rampelyset. Forhåbentlig yder rapporten et bidrag til, at denne store gruppe af virksomheder kan træde frem på scenen til gavn for dansk konkurrenceevne og beskæftigelse.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Niels Axel","Molzen, Jan Eiersted","Pedersen, Anja Legind","Siggaard Knudsen, Søren","Andersen, Morten","Holck, Ane","Thomsen, Kenneth","Buhl, Thomas","Pedersen, Niels Leergaard","Holbøll, Joachim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305647"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Wind Industry Association"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vindbranchens vækstlag","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/143486369/501157_Sektorudviklingsrapport_samlet_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305647","ids":["dtu-0392c800-cc0b-4cd5-9228-bd6ed36af322"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E1F51BF84F1ADE71CEC1C39FC9F05BC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/143486369/501157_Sektorudviklingsrapport_samlet_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Administration, Office for Innovation & Sector Services"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Wind Industry Association"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Axel","key":"nielsennielsaxelpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9a7978de-56da-4293-b54d-018431526912","name":"Nielsen, Niels Axel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Eiersted","key":"molzenjaneierstedpau","last":"Molzen","locid":"b3b274f8-c15e-42bd-a8ae-90db55966789","name":"Molzen, Jan Eiersted","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Legind","key":"pedersenanjalegindpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anja Legind","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"siggaardknudsensørenpau","last":"Siggaard Knudsen","locid":"1f695aa6-1944-4f12-a54e-9b0fc7621d01","name":"Siggaard Knudsen, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"andersenmortenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ane","key":"holckanepau","last":"Holck","locid":"959a59fe-bc22-4b5d-80a2-2829ed32abf1","name":"Holck, Ane","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"thomsenkennethpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"84ecad0d-a1f3-4785-aad5-86eec7c72b2d","name":"Thomsen, Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0002-4913-0039","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"buhlthomaspau","last":"Buhl","locid":"03057fd7-6d51-4def-b381-d9056c08663c","name":"Buhl, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-9372-3851","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Leergaard","key":"pedersennielsleergaardpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e21a6065-e719-4ef8-ad66-a777acae6885","name":"Pedersen, Niels Leergaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4659-5623","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joachim","key":"holbølljoachimpau","last":"Holbøll","locid":"7c8dfa14-3e22-46aa-9345-505f2a876c9d","name":"Holbøll, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-7578-8304","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"33","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0392c800-cc0b-4cd5-9228-bd6ed36af322"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Vindbranchens vækstlag","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305647","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We present a lg n + 2 lg lg n + 3 ancestry labeling scheme for trees. The problem was first presented by Kannan et al. [STOC 88’] along with a simple 2 lg n solution. Motivated by applications to XML files, the label size was improved incrementally over the course of more than 20 years by a series of papers. The last, due to Fraigniaud and Korman [STOC 10’], presented an asymptotically optimal lg n+4 lg lg n+ O(1) labeling scheme using non-trivial tree-decomposition techniques. By providing a framework generalizing interval based labeling schemes, we obtain a simple, yet asymptotically optimal solution to the problem. Furthermore, our labeling scheme is attained by a small modification of the original 2 lg n solution.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dahlgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","Rotbart, Noy Galil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-537562"],"event":{"acronym":"ICALP","end":"2015-07-10","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2015-07-06","title":"International Colloquium on Automata, Languages and Programming 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simple and optimal ancestry labeling scheme for trees","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-537562","identifier":[{"id":"84950128629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f18b3c63-6ffb-4264-b142-4c54376d7807"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7C1C1BB92BA43FCE6441289E767B934B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The APL Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"4788aa93-be24-420b-8767-e735d6dcc61d","name":"Dahlgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2925-746X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"28c3a2af-0485-4bfb-83ba-e8a330c65b22","name":"Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","orcid":"0000-0001-5308-9609","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Noy Galil","key":"rotbartpau","last":"Rotbart","locid":"3d51a60b-12df-4a73-8391-8aeab856ec6a","name":"Rotbart, Noy Galil","orcid":"0000-0003-1882-0755","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Magnús M.","key":"halldórssonpedh","last":"Halldórsson","name":"Halldórsson, Magnús M.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kazuo","key":"iwamapedh","last":"Iwama","name":"Iwama, Kazuo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naoki","key":"kobayashipedh","last":"Kobayashi","name":"Kobayashi, Naoki","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bettina","key":"speckmannpedh","last":"Speckmann","name":"Speckmann, Bettina","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-47666-6_45","eisbn":["9783662476666"],"isbn":["9783662476659"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"564-574","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"42nd International Colloquium, ICALP 2015, Kyoto, Japan, July 6-10, 2015, Proceedings, Part II","title":"Automata, languages, and programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84950128629"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f18b3c63-6ffb-4264-b142-4c54376d7807"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A simple and optimal ancestry labeling scheme for trees","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-537562","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Current lithium-ion battery research aims in not only increasing their energy density but also power density. Emerging applications of lithium-ion batteries (HEV, PHEV, grid support) are becoming more and more power demanding. The increasing charging and discharging power capability rates of lithium-ion batteries raises safety concerns and requires thermal management of the entire battery system. Moreover, lithium-ion battery’s temperature influences both battery short term (capacity, efficiency, self-discharge) and long-term (lifetime) behaviour. Thus, thermal modelling of lithium-ion battery cells and battery packs is gaining importance. Equivalent thermal circuits’ models have proven to be relatively accurate with low computational burden for the price of low spatial resolution; nevertheless, they usually require expensive equipment for parametrization. Recent research initiated by Barsoukov et al. proposed electrothermal impedance spectroscopy (ETIS) as a novel and non-destructive method of characterizing the thermal properties of batteries by defining frequency dependent thermal impedance. This paper aims to systematize the state of knowledge about ETIS, presents measurement methods on the example of a high-power LiMO2/Li4Ti5O12 battery cell and discusses the prospect.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Stanciu, Tiberiu","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057229"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-02","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2015-09-27","title":"10th Conference on Sustainable Development of Energy, Water and Environment Systems","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery thermal model","Lithium ion battery","Thermal impedance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrothermal impedance spectroscopy as a cost efficient method for determining thermal parameters of lithium ion batteries prospects measurement methods and state of knowledge","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-057229","ids":["aau-1880c563-9d94-4457-8b6a-dea2abbc687f"],"keyword":["Battery thermal model","Ilectrothermal impedance spectroscopy","Lithium-ion battery","Thermal impedance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F094A473C824C3B29047E6A2110CC18"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tiberiu","key":"stanciupau","last":"Stanciu","locid":"f16625ba-f630-4152-b06a-7bfbb0561d5e","name":"Stanciu, Tiberiu","orcid":"0000-0003-2447-5257","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1880c563-9d94-4457-8b6a-dea2abbc687f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Electrothermal Impedance Spectroscopy as a Cost Efficient Method for Determining Thermal Parameters of Lithium Ion Batteries : Prospects, Measurement Methods and State of Knowledge","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-057229","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper focuses on the indoor climate in new Danish low-energy houses and discusses the issue of overheating in relation to evaluation methods and user satisfaction. The user satisfaction has been evaluated among 370 owners of new low-energy class 2015 detached single-family houses based on a questionnaire survey. The survey evaluated overall satisfaction, and more specifically satisfaction with the indoor climate parameters temperature, draught, air quality, noise and daylight, and also technical installations of the house. The survey showed satisfaction with living in new low-energy houses and more than 90% perceived the indoor environment as satisfactory both in summer and winter. The majority perceived the various indoor climate parameters to be better in their new low-energy house compared to conditions in their former house. Compared with earlier studies on previous generations of low-energy houses, problems with overheating seem to have decreased, as only 12% found temperature conditions to be unsatisfactory in summer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","Mortensen, Lone Hedegaard","Kragh, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-060723"],"event":{"acronym":"PHN","end":"2015-08-21","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-08-20","title":"Passiv hus Norden","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Indoor climate","Indoor environment","Low energy houses","Occupant satisfaction","Overheating","Perceived indoor climate","Questionnaire survey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"satisfaction with indoor climate in new danish low energy houses","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"htt