{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A Danish cancer pathway has been implemented for patients with serious non-specific symptoms and signs of cancer (NSSC-CPP). The initiative is one of several to improve the long diagnostic interval and the poor survival of Danish cancer patients. However, little is known about the patients investigated under this pathway. We aim to describe the characteristics of patients referred from general practice to the NSSC-CPP and to estimate the cancer probability and distribution in this population. METHODS: A cross-sectional study was performed, including all patients referred to the NSSC-CPP at the hospitals in Aarhus or Silkeborg in the Central Denmark Region between March 2012 and March 2013. Data were based on a questionnaire completed by the patient's general practitioner (GP) combined with nationwide registers. Cancer probability was the percentage of new cancers per investigated patient. Associations between patient characteristics and cancer diagnosis were estimated with prevalence rate ratios (PRRs) from a generalised linear model. RESULTS: The mean age of all 1278 included patients was 65.9 years, and 47.5 % were men. In total, 16.2 % of all patients had a cancer diagnosis after six months; the most common types were lung cancer (17.9 %), colorectal cancer (12.6 %), hematopoietic tissue cancer (10.1 %) and pancreatic cancer (9.2 %). All patients in combination had more than 80 different symptoms and 51 different clinical findings at referral. Most symptoms were non-specific and vague; weight loss and fatigue were present in more than half of all cases. The three most common clinical findings were 'affected general condition' (35.8 %), 'GP's gut feeling' (22.5 %) and 'findings from the abdomen' (13.0 %). A strong association was found between GP-estimated cancer risk at referral and probability of cancer. CONCLUSIONS: In total, 16.2 % of the patients referred through the NSSC-CPP had cancer. They constituted a heterogeneous group with many different symptoms and clinical findings. The GP's gut feeling was a common reason for referral which proved to be a strong predictor of cancer. The GP's overall estimation of the patient's risk of cancer at referral was associated with the probability of finding cancer.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ingeman, Mads Lind","Christensen, Morten Bondo","Bro, Flemming","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Vedsted, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-184251"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish cancer pathway for patients with serious non specific symptoms and signs of cancer a cross sectional study of patient characteristics and cancer probability","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-015-1424-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-184251","identifier":[{"id":"25990247","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4445271","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85019185782","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-602fb2d4-54fd-447f-8413-e6c31bb8d434"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2AAAEB6A42A9B855F432528A197490F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-015-1424-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Lind","key":"ingemanpau","last":"Ingeman","locid":"e2e19f92-ba3a-4d1a-8753-cfbec6562af9","name":"Ingeman, Mads Lind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Bondo","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b40aa4d7-4e95-4e8a-bef8-e7602ddabb82","name":"Christensen, Morten Bondo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"bropau","last":"Bro","locid":"17ebdde1-74d4-4ff7-a0c8-8f1d2a0da1f8","name":"Bro, Flemming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren T","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","name_org":"Knudsen, Søren T","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vedstedpau","last":"Vedsted","locid":"bb00d9e7-866c-4f04-8e3b-a71c913c39b0","name":"Vedsted, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2113-5599","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25990247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12885-015-1424-5","issn":["14712407"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Cancer","pages":"421","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Cancer","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019185782"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-602fb2d4-54fd-447f-8413-e6c31bb8d434"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Danish cancer pathway for patients with serious non-specific symptoms and signs of cancer-a cross-sectional study of patient characteristics and cancer probability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-184251","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The objective was to study the effect of a commercially available xylanase (CAX), an experimental xylanase (EX), and EX in combination with protease (EXP) on the degradation of nondigestible carbohydrates (NDC) and apparent ileal digestibility (AID) of nutrients in wheat distillers dried grains with solubles (wDDGS). The control and 3 enzyme diets contained 96% wDDGS supplemented with vitamins, minerals, l-lysine, and chromic oxide as a digestibility marker in addition to enzyme premix. Eight ileal cannulated pigs were fed 4 experimental diets containing 96% wDDGS—a control diet or 1 of 3 diets with CAX, EX, or EXP—in a double 4 × 4 Latin square design. The experimental period lasted 7 d; adaptation lasted 4 d, and the ileal digesta were collected for 8 h on d 5 and 7, when spot samples of feces were also collected. Digesta samples were analyzed for NDC, total and soluble nonstarch polysaccharides (NSP), low molecular weight (LMW) NDC, OM, CP, fat, starch, and marker. Compared with the control diet, addition of CAX, EX, and EXP increased the AID of arabinoxylan by 32 (P < 0.001), 28 (P = 0.001), and 24% (P = 0.004), respectively. In addition, EXP increased the AID of noncellulosic polysaccharide glucose by 21% compared with the control (P = 0.005). Compared with the control, addition of EX, EXP, and CAX decreased the concentration of soluble arabinoxylan in ileal digesta by 40 (P < 0.0001), 40 (P < 0.0001), and 21% (P = 0.022), respectively. Furthermore, addition of CAX, EXP, and EX increased the concentration of LMW arabinoxylan in ileal digesta by 40 (P = 0.0001), 36 (P = 0.0006), and 24% (P = 0.023), respectively, compared with the control. Addition of EX and EXP decreased the concentration of soluble NSP of ileal digesta by 25 (P = 0.001) and 26% (P < 0.001), respectively, compared with the control diet. Addition of CAX (P < 0.0001) and EXP (P = 0.013) increased the arabinose-to-xylose ratio in the insoluble arabinoxylan fraction in ileal digesta compared with the control diet, and CAX increased the uronic acid-to-xylose ratio of the ileal insoluble NSP fraction (P < 0.0001) compared with the control diet. Enzyme addition did not affect AID of OM, CP, starch, and fat (P > 0.3). In conclusion, addition of xylanases to wDDGS diets increased the ileal digestibility of NSP and generated LMW NDC components in the small intestine of pigs but did not affect ileal digestibility of nutrients in the current study.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","Yu, Shukun","Arent, Susan","Dalsgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Lærke, Helle Nygaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-189872"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"xylanase increased the ileal digestibility of non starch polysaccharides and concentration of low molecular weight non digestible carbohydrates in pigs fed high levels of wheat ddgs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2527/jas.2014-8829","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-189872","identifier":[{"id":"84971283901","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26115275","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6a14d32c-9ea4-4190-8c7d-e37b7ed6ad4a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A3C6B0D0DF3CD0DF527EF0F63C33C188"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2527/jas.2014-8829","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Brøgger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4fbc8c90-2c05-4233-a45a-b80c6cbab818","name":"Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shukun","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Shukun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan","key":"arentpau","last":"Arent","name":"Arent, Susan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26115275"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2527/jas.2014-8829","issn":["00218812","15253163"],"issn_org":["00218812"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Animal Science","pages":"2885-2893","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Animal Science","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84971283901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6a14d32c-9ea4-4190-8c7d-e37b7ed6ad4a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Xylanase Increased the Ileal Digestibility of Non-Starch Polysaccharides and Concentration of Low Molecular Weight Non-Digestible Carbohydrates in Pigs Fed High Levels of wheat DDGS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-189872","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Erlang-Nielsen, Michael","Jørgensen, Johannes Ravn","Knudsen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263504"],"event":{"end":"2015-03-10","place":"Skælskør, dk","start":"2015-03-09","title":"DanSeed Symposium 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determination of germination capacity of malting barley em hordeum vulgare em l by single seed respiration measurement based on novel oxygen sensing technology","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://danseed.dk/fileadmin/danseed/009_Michael_Erlang_Nielsen_determination_of_germination_capacity.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263504","ids":["au-eb14e812-8b18-4f93-88fc-b0edd67458cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9D269B6799CAECD0A1C93B361635F713"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://danseed.dk/fileadmin/danseed/009_Michael_Erlang_Nielsen_determination_of_germination_capacity.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"carlsberg foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CARL","l3nn":"Carlsberg Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Carlsberg Foundation","namevar":["Carlsberg Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CARL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"erlangnielsenpau","last":"Erlang-Nielsen","locid":"3e116de3-ec7c-40e9-b589-5d358f062ba9","name":"Erlang-Nielsen, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes Ravn","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"20741068-2b9e-49c0-b7d5-551e049b45b2","name":"Jørgensen, Johannes Ravn","orcid":"0000-0003-3133-2350","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb14e812-8b18-4f93-88fc-b0edd67458cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Determination of germination capacity of malting barley <em>(Hordeum vulgare</em> L.) by single-seed respiration measurement based on novel oxygen-sensing technology","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263504","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Danish patients diagnosed with cancer who present with unspecific signs and symptoms are diagnosed with unfavourable delay, which has led to the establishment of a national fast-track (cancer) pathway. The aim of this study was to estimate the prevalence of cancer and other diagnoses in patients referred to this programme at Aarhus University Hospital from general practitioners. Furthermore, we aimed to characterise the patient cohort, assess survival and estimate the predictive values of symptoms, signs and biochemical abnormalities. METHODS: From 1 March 2011 to 31 December 2013, data of interest were consecutively collected from the electronic patient record by two medical doctors. RESULTS: Overall, 18% (58/323) had cancer, but the prevalence decreased from 22% in 2011 to 16% in 2013. Haematological cancers and cancers originating from the digestive system were the predominant cancer diagnoses. Patients diagnosed with cancer unfortunately had a high mortality suggesting that we diagnose cancer in the late, non-curable stages. Patients referred to the fast-track pathway had a median of four symptoms, most commonly weight loss and fatigue. In one fourth of the patients, a final diagnosis was not reached at discharge. For the rest (n = 185), gastrointestinal conditions, infectious and rheumatological diseases were most common. The predictive value of the presenting symptoms was poor. Age and biochemical markers considered as unspecific markers of cancer were better predictors. Anaemia was seen in 71% versus 34% of patients with/without diagnosed cancer, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: Unspecific signs and symptoms that may be indicative of cancer represent a clinical challenge. A fast-track (cancer) pathway is a new option for patients not entitled to enter an organ-specific programme. FUNDING: none. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bislev, Lise Sofie","Bruun, Bjarke Johannesen","Gregersen, Søren","Knudsen, Søren Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274446"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of cancer in danish patients referred to a fast track diagnostic pathway is substantial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84940376566","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-274446","identifier":[{"id":"26324087","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84940376566","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fe59fc74-a3ff-4ea8-a654-0d19d2ded2d3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB912F55F03DAB49EF06FBADE2DFE694"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism C"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Sofie","key":"bislevpau","last":"Bislev","locid":"536fa61a-a576-4912-a695-15bad7936431","name":"Bislev, Lise Sofie","orcid":"0000-0002-9720-9518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke Johannesen","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Bjarke Johannesen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"59b0d84c-a135-49bf-afba-7783f90976c2","name":"Gregersen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1953-8631","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26324087"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"9","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940376566"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fe59fc74-a3ff-4ea8-a654-0d19d2ded2d3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prevalence of cancer in Danish patients referred to a fast-track diagnostic pathway is substantial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-274446","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: MicroRNAs (miRNAs) are emerging as key regulators of cardiovascular development and disease, being involved in cardiac hypertrophy, fibrosis, remodeling and heart failure. Aortic stenosis is the most common valvular heart disease, and thus, we undertook a detailed analysis of differentially expressed miRNAs in this disease. Methods and Findings: We set up a model of aortic stenosis by performing transverse aorta constriction (TAC) in adult mice resulting in a rapid increase in left ventricle pressure load, pronounced hypertrophy, initiated fibrosis, impaired ejection performance and dysfunctional diastole. Using miRNA microarray we then identified more than 300 differentially regulated miRNAs in the hearts of mice affected by aortic stenosis. Five of these were validated using qRT-PCR in which miR-21 and miR-208b were striking because of their substantial 2-4 fold increase at day 21 post TAC when compared with the control group. Furthermore, we identified three novel miRNAs (miR-24, miR-301a and miR-335) that were highly induced in transverse aorta constricted mice compared to SHAM operated mice. Interestingly, the increased expression of miR-24, miR-301a and miR-335 in TAC affected hearts were not found in an animal model of myocardial infarction. Conclusion: These data suggests that the novel miRNAs are regulated in the heart specific to aortic stenosis, and may serve as biomarker candidates for future diagnosis, prognosis or treatment. Keywords: Aorta stenosis; Transverse aorta constriction; Hypertrophy; Fibrosis; Echocardiography; MicroRNA","author_count":8,"contributors":["Eskildsen, Tilde","Schneider, Mikael","Zha, Peiyong","Sandberg, Maria Boysen","Almind Knudsen, Lina","Andersen, Ditte Caroline","Sadoshima, Junichi","Sheikh, Søren Paludan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601430"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comprehensive microarray analysis identify dysregulated micrornas in pressure overload affected hearts","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182299619/comprehensive_microarray_analysis_identify_dysregulated_micrornas_in_pressure_overload_affected_hearts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601430","ids":["sdu-62a90791-eaee-4fb2-92a9-49be0688f508"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D516F725656C617E461D29B693F7CCE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.transbiomedicine.com/translational-biomedicine/comprehensive-microarray-analysis-identify-dysregulated-micrornas-in-pressure-overload-affected-hearts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182299619/comprehensive_microarray_analysis_identify_dysregulated_micrornas_in_pressure_overload_affected_hearts.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cardiovascular and Renal Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tilde","key":"eskildsenpau","last":"Eskildsen","locid":"73c01a45-283b-4773-8208-eeb7fe78bfa4","name":"Eskildsen, Tilde","orcid":"0000-0001-5264-6434","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"eb5de404-4255-412c-90cb-36857b7baa5e","name":"Schneider, Mikael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peiyong","key":"zhapau","last":"Zha","name":"Zha, Peiyong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Boysen","key":"sandbergpau","last":"Sandberg","locid":"0f5630ea-a6bd-4e57-87ec-1c3d4df2141d","name":"Sandberg, Maria Boysen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"almindknudsenpau","last":"Almind Knudsen","locid":"ea5c6260-7b47-4405-b4c9-c723270debe1","name":"Almind Knudsen, Lina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ditte Caroline","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"884ca799-a3a4-4b7c-8b36-270846e5b8f9","name":"Andersen, Ditte Caroline","orcid":"0000-0003-4940-7912","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Junichi","key":"sadoshimapau","last":"Sadoshima","name":"Sadoshima, Junichi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Paludan","key":"sheikhpau","last":"Sheikh","locid":"5773a0d9-ed2e-4bd4-8232-b68ee8d6cb09","name":"Sheikh, Søren Paludan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21720479"],"issue":"Special Issue","journal":"Translational Biomedicine","publisher":"iMedPub","status":"p","title":"Translational Biomedicine","volume":"2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-62a90791-eaee-4fb2-92a9-49be0688f508"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comprehensive Microarray Analysis Identify Dysregulated MicroRNAs in Pressure Overload Affected Hearts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-601430","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we analyze a hash function for k-partitioning a set into bins, obtaining strong concentration bounds for standard algorithms combining statistics from each bin. This generic method was originally introduced by Flajolet and Martin [FOCS'83] in order to save a factor Ω(k) of time per element over k independent samples when estimating the number of distinct elements in a data stream. It was also used in the widely used Hyper Log Log algorithm of Flajolet et al. [AOFA'97] and in large-scale machine learning by Li et al. [NIPS'12] for minwise estimation of set similarity. The main issue of k-partition, is that the contents of different bins may be highly correlated when using popular hash functions. This means that methods of analyzing the marginal distribution for a single bin do not apply. Here we show that a tabulation based hash function, mixed tabulation, does yield strong concentration bounds on the most popular applications of k-partitioning similar to those we would get using a truly random hash function. The analysis is very involved and implies several new results of independent interest for both simple and double tabulation, e.g. A simple and efficient construction for invertible bloom filters and uniform hashing on a given set.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dahlgaard, Soren","Knudsen, Mathias Baek Tejs","Rotenberg, Eva","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S02-090.51-033061"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-20","place":"Berkeley, California, us","start":"2015-10-18","title":"56th IEEE Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science, FOCS 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Concentration Bounds","Hashing","Peelability","Tabulation Hashing","Uniform Hashing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hashing for statistics over i k i partitions","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.7191v3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-090.51-033061","identifier":[{"id":"84960345251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-15df3d4a-547b-4fae-a798-31150e6169e8","ku-c6fe98db-37a3-4a4b-9312-81570a06b1f3"],"keyword":["Hashing","concentration bounds","constant moments","invertible bloom filters","joint distributions","k-partition","peelability","tabulation hashing","uniform hashing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB0443E7D87E7EA19439B3168EC3180C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.7191v3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The APL Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"4788aa93-be24-420b-8767-e735d6dcc61d","name":"Dahlgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2925-746X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"28c3a2af-0485-4bfb-83ba-e8a330c65b22","name":"Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","orcid":"0000-0001-5308-9609","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/focs.2015.83","eisbn":["9781467381918"],"pages":"1292-1310","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2015 IEEE 56th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science, FOCS 2015","volume":"2015-December"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960345251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-15df3d4a-547b-4fae-a798-31150e6169e8","ku-c6fe98db-37a3-4a4b-9312-81570a06b1f3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hashing for Statistics over K-Partitions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.51-033061","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The naturally occurring geogenic elements iodine (I), lithium (Li), and strontium (Sr) have a beneficial effect on human health. Iodine has an essential role in human metabolism while Li and Sr are used, respectively, as a treatment for various mental disorders and for post-menopausal osteoporosis. The aim here is to evaluate the potential for future epidemiological investigations in Denmark of lifelong and chronic exposure to low doses of these compounds. The drinking water data represents approximately 45% of the annual Danish groundwater abstraction for drinking water purposes, which supplies approximately 2.5 million persons. The spatial patterns were studied using inverse distance weighted interpolation and cluster analysis. The exposed population was estimated based on two datasets: (1) population density in the smallest census unit, the parishes, and (2) geocoded addresses where at least one person is residing. We found significant spatial variation in the exposure for all three elements, related mainly to geochemical processes. This suggests a prospective opportunity for future epidemiological investigation of long-term effects of I, Li, and Sr, either alone or in combinations with other geogenic elements such as Ca, Mg or F.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Voutchkova, Denitza","Schullehner, Jörg","Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016276"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Voutchkova, Denitza"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"keyword":["Denmark","Drinking wate","Epidemiology","Exposure","Iodine","Lithium","Spatial trends","Strontium","Treated groundwater"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposure to selected geogenic trace elements i li and sr from drinking water in denmark","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/geosciences5010045","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-016276","identifier":[{"id":"84925869436","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3261193e-c3c2-4f03-a053-4c90302c26c1","sdu-82fa51ba-8f19-4a2b-ae86-420aa98d23b0"],"keyword":["Denmark","Drinking wate","Epidemiology","Exposure","Iodine","Lithium","Spatial trends","Strontium","Treated groundwater"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9BF1B81E2D8FE18A7C89FD17A2650E6C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129631327/Exposure_to_Selected_Geogenic_Trace_Elements_I_Li_and_Sr_from_Drinking_Water_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/geosciences5010045","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84925869436&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Denitza Dimitrova","key":"voutchkovapau","last":"Voutchkova","locid":"3ca8a082-f717-4a20-a043-48e33b88a7bb","name":"Voutchkova, Denitza","name_org":"Voutchkova, Denitza Dimitrova","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jörg","key":"schullehnerpau","last":"Schullehner","locid":"f7647c26-21ff-4d28-8645-ac66742707e9","name":"Schullehner, Jörg","orcid":"0000-0002-1153-6885","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikoline Nygård","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"42deac4a-cdd7-47dd-9738-d5801af12a4a","name":"Knudsen, Nikoline Nygård","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Flindt","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Munch","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Birgitte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/geosciences5010045","issn":["20763263"],"issue":"1","journal":"Geosciences","pages":"45-66","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Geosciences","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925869436"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3261193e-c3c2-4f03-a053-4c90302c26c1","sdu-82fa51ba-8f19-4a2b-ae86-420aa98d23b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exposure to Selected Geogenic Trace Elements (I, Li, and Sr) from Drinking Water in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-016276","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Modern lithium-ion batteries, like LiMO2/Li4Ti5O12 chemistry, are having very high power capability, which drives the need for precise thermal modelling of the battery. Battery thermal models are required to avoid possible safety issues (thermal runaways, high-temperature gradients) but also for the optimal battery pack design and for predicting battery electrical performance during operation (especially at low temperatures). Equivalent electrical circuit battery models (thermal and electro-thermal) are able to offer relatively good performance with relatively low computational efforts and may be executed on-line (e.g. in the electric vehicle Battery Management System). The Electrothermal Impedance Spectroscopy (ETIS) can be used as a relatively simple and fast method for non-destructive parametrization of the battery thermal models. However, the ETIS requires expensive galvanostat with high-bandwidth and high-current capability for large format battery cells. Thus, this paper evaluates the possibility and accuracy of performing ETIS measurements with a standard battery test station (or bidirectional power supply) with low-bandwidth.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Stanciu, Tiberiu","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093961"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-05","place":"Búzlos, Rio de Janeiro , br","start":"2015-06-03","title":"2015 IEEE 24th International Symposium on Industrial Electronics (ISIE)","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrothermal impedance spectroscopy measurement on high power limo000000000002 li000000000004ti000000000005o000000000012 battery cell with low bandwidth test setup","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-093961","identifier":[{"id":"84947262139","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-977bd64e-a0cf-44bb-a242-99288867a48c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7BFF3414E4A20F13F1663B3082A7F767"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Loan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Loan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tiberiu","key":"stanciupau","last":"Stanciu","locid":"f16625ba-f630-4152-b06a-7bfbb0561d5e","name":"Stanciu, Tiberiu","orcid":"0000-0003-2447-5257","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isie.2015.7281652","isbn":["9781467375542"],"pages":"1253-1259","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2015 IEEE 24th International Symposium on Industrial Electronics (ISIE)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84947262139"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-977bd64e-a0cf-44bb-a242-99288867a48c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Electrothermal impedance spectroscopy measurement on high power LiMO2/Li4Ti5O12 battery cell with low bandwidth test setup","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093961","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
