earch":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-06f6133c-9497-4f3f-82ed-3f9032aec91c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"Ungdom og ungdomskultur\"","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052041","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the electrolysis of water it is convenient and advantageous to directly compress hydrogen at the cathode. This reduces system requirements and energy consumption associated with subsequent mechanical compression [1–3]. The simplest and most energy efficient system configuration is the so-called asymmetric setup, where only the cathode is operated at elevated pressures [2]. Under these conditions a large pressure difference forms across the polymer electrolyte membrane which mechanically compresses the polymer backbone and the anode electrode. While titanium felt has to be used as a gas diffusion layer at the anode, to withstand the mechanical compression, a conventional perfluorinated sulfonic acid (PFSA) membrane can be used as the electrolyte. Although PFSA membranes like Nafion exhibit high thermo-mechanical stability, water uptake and transport properties are significantly affected by mechanical compression depending on the temperature, relative humidity and the amount of liquid water present [4]. Consequently, it is of great importance to accurately account for the physiochemical relationship between mechanical compression and equilibrium water uptake, when attempting to predict the electrochemical behavior of an asymmetric pressurized PEM electrolysis cell In this work, a non-equilibrium formulation of the water uptake model by Kusoglu et al. [4] has been implemented in a two-dimensional, two-phase, multi-component and non-isothermal PEM electrolysis model. The non-equilibrium formulation of the water uptake model was chosen in order to account for interfacial transport kinetics between each fluid phase and the PFSA membrane. Besides modeling water uptake, the devised membrane model accounts for water transport through diffusion and electro-osmotic drag in the polymer phase, and hydraulic permeation in the liquid phase. Charge transport and Butler-Volmer electrochemistry are likewise included. In order to investigate the effect of accounting for membrane compression, a parametric study is carried out with and without the compression corrected water uptake model by Kusoglu et al. [4]. The obtained simulation results confirm and underline that the predicted water uptake and cell voltage are highly dependent on the applied water uptake model.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053211"],"event":{"end":"2015-07-31","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2015-07-26","title":"ECS Conference on Electrochemical Energy Conversion &amp; Storage with SOFC-XIV","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of pfsa membrane compression on the predicted performance of a high pressure pem electrolysis cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/sofc2015/webprogram/Paper53905.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053211","ids":["aau-0aee6450-8c75-4983-8bb6-b372d2243d2b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F63647769704ADC8C87C025541C87865"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/sofc2015/webprogram/Paper53905.html","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0aee6450-8c75-4983-8bb6-b372d2243d2b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Effect of PFSA Membrane Compression on the Predicted Performance of a High Pressure PEM Electrolysis Cell","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053211","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The poster presents a methodology to account for thermal effects on battery cells to improve the typical thermal performances in a pack through heating calculations generally performed under the operating condition assumption. The aim is to analyze the issues based on battery thermo-physical characteristics and their impact on the electrical state of battery cells(Khan, Mulder et al. 2013, Khan, Andreasen et al. 2014, Khan et al. 2014, Khan, Mulder et al. 2014, Khan, Nielsen et al. 2014). Based on this analysis, we derive strategies in achieving the goal, and then propose a battery thermal management system with cell-level thermal controls.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-083041"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-16","place":"Grenoble, fr","start":"2015-10-14","title":"COMSOL Conference 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery management system","CFD application","Cooling systems","Electric vehicle EV","Performance analysis","Thermal management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling thermal effects of battery cells inside electric vehicle battery packs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.1.4567.2085","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-083041","ids":["aau-7165a3cc-53f7-4088-9db9-4fd9cdcdd355"],"keyword":["Battery management system","CFD application","Cooling systems","Electric vehicle (EV)","Performance analysis","Thermal management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C9BFEB6C0462288E55F9A44F8DE6DBC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.1.4567.2085","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohammad Rezwan","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"93d828d4-c1bf-44a2-bf94-b1fd3dcc29cf","name":"Khan, Mohammad Rezwan","orcid":"0000-0002-1532-0598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7165a3cc-53f7-4088-9db9-4fd9cdcdd355"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modelling Thermal Effects of Battery Cells inside Electric Vehicle Battery Packs","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083041","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this study a micro-combined-heat-and-power (micro-CHP) system is coupled to a vapor-compression heat pump to fulfill the residential needs for heating (space heating and water heating) and electricity in detached single-family households in Denmark. Such a combination is assumed to be attractive for application, since both fuel cell technology and electric heat pumps are found to be two of the most efficient technologies for generation/conversion of useful energy. The micro-CHP system is fueled with natural gas and includes a fuel cell stack, a fuel processor and other auxiliary components. The micro-CHP system assumes heat-led operation, to avoid dumping of heat and the use of complicated thermal energy storage. The overall system is grid-interconnected to allow importing and exporting of electricity as necessary. In this study emphasis is given on the operational characterization of the system. The variational loads are considered from full to quarter load, and the micro-CHP system is optimized in terms of operating thermophysical parameters for every different load. The results clearly indicate the capability of the proposed system to perform efficiently throughout all necessary load changes to fulfill the residential load profile. The average net electrical efficiency and average total system efficiency are 0.380 and 0.815, respectively. However cost analysis shows that certain synergies are necessary to allow the proposed system to make an entry to the energy market as a possible candidate to replace heat pump-only equipped households.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arsalis, Alexandros","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Nielsen, Mads Pagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086619"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cost analysis","Heat pump","Micro combined heat and power","Polybenzimidazole","Proton exchange membrane fuel cell","System optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and optimization of a heat pump assisted high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell micro combined heat and power system for residential applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-086619","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000353755000051","type":"wos"},{"id":"84925354930","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7db78f7e-32dd-4c0e-b309-6bf244dd4380"],"keyword":["Cost analysis","Heat pump","Micro-combined-heat-and-power","Polybenzimidazole","Proton exchange membrane fuel cell","System optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-481231F620EDC0C96B05A703FC32BE54"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"arsalispau","last":"Arsalis","locid":"78eb1abb-bd28-461a-8c05-68a79cd90e77","name":"Arsalis, Alexandros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2015.03.031","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","pages":"569-581","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"147"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925354930"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7db78f7e-32dd-4c0e-b309-6bf244dd4380"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and optimization of a heat-pump-assisted high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell micro-combined-heat-and-power system for residential applications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086619","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This work investigates the system performance when reforming methanol in an oil heated reformer system for a 5 kW fuel cell system. A dynamic model of the system is created and evaluated. The system is divided into 4 separate components. These components are the fuel cell, reformer, burner and evaporator, which are connected by two separate oil circuits, one with a burner and reformer and one with a fuel cell and evaporator. Experiments were made on the reformer and measured oil and bed temperatures are presented in multiple working points. The system is examined at loads from 0 to 5000 W electric and the response time and efficiency of the system are evaluated. The efficiency is estimated to be around 28–30% during load. Startup of the system is estimated to be around 45 min.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113183"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dynamic model","HTPEM","Methanol","Reformer","Steam reforming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"system model development for a methanol reformed 000000000005 kw high temperature pem fuel cell system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-113183","identifier":[{"id":"84941183177","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000361778500017","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d9399763-019a-44e6-83f2-36410cb48bf7"],"keyword":["Dynamic model","HTPEM","Methanol","Reformer","Steam reforming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C64E56A911989B1F763526D650310B0E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2015.07.145","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"38","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"13080-13089","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941183177"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d9399763-019a-44e6-83f2-36410cb48bf7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"System model development for a methanol reformed 5 kW high temperature PEM fuel cell system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113183","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
