{"abstract":"We show that there exists a graph G with O(n) nodes, where any forest of n nodes is a node-induced subgraph of G. Furthermore, for constant arboricity k, the result implies the existence of a graph with O(nk) nodes that contains all n-node graphs as node-induced subgraphs, matching a Ω(nk) lower bound. The lower bound and previously best upper bounds were presented in Alstrup and Rauhe (FOCS'02). Our upper bounds are obtained through a log2 n + O(1) labeling scheme for adjacency queries in forests. We hereby solve an open problem being raised repeatedly over decades, e.g. in Kannan, Naor, Rudich (STOC 1988), Chung (J. of Graph Theory 1990), Fraigniaud and Korman (SODA 2010).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Alstrup, Stephen","Dahlgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443943"],"event":{"acronym":"FOCS","end":"2015-10-20","place":"Berkeley, California, us","start":"2015-10-18","title":"The Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimal induced universal graphs and adjacency labeling for trees","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1504.02306","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-443943","identifier":[{"id":"84959111631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-54927023-eb75-43d2-be96-40c0b696ecb6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C7E8B1B346447FA794180D715A6AD43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1504.02306","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The APL Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stephen","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"6d1b63fb-235a-4932-8345-413b4ac8d6a5","name":"Alstrup, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0001-7896-8386","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"4788aa93-be24-420b-8767-e735d6dcc61d","name":"Dahlgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2925-746X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"28c3a2af-0485-4bfb-83ba-e8a330c65b22","name":"Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","orcid":"0000-0001-5308-9609","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/focs.2015.84","issn":["15238288"],"pages":"1311-1326","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science. Annual Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2015 IEEE 56th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science (FOCS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959111631"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-54927023-eb75-43d2-be96-40c0b696ecb6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Optimal induced universal graphs and adjacency labeling for trees","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443943","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Diabetic retinopathy may be present at the time type 2 diabetes is diagnosed, and initial screening encompassing an eye examination performed by an ophthalmologist or optometrist is therefore recommended. However, proper screening for retinopathy may be challenging in many parts of the world. We hypothesized that simple, commonly available patient characteristics can be used to identify patients at high risk for having retinopathy. We investigated data from multiple years extracted from the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey which holds information about blood glucose and eye examinations. Individuals with hitherto undiagnosed diabetes were classified according to the presence or absence of retinopathy. Linear classification was used to predict which patients had retinopathy at the time of diagnosis. A total of 266 individuals with undiagnosed diabetes were identified from the cohorts. Of these, 222 individuals had no sign of retinopathy, whereas 44 had mild or moderate non-proliferative retinopathy. Using information regarding HbA1c, BMI, waist circumference, age, systolic blood pressure, urinary albumin, and urinary creatinine, we were able to construct a model that predicts the presence of retinopathy with a positive predictive value of 22% and a negative predictive value of 99%. Only one true positive (1/44) with mild non-proliferative retinopathy was falsely classified. A classification model using readily available patient information and routine biochemical measures can be used to identify patients at high risk of having retinopathy at the time their diabetes is diagnosed. The model may be used to identify high-risk patients for retinopathy screening.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cichosz, Simon Lebech","Johansen, Mette Dencker","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Hansen, Troels Krarup","Hejlesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-098.75-005013"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institut for Klinisk Medicin - Medicinsk Endokrinologisk afdeling MEA, NBG"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a classification model for predicting eye disease in newly diagnosed people with type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2015.02.020","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.75-005013","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000353215500006","type":"wos"},{"id":"25765665","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84927912795","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-678e8ff6-0142-447c-b71a-d1d99eac4f48","au-5c1782d0-4bdb-4403-a7ba-89c4e6746ec0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-063A2151FCDF751BEDD8970A02577AFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2015.02.020","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Medical Informatics Group (MIIA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut for Klinisk Medicin - Medicinsk Endokrinologisk afdeling MEA, NBG"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lebech","key":"cichoszpau","last":"Cichosz","locid":"347d3dc8-695e-47b3-8d97-c520cba30523","name":"Cichosz, Simon Lebech","orcid":"0000-0002-3484-7571","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Dencker","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"a5598dc9-1c14-4b31-bced-298c1a2ec63f","name":"Johansen, Mette Dencker","orcid":"0000-0001-7623-8312","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels Krarup","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4af39f3a-9bb3-4f30-8fee-29a550538de8","name":"Hansen, Troels Krarup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hejlesenpau","last":"Hejlesen","locid":"84d50796-bc01-486c-be4b-18ca00e97c7d","name":"Hejlesen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-3578-8750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25765665"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diabres.2015.02.020","issn":["01688227","15721671"],"issn_org":["01688227"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","pages":"210-5","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927912795"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-678e8ff6-0142-447c-b71a-d1d99eac4f48","au-5c1782d0-4bdb-4403-a7ba-89c4e6746ec0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A classification model for predicting eye disease in newly diagnosed people with type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.75-005013","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Several studies in different populations have suggested that nighttime blood pressure (BP) is a stronger predictor of cardiovascular events than daytime BP. Consequently, treatment strategies to target nighttime BP have come into focus. The aim of the present study was to investigate the effect of change of administration time of antihypertensive drugs. We included 41 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and nocturnal hypertension (nighttime systolic BP >120 mm Hg) in an open-label, crossover study. Patients were randomized to 8 weeks of either morning or bedtime administration of all of the individual's once-daily antihypertensive drugs, followed by 8 weeks of switched dosing regimen. Bedtime administration of antihypertensive drugs resulted in a significant reduction in nighttime (7.5 mm Hg; P<0.001) and 24-hour (3.1 mm Hg; P=0.014) systolic BP, with a nonsignificant reduction in daytime (1.3 mm Hg; P=0.336) systolic BP. We did not find morning BP surge to be different between dosing regimens. Levels of C-reactive protein were significantly lower with bedtime administration, which may indicate an effect on low-grade inflammation. We found no difference in urinary albumin excretion, regardless of albuminuria status. Urinary sodium/creatinine was significantly increased and urinary osmolality significantly reduced with bedtime administration, which can be interpreted as increased nocturnal natriuresis. In patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and nocturnal hypertension, administration of once-daily antihypertensive drugs at bedtime may be favorable. The increased nocturnal natriuresis may reflect increased effect of bedtime-administered thiazides and renin-angiotensin system inhibitors, suggesting a potential mechanism of the observed effects on BP with chronotherapeutic intervention.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rossen, Niklas B","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Fleischer, Jesper","Hvas, Anne-Mette","Ebbehøj, Eva","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","Hansen, Klavs Würgler"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-141394"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting nocturnal hypertension in type 000000000002 diabetes mellitus","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/HYPERTENSIONAHA.114.03958","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-141394","identifier":[{"id":"84922394408","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25259747","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-14d3c15c-7e1f-4a36-a0fb-3ec02050bd98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6603BBAC91F31816571965CFC08CD0D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/HYPERTENSIONAHA.114.03958","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afdeling, Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niklas Blach","key":"rossenpau","last":"Rossen","locid":"fde04f7b-b73f-42bb-8fed-7ced5a87b6fc","name":"Rossen, Niklas B","name_org":"Rossen, Niklas Blach","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"fleischerpau","last":"Fleischer","locid":"d05675bb-341e-4913-90d7-0277ad912141","name":"Fleischer, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne-Mette","key":"hvaspau","last":"Hvas","locid":"b4362b49-6deb-4c2c-9027-48dc6cdbd5e6","name":"Hvas, Anne-Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"ebbehøjpau","last":"Ebbehøj","locid":"771ecd1e-220d-410b-8c3e-b83b391fa1f3","name":"Ebbehøj, Eva","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Løgstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klavs Würgler","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2dc4053-a6dd-47ea-bfeb-e689b3b6fc94","name":"Hansen, Klavs Würgler","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25259747"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/hypertensionaha.114.03958","issn":["0194911X","15244563"],"issn_org":["0194911X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Hypertension","pages":"1080-7","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Hypertension","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84922394408"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-14d3c15c-7e1f-4a36-a0fb-3ec02050bd98"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Targeting nocturnal hypertension in type 2 diabetes mellitus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-141394","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The effect of a current commercial xylanase (DAN) and experimental xylanase (EX), and EX in combination with protease (EXP), on the degradation and apparent ileal digestibility (AID) of non-starch polysaccharides (NSP) in wheat Distillers Dried Grains with Solubles (DDGS), was studied in 8 ileum-cannulated pigs (initial BW 36.6±2.8 kg) following a double 4x4 Latin Square design. The control and three enzyme diets, each containing 96% DDGS, were supplemented with vitamins, minerals, L-lysine, 500 FTU phytase/kg feed, dust-binder and chromic oxide (3 g/kg). The pigs were fed 3 times daily for 1 week and ileal content collected for 8 h on day 5 and 7. For each pig, weekly samples were pooled and analyzed for composition of total- and soluble NSP, total non-digestible carbohydrates (NDC) and marker. Low molecular weight (LMW)-NDC was determined as the difference between NDC and NSP concentration. Data were analyzed with enzyme treatment and week as fixed effects, and pig as random effect. Enzyme treatments were compared to the control treatment, and considered statistically significant at P<0.05. Enzyme addition overall increased AID of total NSP (P=0.024) with an AID of 25 % for control to 32 % with DAN (P=0.02) and 31 % with EXP (P=0.03). Enzyme addition overall increased AID of high molecular weight arabinoxylan (P<0.001) from 31 % for control to 41 % with DAN (P=0.0001), 40 % with EXP (P=0.0006), and 39 % with EX (P=0.0021). Enzyme addition also increased the concentration of LMW-NDC (P=0.005) in ileal content from 6.4 % in control to 8.6 % for DAN (P=0.0026) and to 8.3 % for EXP (P=0.0084), and the content of LMW-arabinoxylan (P<0.0001) from 5.0 % in control to 7.0 % for DAN (P=0.0001), 6.8 % for EXP (P=0.0003), and 6.2 % for EX (P=0.0129). Collectively, the results suggest that exogenous enzymes increase the degradation of NSP and arabinoxylan in wheat DDGS, with ranking of DAN > EXP > EX. Keywords: DDGS, non-starch polysaccharide digestibility, xylanase","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","Dalsgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Yu, S","Lærke, Helle Nygaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244372"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"xylanases increase the ileal digestibility of non starch polysaccharides in pigs fed wheat ddgs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3920/978-90-8686-799-8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244372","ids":["au-c965ee82-dbf3-4921-8e14-d6266f0f43d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7FDADF403CB01AC52ADF1C6D4AA20283"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3920/978-90-8686-799-8","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://wageningenacademic.metapress.com/content/u33362/?genre=issue&id=doi%3a10.3920%2f978-90-8686-799-8#.VC6a0RZBEs0","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Brøgger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4fbc8c90-2c05-4233-a45a-b80c6cbab818","name":"Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik Bach","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3918454e-241b-4712-ab7f-aa9d26a508f7","name":"Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"408fb476-f1b2-4eb6-8436-edc3cc039743","name":"Lærke, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0303-0745","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3920/978-90-8686-799-8","issn":["13826077"],"journal":"EAAP Book of Abstracts","pages":"174-174","publisher":"Wageningen Academic Publishers","status":"p","title":"EAAP Book of Abstracts","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c965ee82-dbf3-4921-8e14-d6266f0f43d4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Xylanases increase the ileal digestibility of non-starch polysaccharides in pigs fed wheat DDGS","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244372","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background: Salmonellae are food-borne pathogens of great health and economic importance. To pose a threat to humans, Salmonellae normally have to cope with a series of stressful conditions in the food chain, including low temperature. In the current study, we evaluated the importance of the Clp proteolytic complex and the carbon starvation protein, CsrA, for the ability of Salmonella Typhimurium to grow at low temperature. Results: A clpP mutant was severely affected in growth and formed pin point colonies at 10 degrees C. Contrary to this, rpoS and clpP/rpoS mutants were only slightly affected. The clpP mutant formed cold resistant suppressor mutants at a frequency of 2.5 x 10(-3) and these were found not to express RpoS. Together these results indicated that the impaired growth of the clpP mutant was caused by high level of RpoS. Evaluation by microscopy of the clpP mutant revealed that it formed filamentous cells when grown at 10 degrees C, and this phenotype too, disappered when rpoS was mutated in parallel indicating a RpoS-dependency. A csrA (sup) mutant was also growth attenuated a low temperature. An rpoS/csrA (sup) double mutant was also growth attenuated, indicating that the phenotype of the csrA mutant was independent from RpoS. Conclusions: The cold sensitivity of clpP mutant was associated with increased levels of RpoS and probably caused by toxic levels of RpoS. Although a csrA mutant also accumulated high level of RpoS, growth impairment caused by lack of csrA was not related to RpoS levels in a similar way.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Gitte Maegaard","Nielsen, Maj-Britt","Thomsen, Line Elnif","Aabo, Søren","Rychlik, Ivan","Olsen, John Elmerdahl"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033018"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Czech Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Czech Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Cell Size","ClpP","Cold adaptation","CsrA","Escherichia coli","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","GENES","Global regulation","Microbiology","RpoS","Salmonella","Staphylococcus aureus","Stress","Stress response","Virulence","cold resistance","small RNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Division of Industrial Food Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of clpp rpos and csra in growth and filament formation of i salmonella enterica i serovar typhimurium at low temperature","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/100293729/s12866_014_0208_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-033018","identifier":[{"id":"25123657","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84906926453","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4236599","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-14226e02-b1a0-45c5-b644-a99e572fca0c","ku-7bab12d9-1608-4ecf-beef-8aa9393ab12b"],"keyword":["CELL-SIZE","COLD-SHOCK RESPONSE","ClpP","Cold adaptation","CsrA","ESCHERICHIA-COLI","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","GENES","GLOBAL REGULATION","MICROBIOLOGY","PROTEIN CSRA","RpoS","SMALL RNA","STAPHYLOCOCCUS-AUREUS","STRESS-RESPONSE","Salmonella","Stress","VIRULENCE","cold resistance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6288E5A27505760F7D730258D08F8614"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/100293729/s12866_014_0208_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12866-014-0208-4","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/126010998/s12866_014_0208_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-2180/14/208","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Bacterial Ecophysiology and Biotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Division of Industrial Food Research"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center, Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cz","key":"czech academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Czech Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cz","key":"czech academy of sciences","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Czech Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte Maegaard","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"bb84b997-02d1-4569-be9c-278ebb453bf3"