lace":"København","publisher":"FADL's Forlag","status":"p","title":"Fysisk helbred bland psykisk syge"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-551b555a-5e14-49d1-a74f-77be0c13b841"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Diabetes mellitus og andre endokrinologisk sygdomme","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177861","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Diabetic retinopathy is one of the leading causes of blindness in the Western world. The disease is characterized by morphological lesions secondary to disturbances in retinal blood flow assumed to be related to disturbances in retinal autoregulation. However, there is a need for elucidating the relation between disturbances in diameter regulation of retinal vessels and the development of diabetic retinopathy in longitudinal studies. METHODS: Sixty-four patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus were subjected to measurement of pressure autoregulation of retinal arterioles using the Dynamic Vessel Analyzer (DVA) and measurement of retinal thickness using OCT scanning, and after a mean of 6.8 years, 42 of the patients were re-examined. The vascular response was compared in patients in whom retinopathy had disappeared, was unchanged, or had worsened. RESULTS: At baseline, hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) was significantly higher in the patients who would later experience worsening of diabetic retinopathy than in the other groups, but had been reduced at the follow-up examination. During the follow-up period, the resting diameter of retinal arterioles decreased significantly in the patients who experienced improvement in diabetic retinopathy but was unchanged in the other groups, whereas both the diameter response of retinal arterioles to isometric exercise and retinal thickness increased non-significantly with worsening of retinopathy. CONCLUSIONS: The development of diabetic retinopathy is related to the diameter of retinal arterioles. Future clinical intervention studies should aim at investigating the effects of normalizing arteriolar diameters in diabetic retinopathy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Petersen, Line","Jeppesen, Peter","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","Bek, Toke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-208762"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improvement of mild retinopathy in type 000000000002 diabetic patients correlates with narrowing of retinal arterioles a prospective observational study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00417-014-2614-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-208762","identifier":[{"id":"24687143","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84897120032","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8b3b6903-9c98-4609-98d1-efd3a48ee0eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CEEBD62469188B204801C951B1EB647E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00417-014-2614-6","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"acb1084c-d77c-4f15-a106-e12d03f13ab2","name":"Petersen, Line","name_org":"Pedersen, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"efd0c182-11f8-427d-a911-c2a06e14c261","name":"Jeppesen, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Løgstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24687143"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00417-014-2614-6","issn":["0721832X","1435702X"],"issn_org":["0721832X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Graefe's Archive for Clinical and Experimental Ophthalmology","pages":"1561-7","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Graefe's Archive for Clinical and Experimental Ophthalmology","volume":"252"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897120032"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b3b6903-9c98-4609-98d1-efd3a48ee0eb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Improvement of mild retinopathy in type 2 diabetic patients correlates with narrowing of retinal arterioles. A prospective observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-208762","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Bioremediation of pesticide-polluted soil may be more efficient using mixed fungal–bacterial cultures rather than the individual strains alone. This may be due to cooperative catabolism, where the first organism transforms the pollutant to products which are then used by the second organism. In addition, fungal hyphae may function as transport vectors for bacteria, thereby facilitating a more effective spreading of degrader organisms in the soil. A more rapid mineralization of the phenylurea herbicide diuron was found in sand with added microbial consortia consisting of both degrading bacteria and fungi. Facilitated transport of bacteria by fungal hyphae was demonstrated using a system where herbicide-spiked sand was separated from the consortium by a layer of sterile glass beads. Several fungal–bacterial consortia were investigated by combining different diuron-degrading bacteria (Sphingomonas sp. SRS2, Variovorax sp. SRS16, and Arthrobacter globiformis D47) and fungi (Mortierella sp. LEJ702 and LEJ703). The fastest mineralization of 14C-labeled diuron was seen in the consortium consisting of Mortierella LEJ702, Variovorax SRS16, and A. globiformis D47, as measured by evolved 14CO2. In addition, the production of diuron metabolites by this consortium was minimal. Analyses of 16S rDNA suggested that bacteria were transported more efficiently by LEJ702 than by LEJ703. Finally, it was determined that the fungal growth differed for LEJ702 and LEJ703 in the three-member consortia. This study demonstrates new possibilities for applying efficient fungal–bacterial consortia for bioremediation of polluted soil.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","Knudsen, Berith Elkær","Johansen, Anders","Albers, Christian Nyrop","Aamand, Jens","Rosendahl, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-028061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea"],"keyword":["Biodegradation","Fungal highway","Microbial consortia","Pesticide","Phenylurea herbicide","Synergistic interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fungal bacterial consortia increase diuron degradation in water unsaturated systems","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2013.07.095","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-028061","identifier":[{"id":"23973535","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84882980031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d4b8483b-9025-4bbf-b552-8c6cbb35990b","ku-e8531525-1541-4735-b962-97d2ecc81b93"],"keyword":["Biodegradation","Fungal highway","Microbial consortia","Pesticide","Phenylurea herbicide","Synergistic interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-93842B792C578BC1D7E0CA7A58109870"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2013.07.095","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0048969713008772","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lea","key":"ellegaardjensenpau","last":"Ellegaard-Jensen","locid":"3a2e1d17-58b6-412f-b224-a5a0bf5aebe8","name":"Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Berith Elkær","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Berith Elkær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"a321bf32-5b17-4273-866a-cf276147b4f0","name":"Johansen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5893-6165","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian Nyrop","key":"alberspau","last":"Albers","name":"Albers, Christian Nyrop","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","locid":"25b0aa8d-b223-4ae0-ab6f-26d47230e97d","name":"Rosendahl, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-5202-6585","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23973535"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2013.07.095","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"699-705","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"466-467"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882980031"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d4b8483b-9025-4bbf-b552-8c6cbb35990b","ku-e8531525-1541-4735-b962-97d2ecc81b93"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fungal-bacterial consortia increase diuron degradation in water-unsaturated systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-028061","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cells are getting growing interest in both backup systems and electric vehicles. Although these systems are characterized by long periods of inactivity, they must be able to start at any instant in the shortest time. However, the membrane of which PEMFCs are made tends to dry out when not in use. This increases the time required to start the system and could lead to the destruction of the fuel cell. In this article an impedance measurement circuit is presented, which is part of a humidity status estimator for monitoring the humidity status of a fuel cell stack during standby. The impedance measurement circuit has been connected to a fuel cell stack and the operation of estimating the relative humidity has been demonstrated.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bidoggia, Benoit","Rugholt, Mark","Nielsen, Morten Busk","Jensen, Mathias","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056078"],"event":{"end":"2014-03-27","place":"Monte Carlo, mc","start":"2014-03-25","title":"9th International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies, EVER 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Distributed power generation","Fuel cells","Humidity measurement","Impedance","Uninterruptible power systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of membrane hydration status for standby proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems by impedance measurement first impedance measurement circuit","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVER.2014.6844152","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-056078","identifier":[{"id":"84904490803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-14a7505c-94b5-4bfd-8037-4ddc586875bd"],"keyword":["Distributed power generation","Fuel cells","Humidity measurement","Impedance","Uninterruptible power systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99FCB1F81C21E040C11E202E84937729"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVER.2014.6844152","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84904490803&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benoit","key":"bidoggiapau","last":"Bidoggia","locid":"132f2659-f4a2-4324-8b4e-88cec8230dea","name":"Bidoggia, Benoit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"rugholtpau","last":"Rugholt","locid":"cfbf3ed3-4f17-4185-90e4-b91e9359f23a","name":"Rugholt, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Busk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"07d272d7-4a08-4466-9522-73fbcc244f71","name":"Nielsen, Morten Busk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9e1fbbea-aa6b-4725-8813-49a6e462943e","name":"Jensen, Mathias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ever.2014.6844152","isbn":["9781479937868"],"pages":"1-7","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies, EVER 2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904490803"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-14a7505c-94b5-4bfd-8037-4ddc586875bd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of membrane hydration status for standby proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems by impedance measurement : First impedance measurement circuit","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056078","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"There are currently many different lithium ion chemistries available on the market and several new players are in the research and development process; however, none of them is superior to the other chemistries in all the aspects. Relatively low price, long cycle and calendar lifetime, and intrinsic safety of the nanophosphate LiFePO4/C lithium ion chemistry make it possible to consider this chemistry for electric vehicle applications. This paper investigates the lifetime of the nanophosphate LiFePO4/C battery chemistry when it is used for full electrical vehicles. The investigation is performed considering a semi-empirical calendar and cycle lifetime model, which was developed based on extended accelerated lifetime tests. Both capacity and power capability degradations during calendar and cycle life ageing are considered and quantified. Finally, the developed battery cell lifetime model is used to study the capacity and power capability degradation behaviour of the tested nanophosphate LiFePO4/C battery for two electric vehicle operational scenarios.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Stroe, Ana-Irina","Teodorescu, Remus","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080264"],"event":{"end":"2014-03-27","place":"Monte Carlo, mc","start":"2014-03-25","title":"9th International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies, EVER 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Capacity fade","Electrical vehicle","Lifetime modelling","Lithium iron phosphate","Power degradation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"suitability of the nanophosphate lifepo000000000004 c battery chemistry for the fully electric vehicle lifetime perspective","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVER.2014.6844119","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-080264","identifier":[{"id":"84904497748","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-67ef29d5-c746-4549-8be0-442317dde911"],"keyword":["Capacity fade","Electrical vehicle","Lifetime modelling","Lithium iron phosphate","Power degradation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5755CC90B2EC73880AC19FC1FDF91A06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVER.2014.6844119","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jozef","key":"swierczynskipau","last":"Swierczynski","locid":"767958b2-8061-4038-82d6-7a0068c26efe","name":"Swierczynski, Maciej Jozef","orcid":"0000-0003-3837-9696","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Ioan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","name_org":"Stroe, Daniel Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ana-Irina","key":"stanpau","last":"Stan","locid":"e6ff6bac-362f-4fd1-b46c-d5f62d1e2c1a","name":"Stroe, Ana-Irina","name_org":"Stan, Ana-Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-8254","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescupau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ever.2014.6844119","eisbn":["9781479937868"],"isbn":["9781479937882"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Conference on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies, EVER 2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904497748"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-67ef29d5-c746-4549-8be0-442317dde911"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Suitability of the Nanophosphate LiFePO4/C Battery Chemistry for the Fully Electric Vehicle : Lifetime Perspective","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080264","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This work presents the proof-of-concept of an electric traction power system with a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell range extender, usable for automotive class electrical vehicles. The hybrid system concept examined, consists of a power system where the primary power is delivered by a lithium ion battery pack. In order to increase the run time of the application connected to this battery pack, a high temperature PEM (HTPEM) fuel cell stack acts as an on-board charger able to charge a vehicle during operation as a series hybrid. Because of the high tolerance to carbon monoxide, the HTPEM fuel cell system can efficiently use a liquid methanol/water mixture of 60%/40% by volume, as fuel instead of compressed hydrogen, enabling potentially a higher volumetric energy density. In order to test the performance of such a system, the experimental validation conducted uses a down-sized version of the battery pack used in the Mitsubishi iMiEV, which is subjected to power cycles derived from simulations of the vehicle undergoing multiple New European Drive Cycles (NEDC).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Ashworth, Leanne","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094940"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Drive cycle","Fuel cell system","Methanol reforming","PEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"test of hybrid power system for electrical vehicles using a lithium ion battery pack and a reformed methanol fuel cell range extender","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360319913027936%23","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094940","identifier":[{"id":"84891826181","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000331420900024","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-9ad1b9d1-a1dc-48c4-a69c-c2d3192883b5"],"keyword":["Drive cycle","Fuel cell system","Hybrid electrical vehicle","Methanol reforming","PEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9EF37C44EDAB60A598FF21C0FC6ADEE9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SerEnergy"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leanne","key":"ashworthpau","last":"Ashworth","name":"Ashworth, Leanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Christian Becker","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"372be06d-7f4f-4025-86a1-75eb41ce5af8","name":"Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2013.11.068","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"1856-1863","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891826181"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","serenergy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9ad1b9d1-a1dc-48c4-a69c-c2d3192883b5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Test of hybrid power system for electrical vehicles using a lithium-ion battery pack and a reformed methanol fuel cell range extender","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094940","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this paper six High Temperature PEM (HTPEM) MEAs from two manufacturers have been tested. The MEAs are three Dapozol 77 from Danish Power Systems (DPS) with varying electrode composition and two Celtec P2100 and one Celtec P1000 from BASF. The break in process of the MEAs has been monitored using voltage measurements and impedance spectroscopy. The purpose of this study is twofold. One aim is to try and interpret the processes happening during break in. The other aim is to investigate whether the impedance spectra or the voltage profiles contain information that can be used to determine when an MEA has been broken in. To aid in the interpretation of the impedance spectra, equivalent circuit models are used. Three models are evaluated. The most detailed models produce the best fits but the most simple model is chosen, since it produces the most consistent results. The processes happening during break in cannot be determined with certainty but for the Celtec P MEAs the main changes seem to be related to improved electrode kinetics. Judging from the voltage and the fitted resistances, the Celtec P MEAs seem to have been broken in after 30 h. The Dapozol MEAs only undergo minor changes in impedance and voltage during the break in period. This may indicate that this MEA type can be used directly without the need for break in.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107077"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Break in","Equivalent circuit model","High temperature PEM fuel cell","Impedance spectroscopy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative study of the break in process of post doped and sol gel high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/204105516/comparative_study_of_the_break_in_process_of_post_doped_and_sol_gel.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-107077","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000341897500051","type":"wos"},{"id":"84906778712","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c48798c5-07b0-4004-865d-56880b2da65d"],"keyword":["Break in","Celtec","Dapozol","Equivalent circuit model","High temperature PEM fuel cell","Impedance spectroscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9DA498ED315C48232BDFB196E303AD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/204105516/comparative_study_of_the_break_in_process_of_post_doped_and_sol_gel.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2014.07.017","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"27","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"14959-14968","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84906778712"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c48798c5-07b0-4004-865d-56880b2da65d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparative study of the break in process of post doped and sol–gel high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107077","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a novel energy management strategy (EMS) to control an isolated microgrid powered by a photovoltaic array and a wind turbine and equipped with two different energy storage systems: electric batteries and a hydrogen production and storage system. In particular, an optimal scheduling of storage devices is carried out to maximize the benefits of available renewable resources by operating the photovoltaic systems and the wind turbine at their maximum power points and by minimizing the overall utilization costs. Unlike conventional EMS based on the state-of-charge (SOC) of batteries, the proposed EMS takes into account the uncertainty due to the intermittent nature of renewable resources and electricity demand. In particular, the uncertainties are evaluated with a stochastic approach through the construction of different scenarios with corresponding probabilities. The EMS is defined by minimizing the utilization costs of the energy storage equipment. The weather conditions recorded in four different weeks between April and December are used as case studies to test the proposed EMS and the results obtained are compared with a conventional EMS based on the state-of-charge of batteries. The results show a reduction of utilization costs of about 15% in comparison to conventional SOC-based EMS and an increase of the average energy storage efficiency.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cau, Giorgo","Cocco, Daniele","Petrollese, Mario","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Milan, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116029"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cagliari"],"keyword":["Energy management strategy","Photovoltaic systems","Wind turbine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy management strategy based on short term generation scheduling for a renewable microgrid using a hydrogen storage system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-116029","identifier":[{"id":"84907347052","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000343337200083","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-e2f4823a-482d-4e5f-846e-f90bf2f99f4c"],"keyword":["Energy management strategy","Hydrogen storage system","Photovoltaic systems","Stand-alone power system","Wind turbine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF26414D1A81AC54A7AEADEC84EFEB57"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of cagliari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cagliari","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giorgo","key":"caupau","last":"Cau","name":"Cau, Giorgo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"coccopau","last":"Cocco","name":"Cocco, Daniele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"petrollesepau","last":"Petrollese","name":"Petrollese, Mario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b7