{"abstract":"Pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A) and PAPP-A2, two homologous metzincin metalloproteases, are both tightly linked to regulation within the insulin-like growth factor (IGF) system because of their specific cleavage of IGF binding proteins. Recent studies suggest that PAPP-A may be involved in clinical conditions related to unwanted cellular growth, and the circulating levels of PAPP-A is an established biomarker in prenatal screening for chromosomal abnormalities. Microarray data indicate that PAPP-A2 has potential as a biomarker for pre-eclampsia. However, well-characterized immunological methods of quantification are not available. We therefore developed monoclonal antibodies against recombinant PAPP-A2. The antibodies were epitope mapped against recombinantly expressed chimeras between PAPP-A2 and PAPP-A. Furthermore, circulating PAPP-A2 was immunoaffinity purified and characterized by sequence analysis and mass spectrometry. Unlike PAPP-A, PAPP-A2 is a noncovalent dimer in which each subunit of 1558 amino acids originates from all of the 22 predicted coding exons. A previously hypothesized variant (PAPP-E) does not exist, but low amounts of a C-terminally truncated PAPP-A2 variant was detected. A sensitive and robust ELISA for full-length PAPP-A2 was developed and used to establish normal ranges of PAPP-A2 through pregnancy. The functional sensitivity of this ELISA at 20% CV was 0.08 ng/ml, and the serum concentration of PAPP-A2 was found to increase during pregnancy in agreement with placental synthesis. The existence of this assay will enable an assessment of the biomarker potential of PAPP-A2 in pre-eclampsia as well as other clinical conditions.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kløverpris, Søren","Gaidamauskas, Ervinas","Rasmussen, L C V","Overgaard, Michael Toft","Kronborg, C","Knudsen, U B","Christiansen, M","Kumar, A","Oxvig, C"],"cuid":["S03-098.68-741414"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Oxvig, Claus"],"keyword":["Biomarker","ELISA","PAPP A2","Pappalysin 2","Pregnancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Institut for Molekylærbiologi og Genetik - Molekylær intervention"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robust immunoassay for pregnancy associated plasma protein a000000000002 based on analysis of circulating antigen establishment of normal ranges in pregnancy","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molehr/gat047","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.68-741414","identifier":[{"id":"000326745700007","type":"wos"},{"id":"23804707","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84887013308","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6bab4491-0e5d-4ac6-b34a-861967fb3296","au-7742abcc-1696-4631-b6c4-c57af6d89278","au-b21b9e24-aeaf-4ec3-bff1-d494b411b2be"],"keyword":["ELISA","PAPP-A2","biomarker","pappalysin-2","pregnancy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-7C3E08CAFA5DEFE4497C34E1D749419E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molehr/gat047","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Gene