Molecular Human Reproduction","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887013308"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Undetermined","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6bab4491-0e5d-4ac6-b34a-861967fb3296","au-7742abcc-1696-4631-b6c4-c57af6d89278","au-b21b9e24-aeaf-4ec3-bff1-d494b411b2be"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A robust immunoassay for pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A2 based on analysis of circulating antigen : Establishment of normal ranges in pregnancy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.68-741414","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This work presents a control strategy for controlling the methanol reformer temperature of a 350 W high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell system, by using a cascade control structure for reliable system operation. The primary states affecting the methanol catalyst bed temperature is the water and methanol mixture fuel flow and the burner fuel/air ratio and combined flow. An experimental setup is presented capable of testing the methanol reformer used in the Serenergy H3 350 Mobile Battery Charger; a high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane (HTPEM) fuel cell system. The experimental system consists of a fuel evaporator utilizing the high temperature waste gas from the cathode air cooled 45 cell HTPEM fuel cell stack. The fuel cells used are BASF P1000 MEAs which use phosphoric acid doped polybenzimidazole membranes. The resulting reformate gas output of the reformer system is shown at different reformer temperatures and fuel flows, using the implemented reformer control strategy. The gas quality of the output reformate gas is of HTPEM grade quality, and sufficient for supporting efficient and reliable HTPEM fuel cell operation with CO concentrations of around 1% at the nominal reformer operating temperatures. As expected increasing temperatures also increase the dry gas CO content of the reformate gas and decreases the methanol slip. The hydrogen content of the gas was measured at around 73% with 25% CO2.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Sahlin, Simon Lennart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-083113"],"event":{"end":"2011-12-05","place":"Xcaret, mx","start":"2011-12-01","title":"Zing Hydrogen and Fuel Cell Conference 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["PEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"control and experimental characterization of a methanol reformer for a 000000000350 w high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72602342/IJHE_Control_and_experimental_characterization_of_a_methanol_personal_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-083113","identifier":[{"id":"84872317887","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000315430600052","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-71acc511-0889-4428-99d8-06c398234720"],"keyword":["PEM","brændselceller","metanol reformering","styring og regulering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD388793DA9CCAA4297B7D15C9769830"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72602342/IJHE_Control_and_experimental_characterization_of_a_methanol_personal_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2012.09.032","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2012.09.032","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"1676-1684","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872317887"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-71acc511-0889-4428-99d8-06c398234720"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Control and experimental characterization of a methanol reformer for a 350 W high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083113","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A proposed residential energy system based on the PBI (Polybenzimidazole) fuel cell technology is analyzed in terms of operational performance. Conventional operational strategies, such as heat-led and electricity-led, are applied to the simulated system to investigate their performance characteristics. Based on these findings, an improved operational strategy is formulated and applied in an attempt to minimize the shortcomings of conventional strategies. System parameters, such as electrical and thermal efficiencies, heat dumping, and import/export of electricity, are analyzed. The applied load profile is based on average data for a single-family household in Denmark and includes consumption data for electricity and heat demands. The study analyzes the potential of the proposed system on market penetration in the area of residential heat-and-power generation and whether this deployment can be justified as compared to other micro-CHP system technologies. The most important findings of this research study indicate that in comparison to non-fuel cell-based micro-CHP systems, such as Stirling Engine-based systems, the proposed system has significantly higher efficiencies. Moreover, the lower heat-to-power ratios allow the system to avoid high thermal surpluses throughout the whole annual operational profile.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arsalis, Alexandros","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121884"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"application of an improved operational strategy for a high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell based micro combined heat and power system for danish single family households","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.07.025","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121884","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000314191100081","type":"wos"},{"id":"84866527442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f7294126-7389-4801-b0d3-3b625d7715e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F67C81C5E6ACB9418F1AA3A6C9921F8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1359431112005078#","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.07.025","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"arsalispau","last":"Arsalis","locid":"78eb1abb-bd28-461a-8c05-68a79cd90e77","name":"Arsalis, Alexandros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.07.025","issn":["13594311"],"issue":"1","journal":"Applied Thermal Engineering","pages":"704-713","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Thermal Engineering","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866527442"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f7294126-7389-4801-b0d3-3b625d7715e1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Application of an improved operational strategy for a high temperature-proton exchange membrane fuel cell-based micro-combined heat and power system for Danish single-family households","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121884","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Diabetic retinopathy is accompanied by disturbances in retinal blood flow, which is assumed to be related to the diabetic metabolic dysregulation. It has previously been shown that normoinsulinemic hyperglycemia has no effect on the diameter of retinal arterioles at rest and during an increase in the arterial blood pressure induced by isometric exercise. However, the influence of hyperinsulinemia on this response has not been studied in detail. In seven normal persons, the diameter response of retinal arterioles to an increased blood pressure induced by isometric exercise, to stimulation with flickering light, and to the combination of these stimuli was studied during euglycemic normoinsulinemia (protocol N) on one examination day, and euglycemic hyperinsulinemia (protocol H) on another examination day. Isometric exercise induced significant contraction of retinal arterioles at all examinations, but during a repeated examination the diameter response was significantly reduced in the test persons following the N protocol and increased in the persons following the H protocol. Flicker stimulation induced a significant dilatation of retinal arterioles at all examinations, and the response was significantly higher during a repeated examination, irrespective of the insulin level. Repeated exposure to isometric exercise reduces contraction, whereas repeated exposure to flickering light increases dilatation of retinal arterioles in vivo. Hyperinsulinemia increases contraction of retinal arterioles induced by isometric exercise.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Peter","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","Hessellund, Anders","Schmitz, Ole","Bek, Toke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-226639"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acute hyperinsulinemia increases the contraction of retinal arterioles induced by elevated blood pressure","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpheart.00560.2013","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-226639","identifier":[{"id":"84888869867","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24056905","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-aa97fca7-c93b-4e4a-ac4e-f2aae0faa436"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5B23944BC40EFA82E8DB116121F5A81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpheart.00560.2013","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"efd0c182-11f8-427d-a911-c2a06e14c261","name":"Jeppesen, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Løgstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"hessellundpau","last":"Hessellund","locid":"be5b9d95-12a0-483d-b066-c258eeee0356","name":"Hessellund, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"schmitzpau","last":"Schmitz","locid":"41fa79be-b138-48f3-82fb-7c754220e6e5","name":"Schmitz, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24056905"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpheart.00560.2013","issn":["03636135","15221539"],"issn_org":["15221539"],"issue":"11","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Heart and Circulatory Physiology","publisher":"American Physiological Society","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Heart and Circulatory Physiology","title_org":"A J P: Heart and Circulatory Physiology (Online)","volume":"305"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84888869867"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aa97fca7-c93b-4e4a-ac4e-f2aae0faa436"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Acute hyperinsulinemia increases the contraction of retinal arterioles induced by elevated blood pressure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-226639","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Mikkel Rønne","Haile, Yonas Sahlemariam","Knudsen, Søren","Hornbæk, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418785"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"information visualization and proxemics design opportunities and empirical findings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-418785","identifier":[{"id":"84886709754","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24051805","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2a80690c-14eb-4c16-8139-986e6556803c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22BFE2FF42546C0B0483861948A09693"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Rønne","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"7cde66fc-02bc-4849-a559-b3429b2b36b0","name":"Jakobsen, Mikkel Rønne","orcid":"0000-0001-6494-9037","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yonas Sahlemariam","key":"hailepau","last":"Haile","name":"Haile, Yonas Sahlemariam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"60aa66e8-eac5-4487-94e1-f1379643b27d","name":"Knudsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8306-1102","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"hornbækpau","last":"Hornbæk","locid":"148d1e88-e306-46e1-9218-f420470b1ce1","name":"Hornbæk, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0001-8742-1198","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24051805"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tvcg.2013.166","issn":["10772626","19410506"],"issn_org":["10772626"],"issue":"12","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics","pages":"2386-2395","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886709754"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2a80690c-14eb-4c16-8139-986e6556803c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Information visualization and proxemics : design opportunities and empirical findings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418785","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Introduction of specific degrading microorganisms into polluted soil or aquifers is a promising remediation technology provided that the organisms survive and spread in the environment. We suggest that consortia, rather than single strains, may be better suited to overcome these challenges. Here we introduced a fungal–bacterial consortium consisting of Mortierella sp. LEJ702 and the 2,6-dichlorobenzamide (BAM)-degrading Aminobacter sp. MSH1 into small sand columns. A more rapid mineralisation of BAM was obtained by the consortium compared to MSH1 alone especially at lower moisture contents. Results from quantitative real-time polymerase chain reaction (qPCR) demonstrated better spreading of Aminobacter when Mortierella was present suggesting that fungal hyphae may stimulate bacterial dispersal. Extraction and analysis of BAM indicated that translocation of the compound was also affected by the fungal hyphae in the sand. This suggests that fungal–bacterial consortia are promising for successful bioremediation of pesticide contamination.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Knudsen, Berith Elkær","Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","Albers, Christian Nyrop","Rosendahl, Søren","Aamand, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525926"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["2 6 Dichlorobenzamide BAM","Consortium"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fungal hyphae stimulate bacterial degradation of 000000000002 000000000006 dichlorobenzamide bam","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2013.06.013","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-525926","identifier":[{"id":"84880272614","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ddd3168c-6358-4736-9454-6d8beef54f46"],"keyword":["2,6-dichlorobenzamide (BAM)","Bacterial dispersal","Consortium","Fungal–bacterial interactions","Pesticide biodegradation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E6D84D055AD9FE0E5C305AFACC0E942"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0269749113003308","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2013.06.013","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Berith Elkær","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"c15dabdc-a4f1-4084-a458-8034af5762c5","name":"Knudsen, Berith Elkær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lea","key":"ellegaardjensenpau","last":"Ellegaard-Jensen","locid":"3a2e1d17-58b6-412f-b224-a5a0bf5aebe8","name":"Ellegaard-Jensen, Lea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian Nyrop","key":"alberspau","last":"Albers","name":"Albers, Christian Nyrop","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","locid":"25b0aa8d-b223-4ae0-ab6f-26d47230e97d","name":"Rosendahl, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-5202-6585","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envpol.2013.06.013","issn":["02697491","18736424"],"issn_org":["02697491"],"journal":"Environmental Pollution","pages":"122-127","status":"p","title":"Environmental Pollution","volume":"181"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880272614"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ddd3168c-6358-4736-9454-6d8beef54f46"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fungal hyphae stimulate bacterial degradation of 2,6-dichlorobenzamide (BAM)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-525926","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In comparison to the technology platforms developed to localize transcripts and proteins, imaging tools for visualization of metabolite distributions in plant tissues are less well developed and lack versatility. This hampers our understanding of plant metabolism and dynamics. In this study we demonstrate that Desorption Electrospray Ionization Mass Spectrometry Imaging (DESI-MSI) of tissue imprints on porous Teflon can be used to accurately image the distribution of even labile plant metabolites such as hydroxynitrile glucosides, which normally undergo enzymatic hydrolysis by specific ß-glucosidases upon cell disruption. This fast and simple sample preparation resulted in no substantial differences in the distribution and ratios of all hydroxynitrile glucosides between leaves from wildtype Lotus japonicus and a ß-glucosidase mutant plant lacking the ability to hydrolyze certain hydroxynitrile glucosides. In wildtype, the enzymatic conversion of hydroxynitrile glucosides and the concomitant release of glucose was easily visualized when a restricted area of the leaf tissue was damaged prior to sample preparation. The gene encoding the first enzyme in hydroxynitrile glucoside biosynthesis in L. japonicus leaves, CYP79D3, was found to be highly expressed during the early stages of leaf development, and the hydroxynitrile glucoside distribution in mature leaves reflected this early expression pattern. Direct DESI-MSI of plant tissue was demonstrated using cryo-sections of cassava (Manihot esculenta) tubers. The hydroxynitrile glucoside levels were highest in the outer cell layers, as verified by LC-MS analyses. The unexpected discovery of a hydroxynitrile derived di-glycoside shows the potential of DESI-MSI to discover and guide investigations into new metabolic routes. © 2013 The Authors. The Plant Journal © 2013 Blackwell Publishing Ltd.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Li, Bin","Knudsen, Camilla","Hansen, Natascha Kristine Krahl","Jørgensen, Kirsten","Kannangara, Rubini Maya","Bak, Søren","Takos, Adam Matthew","Rook, Frederik","Hansen, Steen Honoré","Møller, Birger Lindberg","Janfelt, Christian","Bjarnholt, Nanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528077"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visualizing metabolite distribution and enzymatic conversion in plant tissues by desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry imaging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-528077","identifier":[{"id":"23551340","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84878780029","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e14f80af-1a03-4c44-a03f-8a0150630bf8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6460E89A5663E63AD4C606D9207784FC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Analytical Biosciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Bin","key":"libinpau","last":"Li","locid":"6aab4954-aad0-4fef-8072-1f5245b2dc1c","name":"Li, Bin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla Knudsen","key":"knudsencamillapau","last":"Baden","locid":"028ed2c9-0fe6-4d43-9a0b-1ec9504c1f7c","name":"Knudsen, Camilla","name_org":"Baden, Camilla Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0001-9573-5699","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Natascha Kristine Krahl","key":"hansennataschakristin