":"Gao","key":"xinpau","last":"Xin","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","name_org":"Xin, Gao","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","name":"Rosendahl, Lasse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aliraza","key":"rezaniakolaeipau","last":"Rezaniakolaei","locid":"6c2a84b4-6efc-4a1f-9ddb-cfda7efcb620","name":"Rezaniakolaei, Alireza","name_org":"Rezaniakolaei, Aliraza","orcid":"0000-0003-4582-2342","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6f6a9802-dd35-4fbb-8625-09b42b36636e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Heat exchanger selection and optimization of a thermoelectric generator subsystem for HT-PEM fuel cell exhaust heat recovery","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-082475","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Storing electrical energy is one of the main challenges for modern society grid systems containing increasing amounts of renewable energy from wind, solar and wave sources. Although batteries are excellent storage devices for electrical energy, their usage is often limited by a low energy density, a possible solution, an avoidance of the long recharging time is combining them with the use of fuel cells. Fuel cells continuously deliver electrical power as long as a proper fuel supply is maintained. The ideal fuel for fuel cells is hydrogen, which in it’s pure for has high volumetric storage requirements. One of the solutions to this fuel storage problem is using liquid fuels such as methanol that through a chemical reformer converts the fuel into a hydrogen rich gas mixture. Methanol is a liquid fuel, which has low storage requirements and high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane (HTPEM) fuel cells can eciently run on the reformed hydrogen rich gas, although with reduced performance depending on the contaminants, such as CO, in the gas. By estimating the amount of CO in the fuel cell, it could be possible to adjust the fuel cell system operating parameters to increase performance of the reformer and fuel cell stack. This work focus on the estimation of CO percentage in the hydrogen rich anode gas in a fuel cell, by combining signal processing ideas with impedance information of the fuel cell while it is running. The presented approach functions during in the normal operating range of an HTPEM fuel cell.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Schaltz, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086117"],"event":{"end":"2013-04-18","place":"Karlsruhe, de","start":"2013-04-16","title":"5th International Conference FDFC2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fuel cell","HTPEM","Methanol","Reforming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of co concentration in high temperature pem fuel cells using electrochemical impedance","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/123215089/Estimation_of_CO_concentration_in_high_temperature_PEM_fuel_cells_using_electrochemical_impedance_spectroscopy.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-086117","ids":["aau-7c030737-1ae8-4a54-862e-3e88867434d6"],"keyword":["CO estimation","Fuel cell","HTPEM","Methanol","Reforming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5BDFEC3A282549EE962DE0074C7306E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/123215089/Estimation_of_CO_concentration_in_high_temperature_PEM_fuel_cells_using_electrochemical_impedance_spectroscopy.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Christian Becker","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"372be06d-7f4f-4025-86a1-75eb41ce5af8","name":"Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"European Institute for Energy Research (EIFER)","status":"p","subtitle":"FDFC 2013","title":"Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Fundamentals &amp; Development of Fuel Cells"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7c030737-1ae8-4a54-862e-3e88867434d6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of CO concentration in high temperature PEM fuel cells using electrochemical impedance","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086117","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"How quickly large biomass particles can ignite and burn out when transported into a pulverized-fuel (pf) furnace and suddenly exposed to a hot gas flow containing oxygen is very important in biomass co-firing design and optimization. In this paper, the ignition and burnout of the largest possible biomass (pine wood) particles in a pf furnace (a few millimeters in diameter) are studied experimentally in a single particle combustion reactor rig, in which the ambient gas temperature and oxygen concentration can vary in the ranges of 1473-1873 K and 5-20%, respectively. A one dimensional (1D) transient model is also developed to predict their conversion, in which the key processes inside the particle and in the boundary layer outside the particle are properly considered. For the pine wood particles in which large temperature gradients exist, the primary heterogeneous ignition is always detected for all the test conditions. As the particle is further heated up and the volume-weighted average temperature reaches the onset of rapid decomposition of hemicellulose and cellulose, a secondary homogeneous ignition occurs. The model-predicted ignition delays and burnout times show a good agreement with the experimental results. Homogeneous ignition delays are found to scale with specific surface areas while heterogeneous ignition delays show less dependency on the areas. The ignition and burnout are also affected by the process conditions, in which the oxygen concentration is found to have a more pronounced impact on the ignition delays and burnout times at lower oxidizer temperatures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","Yin, Chungen","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Hvid, Søren Lovmand"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112015"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomass","Burnout"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comprehensive study of ignition and combustion of single wooden particles","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ef302153f","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-112015","identifier":[{"id":"84874129154","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000315431900052","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d55b919c-b91e-45aa-9181-d44efde20ed0"],"keyword":["Biomass","Burnout","Heterogeneous ignition","Homogeneous ignition","Ignition delays"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1CC322B99CC6A22C74FBCA1C9F5DD5F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ef302153f","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["DONG Energy A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maryam","key":"momenikouchaksaraeipau","last":"Momenikouchaksaraei","locid":"f9706a2b-7ab1-4b2d-b289-7dfee67472f8","name":"Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chungen","key":"yinpau","last":"Yin","locid":"a24ca845-2626-44cc-b726-b6c5ec9ddd24","name":"Yin, Chungen","orcid":"0000-0002-9885-7744","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Lovmand","key":"hvidpau","last":"Hvid","name":"Hvid, Søren Lovmand","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/ef302153f","issn":["08870624","15205029"],"issn_org":["08870624"],"issue":"2","journal":"Energy and Fuels","pages":"1061-1072","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Energy and Fuels","title_org":"Energy & Fuels","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874129154"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d55b919c-b91e-45aa-9181-d44efde20ed0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comprehensive study of ignition and combustion of single wooden particles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112015","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Offshore wind energy capitalizes on the higher and less turbulent wind speeds at sea. To enable deployment of wind turbines in deep-water locations, structures are being explored, where wind turbines are placed on a floating platform. This combined structure presents a new control problem, due to the partly unconstrained movement of the platform and ocean wave excitation. If this additional complexity is not dealt with properly, this may lead to a significant increase in the structural loads and, potentially, instability of the controlled system. In this paper, the wave excitation is investigated, and we show the influence that both wind speed, wave frequencies and misalignment between wind and waves have on the system dynamics. A new control model is derived that extends standard turbine models to include the hydrodynamics, additional platform degrees of freedom, the platform mooring system and tower side-side motion, including gyroscopic effects. The models support a model-based design that includes estimators for wind speed and wave frequency. The design is applied to a number of examples representing different wind and wave conditions and successfully demonstrates a reduction in the structural oscillations, while improving power performance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christiansen, Søren","Bak, Thomas","Knudsen, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116340"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"damping wind and wave loads on a floating wind turbine","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/80051496/energies_06_04097_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-116340","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000330282200023","type":"wos"},{"id":"84884636244","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e411fdbc-cf9c-4d7a-a7ef-36f10c3cfb35"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-169C7611771A74F5F189A4CDDD34FD74"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/6/8/4097","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en6084097","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/80051496/energies_06_04097_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Automation & Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"31e1968a-95d9-469a-bc94-0ce41a58b13b","name":"Christiansen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"474a52b5-2182-461f-8b5c-4ef451576fe4","name":"Bak, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8282-5932","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2320ea13-8eb2-4116-9386-b562514277b8","name":"Knudsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-5478-8513","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en6084097","issn":["19961073"],"journal":"Energies","pages":"4097-4116","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884636244"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e411fdbc-cf9c-4d7a-a7ef-36f10c3cfb35"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Damping Wind and Wave Loads on a Floating Wind Turbine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-116340","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"To better manage the magnitude and the direction of the heat flux in an exchanger-based methanol evaporator of a fuel cell system, thermoelectric (TE) modules can be deployed as TE heat flux regulators (TERs). The performance of the TE-integrated evaporator is strongly influenced by its heat exchange structure. The structure transfers the fuel cell exhaust heat to the evaporation chamber to evaporate the methanol, where TE modules are installed in between to facilitate the heat regulation. In this work, firstly, a numerical study is conducted to determine the working currents and working modes of the TERs under the system working condition fluctuations and during the system cold start. A 3-dimensional evaporator model is generated in ANSYS FLUENT® by combining a compact TE model with various heat exchange structure geometries. The compact TE model can dramatically improve the computation efficiency, and uses a different material property acquisition method based on module manufacturers’ datasheets. Secondly, a simulation study is carried out on the novel evaporator to minimize its thermal resistance and to assess the evaporator pressure drop. The factors studied include: type of the fins of the heat exchange structure, thickness of the fins, axial conduction penalty, etc. Results show that the TE-integrated evaporator can work more efficiently and smoothly during both load fluctuations and system cold start, it is of superior performance.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gao, Xin","Chen, Min","Snyder, G. Jeffrey","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118286"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-12","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2012-07-09","title":"The 31st International &amp; 10th European Conference on Thermoelectrics","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["2- Materials Science, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, California 91125, USA","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Heat loss","Heat regulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thermal management optimization of a thermoelectric integrated methanol evaporator using a compact cfd modeling approach","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72963526/Xin_Gao_Heat_exchanger_structure_optimization_for_a_TE_integrated_methanol_evaporator.docx","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-118286","identifier":[{"id":"2-s2.0-84879799928","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000320890800120","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-eacdb711-c255-4dca-8aa9-81128e09aa58"],"keyword":["Compact TE model","Heat loss","Heat regulation","TE-integrated methanol evaporator","Thermoelectric heat regulator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55EE95781E7599315B6E8CA5EC1DB240"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2Fs11664-013-2514-2","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72963526/Xin_Gao_Heat_exchanger_structure_optimization_for_a_TE_integrated_methanol_evaporator.docx","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11664-013-2514-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"2 materials science california institute of technology pasadena california 91125 usa","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"2- Materials Science, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, California 91125, USA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gao","key":"xinpau","last":"Xin","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","name_org":"Xin, Gao","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"9efe2461-3f4a-46b4-82d6-8e5fb687cc3b","name":"Chen, Min","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G. Jeffrey","key":"snyderpau","last":"Snyder","name":"Snyder, G. Jeffrey","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11664-013-2514-2","issn":["03615235","1543186X"],"issn_org":["03615235"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Electronic Materials","pages":"2035-2042","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"Journal of Electronic Materials","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879799928"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-eacdb711-c255-4dca-8aa9-81128e09aa58"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Thermal management optimization of a thermoelectric-integrated methanol evaporator using a compact CFD modeling approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118286","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":" INTRODUCTION: Patients treated with a temporary pacemaker (TPM) due to atrioventricular (AV) block are often monitored after discontinuation of AV node blocking drugs to evaluate the indication for permanent pacing. However, the impact of drug discontinuation is sparsely documented. We investigated to what extent drug discontinuation abolished the need for permanent pacemaker (PPM) implantation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Maria Bisgaard","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","Riahi, Sam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123133"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of drug discontinuation in patients treated with temporary pacemaker due to atrioventricular block","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jce.12211","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-123133","identifier":[{"id":"84886789905","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23869746","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000326228000010","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-fbb58374-92a6-415e-b044-c9644493e6ba"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AEC8CE69CBDBCC80FF8B29309AB44B2A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jce.12211","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Kardiovaskulært Forskningscenter","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Bisgaard","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"d7c464db-a540-41e5-b9e8-2bbb31899c3e","name":"Knudsen, Maria Bisgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Margrethe","key":"thøgersenpau","last":"Thøgersen","locid":"040c49e1-e9f1-4e74-8cd0-4a9ef9fb7006","name":"Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Pihlkjaer","key":"hjortshøjpau","last":"Hjortshøj","locid":"d24227f4-62ce-4a90-86ec-482cf4e88a34","name":"Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","name_org":"Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjaer","orcid":"0000-0002-4231-9963","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sam","key":"riahipau","last":"Riahi","locid":"9e5489d8-981a-469c-bd84-20b2e24832de","name":"Riahi, Sam","orcid":"0000-0003-1849-9463","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23869746"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jce.12211","issn":["10453873","15408167"],"issn_org":["10453873"],"issue":"11","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","pages":"1255-1258","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886789905"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fbb58374-92a6-415e-b044-c9644493e6ba"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Impact of Drug Discontinuation in Patients Treated with Temporary Pacemaker Due to Atrioventricular Block","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123133","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVEPatients with type 2 diabetes have a high incidence of cardiovascular events including stroke. Increased arterial stiffness (AS) predicts cardiovascular events in the general population. Cerebral white matter lesions (WMLs) are associated with an increased risk of stroke. It is unknown whether AS in patients with type 2 diabetes is associated with WMLs.RESEARCH DESIGN AND METHODSWe examined 89 patients recently diagnosed with type 2 diabetes (","author_count":12,"contributors":["Laugesen, Esben","Høyem, Pernille","Stausbøl-Grøn, Brian","Mikkelsen, Anders P","Thrysøe, Samuel Alberg","Erlandsen, Mogens","Christiansen, Jens Sandahl","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Hansen, Klavs Würgler","Kim, Won Yong","Hansen, Troels Krarup","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-149246"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carotid femoral pulse wave velocity is associated with cerebral white matter lesions in type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2337/dc12-0942","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-149246","identifier":[{"id":"23129135","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3579355","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84874447837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-22b832c0-ef04-415f-a9f0-fc4e39698cac"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26AA046AF440DB22C4925E18924C118C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2337/dc12-0942","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"laugesenesbenpau","last":"Laugesen","locid":"e06ca9b7-d51f-40f2-b042-696ca2b18492","name":"Laugesen, Esben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"høyempernillepau","last":"Høyem","locid":"cbd0d45d-3fcf-4208-93ca-d5f580739f1a","name":"Høyem, Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"stausbølgrønbrianpau","last":"Stausbøl-Grøn","locid":"cdff3a14-083d-4bfa-a9bf-a96f11fc29c0","name":"Stausbøl-Grøn, Brian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"mikkelsenandersppau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"501f746e-68c2-4e96-81c2-1669bfd916d5","name":"Mikkelsen, Anders P","name_org":"Mikkelsen, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel","key":"thrysøesamuelalbergpau","last":"Thrysøe","locid":"b9b2f590-9b26-41d9-ac0a-a7968e836012","name":"Thrysøe, Samuel Alberg","name_org":"Thrysøe, Samuel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"erlandsenmogenspau","last":"Erlandsen","locid":"2e9afb75-6fd0-4f6a-be20-9034d4975fe4","name":"Erlandsen, Mogens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens S","key":"christiansenjenssandahlpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"3af3a403-0f32-4202-aaec-135d99299f52","name":"Christiansen, Jens Sandahl","name_org":"Christiansen, Jens S","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren T","key":"knudsensørentangpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","name_org":"Knudsen, Søren T","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klavs Würgler","key":"hansenklavswürglerpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2dc4053-a6dd-47ea-bfeb-e689b3b6fc94","name":"Hansen, Klavs Würgler","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Won Y","key":"kimwonyongpau","last":"Kim","locid":"5124a60e-0d6b-4fce-947f-75ec72c482e6","name":"Kim, Won Yong","name_org":"Kim, Won Y","orcid":"0000-0003-1302-1671","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels K","key":"hansentroelskraruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4af39f3a-9bb3-4f30-8fee-29a550538de8","name":"Hansen, Troels Krarup","name_org":"Hansen, Troels K","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per L","key":"poulsenperløgstruppau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","name_org":"Poulsen, Per L","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23129135"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/dc12-0942","issn":["01495992"],"issue":"3","journal":"Diabetes Care","pages":"722-728","publisher":"American Diabetes Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Care","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874447837"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-22b832c0-ef04-415f-a9f0-fc4e39698cac"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Carotid-Femoral Pulse Wave Velocity Is Associated With Cerebral White Matter Lesions in Type 2 Diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-149246","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: [(11)C]Cimbi-36 was recently developed as an agonist radioligand for brain imaging of serotonin 2A receptors (5-HT(2A)) with positron emission tomography (PET). This may be used to quantify the high-affinity state of 5-HT(2A) receptors and may have the potential to quantify changes in cerebral 5-HT levels in vivo. We here investigated safety aspects related to clinical use of [(11)C]Cimbi-36, including radiation dosimetry and in vivo pharmacology. PROCEDURES: [(11)C]Cimbi-36 was injected in rats or pigs, and radiation dosimetry was examined by ex vivo dissection or with PET scanning, respectively. Based on animal data, the Organ Level INternal Dose Assessment software was used to estimate extrapolated human dosimetry for [(11)C]Cimbi-36. The 5-HT(2A) receptor agonist actions of [(11)C]Cimbi-36 in vivo pharmacological effects in mice elicited by increasing doses of Cimbi-36 were assessed with the head-twitch response (HTR). RESULTS: The effective dose as extrapolated from both rat and pig data was low, 7.67 and 4.88 μSv/MBq, respectively. In addition, the estimated absorbed radiation dose to human target organs did not exceed safety levels. Administration of 0.5 mg/kg Cimbi-36 leads to significant HTR compared to saline, whereas 0.05 mg/kg Cimbi-36 (doses much larger than those given in conjunction with a PET scan) did not elicit a significant HTR. CONCLUSIONS: Administration of tracer doses of [(11)C]Cimbi-36 does not seem to be associated with unusual radiation burden or adverse clinical effects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ettrup, Anders","Holm, Søren","Hansen, Martin","Wasim, Muhammad","Santini, Martin Andreas","Palner, Mikael","Madsen, Jacob","Svarer, Claus","Kristensen, Jesper Langgaard","Knudsen, Gitte Moos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-540997"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preclinical safety assessment of the 000000000005 ht 000000000002a receptor agonist pet radioligand 000000000011 c cimbi 000000000036","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11307-012-0609-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-540997","identifier":[{"id":"23306971","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880326182","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f7321f59-b101-4c64-bae8-983917974c02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EEE801282ED1445F018E0ED1E8D42883"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11307-012-0609-4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Diagnostic Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","name":"Ettrup, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"f6989f1e-f730-4207-9ef1-9a6c380a4aa2","name":"Holm, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5a430dba-481e-41d2-bbce-ab017198cfa8","name":"Hansen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4663-8742","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Muhammad","key":"wasimpau","last":"Wasim","name":"Wasim, Muhammad","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin Andreas","key":"santinipau","last":"Santini","name":"Santini, Martin Andreas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael","key":"palnerpau","last":"Palner","locid":"203c8a01-1e49-4175-a10a-aed3042076e1","name":"Palner, Mikael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Jacob","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claus","key":"svarerpau","last":"Svarer","name":"Svarer, Claus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Langgaard","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"33965c96-9f54-48ed-9a82-ed0c062174f8","name":"Kristensen, Jesper Langgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5613-1267","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gitte Moos","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Moos","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23306971"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11307-012-0609-4","issn":["15361632","18602002"],"issn_org":["15361632"],"issue":"4","journal":"Molecular Imaging and Biology","pages":"376-83","status":"p","title":"Molecular Imaging and Biology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880326182"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f7321f59-b101-4c64-bae8-983917974c02"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preclinical Safety Assessment of the 5-HT(2A) Receptor Agonist PET Radioligand [ (11)C]Cimbi-36","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-540997","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This work analyses the conditioning of single fuel cell assemblies based on different membrane electrode assembly (MEA) types, produced by different methods. The analysis was done by means of electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, and the changes in the fitted resistances of the all the tested MEAs are studied. The ohmic resistances increase in most cases, implying that the proton conductivity of polybenzimidazole (PBI) membrane degrades during the conditioning process. On the other hand, the intermediate frequency resistances generally decrease showing enhancement in cathodic activities during the process.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Araya, Samuel Simon","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056711"],"event":{"end":"2013-12-13","place":"Rome, it","start":"2013-12-11","title":"5th European Fuel Cell Technology &amp; Applications Conference - Piero Lunghi Conference","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Break in","Conditioning","High temperature PEM fuel cell","PBI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impedance analysis of the conditioning of pbi based electrode membrane assemblies for high temperature pem fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-056711","identifier":[{"id":"84926311578","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-16b222ff-a893-4a74-8fb4-74423d43abb7"],"keyword":["Break-in","Conditioning","High temperature PEM fuel cell","PBI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-52A69CF5D9862F0659AED8ACDD8F1E61"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viviana","key":"cigolottipedh","last":"Cigolotti","name":"Cigolotti, Viviana","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chiara","key":"barchiesipedh","last":"Barchiesi","name":"Barchiesi, Chiara","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michela","key":"chianellapedh","last":"Chianella","name":"Chianella, Michela","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788882862978"],"pages":"169-170","place":"Rome, Italy","publisher":"Italian National Agency for New Technologies, Energy and Sustainable Economic Devlopment","status":"p","subtitle":"Fifth European Fuel Cell Technology &amp; Applications Conference - Piero Lunghi Conference","title":"Proceedings of EFC2013"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926311578"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-16b222ff-a893-4a74-8fb4-74423d43abb7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impedance Analysis of the Conditioning of PBI–Based Electrode Membrane Assemblies for High Temperature PEM Fuel Cells","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056711","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The present work describes the ongoing development of high temperature PEM fuel cell systems fuelled by steam reformed methanol. Various fuel cell system solutions exist, they mainly differ depending on the desired fuel used. High temperature PEM (HTPEM) fuel cells offer the possibility of using liquid fuels such as methanol, due to the increased robustness of operating at higher temperatures (160-180oC). Using liquid fuels such as methanol removes the high volume demands of compressed hydrogen storages, simplifies refueling, and enables the use of existing fuel distribution systems. The liquid methanol is converted to a hydrogen rich gas with CO2 trace amounts of CO, the increased operating temperatures allow the fuel cell to tolerate much higher CO concentrations than Nafion-based membranes. The increased tolerance to CO also enables the use of reformer systems with less hydrogen cleaning steps and requirements for hydrogen purity, reducing the complexity of the reformer systems. Using hydrogen containing CO, affects the steady-state as well as dynamic electrical performance of the fuel cell, but stable operation is still possible with concentrations up to 3%. The typical polymer used in HTPEM fuel cells is polybenzimidazole (PBI), doped with phosphoric acid for proton conduction. The work will present a few different methanol reformer concepts, some experimental results of details related to reformer gas quality, control of burner temperature and the aspects of implementing advanced modeling based control approaches using the commercial Serenergy H3-350 methanol reformer system as an example.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Sahlin, Simon Lennart","Justesen, Kristian Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-087517"],"event":{"end":"2013-04-18","place":"Karlsruhe, de","start":"2013-04-16","title":"5th International Conference FDFC2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fuel cell","HTPEM","PBI","SYSTEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design and control of high temperature pem fuel cell systems using methanol reformers with air or liquid heat integration proceedings cd","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/77237450/FDFC2013_SJA.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-087517","ids":["aau-80deb9a4-0dd4-42b0-b282-74cb449e83c2"],"keyword":["fuel cell","htpem","pbi","system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ABAA6FB93C883227025E7EFD2BADF0E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/77237450/FDFC2013_SJA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Kjær","key":"justesenpau","last":"Justesen","locid":"071a392f-a11c-48e9-a4c7-d15094d235c8","name":"Justesen, Kristian Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9703-8747","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"European Institute for Energy Research (EIFER)","status":"p","subtitle":"Fundamentals &amp; Development of Fuel Cells","title":"5th International Conference FDFC 2013 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-80deb9a4-0dd4-42b0-b282-74cb449e83c2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Design and Control of High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell Systems using Methanol Reformers with Air or Liquid Heat Integration : Proceedings CD","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-087517","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The use of electric vehicles (EVs) is advantageous because of zero emission, but their market penetration is limited by one disadvantage, i.e., energy storage. Battery EVs (BEVs) have a limited range, and their batteries take a long time to charge, compared with the time it takes to refuel the tank of a vehicle with an internal combustion engine (ICE). Fuel cells (FCs) can be added to an EV as an additional energy source. These are faster to refill and will therefore facilitate the transition from vehicles running on fossil fuel to electricity. Different EV setups with FC strategies are presented and compared. The results of the setups are presented by range, efficiency, and price. These show the negative effect on the range when purpose-designed setups are driven above the design requirement as the range drops considerably. The simulations also showed the necessity of good FC control when driving in start/stop city cycles. Simulations with the New European Driving Cycle (NEDC) showed that efficiency fell by at least 15% for the FC hybrid EV (FCHEV) when compared with BEVs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","Schaltz, Erik","Koustrup, Per Sune","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107091"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery Electric Vehicle BEV","Fuel cell FC","Methanol"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Intelligent Cells"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of fuel cell range extender impact on hybrid electrical vehicle performance","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TVT.2012.2218840","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107091","identifier":[{"id":"84884717228","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000318514000005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-c497ecf7-6660-4858-abb8-d82b895ded88"],"keyword":["Battery electric vehicle (BEV)","fuel cell (FC)","fuel-cell hybrid electric vehicle (FCHEV)","methanol","range extender (RE)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F677D9E0BFFCA21719F27AE7C7C0895"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/search/searchresult.jsp?newsearch=true&queryText=Evaluation+of+Fuel+Cell+Range+Extender+Impact+on+Hybrid+Electrical+Vehicle+Performance&x=49&y=21","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TVT.2012.2218840","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Intelligent Cells"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Christian Becker","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"372be06d-7f4f-4025-86a1-75eb41ce5af8","name":"Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"schaltzpau","last":"Schaltz","locid":"6e39b31c-c3fa-470a-b47b-e69ee21195c1","name":"Schaltz, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-8540-0040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Sune","key":"koustruppau","last":"Koustrup","name":"Koustrup, Per Sune","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tvt.2012.2218840","issn":["00189545"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology","pages":"50-60","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Vehicular Technology","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884717228"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c497ecf7-6660-4858-abb8-d82b895ded88"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Evaluation of Fuel-Cell Range Extender Impact on Hybrid Electrical Vehicle Performance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107091","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: National guidelines recommend strict control of blood pressure (BP) and plasma low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL) in type 2 diabetes (T2DM), aiming at a BP ≤ 130/80 mmHg and an LDL concentration ≤ 2.5 mmol/l. Angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors (ACEI) or angiotensin II-receptor blockers (ARB) are recommended as primary antihypertensive therapy (AHT). To which extent these targets are met in Danish primary care is unknown. MATERIAL AND METHODS: This study was based on data from 2,057 patients with T2DM who were randomly selected from 64 general practitioners (GPs) from different regions of Denmark. Data were collected from the GPs' electronic records. RESULTS: The mean age ± standard deviation was 66.2 ± 11.6 years; 58.7% were male. The mean systolic BP ± standard deviation was 132.6 ± 14.6 mmHg and the mean diastolic BP ± standard deviation was 78.1 ± 9.0 mmHg. 47.7% of the patients met the BP target. 79.5% of the patients were on AHT. 55.1% of the untreated and 46.0% of the treated patients met the BP target. 83.4% of the treated patients received ACEI or ARB. The median LDL was 2.2 (1.7-2.7) mmol/l. 63.7% of the patients met the LDL target. 73.7% of the patients received lipid-lowering therapy. 32.8% of the untreated and 74.4% of the treated patients met the LDL target. CONCLUSION: AHT including ACEI and ARB and lipid-lowering therapy are widely used in T2DM in Danish primary care, but only half of the patients are at target for BP and two thirds are at target for LDL. Increased use of diuretics may improve BP control. FUNDING: This study was funded by a grant from Boehringer Ingelheim, Denmark. The grant covered costs related to data collection, time spent by the general practitioners and data analysis by the DTU. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren Tang","Mosbech, Thomas Hammershaimb","Hansen, Birtha Petrea","Kønig, Else","Johnsen, Peter Christian","Kamper, Anne-Lise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240777"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"difficulties in reaching therapeutic goals for hypertension and dysplipidaemia in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes in general practice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84888806976","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240777","identifier":[{"id":"84888806976","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24355449","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c3535546-eda7-4ea8-86e7-6217532a090b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-02C291A3BC6D87C73A0081E843D85DE5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Hammershaimb","key":"mosbechpau","last":"Mosbech","name":"Mosbech, Thomas Hammershaimb","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birtha","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a1d570fa-0545-410e-bf76-8e9b1da12a37","name":"Hansen, Birtha Petrea","name_org":"Hansen, Birtha","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Else","key":"kønigpau","last":"Kønig","name":"Kønig, Else","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Christian","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Peter Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Lise","key":"kamperpau","last":"Kamper","name":"Kamper, Anne-Lise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24355449"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"12","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c3535546-eda7-4ea8-86e7-6217532a090b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Difficulties in reaching therapeutic goals for hypertension and dysplipidaemia in patients with type 2 diabetes in general practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240777","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A fast pyrolysis study on lignin and macroalgae (non-conventional biomass) and wood and straw (conventional biomass) were carried out in a pyrolysis centrifugal reactor at pyrolysis temperature of 550 ºC. The product distributions and energy recoveries were measured and compared among these biomasses. The fast pyrolysis of macroalgae showed a promising result with a bio-oil yield of 65 wt% dry ash free basis (daf) and 76 % energy recovery in the bio-oil while the lignin fast pyrolysis provides a bio-oil yield of 47 wt% daf and energy recovery in bio-oil of 45 %. The physiochemical properties of the bio-oils were characterized with respect to higher heating value (HHV), molecular mass distribution, viscosity, pH, density, thermal behaviors, elemental concentrations, phase separation and aging. The lignin and macroalgae oil properties were different compared to those of the wood and straw oils with respect to carbon and oxygen contents, HHV, thermal behaviors and mean molecular weight. The HHV of wood, straw, lignin and algae oils were 24.0, 23.7, 29.7 and 25.7 MJ/kg db, respectively. The distributions of metals, Cl and S in char and bio-oil were investigated for the biomasses. Almost all the metals (Al, Ca, Fe, K, Mg, Na, P and Si) were contained in the chars at the pyrolysis temperature of 550 ºC. The char properties were characterized and their potential applications are discussed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Trinh, Ngoc Trung","Jensen, Peter Arendt","Dam-Johansen, Kim","Knudsen, Niels Ole","Sørensen, Hanne Risbjerg","Hvilsted, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio oil properties","Fast pyrolysis","Lignin","Macroalgae","Straw","Wood"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparison of lignin macroalgae wood and straw fast pyrolysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ef301927y","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340220","identifier":[{"id":"84875440186","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7769f38a-fe2c-4980-8a2e-e8db4af9c6d4"],"keyword":["Bio-oil properties","Fast pyrolysis","Lignin","Macroalgae","Straw","Wood"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D944561BB270D8058D34AFE56BF4CA3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ef301927y","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["Ørsted A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ngoc Trung","key":"trinhpau","last":"Trinh","locid":"75db04fa-9338-4691-ad8a-72b3a8ca8f9d","name":"Trinh, Ngoc Trung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"61f75c0e-450b-4b80-9f3d-3f28b888ddb4","name":"Jensen, Peter Arendt","orcid":"0000-0001-6784-5321","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"damjohansenpau","last":"Dam-Johansen","locid":"ca095f0d-81ca-4127-b341-7d3578a38976","name":"Dam-Johansen, Kim","orcid":"0000-0003-1658-6176","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Ole","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Niels Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Risbjerg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Hanne Risbjerg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"hvilstedpau","last":"Hvilsted","locid":"871ab09e-1665-4af0-a062-d2edb2f0b561","name":"Hvilsted, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/ef301927y","issn":["08870624","15205029"],"issn_org":["08870624"],"issue":"3","journal":"Energy and Fuels","pages":"1399-1409","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Energy and Fuels","title_org":"Energy & Fuels","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875440186"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7769f38a-fe2c-4980-8a2e-e8db4af9c6d4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Comparison of Lignin, Macroalgae, Wood and Straw Fast Pyrolysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340220","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Dietary fibers (DF) may affect energy balance, an effect often ascribed to the viscous nature of some water soluble DF, which affect luminal viscosity and thus multiple physiological processes. We have tested the hypothesis that viscous linseed DF reduce apparent nutrient digestibility, and limit weight gain, in a randomized feeding trial where 60 male, growing, Wistar rats, with an initial weight of ~200 g, were fed different diets (n = 10 per group): low DF control (C), 5% DF from cellulose (5-CEL), CEL + 5% DF from whole (5-WL) or ground linseed (5-GL), CEL + 5% DF from linseed DF extract (5-LDF), and CEL + 10% DF from linseed DF extract (10-LDF). Diets were provided ad libitum for 21 days. Feed intake and faecal output were measured during days 17–21. Faecal fat excretion increased with increasing DF content and was highest in the 10-LDF group. Apparent fat digestibility was highest with the C diet (94.9% ± 0.8%) and lowest (74.3% ± 0.6%) with the 10-LDF diet, and decreased in a non-linear manner with increasing DF (p < 0.001). Apparent fat digestibility also decreased with increased accessibility of DF (5-WL vs. 5-GL) and when the proportion of viscous DF increased (5-GL vs. 5-LDF). The 10-LDF resulted in a lower final body weight (258 ± 6.2 g) compared to C (282 ± 5.9 g), 5-CEL (281 ± 5.9 g), and 5-WL (285 ± 5.9 g) (p < 0.05). The 10-LDF diet reduced body fat compared to 5-CEL (p < 0.01). In conclusion, DF extracted from linseed reduced apparent energy and fat digestibility and resulted in restriction of body weight gain in growing rats.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kristensen, Mette","Knudsen, Knud Erik Bach","Jørgensen, Henry","Oomah, David","Bügel, Susanne","Toubro, Søren","Tetens, Inge","Astrup, Arne"],"cuid":["S03-096.79-018133"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["ANTHROPOMETRIC PARAMETERS","Animal models","Availability","BODY WT","Bioavailability","Dietary fibers","Dietary fibre","Digestibility","Fibre","Human physiology","Linseed","Linseeds","Obesity","Oilseeds","Physiological effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linseed dietary fibers reduce apparent digestibility of energy and fat and weight gain in growing rats","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60022473/3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.79-018133","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3775254","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23966109","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84882594362","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4b0e1e2b-3adc-434c-9931-eccae1425abc","dtu-50666be5-7cc4-4bae-8950-82f1b2f594ac","ku-95cdcee1-d109-446f-a90e-8909ab23a3b0"],"keyword":["ANIMAL MODELS","ANTHROPOMETRIC PARAMETERS","AVAILABILITY","BIOAVAILABILITY","BODY FATS","BODY WT.","DIETARY FIBRE","DIGESTIBILITY","FIBRE","HUMAN PHYSIOLOGY","LINSEEDS","OILSEEDS","PHYSIOLOGICAL EFFECTS","dietary fibers","fat digestibility","linseed","obesity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-0D3ED904AE04AE29E33439B5520D070C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu5083287","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60022473/3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/2072-6643/5/8/3287","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearP