{"abstract":"The SphygmoCor is used for noninvasive assessment of ascending aortic blood pressure (BP). However, the validity of the SphygmoCor transfer function has not been tested in an exclusively type 2 diabetic patient sample. Calibration with systolic (SBP) and diastolic (DBP) brachial BP has previously been associated with substantial imprecision of central BP estimates. We hypothesized that different noninvasive calibration strategies might improve the accuracy of the estimated ascending aortic BPs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Laugesen, Esben","Rossen, Niklas B","Peters, Christian Daugaard","Maeng, Michael","Ebbehøj, Eva","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Hansen, Klavs Würgler","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Poulsen, Per Løgstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-151480"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of central blood pressure in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes a comparison between sphygmocor and invasively measured values","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ajh/hpt195","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-151480","identifier":[{"id":"24304654","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891598250","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-26877317-4049-4762-b21b-55f0ac7f12f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90C26372AE26CFC4E9BC60CFBB78E5A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ajh/hpt195","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus U