Løgstrup","key":"poulsenperløgstruppau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a965cecb-44f9-4913-a8e1-7bc669e8ffd9","name":"Poulsen, Per Løgstrup","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Melholt","key":"rasmussenlarsmelholtpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"bf5d4e3b-cb51-4e61-a6d1-e22445213324","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","orcid":"0000-0001-5795-4794","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23866070"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1475-2840-12-107","issn":["14752840"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cardiovascular Diabetology","pages":"107","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Diabetology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880183610"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-03f02c9e-215a-4eb5-9ffc-90b0a3a06e01","sdu-32a7d2d6-968f-4287-8791-ad859d1a0570"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Plasma levels of the arterial wall protein fibulin-1 are associated with carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity : a cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.35-012886","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"— Offshore wind energy capitalizes on the higher and less turbulent wind at sea. Shallow water sites are proﬁtable for deployment of monopile wind turbines at water depths of up to 30 meters. Beyond 30 meters, the wind is even stronger and less turbulent. At these depths, ﬂoating wind turbines become proﬁtable, capable of accessing unexploited wind resources while reaching regions of new consumers. However, ﬂoating wind turbines are subject to reduced structural stiffness which results in instabilities when standard wind turbine control systems are applied. Based on optimal control, this paper presents a new minimum thrust control strategy capable of stabilizing a ﬂoating wind turbine. The new control strategy explores the freedom of variable generator speed above rated wind speed. A comparison to the traditional constant speed strategy, shows improvements in structural fore-aft oscillations and power stability when using the new control strategy.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christiansen, Søren","Bak, Thomas","Knudsen, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055276"],"event":{"end":"2012-10-05","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2012-10-03","title":"2012 IEEE Multi-conference on Systems and Control","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minimum thrust load control for floating wind turbine","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CCA.2012.6402358","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-055276","identifier":[{"id":"84873144519","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-11e6b98a-bc85-4d18-ab90-0a153f81fa3c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D62E25BD21EA33116BC149EA3989CB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CCA.2012.6402358","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Automation & Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"31e1968a-95d9-469a-bc94-0ce41a58b13b","name":"Christiansen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"474a52b5-2182-461f-8b5c-4ef451576fe4","name":"Bak, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8282-5932","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2320ea13-8eb2-4116-9386-b562514277b8","name":"Knudsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-5478-8513","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cca.2012.6402358","eisbn":["9781467345040"],"isbn":["9781467345033"],"issn":["10851992"],"pages":"587-592","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"IEEE International Conference on Control Applications. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Control Applications (CCA), 2012 IEEE International Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873144519"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-11e6b98a-bc85-4d18-ab90-0a153f81fa3c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Minimum Thrust Load Control for Floating Wind Turbine","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055276","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A multiphase fuel cell model based on computational fluid dynamics is used to investigate the possibility of operating a proton exchange membrane fuel cell at low stoichiometric flow ratios (ξ < 1.5) employing the interdigitated flow field design and using completely dry inlet gases. A case study of two different operating temperatures and two different operating pressures is presented. In all cases the cathode side stoichiometric flow ratio was varied from ξc = 1.5 to 1.2, and the anode side varied to as low as ξa = 1.05. It is found that operating at ambient pressure leads to a generally dryer cell, and the only possibility to prevent membrane dry-out is to operate at or below 70 °C. The cell is generally better humidified at an elevated pressure, and here it is found that the cathode channels will become flooded when the operating temperature is too low, e.g. 70 °C, while membrane hydration levels of λ = 7–10 can be achieved at 80 °C. Operation at stoichiometric flow ratios as low as ξ = 1.2 at the cathode side and ξ = 1.05 at the anode side appear feasible. If this can be verified, it would allow open-ended anode operation without recirculation or flow shifting, thus significantly reducing system complexity and cost.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068547"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low stoichiometry operation of a proton exchange membrane fuel cell employing the interdigitated flow field a modeling study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2012.02.137","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-068547","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000305040400041","type":"wos"},{"id":"84860387325","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3fe6b26c-b5a8-4105-9cd2-c61d5a910226"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-96371C17ED41FF0E65B1CBC8464548E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2012.02.137","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2012.02.137","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"10","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"8477-8489","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860387325"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3fe6b26c-b5a8-4105-9cd2-c61d5a910226"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Low stoichiometry operation of a proton exchange membrane fuel cell employing the interdigitated flow field : A modeling study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068547","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A high temperature-proton exchange membrane (HT-PEMFC)-based micro-combined-heat-and-power (CHP) residential system is designed and optimized, using a genetic algorithm (GA) optimization strategy. The proposed system consists of a fuel cell stack, steam methane reformer (SMR) reactor, water gas shift (WGS) reactor, heat exchangers, and other balance-of-plant (BOP) components. The objective function of the single-objective optimization strategy is the net electrical efficiency of the micro-CHP system. The implemented optimization procedure attempts to maximize the objective function by variation of nine decision variables. The value of the objective function for the optimum design configuration is significantly higher than the initial one, with a 20.7% increase.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arsalis, Alexandros","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-074856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and optimization of a 000000000001 kwe ht pemfc based micro chp residential system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.10.081","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-074856","identifier":[{"id":"84855845077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5579a4db-a8c1-4aad-9a58-10f720877b58"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9668CDADD58423C9F6C97701C01BE9B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.10.081","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"arsalispau","last":"Arsalis","locid":"78eb1abb-bd28-461a-8c05-68a79cd90e77","name":"Arsalis, Alexandros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.10.081","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"2470-2481","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855845077"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5579a4db-a8c1-4aad-9a58-10f720877b58"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and optimization of a 1 kWe HT-PEMFC-based micro-CHP residential system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-074856","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A fully coupled three-dimensional, steady-state, two-fluid, multi-component and non-isothermal DMFC model has been developed in the commercial CFD package CFX 13 (ANSYS inc.). It accounts for the presence of micro porous layers, non-equilibrium phase change, and methanol and water uptake in the ionomer phase of the catalytic layer, and detailed membrane transport of methanol and water. In order to verify the models ability to predict methanol crossover, simulation results are compared with experimental measurements under different current densities along with air and methanol stoichiometries. Methanol crossover is indirectly measured based on the combined anode and cathode exhaust CO2 mole fraction and by accounting for the CO2 production at the anode as a function of current density. This approach is simple and assumes that all crossed over methanol is oxidized. Moreover, it takes CO2 crossover into account.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-099138"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-26","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2012-07-23","title":"ASME 2012 6th International Conference on Energy Sustainability &amp; 10th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental validation of methanol crossover in a three dimensional two fluid model of a direct methanol fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-099138","identifier":[{"id":"84892631792","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a93c0341-3788-4d16-9780-e36f42fae5fc"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7086CEA298E0C0C4DA4B92A028F44100"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","status":"p","subtitle":"ESFuelCell2012","title":"Proceedings of ASME 2012 6th International Conference on Energy Sustainability &amp; 10th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a93c0341-3788-4d16-9780-e36f42fae5fc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental Validation of Methanol Crossover in a Three-dimensional, Two-Fluid Model of a Direct Methanol Fuel Cell","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-099138","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Numerical and experimental study is performed to evaluate the reactant by-pass flow in a catalytic plate reactor with a coated wire mesh catalyst for steam reforming of methane for hydrogen generation. By-pass of unconverted methane is evaluated under different wire mesh catalyst width to reactor duct width ratios, the results show that altering this ratio from 0.98 to 0.96 results in an increase in by-pass mass flow of 22%. Effect of catalytic wire mesh flow resistance on by-pass flow has also been investigated and results show increased by-pass flow as catalytic wire mesh flow resistance increases. The numerical results are in good agreement with experimental data. The study improves the understanding of the underlying transport phenomena in these reactors and shows that the flow maldistribution in a catalytic plate reactor using a coated wire mesh has to be considered.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sigurdsson, Haftor Örn","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-108999"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-10","place":"Washington, us","start":"2011-08-07","title":"ASME 2011 5th International Conference on Energy Sustainability &amp; 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology, ESFuelCell2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental and numerical evaluation of the bypass flow in a catalytic plate reactor for hydrogen production","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4005630","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-108999","identifier":[{"id":"84859022856","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000302597100016","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-cb3698ca-27f9-445b