s-Georg","key":"sahlpau","last":"Sahl","name":"Sahl, Hans-Georg","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","locid":"0ec06c22-1f74-4dd2-a894-af30b6565766","name":"Otzen, Daniel E","name_org":"Otzen, Daniel","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reinhard","key":"wimmerpau","last":"Wimmer","locid":"1d80e9f3-a391-40e6-a73a-84194aecbb6a","name":"Wimmer, Reinhard","orcid":"0000-0001-6942-5056","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23093408","PMC3516779"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m112.382028","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"50","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"42361-42372","publisher":"American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871338911"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a74a97ca-fbd8-4392-87a7-a6f77d66d463","au-da7844f6-523d-4a53-9402-505cd66c521a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Eurocin, a New Fungal Defensin : Structure, lipid binding and its mode of action","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.10-008093","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cells have started replacing traditional lead-acid battery banks in backup systems. Although these systems are characterized by long periods of standby, they must be able to start at any instant in the shortest time. In the case of low temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems, a precise estimation of hydration status of the fuel cell during standby is important for a fast and safe startup. In this article, the measurement of the complex impedance of the fuel cell is suggested as a method to estimate the membrane hydration status. A 56-cell fuel cell stack has been symmetrically fed with air whose temperature and relative humidity were controlled, and its complex impedance was measured at different frequencies and for different values of relative humidity. After showing that the experiment was repeatable, the fuel cell stack was characterized, a power regression model was applied, and the relationship between module of impedance and relative humidity was found. The results showed that measuring the impedance of a fuel cell during standby can be a viable way for estimating the hydration status of its membrane.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bidoggia, Benoit","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071019"],"event":{"end":"2012-03-25","place":"Monte-Carlo, mc","start":"2012-03-22","title":"7th International Conference &amp; Exhibition on Ecological Vehicles and Renewable Energies, EVER2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Distributed power generation","Fuel cells","Humidity measurement","Impedance","Uninterruptible power systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of membrane hydration status for standby proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems by impedance measurement first results on stack characterization","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-071019","ids":["aau-48544e16-75e6-4e1b-ad82-ed7b5b6ba564"],"keyword":["Distributed power generation","Fuel cells","Humidity measurement","Impedance","Uninterruptible power systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-87EBDDE41B67517572F4794538ECD4A3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benoit","key":"bidoggiapau","last":"Bidoggia","locid":"132f2659-f4a2-4324-8b4e-88cec8230dea","name":"Bidoggia, Benoit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-48544e16-75e6-4e1b-ad82-ed7b5b6ba564"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of Membrane Hydration Status for Standby Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell Systems by Impedance Measurement: First Results on Stack Characterization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071019","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a numerical investigation using large-eddy simulation. Two isothermal cases from the Sydney swirling flame database with different swirl numbers were tested. Rational grid system and mesh details were presented firstly. Validations showed overall good agreement in time averaged results. In medium swirling case, there are two reverse-flow regions with a collar-like structure between them. The existence of strong unsteady structure, precessing vortex core, was proven. Coherent structures are detached from the instantaneous field. Q-criterion was used to visualize vorticity field with distinct clear structure of vortice tubes. Dominating spatial–temporal structures contained in different cross sections were extracted using proper orthogonal decomposition. In high swirling case, there is only one long reverse-flow region. In this paper, we proved the capability of a commercial CFD package in predicting complex flow field and presented the potential of large eddy simulation in understanding dynamics.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Yang, Yang","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-074359"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coherent structure","Large eddy simulation","Proper orthogonal decomposition","Vortex breakdown","Vorticity field"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"large eddy simulations of the non reactive flow in the sydney swirl burner","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheatfluidflow.2012.02.008","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-074359","identifier":[{"id":"84863865247","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000307416700005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-53b840e8-99fc-4291-b600-82605c16a3d4"],"keyword":["Coherent structure","Large Eddy Simulation","Vortex breakdown","Vorticity field","proper orthogonal decomposition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1CC89F5F851C6206F50D7AB856200FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0142727X12000525","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheatfluidflow.2012.02.008","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yang","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"c4d85e83-0cad-45da-a4d9-7577cd33f0c6","name":"Yang, Yang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijheatfluidflow.2012.02.008","issn":["0142727X"],"journal":"International Journal of Heat and Fluid Flow","pages":"47-57","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Heat and Fluid Flow","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863865247"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-53b840e8-99fc-4291-b600-82605c16a3d4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Large-eddy simulations of the non-reactive flow in the Sydney swirl burner","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-074359","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The reforming of methanol can be an alternative source of hydrogen for fuel cells because it has many practical advantages over hydrogen, mainly due to the technological limitations related to the storage, supply, and distribution of the latter. However, despite the ease of methanol handling, impurities in the reformate gas produced from methanol steam reforming can affect the performance and durability of fuel cells. In this paper different vapor delivery systems, intended to assist in the study of the effects of some of the impurities, are described and compared with each other. A system based on a pump and electrically heated evaporator was found to be more suitable for the typical flow rates involved in the anode feed of an H3PO4/PBI based HT-PEMFC unit cell assembly. Test stations composed of vapor delivery systems and mass flow controllers for testing the effects of methanol slip, water vapor, CO, and CO2 are also illustrated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Andreasen, Søren Juhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089603"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vapor delivery systems for the study of the effects of reformate gas impurities in ht pem fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4005123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-089603","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000298542000021","type":"wos"},{"id":"84555178259","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-87d8f786-5383-4660-8352-85c8d03350c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-FB81AC5B821ED6338EDF0AD0F0A337C9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4005123","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1115/1.4005123","issn":["1550624X","15516989"],"issn_org":["1550624X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Fuel Cell Science and Technology","publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","status":"p","title":"Journal of Fuel Cell Science and Technology","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84555178259"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-87d8f786-5383-4660-8352-85c8d03350c8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Vapor Delivery Systems for the Study of the Effects of Reformate Gas Impurities in HT-PEM Fuel Cells","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089603","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In this work the effects of reformate gas impurities on a H3PO4-doped polybenzimidazole (PBI) membrane-based high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell (HT-PEMFC) are studied. A unit cell assembly with a BASF Celtec®-P2100 high temperature membrane electrode assembly (MEA) of 45 cm2 active surface area is investigated by means of impedance spectroscopy. The concentrations in the anode feed gas of all impurities, unconverted methanol-water vapor mixture, CO and CO2 were varied along with current density according to a multilevel factorial design of experiments. Results show that all the impurities degrade the performance, with CO being the most degrading agent and CO2 the least. The factorial analysis shows that there is interdependence among the effects of the different factors considered. This interdependence suggests, for example, that tolerances to concentrations of CO above 2% may be compromised by the presence in the anode feed of CO2. Methanol has a poisoning effect on the fuel cell at all the tested feed ratios, and the performance drop is found to be proportional to the amount of methanol in feed gas. The effects are more pronounced when other impurities are also present in the feed gas, especially at higher methanol concentrations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Araya, Samuel Simon","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CO","CO2","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy EIS","High temperature PEM fuel cell","Methanol"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental characterization of the poisoning effects of methanol based reformate impurities on a pbi based high temperature pem fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/5/11/4251","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-101157","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000311422300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84868606449","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b0245f29-57c2-424e-8b80-2c16cbd14351"],"keyword":["CO","CO2","Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy (EIS)","high temperature PEM fuel cell","methanol"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D39DC3CD7344AA60D44433A39C9FCF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/5/11/4251","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19961073"],"issue":"11","journal":"Energies","pages":"4251-4267","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84868606449"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b0245f29-57c2-424e-8b80-2c16cbd14351"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental Characterization of the Poisoning Effects of Methanol-Based Reformate Impurities on a PBI-Based High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101157","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this study is to investigate a small scale steam methane reformer for syngas production for a micro combined heat and power (mCPH) unit under different operational conditions. The study presents an experimental analysis of the performance of a specially built single channel of a catalytic parallel plate type heat exchanger (CPHE) reformer stack, where coated Pt/Rh based wire mesh is used as a catalyst. Heat is supplied to the endothermic reaction with infrared electric heaters. All the experiments were performed under atmospheric pressure and at stable operating conditions. The following parameters are considered in the experiment: catalyst temperature, gas hourly space velocity (GHSV) and steam to carbon ratio (S/C). The catalyst was tested at temperatures between 600 and 900°C, S/C ratios between 2 and 5 and GHSV between 319 and 2201 1/h. The experimental results are used to evaluate the effect of flow maldistribution in a CPHE reformer stack on the CH4 conversion and H2 yield.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sigurdsson, Haftor Örn","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-124003"],"event":{"acronym":"ECOS","end":"2012-06-29","place":"Perugia, it","start":"2012-06-26","title":"ECOS 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"steam reforming of methane over pt rh based wire mesh catalyst in single channel reformer for small scale syngas production","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ecos2012.unipg.it/public/proceedings/pdf/CCR/CCR_ecos2012_317.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-124003","identifier":[{"id":"84896538023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fec7761a-85f9-443f-b596-bcb4f35d67dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CE15C09C2A02F1625578143C4594F585"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ecos2012.unipg.it/public/proceedings/pdf/CCR/CCR_ecos2012_317.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Haftor Örn","key":"sigurdssonpau","last":"Sigurdsson","locid":"e86e6b80-8c06-43b4-af0b-b2bab7e9d408","name":"Sigurdsson, Haftor Örn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788866553229"],"pages":"1-10","publisher":"Firenze University Press (FUP)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of ECOS 2012 - the 25th International Conference on Efficiency, Cost, Optimization, Simulation and Environmental Impact of Energy Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896538023"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fec7761a-85f9-443f-b596-bcb4f35d67dd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Steam reforming of methane over Pt/Rh based wire mesh catalyst in single channel reformer for small scale syngas production","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-124003","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper deals with field measurements of undulations of the bottom bathymetry along an otherwise straight coast at the Danish West Coast. Two bathymetric datasets and two time series of wave measurements are used in order to determine the following properties: the offshore extent of shoreline undulations, the amount of sediment transported alongshore in the shoreline undulations, the relationship between the shoreline undulations and longshore bars and the relationship between the morphology and the hydrodynamics. In one of the data sets the shoreline undulations are well correlated with undulations on the depth contours between −5m and +2m relative to mean sea level. In the other data set, only undulations on the depth contours between −1m and +1m are well correlated with the shoreline undulations. The main difference in the wave climate between the two locations is the orientation of the shoreline such that the wave incidence angle is more oblique on the section of shoreline with well correlated depth contours, suggesting that the well correlated depth contours are a result of the oblique wave incidence.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kærgaard, Kasper Hauberg","Fredsøe, Jørgen","Knudsen, Søren B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-329993"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Breaker bars","Longshore sediment transport","Shoreline undulations","Stability analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Coastal Authority"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coastline undulations on the west coast of denmark offshore extent relation to breaker bars and transported sediment volume","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.coastaleng.2011.09.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-329993","identifier":[{"id":"84855188305","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-558921b3-eaaf-4bda-b6a3-ac09c74aeb4c"],"keyword":["Breaker bars","Longshore sediment transport","Shoreline instability","Shoreline undulations","Stability analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAC492A6E9ABDA6FB773B5451B001AFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.coastaleng.2011.09.002","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Coastal Authority"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Hauberg","key":"kærgaardpau","last":"Kærgaard","locid":"708feb74-f25d-4f98-91f9-b1e930d34ac8","name":"Kærgaard, Kasper Hauberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"fredsøepau","last":"Fredsøe","locid":"033cdf7f-f3a8-48e2-91ef-95fb2ff82ef9","name":"Fredsøe, Jørgen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren B.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.coastaleng.2011.09.002","issn":["03783839","18727379"],"issn_org":["03783839"],"journal":"Coastal Engineering","pages":"109-122","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Coastal Engineering","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855188305"],"sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-558921b3-eaaf-4bda-b6a3-ac09c74aeb4c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Coastline undulations on the West Coast of Denmark: Offshore extent, relation to breaker bars and transported sediment volume","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-329993","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: National Danish guidelines recommend screening for microalbuminuria with assessment of urinary albumin/creatinine ratio at least annually in patients with type 2 diabetes. To which extent such screening is actually performed is not known. MATERIAL AND METHODS: A total of 2,057 patients with type 2 diabetes were randomly selected from 64 general practitioners (GPs) from different geographical areas of Denmark. Clinical and laboratory data on the individual patients were collected through the GPs' electronic medical patient records; particular emphasis was given to annual screening for microalbuminuria. RESULTS: The mean age of the patients was 66.2 +/- 11.6 years and 58.7% were male. Only 57.2% of the patients had been screened for microalbuminuria with any method within the preceding 12 months period; of these 76.0% had normo- and 21.0% had microalbuminuria, whereas 3.0% had overt proteinuria. In contrast, 97.6% of patients had had a minimum of one plasma-creatinine measurement within the past year. CONCLUSION: In Danish primary care, screening for microalbuminuria in type 2 diabetes is insufficiently implemented, whereas renal function is evaluated in almost all patients by plasma-creatinine measurements. The importance of diagnosing microalbuminuria in patients with type 2 diabetes needs to be emphasised.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren Tang","Mosbech, Thomas Hammershaimb","Hansen, Birtha Petrea","Kønig, Else","Johnsen, Peter Christian","Kamper, Anne-Lise"],"cuid":["S02-086.91-785131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease","Medicine","Multifactorial intervention","Nephropathy","Prevalence","Reduction","United States"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"screening for microalbuminuria in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes is incomplete in general practice","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.danmedj.dk/portal/page/portal/danmedj.dk/dmj_forside/PAST_ISSUE/2012/DMJ_2012_09/A4502","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.91-785131","identifier":[{"id":"84873275907","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22951198","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8900ae38-75d6-4a10-8c47-de78551f1436","dtu-53604046-bc4a-4bd4-a329-75ff42149db4"],"keyword":["CHRONIC KIDNEY-DISEASE","MEDICINE","MULTIFACTORIAL INTERVENTION","NEPHROPATHY","PREVALENCE","REDUCTION","UNITED-STATES"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EFB63CB784F962DF0DF58467885C2382"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.danmedj.dk/portal/page/portal/danmedj.dk/dmj_forside/PAST_ISSUE/2012/DMJ_2012_09/A4502","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling, DTU Data Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Studienævnene på HE, Studienævnene på HE - Master in Clinical Nursing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Tang","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f4fb113c-f8d2-4bb3-9a9d-0bc2ef14590d","name":"Knudsen, Søren Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Hammershaimb","key":"mosbechpau","last":"Mosbech","locid":"e3c2b6d0-f3a6-43e3-aad0-1df716201a91","name":"Mosbech, Thomas Hammershaimb","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birtha","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a1d570fa-0545-410e-bf76-8e9b1da12a37","name":"Hansen, Birtha Petrea","name_org":"Hansen, Birtha","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Else","key":"kønigpau","last":"Kønig","name":"Kønig, Else","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Christian","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"c2758f31-65dc-4b5b-95eb-3c8383c3c6f4","name":"Johnsen, Peter Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Lise","key":"kamperpau","last":"Kamper","name":"Kamper, Anne-Lise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22951198"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"9","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873275907"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","general practice"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8900ae38-75d6-4a10-8c47-de78551f1436","dtu-53604046-bc4a-4bd4-a329-75ff42149db4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Screening for microalbuminuria in patients with type 2 diabetes is incomplete in general practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.91-785131","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The flow structure of one isothermal swirling case in the Sydney swirl flame database was studied using two numerical methods. Results from the Reynolds-averaged Navier-Stokes (RANS) approach and large eddy simulation (LES) were compared with experimental measurements. The simulations were applied in two different Cartesian grids which were investigated by a grid independence study for RANS and a post-estimator for LES. The RNG k-ε turbulence model was used in RANS and dynamic Smagorinsky-Lilly model was used as the sub-grid scale model in LES. A validation study and cross comparison of ensemble average and root mean square (RMS) results showed LES outperforms RANS statistic results. Flow field results indicated that both approaches could capture dominant flow structures, like vortex breakdown (VB), and precessing vortex core (PVC). Streamlines indicate that the formation mechanisms of VB deducted from the two methods were different. The vorticity field was also studied using a velocity gradient based method. This research gained in-depth understanding of isothermal swirling flow.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Yang, Yang","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081805"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coherent structure","Large eddy simulation","Vortex breakdown","Vorticity field"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of reynolds averaged navier stokes based simulation and large eddy simulation for one isothermal swirling flow","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11630-012-0530-9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081805","identifier":[{"id":"84861022273","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6d318204-56f9-4bd5-8f13-011b928d7315"],"keyword":["Coherent structure","Large eddy simulation","Vortex breakdown","Vorticity field"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-75451D80399DDB4F8310250FCF595C1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11630-012-0530-9","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/xk14117276n41610/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yang","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"c4d85e83-0cad-45da-a4d9-7577cd33f0c6","name":"Yang, Yang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11630-012-0530-9","issn":["10032169","1993033X"],"issn_org":["10032169"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Thermal Science","pages":"154-161","publisher":"Science Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thermal Science","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861022273"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6d318204-56f9-4bd5-8f13-011b928d7315"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparison of reynolds averaged navier stokes based simulation and large eddy simulation for one isothermal swirling flow","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081805","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates the combustion characteristics of firing pure coal and firing pure wheat straw in a 150 kW swirl-stabilized burner flow reactor under nearly same conditions. The results indicate very different combustion characteristics between the coal flame and straw flame. In the straw flame, the straw particles are little affected by the swirling secondary air jet and travel in a nearly straight line through the oxygenlean core zones. In the coal flame, most of the coal particles are strongly affected by the secondary air jet and swirled into the oxygen-rich outer radius, which also increases the residence time of coal particles. Both the factors favor a complete burnout of the coal particles. The higher volatile yields of the straw produce more off-gas, requiring more O2 for the fast gas phase combustion and causing the off-gas to proceed to a much larger volume in the reactor prior to mixing with oxidizer. For the pulverized straw particles of a few hundred microns in diameters, the intra-particle conversion is found to be a secondary issue at most in their combustion. The simulations also show that a simple switch of the straw injection mode can not improve the burnout of the straw char.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Yin, Chungen","Rosendahl, Lasse","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085278"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a better understanding of biomass suspension co firing impacts via investigating a coal flame and a biomass flame in a swirl stabilized burner flow reactor under same conditions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.01.024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-085278","identifier":[{"id":"84857422730","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000303034000010","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-795a5a11-b49a-4885-8ae8-f75951d9a5d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66BDF62FB4CD40CD69A3A9CF7744EB9D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.01.024","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chungen","key":"yinpau","last":"Yin","locid":"a24ca845-2626-44cc-b726-b6c5ec9ddd24","name":"Yin, Chungen","orcid":"0000-0002-9885-7744","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","name":"Rosendahl, Lasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.01.024","issn":["03783820","18737188"],"issn_org":["03783820"],"issue":"1","journal":"Fuel Processing Technology","pages":"65-73","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel Processing Technology","volume":"98"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857422730"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-795a5a11-b49a-4885-8ae8-f75951d9a5d4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Towards a better understanding of biomass suspension co-firing impacts via investigating a coal flame and a biomass flame in a swirl-stabilized burner flow reactor under same conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-085278","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Methanol fuelled high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell (HTPEMFC) power systems are promising as the next generation of vehicle engines, efficient and environmentally friendly. Currently, their performance still needs to be improved and they still rely on a large Li-ion battery for system startup. In this paper, to handle these two issues, the potential of thermoelectric (TE) devices applied in a HTPEMFC power system has been preliminarily evaluated. Firstly, right after the fuel cell stack or the methanol reformer, thermoelectric generators (TEGs) are embedded inside a gas-liquid heat exchanger to jointly form a heat recovery subsystem for electricity production. It is calculated that the recovered power can increase the system efficiency and mitigate the dependence on Li-ion battery during system startup. To further improve the TEG subsystem performance, a finite-difference model is then employed and two main parameters are identified. Secondly, TE coolers are integrated into the methanol steam reformer to regulate heat fluxes herein and improve the system dynamic performance. Similar modification is also done on the evaporator to improve its dynamic performance as well as to reduce the heat loss during system startup. The results demonstrate that the TE-assisted heat flux regulation and heat-loss reduction can also effectively help solve the abovementioned two issues. The preliminary analysis in this paper shows that a TE device application inside HTPEMFC power systems is of great value and worthy of further study.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gao, Xin","Chen, Min","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088690"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-21","place":"Traverse City, us","start":"2011-07-17","title":"International Conference on Thermoelectrics","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fuel cell","Heat loss","Heat recovery","Heat regulation","Thermoelectric devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential usage of thermoelectric devices in a high temperature pem fuel cell system two case studies","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11664-012-2098-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-088690","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000304205100139","type":"wos"},{"id":"84862220551","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-84cb65cd-a15b-474c-90bc-b056a9711abc"],"keyword":["fuel cell","heat loss","heat recovery","heat regulation","thermoelectric devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E45D838A46CC5031589BC975D968BCB3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/1ul538r2902p7515/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11664-012-2098-2","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gao","key":"xinpau","last":"Xin","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","name_org":"Xin, Gao","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"9efe2461-3f4a-46b4-82d6-8e5fb687cc3b","name":"Chen, Min","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11664-012-2098-2","issn":["03615235","1543186X"],"issn_org":["03615235"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Electronic Materials","pages":"1838-1844","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"Journal of Electronic Materials","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84862220551"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-84cb65cd-a15b-474c-90bc-b056a9711abc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Potential Usage of Thermoelectric Devices in a High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell System : Two Case Studies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088690","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Steroidal glycoalkaloids (GAs) are toxins, produced by plants of the Solanaceae family. The potato plant (Solanum tuberosum L.) and its tubers predominantly contain the two GAs α-chaconine and α-solanine. These compounds are believed to act in synergy, and the degree of toxicity may therefore depend on their ratio in the potato. To determine the influence of α-solanine: α-chaconine ratio in potatoes on toxicity, a GM potato line (SGT 9-2) with reduced α-solanine content, and the parental control line (Desirée wild-type) having a traditional α-solanine: α-chaconine ratio were (1) studied for compositional similarity by analysing for a range of potato constituents, and (2) used in a 90-day feeding trial with the Syrian Golden hamster to study differential toxicity. The animal feeding study used diets with up to 60% freeze-dried potato powder from either line. Whilst data indicated some compositional differences between the GM line and its wildtype control these did not raise concerns related to nutritional value or safety. Results of the feeding trials showed a low number of significant differences between potato lines with different α-solanine: α-chaconine ratio but none were considered to raise safety concerns with regard to human (or animal) consumption.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Langkilde, Søren","Schrøder, Malene","Frank, Thomas","Shepherd, Louise V.T.","Conner, Sean","Davies, Howard V.","Meyer, Otto A.","Danier, Jürgen","Rychlik, Michael","Belknap, William R.","McCue, Kent F.","Engel, Karl-Heinz","Stewart, Derek","Knudsen, Ib","Poulsen, Morten","Poulsen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325685"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich","The James Hutton Institute","United States Department of Agriculture"],"keyword":["GM","Glycoalkaloid","Hamster","Potato","Toxicity","α Chaconine","α Solanine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"compositional and toxicological analysis of a gm potato line with reduced α solanine content a 000000000090 day feeding study in the syrian golden hamster","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.yrtph.2012.06.018","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325685","identifier":[{"id":"84864401416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-470169dd-db50-4e9c-b06e-ef489f95a5d7"],"keyword":["Acetylcholinesterase (AChE)","Compositional analyses","GM","Glycoalkaloid","Hamster","Potato","Toxicity","α-Chaconine","α-Solanine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DCF4075F5EBEADC0B1C585994974BCD7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.yrtph.2012.06.018","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"the james hutton institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The James Hutton Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"united states department of agriculture","loc":["United States","Ameri