,"corresponding":null,"first":"Derek","key":"stewartderekpau","last":"Stewart","name":"Stewart, Derek","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib","key":"knudsenibpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"dadd43c1-b9d8-406d-86fa-00ad95f0eed8","name":"Knudsen, Ib","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"poulsenmortenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"81612c2f-d703-4cd4-8114-867815d45338","name":"Poulsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-0442-6944","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.yrtph.2012.06.018","issn":["02732300","10960295"],"issn_org":["02732300"],"issue":"1","journal":"Regulatory Toxicology and Pharmacology","pages":"177-185","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Regulatory Toxicology and Pharmacology","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864401416"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-470169dd-db50-4e9c-b06e-ef489f95a5d7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Compositional and toxicological analysis of a GM potato line with reduced α-solanine content – A 90-day feeding study in the Syrian Golden hamster","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325685","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A new remote sensing based research infrastructure for atmospheric boundary-layer wind and turbulence measurements named WindScanner have during the past three years been in its early phase of development at DTU Wind Energy in Denmark. During the forthcoming three years the technology will be disseminated throughout Europe to pilot European wind energy research centers. The new research infrastructure will become an open source infrastructure that also invites collaboration with wind energy related atmospheric scientists and wind energy industry overseas. Recent achievements with 3D WindScanners and spin-off innovation activity are described. The Danish WindScanner.dk research facility is build from new and fast-scanning remote sensing equipment spurred from achievements within fiber optics and telecommunication technologies. At the same time the wind energy society has demanded excessive 3D wind flow and ever taller wind profile measurements for the wind energy resource assessment studies on- and off shore of the future. Today, hub heights on +5 MW wind turbines exceed the 100 m mark. At the Danish DTU test site Østerild testing is ongoing with a Siemens turbine with hub height 120 meters and a rotor diameter of 154 meters; hence its blade tips reaches almost 200 meters into the sky. The wind speed profiles over the rotor planes are consequently no longer representatively measured by a single cup anemometer at hub height from a nearby met-mast; power curve assessment as well as turbine control call for multi-height multi point measurement strategies of wind speed and wind shear within the turbines entire rotor plane. The development of our new remote sensing-based WindScanner.dk facility as well as the first measurement results obtained to date are here presented, including a first wind lidar measurement of turbulence in complex terrain within an internal boundary layer developing behind an escarpment. Also measurements of wind speed and direction profiles, including turbulence, have been acquired from remote sensing to heights above 1.5 km above the ground.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Torben","Siggaard Knudsen, Søren","Sjöholm, Mikael","Angelou, Nikolas","Pedersen, Anders Tegtmeier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357604"],"event":{"end":"2012-11-23","place":"Hyderabad, in","start":"2012-11-22","title":"International Conference on Wind Energy: Materials, Engineering and Policies (WEMEP-2012)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"windscanner eu a new remote sensing research infrastructure for on and offshore wind energy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/12199116/WEMEP2012_Full_Paper_tomi_007a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357604","ids":["dtu-b180a0c3-f9c2-4321-93d5-a7e8232882d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BD7BCEA98095A852D11D94760DDA8503"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/12199116/WEMEP2012_Full_Paper_tomi_007a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Test and Measurements"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"ca910896-9587-4bea-971d-58466b8dd979","name":"Mikkelsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-5428-856X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"siggaardknudsenpau","last":"Siggaard Knudsen","locid":"1f695aa6-1944-4f12-a54e-9b0fc7621d01","name":"Siggaard Knudsen, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael","key":"sjöholmpau","last":"Sjöholm","locid":"6c60d59d-bc1e-4778-9810-f7993c93566b","name":"Sjöholm, Mikael","orcid":"0000-0002-3094-2109","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolas","key":"angeloupau","last":"Angelou","locid":"da0c5f5b-f59a-428d-ae2e-72a2f47f13d9","name":"Angelou, Nikolas","orcid":"0000-0002-9627-422X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Tegtmeier","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4a62f68f-31c6-4144-98bb-5b84c78edb99","name":"Pedersen, Anders Tegtmeier","orcid":"0000-0002-9132-1357","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Wind Energy: Materials, Engineering, and Policies (WEMEP-2012)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b180a0c3-f9c2-4321-93d5-a7e8232882d4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"WindScanner.eu - a new Remote Sensing Research Infrastructure for On- and Offshore Wind Energy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357604","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Objective: There is clear evidence of a genetic component in major depression, and several studies indicate that neuropeptide Y (NPY) could play an important role in the pathophysiology of the disease. A well-known polymorphism encoding the substitution of leucine to proline in the signal peptide sequence of NPY (Leu7Pro variation) was previously found to protect against depression. Our study aimed at replicating this association in a large Danish population with major depression. Method: Leu7Pro was studied in a sample of depressed patients and ethnically matched controls, as well as psychiatric disease controls with schizophrenia. Possible functional consequences of Leu7Pro were explored in vitro. Results: In contrast to previous studies, Pro7 appeared to be a risk allele for depression, being significantly more frequent in the depression sample (5.5%, n = 593; p = 0.009; odds ratio, OR: 1.46) as compared to ethnically matched controls (3.8%, n = 2912), while schizophrenia patients (4.1%, n = 503) did not differ. In vitro, the Pro7 substitution appeared to be associated with reduced levels of NPY without affecting its mRNA level. Conclusion: The Leu7Pro variation may increase the risk of major depression, possibly by affecting the biosynthesis of NPY. Pernille","author_count":37,"contributors":["Koefoed, Pernille","Woldbye, David P D","Hansen, Thomas V O","Eplov, Lene Falgaard","Christiansen, Soren H.","Mors, Ole","Kessing, Lars Vedel","Werge, Thomas","Kaipio, Katja","Pesonen, Ullamari","Fahmy, Thomas","Mellerup, Erling Thyge","Jakobsen, Klaus D.","Hansen, Elsebeth S.","Knudsen, Gitte Maegaard","Bukh, Jens","Bock, Camilla","Lindberg, Camilla","Kristensen, Ann Suhl","Dam, Henrik Friis","Nordentoft, Merete","Als, Thomas Damm","Wang, August Gabriel","Gether, Ulrik","Rehfeld, Jens F.","Bolwig, Tom Gert"],"cuid":["S02-099.87-016017"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Turku"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of the leucine 000000000007 to proline 000000000007 variation in the signal sequence of neuropeptide y with major depression","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38371593/NPY.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-099.87-016017","identifier":[{"id":"26952950","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84859475495","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2ee1b66a-d90f-4442-a349-9df2f60615aa","ku-2237478a-ebf1-48d0-9b05-a6247a68f841"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E4F799214FAF5B6731B4ADDCE72F3EA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38371593/NPY.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1601-5215.2011.00600.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"