{"abstract":"Oxy-fuel firing is a promising technology that should enable the capture and storage of anthropogenic CO2 emissions from large stationary sources such as power plants and heavy industry. However, this new technology has a high energy demand for air separation and CO2 compression and storage. Unresolved issues, such as determination of the optimal recycle location of flue gas, the flue gas cleaning steps required (SO2, NOx, and particles), and the impact of an oxy-fuel flue gas on the cleaning steps, also persist. The aim of this work was to study the performance of the wet flue gas desulfurization (FGD) process under operating conditions corresponding to oxy-fuel firing. The most important output parameters were the overall degree of desulfurization and the residual limestone concentration in the gypsum slurry. Pilot-scale experiments quantified that the introduction of a flue gas with 90 vol % CO2, at a holding tank pH 5.4, reduced the limestone dissolution rate significantly and thereby increased the residual, particulate limestone concentration in the gypsum slurry from 3.2 to 5.0 g/L slurry relative to a base-case (air-firing) experiment with a flue gas CO2 concentration around 7 vol %. In the same experiment, due to the higher residual limestone concentration, the degree of desulfurization increased from 91 to 94%. The addition of 10 mM adipic acid to the slurry was not sufficient to return the increased concentration of residual limestone to the base-case level, but an additional increase in desulfurization degree, from 94 to 97%, was obtained. Using a holding tank pH 5.0 (no adipic acid) returned both parameters to the levels observed in the base-case experiment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Brian Brun","Fogh, Folmer","Knudsen, Niels Ole","Kiil, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-344037"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance of a wet flue gas desulfurization pilot plant under oxy fuel conditions","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ie1022173","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-344037","identifier":[{"id":"79954493035","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8426df83-705a-4c76-b42e-7540a3c909ed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B9E4E460D5159CFA90A066CDC2C1027"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ie1022173","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["Ørsted A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Vattenfall Vindkraft A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian Brun","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"edb1a2c1-f998-4ebc-b6aa-9b1904da9f32","name":"Hansen, Brian Brun","orcid":"0000-0002-5829-9223","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Folmer","key":"foghpau","last":"Fogh","name":"Fogh, Folmer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Ole","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Niels Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"kiilpau","last":"Kiil","locid":"080ff861-7fa8-4b37-a0a7-ee3a7cacb037","name":"Kiil, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-9013-6870","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/ie1022173","issn":["08885885","15205045"],"issn_org":["08885885"],"issue":"8","journal":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","pages":"4238-4244","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79954493035"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","vattenfall vindkraft a/s","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8426df83-705a-4c76-b42e-7540a3c909ed"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Performance of a Wet Flue Gas Desulfurization Pilot Plant under Oxy-Fuel Conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-344037","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this research work is to describe in qualitative and quantitative form the performance of a micro Combined Heat and Power system for residential application based on Solid Oxide Fuel Cell fueled by natural gas with two different types of pre-reforming systems, namely Steam Reforming and Partial Oxidation and recirculation of anode and cathode gas. The comparative analysis among the different configurations will lead us to conclude that maximum efficiency is achieved when cathode and anode gas recirculation are used along with steam methane reforming. Further Steam Methane Reforming process produces a higher electrical system efficiency compared to Partial oxidation reforming process. Efficiency is affected when running the system in part load mode mainly due to heat loss, additional natural gas supplied to the burner to satisfy the required heat demand inside the system, and ejector efficiency drop in the recirculation system. Due to high temperature of operation heat loss strongly affects the system efficiency especially at part load operation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Liso, Vincenzo","Olesen, Anders Christian","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-052297"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Micro CHP","SOFC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance comparison between partial oxidation and methane steam for sofc micro chp systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2011.04.022","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-052297","identifier":[{"id":"79959376292","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000293115600032","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-07cd0069-90eb-414c-a105-16af6d4e1a66"],"keyword":["Micro CHP","SOFC","Thermal system modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F4D6C13B7C0E5462DCCEC837D3844ACB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2011.04.022","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vincenzo","key":"lisopau","last":"Liso","locid":"c3a177b3-f874-40d3-984a-f1587412ec79","name":"Liso, Vincenzo","orcid":"0000-0002-7597-3849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.energy.2011.04.022","issn":["03605442","18736785"],"issn_org":["03605442"],"issue":"7","journal":"Energy","pages":"4216-4226","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79959376292"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-07cd0069-90eb-414c-a105-16af6d4e1a66"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Performance comparison between partial oxidation and methane steam for SOFC micro-CHP systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052297","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This work involves the an experimental characterisation and the development of control strategies for the methanol reformer system used in the Serenergy Serenus H3 E-350 high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane (HTPEM) fuel cell system. The system consists of a fuel evaporator utilizing the high temperature waste gas from a cathode air cooled 45 cell HTPEM fuel cell stack. The MEAs used are BASF P2100 which use phosphoric acid doped polybenzimidazole type membranes; an MEA with high CO tolerance and no complex humidity requirements. The methanol reformer used is integrated into a compact unit that allows the use of waste heat from the fuel cell stack in the reformer system, and a burner unit is also integrated to supplement provide heat using the stack anode hydrogen. The reformer is initially placed in an experimental system capable of emulating the interfaces to the fuel cell system, i.e. cathode and anode gas flows and temperature by using mass flow controllers and controlled heaters. Using this system the methanol reformer is characterized in its different operating points, both steady-state but also dynamically. Methanol steam reforming is a well known process, and provides good advantages when used together with HTPEM fuel cells. Many challenges exist in properly controlling such reformer systems and ensuring that key system states are controlled also during transients. The key system states monitored are different critical system temperatures in the evaporator, reformer and burner and the behaviour of the CO concentration of the reformate gas.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","Sahlin, Simon Lennart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053988"],"event":{"end":"2011-12-05","place":"Xcaret, mx","start":"2011-12-01","title":"Hydrogen and Fuel Cells Conference 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Control architecture","Fuel cell system","High temperature PEM","Methanol reforming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"control and experimental characterization of a methanol reformer for a 000000000350 w high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/58818106/Zingabstract2011_SJA.doc","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053988","ids":["aau-0d75f3b6-02d4-41cd-b31a-77f17942bcae"],"keyword":["Fuel cell system","control architecture","high temperature PEM","methanol reforming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E8DE295AACA9A41950615CED1BCE577E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/58818106/Zingabstract2011_SJA.doc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Christian Becker","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"372be06d-7f4f-4025-86a1-75eb41ce5af8","name":"Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Lennart","key":"sahlinpau","last":"Sahlin","locid":"10be1b68-a59d-4397-ae45-e356bf4c5844","name":"Sahlin, Simon Lennart","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0d75f3b6-02d4-41cd-b31a-77f17942bcae"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Control and Experimental Characterization of a Methanol Reformer for a 350 W High Temperature Polymer Electrolyte Membrane Fuel Cell system","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053988","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A novel proposal for the modeling and operation of a micro-CHP (combined-heat-and-power) residential system based on HT-PEMFC (High Temperature-Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell) technology is described and analyzed to investigate its commercialization prospects. An HT-PEMFC operates at elevated temperatures, as compared to Nafion-based PEMFCs and therefore can be a significant candidate for cogeneration residential systems. The proposed system can provide electric power, hot water, and space heating for a typical Danish single-family household. A complete fuel processing subsystem, with all necessary BOP (balance-of-plant) components, is modeled and coupled to the fuel cell stack subsystem. The micro-CHP system is simulated in LabVIEW environment to provide the ability of Data Acquisition of actual components and thereby more realistic design in the future. A part-load study has been conducted to indicate performance characteristics at off-design conditions. The system is sized to provide realistic dimensioning of the actual system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arsalis, Alexandros","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fuel processing","Micro CHP","PBI membrane","Residential systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and off design performance of a 000000000001 kw sub e sub ht pemfc high temperature proton exchange membrane fuel cell based residential micro chp combined heat and power system for danish single family households","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2010.12.009","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054964","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000288102600032","type":"wos"},{"id":"79551550014","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-10d15352-0f18-47c6-b741-e9e8ec7cea21"],"keyword":["Fuel processing","HT-PEMFC systems","Micro-CHP","PBI membrane","Residential systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF2D165C0EF77A4772632A3A372EF18E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2010.12.009","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"arsalispau","last":"Arsalis","locid":"78eb1abb-bd28-461a-8c05-68a79cd90e77","name":"Arsalis, Alexandros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.energy.2010.12.009","issn":["03605442","18736785"],"issn_org":["03605442"],"issue":"2","journal":"Energy","pages":"993-1002","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79551550014"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-10d15352-0f18-47c6-b741-e9e8ec7cea21"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and off-design performance of a 1 kW<sub>e</sub> HT-PEMFC (high temperature-proton exchange membrane fuel cell)-based residential micro-CHP (combined-heat-and-power) system for Danish single-family households","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054964","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This article summarizes a multi-phase model of a polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell based on the formerly commercial CFD code CFX-4. It is three-dimensional in nature and includes multiphase heat and mass transfer in porous media. An overview is given and some numerical issues are discussed in detail. We then present a three-dimensional study comparing two common flow field designs under normal operating conditions: the conventional straight channel design and the interdigitated design. While the interdigitated design leads to a higher pressure drop compared to the conventional design, its heat and mass transfer properties are superior. Another important aspect of this study is the wetting status of the electrolyte menbrane and the effective drag of water through the menbrane, which indicates what fraction of the product water created at the cathode side diffuses through the membrane and leaves at the anode side. Only a fundamental understanding of the various mechanisms involved can lead to proper water management and hence can prevent \"flooding\" of either anode or cathode side while keeping the membrane humidified, and consequently can optimize the fuel cell performance and durability while reducing cost.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Berning, Torsten","Odgaard, Madeleine","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D model","CFD","Fuel cell modeling","PEM fuel cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a multi fluid model to simulate heat and mass transfer in a pem fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-055735","ids":["aau-13880eb6-1b07-4ab3-bd93-f1e0cb7e493b"],"keyword":["3D model","CFD","Fuel cell modeling","PEM fuel cell"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-15AB82E00A6EBD05F7C29E3C19EDBE05"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["IRD A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Madeleine","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Madeleine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781466231313"],"pages":"1-56","publisher":"IEEF Foundation","status":"p","title":"Computational Fluid Dynamics Modeling in Development of Renewable Energy Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","ird a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-13880eb6-1b07-4ab3-bd93-f1e0cb7e493b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A multi-fluid model to simulate heat and mass transfer in a PEM fuel cell","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055735","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cell operation on dry reactant gases under low stoichiometry conditions employing the interdigitated flow field is investigated using a multi-fluid model. It is assumed that the MEA contains a water uptake layer which facilitates water absorption to the membrane and hence prevents the anode gas phase from drying out. It is shown that the membrane humidity increases with decreasing stoichiometric flow ratios to values of λ ≈ 7. Operating the cathode side at a stoichiometric flow ratio of 1.2 appears feasible under steady state conditions, while our simulations suggest that the anode stoichiometry may even be as low as 1.05. The effect of operation pressure and temperature on the membrane water content is studied. Finally, experiments are suggested to determine the kinetic absorption coefficient and the specific surface area of the electrolyte inside the catalyst layers.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Berning, Torsten","Odgaard, Madeleine","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-073269"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low stoichiometry operation of a polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell employing the interdigitated flow field design","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1149/1.3635720","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-073269","identifier":[{"id":"84860381467","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000309598800182","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-50213b46-7ccf-4b62-8401-4b1ebbb9dbfd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7500B78661F66ECBA8F6FC6F4779DB4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ecst.ecsdl.org/content/41/1/1897","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1149/1.3635720","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["IRD A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Madeleine","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Madeleine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/1.3635720","issn":["19385862"],"issn_org":["19386737"],"issue":"1","journal":"ECS Transactions","pages":"1897-1908","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"ECS Transactions","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860381467"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","ird a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-50213b46-7ccf-4b62-8401-4b1ebbb9dbfd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Low stoichiometry operation of a polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell employing the interdigitated flow field design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-073269","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The reforming of methanol can be an alternative source of hydrogen for fuel cells because it has many practical advantages over hydrogen, mainly due to the technological limitations related to the storage, supply, and distribution of the latter. However, despite the ease of methanol handling, impurities in the reformate gas produced from methanol steam reforming can affect the performance and durability of fuel cells. In this paper different vapor delivery systems, intended to assist in the study of the effects of some of the impurities, are described and compared with each other. A system based on a pump and electrically heated evaporator was found to be more suitable for the typical flow rates involved in the anode feed of an H3PO4/PBI based HT-PEMFC unit cell assembly. Test stations composed of vapor delivery systems and mass flow controllers for testing the effects of methanol slip, water vapor, CO, and CO2 are also illustrated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Araya, Samuel Simon","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Andreasen, Søren Juhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-083237"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-10","place":"Washington, us","start":"2011-08-07","title":"ASME 2011 5th International Conference on Energy Sustainability &amp; 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology, ESFuelCell2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vapor delivery systems for the study of the effects of reformate gas impurities in ht pem fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4005123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-083237","identifier":[{"id":"84881649056","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7218244b-3c8d-41e3-85ad-55fc3736d32a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-FB81AC5B821ED6338EDF0AD0F0A337C9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://fuelcellscience.asmedigitalcollection.asme.org/article.aspx?articleid=1472381","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4005123","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Simon","key":"arayapau","last":"Araya","locid":"31cc4ce7-c9ae-4406-95d1-b95d4269205f","name":"Araya, Samuel Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1115/1.4005123","issn":["1550624X"],"issue":"1","publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","series":"Journal of Fuel Cell Science and Technology","status":"p","subtitle":"ESFuelCell2011","title":"Proceedings of ASME 2011 5th International Conference on Energy Sustainability and 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84555178259"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7218244b-3c8d-41e3-85ad-55fc3736d32a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Vapor Delivery Systems for the Study of the Effects of Reformate Gas Impurities in HT-PEM Fuel Cells","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083237","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, the ability of a micro combined heat and power (mCHP) system to cover the heat and electricity demand of a single-family residence is investigated. A solid oxide fuel cell based mCHP system coupled with a hot water storage tank is analyzed. The energy profiles of single-family households in different European countries are evaluated. The range of Heat-to-Power Ratio for the SOFC based mCHP System of 0.5 to 1.5 shows good agreement with the hot water, space heating and electricity demand during the warm seasons across Europe. This suggests that the fuel cell system should be sized according to the summer energy demand. The winter energy demand shows a Heat-to-Power Ratio which cannot be covered by the mCHP unit alone. To ensure that the mCHP system meets both the thermal and electrical energy demand over the entire year, an auxiliary boiler and a hot water storage tank need to be coupled with the mCHP unit. It is further noted that the size of the auxiliary boiler should match the larger winter space heating demand.In contrast, the hot water tank volume should be sized according to the warm season space heating requirement, when space heating is not required but electricity and hot water are still in demand. This maximises the running time of the fuel cell, and thus the economic and environmental benefit of the system, without wasting produced heat.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liso, Vincenzo","Zhao, Yingru","Brandon, Nigel","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093602"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Cogeneration","SOFC systems","System analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of the impact of heat to power ratio for a sofc based mchp system for residential application under different climate regions in europe","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.07.086","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093602","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000296208800043","type":"wos"},{"id":"83055181335","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9629b93a-db7d-47fe-b7c4-0eeb3ae10832"],"keyword":["Cogeneration","Residential fuel cell systems","SOFC systems","System analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CED52EE5B788C463C994A0AECDCCD970"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.07.086","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360319911017460","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vincenzo","key":"lisopau","last":"Liso","locid":"c3a177b3-f874-40d3-984a-f1587412ec79","name":"Liso, Vincenzo","orcid":"0000-0002-7597-3849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yingru","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Yingru","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nigel","key":"brandonpau","last":"Brandon","name":"Brandon, Nigel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.07.086","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"21","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"13715-13726","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-83055181335"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9629b93a-db7d-47fe-b7c4-0eeb3ae10832"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analysis of the impact of Heat-to-Power Ratio for a SOFC-based mCHP system for residential application under different climate regions in Europe","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093602","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Transport processes inside polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cells (PEMFC’s) are highly complex and involve convective and diffusive multiphase, multispecies flow through porous media along with heat and mass transfer and electrochemical reactions in conjunction with water transport through an electrolyte membrane. We will present a computational model of a PEMFC with focus on capillary transport of water through the porous layers and phase change and discuss the impact of the liquid phase boundary condition between the porous gas diffusion layer and the flow channels, where water droplets can emerge and be entrained into the gas stream.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Multi phase flow"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling multiphase flow inside the porous media of a polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2495/MPF110251","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-101528","identifier":[{"id":"84864839901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b15db909-a8b6-4f79-b278-a3c66857c8cd"],"keyword":["Fuel cell modelling","GDL/channel interface","Multi-phase flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3C1778EC488AE4FF6626A518CB0BA1BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2495/MPF110251","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://library.witpress.com/pages/paperinfo.asp?PaperID=22357","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Heating and Cooling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2495/mpf110251","issn":["17433533"],"issue":"6","journal":"WIT Transactions on Engineering Sciences","pages":"299-310","publisher":"WIT Press","publisher_org":"W I T Press","status":"p","title":"WIT Transactions on Engineering Sciences","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864839901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b15db909-a8b6-4f79-b278-a3c66857c8cd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modelling multiphase flow inside the porous media of a polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101528","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The reduction of a single-layer FeO film grown on Pt(111) by CO at elevated pressures and temperatures has been studied through an interplay of scanning tunneling microscopy, ambient-pressure X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, and density functional theory calculations. Exposure of the FeO thin film to CO at pressures between 1 and 30 Torr and temperatures between 500 and 530 K leads to formation of a honeycomb-structured Fe(3)O(2) film with hollow sites occupied by single Pt atoms extracted from the substrate surface. The formation of these adatoms is driven by an increase in CO adsorption energy. In addition, the structure incorporates undercoordinated Fe centers, which are proposed to have substantial effects on the catalytic properties of the surface.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Merte, Lindsay Richard","Knudsen, Jan","Eichhorn, Falk M","Porsgaard, Søren","Zeuthen, Helene","Grabow, Lars","Lægsgaard, Erik","Bluhm, Hendrik","Salmeron, Miquel","Mavrikakis, Manos","Besenbacher, Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-141855"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co induced embedding of pt adatoms in a partially reduced feo x film on pt 000000000111","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ja2015923","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-141855","identifier":[{"id":"21707081","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79960258123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-159b6b32-568c-4949-8ec9-2d4eea0a733c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59465985DFC29FC0C2E8F018204C0DDA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ja2015923","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, iNano-School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lindsay R","key":"mertepau","last":"Merte","locid":"e64f8b59-427e-459b-abdf-a3d992131a78","name":"Merte, Lindsay Richard","name_org":"Merte, Lindsay R","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"b2acb2da-6ed5-489a-a4f0-0b8ead5c1159","name":"Knudsen, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Falk M","key":"eichhornpau","last":"Eichhorn","name":"Eichhorn, Falk M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soeren","key":"porsgaardpau","last":"Porsgaard","locid":"dbd22f50-75ad-43c3-897b-abc7727d473b","name":"Porsgaard, Søren","name_org":"Porsgaard, Soeren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"zeuthenpau","last":"Zeuthen","locid":"0e005a9c-9bb9-49a5-aa35-b9433897e947","name":"Zeuthen, Helene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"grabowpau","last":"Grabow","name":"Grabow, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"lægsgaardpau","last":"Lægsgaard","locid":"8c682c03-9f69-4594-81b0-bba9275e1ea5","name":"Lægsgaard, Erik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hendrik","key":"bluhmpau","last":"Bluhm","name":"Bluhm, Hendrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Miquel","key":"salmeronpau","last":"Salmeron","name":"Salmeron, Miquel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Manos","key":"mavrikakispau","last":"Mavrikakis","name":"Mavrikakis, Manos","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"besenbacherpau","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"0aa89800-dd75-4f15-a575-c419dda7a69f","name":"Besenbacher, Flemming","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21707081"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/ja2015923","issn":["00027863","15205126"],"issn_org":["00027863"],"journal":"Journal of the American Chemical Society","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Chemical Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960258123"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-159b6b32-568c-4949-8ec9-2d4eea0a733c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"CO-Induced Embedding of Pt Adatoms in a Partially Reduced FeO(x) Film on Pt(111)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-141855","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The aim of this study was to determine the survival of 15 different strains of Salmonella of selected serotypes during prolonged cold storage of beef. Methods and Results: Fifteen strains of eight different serotypes of Salmonella were spiked onto fresh cuts beef portions, and the survival was followed during storage in a laboratory cooling system. Over a 14‐day period, all strains were reduced significantly in numbers; however, strains of Salmonella Typhimurium DT104 and Salmonella Enteritidis PT4 and PT8 survived significantly longer than strains of the serovars Dublin, Derby, Infantis and Newport. For five selected strains, the observations were verified in a pilot plant cooling facility mimicking industrial cooling. No significant differences in reduction were found between the two cooling methods. Conclusions: A significant reduction in Salmonella can be obtained by dry aging of beef during cold storage but the survival is strain dependent. Significance and Impact of the Study: From a hygienic point of view, cold storage of unpacked beef, which is still performed in small slaughterhouses, is a good alternative to vacuum packaging.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Knudsen, Gitte Maegaard","Sommer, Helle Mølgaard","Sørensen, N.D.","Olsen, J. E.","Aabo, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-092.57-036510"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Beef","Chilling","Salmonella"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival of em salmonella em on cuts of beef carcasses subjected to dry aging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2672.2011.05094.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.57-036510","identifier":[{"id":"80052795634","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21714838","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-ad1d186d-95b2-4034-ac93-08fd050cec2e","ku-6a2efdeb-f530-44b9-af4e-8d15e1db83f5"],"keyword":["Beef","Chilling","Dry aging","Salmonella"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B7D751FADCA7B0B099343E930220AE57"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2672.2011.05094.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte Maegaard","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"bb84b997-02d1-4569-be9c-278ebb453bf3","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Maegaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3983-0541","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Mølgaard","key":"sommerpau","last":"Sommer","locid":"27afe1c5-22f0-4a90-8056-a36d35cf61e2","name":"Sommer, Helle Mølgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"N.D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, N.D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"aabopau","last":"Aabo","locid":"b86b74ee-7bf8-41f6-9c29-1cbcc8bbd994","name":"Aabo, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-1430-1480","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21714838"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1365-2672.2011.05094.x","issn":["13645072"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","pages":"848-854","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052795634"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ad1d186d-95b2-4034-ac93-08fd050cec2e","ku-6a2efdeb-f530-44b9-af4e-8d15e1db83f5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Survival of Salmonella on cuts of beef carcasses subjected to dry aging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.57-036510","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this work, extensive electrochemical impedance measurements have been conducted on a 45 cm2 BASF Celtec P2100 high temperature PEM MEA. The fuel cell performance has been examined subject to some of the poisoning effects experienced when running on a reformate gas. The impedance is measured at different temperatures, currents, and different content of CO, CO2 and H2 in the anode gas. The impedance spectrum at each operating point is fitted to an equivalent circuit and an analysis to identify the different mechanisms governing the impedance is performed. The trends observed, when varying the operating conditions under pure H2, generally show good agreement with results from the literature. When adding CO and CO2 to the anode gas the entire frequency spectrum is affected, and especially the measurements conducted at low temperatures and high CO concentrations reveal undesirable transient effects.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-052449"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Brændselscelle","Equivalent circuit","Fuel cell","High temperature","Impedance","PBI","PEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high temperature pem fuel cell performance characterisation with co and co sub 000000000002 sub using electrochemical impedance spectroscopy","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.04.076","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-052449","identifier":[{"id":"79960922352","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000294374800047","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-083df5ae-ef65-415e-ac1c-cd2373736e49"],"keyword":["Brændselscelle","Equivalent Circuit","Fuel cell","High Temperature","Impedance","Impedane","PBI","PEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A7405F852FFE3828C8E7FAB845BF7AB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.04.076","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Rabjerg","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","locid":"863c6a36-4e04-431b-a5b0-9e141fd73553","name":"Vang, Jakob Rabjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4497-3205","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.04.076","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"16","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"9815-9830","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960922352"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-083df5ae-ef65-415e-ac1c-cd2373736e49"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"High Temperature PEM Fuel Cell Performance Characterisation with CO and CO<sub>2</sub> using Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052449","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In order to investigate the role of combustion chemistry and radiation heat transfer in oxy-fuel combustion modeling, a computational fluid dynamics (CFD) modeling study has been performed for two different oxy-fuel furnaces. One is a lab-scale 0.8MW oxy-natural gas flame furnace whose detailed in-flame measurement data are available; the other is a conventional 609MW utility boiler which is assumed to be operating under oxy-fuel combustion condition with dry flue gas recycle. A new model for gaseous radiative properties is developed, validated, and then implemented in the CFD simulations. The CFD results are compared to those based on the widely used model in literature, as well as the in-flame measurement data. The importance and advantage of the new model for gaseous radiative properties have been well demonstrated. Different combustion mechanisms are also implemented and compared in the CFD simulations, from which significant difference in the predicted flame temperature and species is observed. This difference is consistent with those expected from the equilibrium calculation results. As a conclusion, the appropriate combustion mechanisms applicable to oxy-fuel combustion modeling are identified. Among the key issues in combustion modeling, e.g., mixing, radiation and chemistry, this paper derives useful guidelines on radiation and chemistry implementation for reliable CFD analyses of oxy-fuel combustion, particularly for industrial applications.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Yin, Chungen","Rosendahl, Lasse","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053270"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CFD","CO2 capture","Combustion chemistry","Oxy fuel combustion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chemistry and radiation in oxy fuel combustion a computational fluid dynamics modeling study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2011.03.023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053270","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000289976700022","type":"wos"},{"id":"79955478129","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0b1a0f7a-bc79-4346-8d4f-104abe05ac71"],"keyword":["CFD","CO2 capture","Combustion chemistry","Oxy-fuel combustion","Radiation heat transfer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5DF14D9F747C511FF7028E1103BD7CA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2011.03.023","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chungen","key":"yinpau","last":"Yin","locid":"a24ca845-2626-44cc-b726-b6c5ec9ddd24","name":"Yin, Chungen","orcid":"0000-0002-9885-7744","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","name":"Rosendahl, Lasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuel.2011.03.023","issn":["00162361","18737153"],"issn_org":["00162361"],"issue":"7","journal":"Fuel","pages":"2519-2529","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955478129"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b1a0f7a-bc79-4346-8d4f-104abe05ac71"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Chemistry and radiation in oxy-fuel combustion : A computational fluid dynamics modeling study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053270","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Ignition and burnout of a single biomass particle were studied numerically. A one-dimensional particle combustion model was developed which is capable to simulate all the intraparticle conversion processes (drying, recondensation, devolatilization, char gasification/oxidation and heat/mass/momentum transfer) to investigate the conversion and ignition process of single biomass particle. The results indicated that the ignition occurrs homogeneously in all cases. Also the results showed that the homogeneous ignition delay was very sensitive to particle size and shape but the effects of oxygen concentration were not very significant. The influences of these factors on particle burnout were much more remarkable than ignition behaviour.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","Kær, Søren Knudsen","Yin, Chungen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068617"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-01","place":"Cardiff, gb","start":"2012-06-27","title":"5th European Combustion Meeting","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors influencing the ignition and burnout of a single biomass particle","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://data.cas.manchester.ac.uk/database3/SAMPLE%20III/Dropbox%20stuff/ECM/ECM%202011%20Papers/339.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-068617","ids":["aau-4027407d-0669-4551-8395-be36403bb731"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7973125017F1DF08C9D1296059146B37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://data.cas.manchester.ac.uk/database3/SAMPLE%20III/Dropbox%20stuff/ECM/ECM%202011%20Papers/339.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maryam","key":"momenikouchaksaraeipau","last":"Momenikouchaksaraei","locid":"f9706a2b-7ab1-4b2d-b289-7dfee67472f8","name":"Momenikouchaksaraei, Maryam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chungen","key":"yinpau","last":"Yin","locid":"a24ca845-2626-44cc-b726-b6c5ec9ddd24","name":"Yin, Chungen","orcid":"0000-0002-9885-7744","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Cardiff University","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 5th European Combustion Meeting"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4027407d-0669-4551-8395-be36403bb731"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Factors Influencing the Ignition and Burnout of a Single Biomass Particle","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068617","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This article examines two research areas: How interactive floors can be used beneficially in an educational context, and how an interactive floor can be created which is mobile and relatively inexpensive.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Boisen, Ulrik","Hansen, Anders Juul","Knudsen, Lars","Pedersen, Søren Larsen","Overholt, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102894"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Floors","Interaction design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel amp affordable interactive floor for educational applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://elsevier.conference-services.net/programme.asp?conferenceID=2253&action=prog_titles","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-102894","ids":["aau-b606c7ce-29f8-4e0f-ad65-af3904f99755"],"keyword":["Educational Activities","Floors","Interaction Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9515C2F041CE08C6411B676B00A6BCE8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://elsevier.conference-services.net/programme.asp?conferenceID=2253&action=prog_titles","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"4d6c8f1e-b70e-47d1-864d-30dec34ea1ff","name":"Boisen, Ulrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juul","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Anders Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"40a6f0a3-0277-453c-9cb5-29eb248feb12","name":"Knudsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-8206-5638","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Larsen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Søren Larsen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"overholtpau","last":"Overholt","locid":"ffec9cea-8641-4c7f-b9e4-9f57c427bda8","name":"Overholt, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0003-2127-2868","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","subtitle":"Learning Futures: Education, Technology &amp; Sustainability","title":"Proceedings of the CAL 2011 conference - Computer Assisted Learning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b606c7ce-29f8-4e0f-ad65-af3904f99755"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A novel &amp; affordable interactive floor for educational applications","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102894","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Numerical and experimental study is performed to evaluate the reactant by-pass flow in a catalytic plate reactor with a coated wire mesh catalyst for steam reforming of methane for hydrogen generation. By-pass of unconverted methane is evaluated under different wire mesh catalyst width to reactor duct width ratios, the results show that altering this ratio from 0.98 to 0.96 results in an increase in by-pass mass flow of 22%. Effect of catalytic wire mesh flow resistance on by-pass flow has also been investigated and results show increased by-pass flow as catalytic wire mesh flow resistance increases. The numerical results are in good agreement with experimental data. The study improves the understanding of the underlying transport phenomena in these reactors and shows that the flow maldistribution in a catalytic plate reactor using a coated wire mesh has to be considered.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sigurdsson, Haftor Örn","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-111785"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-10","place":"Washington, DC, us","start":"2011-08-07","title":"ASME 2011 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental and numerical evaluation of the by pass flow in a catalytic plate reactor for hydrogen production","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-111785","identifier":[{"id":"84881642363","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d48b0de4-2f83-4a54-ad05-18153e04538d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8158D2831EDA5F717D1A0863D2A8B675"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university",