{"abstract":"Abstract Introduction A specific algorithm has been proposed for classifying impingement related shoulder pain in athletes with overhead activity. Data on the inter-examiner reproducibility of the suggested clinical tests and criteria and their mutual dependencies for identifying subacromial impingement symptoms (SIS) are not available. Objective To test the inter-examiner reproducibility of selected tests and criteria suggested for classifying SIS and the mutual dependencies of each of the individual tests and SIS. Method A standardised three-phase protocol for clinical reproducibility studies was followed, consisting of a training, an overall agreement and a study phase. To proceed to the study phase, an overall agreement of 0.80 was required. In total 10, 20 and 44 subjects were included in the three phases, respectively. The case prevalence in the study phase was 50%. The inclusion criterion for cases was ≥3, and for controls ≤1 positive test out of four. Cohen's κ statistics were used for calculating agreement. Results In the overall agreement phase, an agreement of 0.90 was obtained, while in the study phase it was 0.98 with a κ of 0.95 for SIS. κ Values for the individual tests varied between 0.60 and 0.95. Mutual dependencies between each test and SIS showed Neer's test with anterior pain to be most often used to determine SIS. Conclusions Inter-examiner reproducibility was moderate to almost perfect for the selected tests and criteria for SIS. The next challenge will be to establish reproducibility in clinical practice, as well as the validity of the tests and criteria for SIS.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Vind, Mikkel","Bogh, Søren Bie","Larsen, Camilla Marie","Kromann Knudsen, Hans","Søgaard, Karen","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit"],"cuid":["S03-096.77-048766"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Vind, Mikkel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inter examiner reproducibility of clinical tests and criteria used to identify subacromial impingement syndrome","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2010-%20000042","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.77-048766","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3191397","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84882824231","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22021736","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-34d52a7a-7cf8-4615-bd56-e6e80c9506d0","sdu-dfce871c-e736-49b9-b406-b1ba983514c1","ucl-cfa6d3ee-269d-4921-aea9-6a3327f16d36"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F13FEC206D3EE429E652C058596A9FDA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2010-%20000042","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2010-000042","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"vindpau","last":"Vind","name":"Vind, Mikkel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Bie","key":"boghpau","last":"Bogh","name":"Bogh, Søren Bie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Marie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0fdd3035-e7da-4ae3-9e99-f247aecd54e3","name":"Larsen, Camilla Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-4691-3609","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Kromann","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f6a80c04-acfb-4ebb-bbd9-d996fd6d2885","name":"Knudsen, Hans Kromann","orcid":"0000-0002-8452-5300","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"01571423-fcd0-4dbc-9112-e9b52d4a1131","name":"Søgaard, Karen","orcid":"0000-0003-3968-6364","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","locid":"887ddfe7-cfa6-4b72-a17d-ecf86987c5c0","name":"Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-4973-8415","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22021736"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2010-000042","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e000042","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882824231"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-34d52a7a-7cf8-4615-bd56-e6e80c9506d0","sdu-dfce871c-e736-49b9-b406-b1ba983514c1","ucl-cfa6d3ee-269d-4921-aea9-6a3327f16d36"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Inter-examiner reproducibility of clinical tests and criteria used to identify subacromial impingement syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.77-048766","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A three-dimensional, multi-component, two-fluid model developed in the commercial CFD package CFX 13 (ANSYS inc.), is used to investigate the effect of porous media compression on transport phenomenon of a PEM Fuel cell (PEMFC). The PEMFC model only consist of the cathode channel, gas diffusion layer, micro-porous layer and catalyst layer, excluding the membrane and anode. In the porous media liquid water transport is described by the capillary pressure gradient, momentum loss via the Darcy-Forchheimer equation and mass transfer between phases by a non-equilibrium phase change model. Furthermore, the presence of irreducible liquid water is taken into account. In order to account for compression, porous media morphology variations are specified based on the GDL through-plane strain and intrusion which are stated as a function of compression. These morphology variations affect gas and liquid water transport, and hence liquid water distribution and the risk of blocking active sites. Hence, water transport is studied under GDL compression, in order to investigate the qualitative effects. Two simulation cases are compared; one with and one without compression.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Olesen, Anders Christian","Berning, Torsten","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-062451"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-10","place":"Washington, DC, us","start":"2011-08-07","title":"ASME 2011 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of inhomogeneous compression on water transport in the cathode of a pem fuel cell","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-062451","identifier":[{"id":"84881637393","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2ace5675-32e6-4131-b949-5008b4bab73d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5904023152C0C591F09B64FB3CD2D3C6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Christian","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a6c83a7f-2f25-4b66-b42d-9ef435ffeecf","name":"Olesen, Anders Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8344-914X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten","key":"berningpau","last":"Berning","locid":"eecf017d-14b4-4110-9df5-a10a6c7e9bd9","name":"Berning, Torsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3324-0927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780791854693"],"pages":"839-850","publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","status":"p","subtitle":"ESFuelCell2011","title":"Proceedings of ASME 2011 5th International Conference on Energy Sustainability &amp; 9th Fuel Cell Science, Engineering and Technology Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881637393"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2ace5675-32e6-4131-b949-5008b4bab73d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The effect of inhomogeneous compression on water transport in the cathode of a PEM fuel cell","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-062451","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Methanol fuelled high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cell (HTPEMFC) power systems are promising as new generation vehicle engines, efficient and environmentally friendly. Currently, they still rely on large Li-ion batteries for system startup. In this paper, the application potential of thermoelectric (TE) devices to release this Li-ion dependence has been preliminarily evaluated. Firstly, following the HTPEMFC stack or the methanol reformer, TEGs are embedded inside a gas-liquid heat exchanger to jointly form a TE recovery subsystem for electricity production. A finite-difference model of this subsystem has been built in engineering equation solver (EES) software for optimization. The results show that the recovered power can significantly reduce the dependence on Li-ion battery during startup, especially when this TE subsystem is directly installed after the methanol reformer. Secondly, TE coolers are integrated into the methanol evaporator to reduce the heat loss herein during the HTPEMFC power system startup. It is believed that by reducing this heat loss, the electricity consumption by the evaporator during startup can be steadily reduced. Through the heat-electricity conversion and the TE-assisted heat-loss reduction, the HTPEMFC system dependence on Li-ion battery during startup can be dramatically reduced. The preliminary analyses show that TE device applications inside HTPEMFC power systems are of great value and worth of further studies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gao, Xin","Chen, Min","Andreasen, Søren Juhl","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086662"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-21","place":"Traverse City, us","start":"2011-07-17","title":"International Conference on Thermoelectrics","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["EES","HTPEMFC","Heat recovery","Heat regulation","Thermoelectric devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential usage of thermoelectric devices in a htpemfc system two case studies","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/58196217/Potential_Usage_Xin_Gao.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-086662","ids":["aau-7dde637f-e302-4f3e-acf5-70098254f1af"],"keyword":["EES","HTPEMFC","heat recovery","heat regulation","thermoelectric devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F7A312EDCBB0544D0FC876416CF99C49"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/58196217/Potential_Usage_Xin_Gao.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gao","key":"xinpau","last":"Xin","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","name_org":"Xin, Gao","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Min","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"9efe2461-3f4a-46b4-82d6-8e5fb687cc3b","name":"Chen, Min","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Juhl","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"02115d16-a485-4ac6-b914-7460ef6c4e83","name":"Andreasen, Søren Juhl","orcid":"0000-0002-0767-5874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7dde637f-e302-4f3e-acf5-70098254f1af"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Potential Usage of Thermoelectric Devices in a HTPEMFC System : Two Case Studies","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086662","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A detailed thermodynamic, kinetic and geometric model of a micro-CHP (Combined-Heatand-Power) residential system based on High Temperature-Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell (HT-PEMFC) technology is developed, implemented and validated. HT-PEMFC technology is investigated as a possible candidate for fuel cell-based residential micro-CHP systems, since it can operate at higher temperature than Nafion-based fuel cells, and therefore can reach higher cogeneration efficiencies. The proposed system can provide electric power, hot water, and space heating for a typical Danish single-family household. A complete fuel processing subsystem, with all necessary balance-of-plant components, is modeled and coupled to the fuel cell stack subsystem. The micro-CHP system’s synthesis/ design and operational pattern is analyzed by means of a parametric study. The parametric study is conducted to determine the most viable system/component design based on maximizing total system efficiency, without violating the requirements of the system. Four decision variables (steam-to-carbon ratio, fuel cell operating temperature, combustor temperature and hydrogen stoichiometry) were parameterized within feasible limits to provide insight on their effect on the overall performance of the proposed system under study and also to provide input on more efficient design in the future. The system is designed to provide maximum loads of 1 kWe and 2 kWth. A sensitivity analysis is applied to investigate the influence of the most important parameters on the simulated performance of the system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arsalis, Alexandros","Nielsen, Mads Pagh","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088404"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fuel cell system","HT PEMFC system","Micro CHP","PBI","Parametric study","Residential system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and parametric study of a 000000000001 kw sub e sub ht pemfc based residential micro chp system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.01.121","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-088404","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000290072300040","type":"wos"},{"id":"79953650195","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-83cc4d58-8c4e-410f-af1b-5093a012bc54"],"keyword":["Fuel cell system","HT-PEMFC system","Micro-CHP","PBI","Parametric study","Residential system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D30A5DC7D2F46B4738B641953F81A987"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.01.121","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Fluid Mechanics and Combustion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"arsalispau","last":"Arsalis","locid":"78eb1abb-bd28-461a-8c05-68a79cd90e77","name":"Arsalis, Alexandros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Pagh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4167f94b-c30d-4966-8da7-b9f5a33bb6d0","name":"Nielsen, Mads Pagh","orcid":"0000-0002-9396-8525","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Knudsen","key":"kærpau","last":"Kær","locid":"898d6584-ec2e-430a-b78d-e3e0d670dcdd","name":"Kær, Søren Knudsen","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-8055","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.01.121","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"5010-5020","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953650195"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-83cc4d58-8c4e-410f-af1b-5093a012bc54"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and parametric study of a 1 kW<sub>e</sub> HT-PEMFC-based residential micro-CHP system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088404","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Fuel cells have, by design, a limited effective life time, which depends on how they are operated. The general consent is that operation of the fuel cell at the extreme of the operational range, or operation of the fuel cell without sufficient reactants (a.k.a. starvation), will lower the effective life time of a fuel cell significantly. On air cooled HTPEMFCs, the blower, which supplies the fuel cell with oxygen for the chemical process, also functions as the cooling system. This makes the blower bi-functional and as a result a higher supply of oxygen is often available, hence changes in the fuel cell output can be optimised by the knowledge of how much oxygen is supplied to the fuel cell at any given time, without reducing the effective life time of a fuel cell by starvation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jensen, Hans-Christian Becker","Kær, Søren Knudsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092163"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dynamic load","Fuel cell","HT PEM","Model based"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"boundary model based reference control of blower cooled high temperature polymer electrolyte membrane fuel cells","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2011.01.023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-092163","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000290072300042","type":"wos"},{"id":"79953649019","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-90e57b7b-07e8-4b45-8bba-e406e58aaee9"],"keyword":["Dynamic load","Fuel cell","HT-PEM","Model-based"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7A7484318F1879EB35D581BDB434A23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type"